window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS=(window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2101,"title":"Chapter 2101: An Unknown Demon Emperor","paragraphs":["Sensing the demonic presence, Zhou Yanfei turned to Yan Hara and said grimly, \"We’ll continue this conversation later.\"","Without another word, his gaze shifted toward the middle of the battlefield, where a shadowy figure had emerged out of thin air.","Once its form came into focus, the figure revealed itself to be a grey-skinned demon—its body devoid of any visible crystal, a clear indication that it was at least a Demon General.","\"Quickly! Seal it!\" several Demon Sealers shouted in panic, instinctively rushing forward to subdue the threat.","\"Don’t be reckless!\" Zhou Yanfei warned sharply, but his voice came a second too late.","\"Foolish livestock!\" the demon sneered with contempt, its voice laced with cruel amusement. In the very next instant, a wave of oppressive force erupted from its body—followed by a thunderous explosion. The surrounding Demon Sealers were instantly reduced to a mist of blood and flesh, their deaths so sudden and brutal that it left the battlefield in stunned silence.","\"That level of prowess! It has to be a Demon Emperor!\" Yan Hara exclaimed.","Unfortunately, she’d already exhausted herself, and it would take some time before she could recover and help. Yet, she wasn’t too worried, since the Divine Paragon himself was present.","Yuan turned his focus onto the demon with narrowed eyes.","\"A Demon Emperor...?\" he muttered under his breath.","Yet, its presence was unfamiliar. Three Demon Emperors had once escaped with their lives, and he’d slain one not long ago. That should’ve left only two—both of whom he could recognize without fail.","So who was this one?","’Did a new one emerge?’ Yuan pondered silently. But with the Demon Realm sealed, no new demons should’ve appeared. That could only mean one thing—this one had ascended to the rank of Demon Emperor after the Demon Realm was sealed.","However, an evolution of that magnitude would demand a tremendous amount of time, countless sacrifices, and opportunities that should’ve long vanished with the end of the Demonic Era.","\"How dare you call us foolish?\" Zhou Yanfei stepped forward, unshaken by its overwhelming pressure. \"You may be a Demon Emperor, but this is the heart of the Demon Sealing Grotto. Not even you can deal with all of us alone.\"","The Demon Emperor let out a low, mocking laugh. \"Who said anything about being alone?\"","It clapped its hands once, softly.","A moment later, the space around them twisted.","One after another, dark silhouettes emerged from the shadows, their auras vile and suffocating. In mere moments, hundreds of demons of varying ranks blanketed the horizon, encircling the Demon Sealing Grotto.","The expressions of the Demon Sealers darkened. In an instant, the tides had turned. The sheer number of demons was overwhelming, enough to threaten even the Demon Sealing Grotto.","The Demon Emperor spoke a moment later, \"Honestly, we weren’t planning on making an appearance. However, something peculiar had forced our hands.\"","Its gaze shifted to Yan Hara. Then, it continued with narrowed eyes, \"The Divine Paragon’s legacy, you say? That won’t do. We cannot allow you to live now that we know you have inherited that vermin’s techniques.\"","Realizing the demon’s true intent, Zhou Yanfei roared with urgency, \"Demon Sealing Grotto! Protect Demon Sealer Yan Hara at all costs! We cannot allow the Divine Paragon’s legacy to vanish a second time!\"","Despite Yan Hara belonging to the Demon Sealing Clan—their long-standing rival—the Demon Sealers of the Grotto did not hesitate. In that moment, they understood: the Divine Paragon’s legacy transcended all grudges. Even if it had been Qian Chu standing in her place, they would still decide to protect him.","The Demon Emperor raised his hand and pointed at Yan Hara, his voice eerily calm as he uttered a single command—","\"Kill them all.\"","In the blink of an eye, chaos erupted. Demons and Demon Sealers clashed, painting the battlefield in blood and fury—a scene common in the Demonic Era but unseen for countless years since then.","By now, every Demon Sealer within the Demon Sealing Grotto had joined the battle, their auras clashing violently with the demonic horde. Yuan, too, prepared to step into the fray, but his movements abruptly stopped as he sensed a strange disturbance.","His gaze instinctively shifted toward the portal leading into the Grotto’s headquarters, and just as his attention settled, he caught sight of a lone figure slipping through its entrance.","Typically, such a scene would warrant no suspicion—but this individual was cloaked in a technique that concealed their presence. While not as flawless as Shadow Veil, it came close. Amidst the chaos of battle, even seasoned experts would have easily overlooked it.","Without hesitation, Yuan activated Shadow Veil and chased after the individual into the Demon Sealing Grotto’s headquarters.","However, before doing so, he warned Yan Hara using voice transmission, \"I’m going to investigate something real quick, so you’ll have to deal with these demons without me for a bit.\"","\"WHAT?!\"","Yan Hara cried out, her voice sharp with alarm.","\"What’s wrong, Yan Hara?!\" Zhou Yanfei immediately turned to her, eyes narrowing.","\"N-Nothing...\" she quickly shook her head, forcing a calm facade, but the flicker of worry in her eyes betrayed her.","\"I’m almost ready to fight again,\" she said a moment later as she consumed several more recovery pills.","Meanwhile, after stepping through the portal, Yuan continued following the mysterious figure, taking the opportunity to scrutinize his appearance. He had already memorized the faces of every Demon Sealing Grotto member present on the battlefield, yet this man was unfamiliar.","This individual appeared to be a young man with a nondescript face—so ordinary that one’s gaze would naturally pass over him. Yet beneath that unremarkable exterior, his eyes shone with purpose.","Since nearly all members of the Demon Sealing Grotto had left the headquarters to battle the invading demons, the city was left desolate, allowing the young man to move about unhindered and without concern.","Eventually, they stopped before a massive structure at the heart of the city. Yuan didn’t recognize the building, and unbeknownst to him, it was the Demon Sealing Grotto’s vault, where their most precious treasures were kept."]},{"number":2102,"title":"Chapter 2102: Traitors","paragraphs":["Although the majority of the Demon Sealers had departed to confront the demon invasion outside, the vault was not left unguarded. Seven guards remained stationed before it, each one a True Immortal, their auras sharp and unwavering, ready to act at a moment’s notice.","Yuan silently observed the young man, waiting to see his next move. Yet, the figure remained completely still, as though he had no intention of acting. However, just moments later, Yuan sensed multiple presences rapidly converging on their location.","In the blink of an eye, twenty experts clad in the robes of the Demon Sealing Grotto emerged. Without a word or moment’s hesitation, they launched a coordinated assault on the seven guards, swiftly overwhelming them with ruthless precision.","\"Demon Sealer Jing?! Demon Sealer Yun?! What the hell are you doing?!\"","\"Why are you attacking us?!\"","The guards cried out in disbelief, their voices filled with confusion and betrayal. They recognized the assailants—not as strangers, but as comrades, even close friends. Yet now, those familiar faces bore only cold indifference as they struck with lethal intent.","In fact, even Yuan recognized a few of these individuals, as they were present at the meeting where most of the higher-ups were present.","When questioned by the guards, the traitorous Demon Sealers didn’t utter a single word in response. Instead, they pressed forward with unwavering killing intent.","Although Yuan wanted to remain hidden, he couldn’t let these Demon Sealers die a pointless death, so he revealed his presence to protect them.","\"You! You’re Yan Hara’s disciple!\" The traitors recognized Yuan instantly.","The young man’s gaze sharpened as it fell upon Yuan. A flicker of unease surfaced within him—he hadn’t sensed Yuan’s presence at all until the latter chose to reveal himself. Was this an unfortunate coincidence... or had he been followed all along? That uncertainty gnawed at him.","\"What the hell are you doing here?! You were fighting the demons just moments ago!\" one of the traitors shouted, clearly shaken by Yuan’s sudden appearance.","Yuan smiled calmly and responded, \"I could ask you the same thing. What the hell are you doing here, turning your blades on your own comrades while demons and worshippers tear through the city outside? I sensed something wasn’t right... so I came to see for myself. Looks like my instincts were spot on.\"","He deliberately refrained from mentioning the presence of the young man, careful not to startle his true target.","\"Hmph! You’re just a Golden Immortal! Do you really think you can take on twenty Golden Immortals and True Immortals alone?!\"","\"Perhaps.\"","\"Kill him!\"","In the very next moment, the twenty Demon Sealers launched themselves at Yuan, their attacks fierce and full of killing intent.","Meanwhile, the young man seized the opportunity amidst the chaos, silently slipping past the fray and into the building.","Naturally, Yuan noticed him, as he hadn’t taken his attention off him for even a second. However, he made no move to stop him. Instead, he feigned ignorance and continued exchanging blows with the traitorous Demon Sealers, deliberately holding back his strength to avoid ending the skirmish too quickly.","Once inside the building, the young man made his way directly to the vault, a towering structure layered with intricate and powerful formations. Each one pulsed faintly with energy, silently guarding the priceless treasures within.","But the young man came prepared. Without hesitation, he retrieved several scrolls and talismans from his spatial ring—each one meticulously crafted to counter and disable the specific formations protecting the vault.","Within minutes, he deactivated all of the formations, allowing him to open and enter the vault.","Stepping inside, he was greeted by a grand hall lined with countless treasures—rare artifacts, ancient scrolls, and radiant crystals stacked in meticulous order. Yet, he spared them not a single glance. Without slowing down, he dashed past the wealth of the Demon Sealing Grotto, heading straight toward the far end of the vault with unwavering purpose.","Eventually, he came to a halt before two treasures placed at the very end—both sealed behind layers of intricate formations, far more elaborate than anything else in the vault.","\"Finally...\" he muttered in excitement.","Meanwhile, Yuan continued to gradually thin the traitors’ numbers.","\"Fuck! Why is he so damn powerful?! It doesn’t make any sense!\"","The traitors soon realized that they stood no chance against him.","Yuan then said calmly, \"I’m willing to spare your lives if you tell me why you betrayed the Demon Sealing Grotto. What are you trying to achieve?\"","\"Go fuck yourself!\" one of them spat.","Without a word, Yuan glanced at the man, and in the blink of an eye, unleashed his Supreme Sword Aura. The strike was so swift and precise that none of the others realized what had happened until the man’s head hit the ground with a dull thud.","\"If the next words out of your mouth aren’t related to the truth, I’ll send your head flying. No... perhaps sealing you would be better—letting you spend thousands of years in utter stillness.\"","Before any of the traitors could respond, Yuan released a wave of Demon Sealing Aura—just enough to partially seal the remaining seven.","Terror filled their faces, but none of them dared to speak a single word.","\"Since none of you are willing to speak, why don’t I take a guess?\" Yuan closed his eyes briefly, as though piecing together a puzzle, before continuing, \"You attacked this place right as chaos erupted outside, and real coincidences are rare, especially in this circumstance. Which means this was planned—coordinated. You’re working with the demons and their worshippers out there.\"","\"I doubt the Demon Sealing Grotto would conspire with demons. Which only leaves one conclusion—you’re not really members of the Demon Sealing Grotto but spies from the Demon Sealing Clan... or perhaps another faction entirely.\"","The traitors’ eyes widened with disbelief after hearing Yuan’s speculation.","Yuan narrowed his eyes at them and asked, \"Did Qian Chu send you here?\"","\"Qian Chu? The leader of the Demon Sealing Clan? Ahaha! Yeah, that’s right! We’re working for him! What are you going to do now that you know the truth, huh?!\" one of them suddenly laughed out loud."]},{"number":2103,"title":"Chapter 2103: Demon Sealing Grotto’s Vault","paragraphs":["Although one of the traitors confessed to working for Qian Chu, Yuan didn’t believe it so easily. The admission came too quickly, and the man’s tone felt more like an attempt to shift the blame onto Qian Chu rather than a genuine confession.","\"Oh? Is that so? Then why don’t you tell me a little more about your plans?\" Yuan said as he calmly stepped forward, stopping directly before the half-sealed traitor.","\"T-That’s...\" The man faltered, his eyes darting in panic.","In the next instant, a profound aura erupted from Yuan, and man became fully sealed within seconds.","\"N-NO! SPARE—\"","\"So? Anyone else feel like talking?\" Yuan spoke again after sealing the man, his voice was calm, almost casual. \"If you think silence will spare you... think again. I’ll seal each of you, one by one, until someone decides to speak or there is no one left.\"","He paced slowly in front of the petrified traitors, his footsteps echoing loudly admist the silent atmosphere. They trembled in fear, eyes wide with desperation, but they couldn’t flee, as over half of their bodies already turned to stone.","\"I-I will speak!\" One of them suddenly shouted.","The others instantly snapped their heads to look at him, but none of them tried to stop him.","\"We’re working for the—\"","Before the man could even finish his sentence, he abruptly halted his words. His eyes bulged, and his face turned an unnatural shade of crimson. Then, without warning, his head swelled like a balloon, before violently bursting with a sickening pop, splattering his blood and brain in every direction.","Yuan calmly shielded himself with a thin veil of spiritual energy, letting the mess slide harmlessly off him. The others, however, weren’t so fortunate. With their Dantians sealed and spiritual energy inaccessible, they could only stand there helplessly as the gore splashed across their faces, staining them in silence.","\"I see.\" Yuan muttered afterward. \"Looks like we’ll have to postone the interrogation for later.\"","Without giving the traitors another chance to speak, Yuan sealed them all in an instant before turning away and entering the building to resume his pursuit of the young man.","Inside the vault, the young man was still working to dismantle the final layers of protection surrounding the two treasures. Oddly, the formations guarding them were even more intricate and powerful than those protecting the vault itself.","Eventually, after a tremendous amount of effort, the young man was finally able to remove the final protection on the two treasures, allowing him to acquire them.","However, right as the young man prepared to seize the treasures, a voice resounded in the vault, halting his movements.","\"So you invaded the Demon Sealing Grotto with demons just to get your hands on those two treasures?\"","Despite being discovered, the young man turned around slowly, his movements calm and composed, as though entirely unfazed by his exposure.","His nonchalant gaze stopped at Yuan as he asked, \"What happened to the Demon Sealers outside?\"","\"I killed them all,\" Yuan calmly lied.","\"What a pity. It was quite expensive raising them,\" responded the young man.","\"So, who are you, and what are you trying to achieve with those treasures? You’re clearly working with the demons, so you shouldn’t have any use for them.\"","\"That’s none of your business. Though if you join us, I’ll let you in on the fun. You seem pretty talented, and it’d be a waste to kill you here.\"","\"Kill me? Even though you’re only a Golden Immortal and I’ve just killed twenty of them—including some True Immortals?\" Yuan chuckled.","\"Only a Golden Immortal? Look again.\"","The young man suddenly unleashed his true cultivation, soaring to the peak of the 4th level of God Ascension realm.","\"How scary,\" Yuan said in a sarcastic tone.","He continued, \"If you’re going to invite someone to something, you should, at the very least, let them know what they’re getting into.\"","\"Do you take me for a fool?\" The young man sneered in disdain.","\"What are you afraid of? You are clearly very confident in being able to kill me.\"","\"And you are clearly very confident that you won’t die,\" said the young man.","Yuan shrugged, \"You got me.\"","Yuan advanced toward the young man, yet his gaze bypassed him entirely, drawn instead to the two treasures that hovered silently in the space beyond.","\"The Demon Sealing Scroll and the Demon Sealing Talisman, two of the three demon sealing treasures once owned by the Divine Paragon. Do you even have the capability to wield them?\"","The two treasures the young man was attempting to steal were none other than the Demon Sealing Scroll and the Demon Sealing Talisman—artifacts the Demon Sealing Grotto had obtained from the Demon Sealing Clan. The third treasure, the Demon Sealing Flag, remained in Qian Chu’s possession.","\"Unless you plan to use them against the demons outside, don’t even think about taking them,\" Yuan said, halting a few meters away.","The young man sneered and seized both treasures without hesitation.","\"Are you going to stop me? I’d love to see you try,\" he said with a mocking laugh.","\"I don’t even need to lay a finger on you,\" Yuan said with a shake of his head.","As he released a sliver of his Demon Sealing Aura, the two treasures in the young man’s grasp began to tremble, resonating as if responding to a familiar master.","\"What?!\" The young man recoiled in shock as the treasures trembled violently, causing him to release them without thinking.","Freed from his grasp, the two artifacts shot through the air and landed squarely in Yuan’s hands.","\"W-Who the hell are you?!\" the young man roared, demanding an answer.","\"Just an ordinary Elite Demon Sealer,\" Yuan replied calmly.","\"Don’t give me that crap!\" the young man snarled, then lunged forward with outstretched, claw-like hands, aiming straight for the treasures in Yuan’s grasp in a desperate attempt to reclaim them.","\"Are you Qian Chu?\" Yuan asked suddenly, bringing the young man’s movements to an abrupt halt."]},{"number":2104,"title":"Chapter 2104: Qian Chu","paragraphs":["After hearing Yuan utter the name ’Qian Chu’, the young man stopped moving, even standing up straight to face Yuan.","\"Qian Chu, you say? What makes you think I am him?\" the young man questioned.","\"I was just trying my luck. If you’re not Qian Chu, who are you? I’ll give you one of the demon sealing treasures if you tell me.\"","\"What kind of nonsense is that? Do you really expect me to believe you?\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"No, but even if I give you the demon sealing treasure, you won’t be able to control it, and I will eventually reclaim it.\"","\"Enough of this nonsense! Hand over the demon sealing treasures! This is my last warning!\" the young man shouted.","\"I refuse.\"","The moment Yuan declined, the young man exploded with killing intent and pounced at him again.","\"Sorry, but I don’t have the time to play with you, as there are demons waiting for me outside. I don’t know who you are, but you’re clearly not on our side.\"","Yuan stopped caring about the young man’s identity and began fighting him seriously, even using Celestial Qi with Yu Ning’s assistance.","’How the hell is he using Celestial Qi as a Golden Immortal?!’ the young man cried inwardly.","He initially thought Yuan was also hiding his cultivation, but as they continued fighting, he was convinced that Yuan was only a Golden Immortal.","\"Looks like I will need more than just Celestial Qi to kill you, huh?\" Yuan suddenly muttered.","Then, his body suddenly surged with a chaotic energy that resembled demonic energy, greatly shocking the young man.","\"You were a demon this whole time?!\" the young man exclaimed as he distanced himself from Yuan, mistaking his chaotic essence as demonic energy.","\"Who knows?\" Yuan calmly shrugged.","\"But let’s say that I am a demon. What are you going to do about it?\"","The young man clenched his teeth, his eyes flickering with hesitation. After a brief silence, he reached into his spatial ring and retrieved a familiar treasure.","From his spatial ring, the young man drew a red flag affixed to a black rod. Then, he pointed it at Yuan and shouted, \"Seal!\"","The treasure—none other than the Demon Sealing Flag, the third of the Demon Sealing Treasures—shot toward Yuan, its crimson fabric unfurling mid-air before coiling tightly around him.","\"So, you were Qian Chu all along,\" Yuan said calmly, even as the flag tightened its grip around him.","Now that his identity had been exposed, the young man shed his disguise, revealing his true appearance, and Yuan instantly recognized him as Qian Chu.","\"I heard you left the Demon Sealing Clan for some mysterious business. Who would’ve thought that business was stealing from the Demon Sealing Grotto... while working for the demons?\"","\"Working for the demons? You’re wrong.\" Qian Chu said.","\"Oh? Then enlighten me.\"","\"I am not working for the demons. They are working for me,\" QIan Chu calmly revealed.","Yuan narrowed his eyes and continued, \"One of the traitors died the moment he tried to reveal the truth to me. But another admitted working for you, and nothing happened. Why?\"","Qian Chu chuckled. \"Simple. They think they’re serving the demons—when in truth, they’re serving me.\"","\"I see... so they don’t realize you’re the true mastermind,\" Yuan muttered.","\"You’ve asked enough questions. Now it’s my turn,\" Qian Chu said coldly. \"Why is a demon like you helping the Demon Sealing Grotto? I’ve never heard of a demon working with Demon Sealers.\"","Since Qian Chu had misunderstood the situation, Yuan chose to play along.","\"So humans can work with demons, but demons can’t do the same?\" he replied with a faint smirk. \"I have my own reasons.\"","\"How can a demon like you wield Demon Sealing Aura?\" Qian Chu continued to ask.","\"I am also trying to figure that out since I was suddenly able to use it one day.\"","\"...\"","Qian Chu narrowed his eyes at Yuan.","\"Are you really a demon?\" he asked, suspicion still lingering in his voice.","Although Chaotic Essence bore a strong resemblance to demonic energy, it wasn’t the same. But having never encountered Chaotic Essence before, Qian Chu couldn’t discern the difference.","Of course, he could tell that Yuan’s energy was different from ordinary demonic energy—but he chalked it up to Yuan being a special kind of demon, one capable of wielding Demon Sealing Aura.","\"Maybe I am. Maybe I am not.\" Yuan responded after a moment of silence.","\"...\"","After another moment of silence, Qian Chu finally spoke, \"Why don’t you work for me instead? I’ll help you achieve whatever goal you have.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"My goal is to unseal the Demon Realm and take revenge against those who tossed me out like trash.\"","Qian Chu didn’t appear to be surprised in the slightest and responded with a smile, \"You and I have a similar purpose. I am already preparing to unseal the Demon Realm. Serve me, and I will make sure you return to the Demon Realm. Not only that, but I can even help you improve your power as a demon.\"","Yuan then said, \"So, you’re the one behind that Demon Emperor outside, huh?\"","Qian Chu silently nodded.","\"Very well. In that case, let’s work together.\" Yuan said after pretending to ponder for a moment.","\"You won’t regret it.\"","Qian Chu released him the very next moment.","\"So what do you want me to do?\" Yuan then asked.","\"For starters, hand over the demon sealing treasures to me.\"","\"Sure.\" Yuan casually handed the Demon Sealing Scroll and the Demon Sealing Talisman to Qian Chu.","With a satisfied look on his face, Qian Chu continued, \"I want you to continue assisting the Demon Sealers in secret.\"","He then handed Yuan a black jade slip and said, \"Come find me at this location in twenty years. You can do whatever in the meantime. If you dare to betray me, you’ll regret it.\"","\"Will you return to the Demon Sealing Clan after this?\" Yuan asked him.","\"We’ll see.\" Qian Chu said before leaving the vault."]},{"number":2105,"title":"Chapter 2105: Stolen Treasures","paragraphs":["Once Qian Chu left the vault, Feng Yuxiang questioned Yuan’s decision to let him go so easily.","\"Young Master, are you really going to let him go that easily?\" she asked, her voice laced with worry. \"You even handed over two of your treasures. What if he goes on a rampage? Even if he doesn’t, he’ll surely stir chaos with the demons under his command.\"","\"I don’t have the strength to kill Qian Chu right now,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"And even if I did, it wouldn’t stop the demons. In fact, they are likely to go on a rampage without someone to command them.\"","He then glanced at his hands before continuing, \"As for the two Demon Sealing Treasures... I’ve already re-established our bond. He won’t be able to use them, no matter what he tries. The same goes for the Demon Sealing Flag. That said, I’ve allowed him limited control—for now—so he won’t immediately suspect anything. Not only that, but they serve as a tracking device, allowing me to track his movements.\"","\"I see...\" Feng Yuxiang mumbled.","\"The Demon Realm... looks like I won’t have to open the seal myself, which will save me a lot of headaches.\"","\"That man mentioned having a similar goal as you... Do you know what that is about?\" Yu Ning asked.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Yes, I do. I learned a lot from our encounter, including his true identity.\"","\"His true identity? So he’s a demon in disguise?\"","\"No, he’s not a demon, but he’s no human, either. It’s a bit complicated. You’ll understand once I return to the Demon Realm.\"","\"Okay.\"","Some time later, Yuan emerged from the vault and returned to the battlefield, where Yan Hara and the Demon Sealing Grotto were still locked in combat with the demons.","At first glance, the Demon Sealers appeared to have the upper hand—but only marginally, with heavy casualties scattered across the field.","\"Sorry for the delay. I’m back.\" Yuan said to Yan Hara using voice transmission.","\"Thank the lord!\" she exclaimed in excitement.","However, just as Yuan prepared to unleash his Demon Sealing Aura, the demons halted their movements.","The next moment, they turned around and began fleeing in every direction, including the Demon Worshippers.","\"T-The demons are retreating! Don’t let them escape!\" Zhou Yanfei shouted upon seeing the fleeing enemy.","The Demon Sealers gave chase without hesitation, but fatigue weighed heavily on them after the battle, while the demons, fueled by endless spiritual energy, moved with undiminished strength.","Eventually, the Demon Sealers halted their pursuit, unwilling to risk venturing too far in case more demons were lying in wait. Besides, they had already captured numerous Demon Worshippers, and among them, a black-masked worshipper.","Moreover, Zhou Yanfei had received news that someone had broken into their vault. Hearing this, he instantly returned to the city with several of their top Demon Sealers.","\"Yan Hara, come with me! We still have a lot to talk about!\" Zhou Yanfei didn’t forget to remind her of their business before leaving.","Although reluctant, Yan Hara followed them back to the city. Of course, Yuan was with them.","\"Some bastard broke into our vault while we were distracted by the invasion!\" Zhou Yanfei revealed to Yan Hara as they traveled.","\"What?\" Yan Hara’s eyes widened upon hearing this surprising information.","\"The invasion had only lasted several hours. How did someone manage to break into the vault in such little time?\" she asked.","\"We don’t know, but we’ll definitely catch that bastard!\"","\"What was stolen?\" she asked.","\"...\"","Zhou Yanfei remained silent—not out of reluctance, but uncertainty.","In truth, he didn’t know. The guards had contacted him the moment they discovered the vault had been opened, and none of them had dared to step inside without his presence.","\"We’ll find out soon enough,\" he said a moment later.","However, just as they reached their destination, Yuan spoke, \"I know what was stolen.\"","\"What?!\" Zhou Yanfei and the others halted their movements to look at him.","\"Why in heaven’s name would you know that unless you entered the vault?!\"","\"Because I was inside the vault,\" Yuan calmly admitted.","\"You better have a damn good explanation—\" Zhou Yanfei’s body surged with killing intent.","\"And you better step back!\" Yan Hara immediately stepped in front of Zhou Yanfei, blocking his path.","\"If you want any information about the Divine Paragon’s legacy, you’d better not lay a finger on him! At least let him finish speaking!\"","Zhou Yanfei gritted his teeth, fists clenched with suppressed fury. After a tense moment, he slowly relaxed his grip and withdrew his killing intent—though not entirely.","\"I noticed someone with a hidden presence sneaking into the city, so I followed him. During my chase, I noticed the guards being attacked by members of the Demon Sealing Grotto—\"","\"Fucking bullshit!\" Zhou Yanfei interrupted with a booming voice, \"Do you really expect me to believe—\"","\"It’s true.\"","One of the guards suddenly stepped forward, interrupting Zhou Yanfei.","\"We were attacked by Demon Sealer Jing, Demon Sealer Yun, as well as several other high-ranking members. If it weren’t for this savior, we would’ve died today.\"","Before Zhou Yanfei could speak, another guard stepped forward and said, \"I vouch for his words.\"","\"Me, too.\"","\"I will also vouch for him.\"","All of the guards saved by Yuan stepped forward to vouch for him.","\"That’s...\" Zhou Yanfei was speechless.","Then, Yuan pointed at the sealed figures standing not too far away and said, \"I even sealed them so you can interrogate them later. No need to thank me.\"","\"What was stolen from our vault?\" Zhou Yanfei asked in an anxious voice.","Yuan shrugged and said, \"I don’t know, but it was located at the very end of the vault—\"","\"No! It can’t be!\" Zhou Yanfei and the other Demon Sealers reacted with alarm, interrupting Yuan before he could even finish his sentence.","Without another word, they bolted into the vault. Inside, they passed by the treasures near the entrance without so much as a glance, ignoring even the ones further in—until they reached the far end of the room, where two display pedestals now stood empty.","Upon confirming their worst nightmare, Zhou Yanfei and the other Demon Sealers dropped to their knees, their faces pale with shock and despair."]},{"number":2106,"title":"Chapter 2106: Stolen Treasures(2)","paragraphs":["Seeing Zhou Yanfei and the other Demon Sealers kneeling on the floor, their faces twisted in grief as if they had just witnessed the slaughter of their entire families, Yuan spoke, \"By the time I defeated the traitors and reached the vault... the treasures were already gone. I’m sorry.\"","\"...\"","None of the Demon Sealers responded.","\"Though I did encounter the thief, who was on his way out. He was at the fourth level of God Ascension, so there was nothing I could’ve done to stop him,\" Yuan added.","Upon hearing this, Zhou Yanfei slowly turned to face Yuan, his eyes narrowing sharply.","\"You encountered the thief... and survived? No, something’s not right. You don’t even look injured, not in the slightest. It’s almost as if he let you go without even trying to kill you.\"","He paused, voice hardening.","\"No thief in their right mind would go through all that trouble to infiltrate our vault... only to leave an eyewitness behind.\"","\"That’s—\"","Before Yuan could say another word, Zhou Yanfei suddenly lunged from his kneeling position, his hand shooting toward Yuan’s throat, overflowing with uncontrolled killing intent.","\"You—!\"","His actions were too sudden, and Yan Hara failed to react in time. By the time she even realized what was happening, Zhou Yanfei’s fingers were already at Yuan’s neck.","As for Yuan, he stood still, almost as if he also failed to react. However, his eyes were following Zhou Yanfei’s movements perfectly. It wasn’t that he couldn’t react. He simply didn’t move on purpose so Zhou Yanfei could hit him.","In the very next instant, Zhou Yanfei’s hand reached Yuan’s neck, fingers tightening as if to rip his throat out. But just as he made contact, his movements froze.","However, it wasn’t because Zhou Yanfei had a change of heart, or that he’d suddenly snapped out of his subconscious assault.","\"What in heaven’s name...?\" Zhou Yanfei muttered, staring at his hands frozen around Yuan’s neck, eyes wide with disbelief and confusion.","Despite pouring nearly all of his strength into the strike, he couldn’t harm Yuan in the slightest. In fact, it felt as if his fingers had slammed into solid diamond.","Zhou Yanfei was currently at the third level of God Ascension, and even though he didn’t use Celestial Qi in his strike, it should’ve been more than enough to slaughter a Golden Immortal like Yuan with extreme ease.","Yet, he couldn’t even damage the skin on Yuan’s body, much less kill him.","\"Haa...\" Yuan released a soft sigh before speaking, \"You should really let people finish their sentences.\"","\"I—\"","\"You old bastard! What do you think you’re doing?!\" Yan Hara kicked Zhou Yanfei in the face right as he opened his mouth, sending him flying into the empty treasure pedestal.","\"Master Zhou!\"","\"Leader!\"","The Demon Sealers exclaimed in shock after seeing their leader sent flying.","\"I-I’m okay...\"","Since Yan Hara only used her natural strength, Zhou Yanfei only sustained minimal injuries.","\"Anyway, as I was going to say, while the thief tried to kill me, he simply didn’t have the capability, and not wanting to risk being captured, he fled after failing to kill me for a few minutes,\" Yuan said a moment later.","\"What the hell is your body made of?\" Zhou Yanfei asked after a long moment of silence.","\"The same things as most normal people. Flesh and bone.\"","\"An ordinary person wouldn’t be able to escape unscathed after being attacked by a God Ascension cultivator while only being an Immortal.\"","Yuan casually shrugged.","Yan Hara then spoke, \"What the hell was even stolen for you to have acted like that?\"","Zhou Yanfei’s face darkened after being reminded of the stolen treasures, and with great difficulty, responded, \"The Demon Sealing Scroll and the Demon Sealing Talisman.\"","\"WHAT?!\" Yan Hara screamed, her voice so sharp it nearly pierced their eardrums upon hearing the names of the stolen treasures.","\"The Demon Sealing Scroll and the Demon Sealing Talisman? Aren’t those the Divine Paragon’s treasures?\" Yuan asked, pretending to be ignorant.","\"Precisely,\" confirmed Zhou Yanfei.","Snapping out of her daze, Yan Hara stormed over to Zhou Yanfei, seized him by the collar, and began shaking him violently.","\"Precisely, my ass!\" she shouted. \"How the hell could you let the Divine Paragon’s treasures be stolen?!\"","Zhou Yanfei slapped her hands off him and shouted back, \"Do you think I want them to be stolen?! We locked them in formations that were even stronger than the ones protecting the entire vault!\"","\"That doesn’t say much when your vault was cracked this easily!\"","\"Let’s stop this pointless argument and try to figure out a solution,\" one of the Demon Sealers suddenly said.","He turned to look at Yuan and asked, \"Do you have a description of the thief? Any information about him is fine.\"","Yuan immediately recalled all of the thief’s features, everything from his ordinary facial features to his foot size.","\"What about his techniques? Did you notice anything when he tried to kill you?\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"No, he didn’t use any techniques on me and tried to kill me with brute force.\"","\"I understand. Since it’s essentially impossible to find him with this little information, we’ll have to interrogate the Demon Worshippers we captured, as well as the traitors.\"","\"Master Zhou, please get yourself together. Two of the Divine Paragon’s treasures were stolen. We don’t have the time or energy to waste on bickering.\"","Surprisingly, the Demon Sealers lectured him.","Even more surprisingly, Zhou Yanfei wasn’t offended by it and even thanked them.","\"You’re right. My apologies—I acted in a manner unworthy of my position.\"","Once he had regained his composure, Zhou Yanfei turned to Yan Hara and said, \"I will take full responsibility for this incident. An investigation will begin immediately. I hope you’ll consider staying a while longer, but if you choose to leave now, I won’t stop you.\"","Yan Hara looked at Yuan, who nodded and said, \"I have a few months.\"","\"Then I will also stay,\" Yan Hara said afterward."]},{"number":2107,"title":"Chapter 2107: Stolen Treasures(3)","paragraphs":["\"It won’t take a few months. I will contact you within a week or two,\" said Zhou Yanfei.","He turned to look at a certain Demon Sealer and said to her, \"Bring them to our best guest quarters.\"","Thus, Yuan and Yan Hara were brought out of the vault and to their guest houses.","Once they were alone, Yuan said, \"I have something to tell you. Come with me.\"","Yan Hara nodded her head and quietly followed him to his house.","\"Yu Ning, can you put a sound barrier around us to prevent eavesdropping?\" Yuan asked her upon entering the living room.","\"Sure.\"","Yu Ning took control of Yuan’s body for a brief moment to create the formation.","\"A sound barrier...?\" Yan Hara stared at him with raised eyebrows.","Sometime later, Yuan sat down on a chair and gestured for Yan Hara to do the same.","\"Is this about how we’re going to reveal the Divine Paragon’s—your legacy?\" Yan Hara asked as she took a seat directly in front of him.","\"No, this is about the thief who stole the demon sealing treasures. I will get straight to the point. The treasures weren’t stolen—at least not technically.\"","\"What?\" Yan Hara wore a confused expression on her face.","\"I could’ve prevented the treasures from being stolen, but I willingly gave them to the thief.\"","\"You what?!\" Yan Hara exclaimed in shock.","Yuan continued, \"And that thief was actually Qian Chu.\"","\"QIAN CHU?!\" Yan Hara stood from her seat, her eyes and mouth wide with disbelief.","\"That’s impossible!\" she declared a second later.","\"Impossible? Why would you say that?\" Yuan asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"Because we’ve had people monitoring Qian Chu ever since he left on that so-called business!\" Yan Hara replied firmly. \"Right now, he’s supposed to be in the Ninth Heaven—and he hasn’t left that place in years. If he had, I would’ve been informed immediately!\"","\"There are countless ways to slip past surveillance, especially if he knows he’s being watched,\" Yuan said, shaking his head.","\"Then why are you so certain it was Qian Chu?\" Yan Hara asked. \"What if someone is trying to frame him?\"","\"Because he had the Demon Sealing Flag with him,\" Yuan replied.","Yan Hara drew in a sharp breath upon hearing those words.","\"Of course, it’s not irrefutable evidence,\" Yuan continued, \"but I’m certain that it was Qian Chu.\"","\"If you say so...\" Yan Hara muttered after a brief silence. \"But why would you give him the Demon Sealing Treasures in the first place?\"","\"Two reasons,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"First, I can use them to track his movements. Second, it gives him the illusion that he’s making progress toward his goal. I still don’t know exactly why he needs the treasures, but it doesn’t matter. He can’t use them properly. I’ve already reestablished full control the moment I touched them.\"","\"Then do you know his goal?\" Yan Hara then asked.","Yuan nodded and revealed, \"He’s trying to break the seal on the Demon Realm.\"","\"...\"","Yan Hara wanted to be shocked—expected to be—but for some reason, the words didn’t surprise her at all. It was as if, deep down, she had already suspected it.","\"So, he’s a demon disguised as a human? Why does he know Demon Sealing Aura? I thought demons couldn’t use it.\" Yan Hara asked a moment later.","\"No, he’s not a demon, but he’s not a human either.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"I won’t explain it now since I want you to see it for yourself.\"","\"I don’t understand.\"","Yuan looked into her eyes and said calmly, \"I intend to bring you with me when I go to the Demon Realm.\"","\"M-Me?! To the Demon Realm?!\" Yan Hara exclaimed, stumbling backward in shock. She collided with the chair behind her and toppled over, landing hard on the floor.","Yan Hara quickly got back up, but she didn’t fully stand on her feet.","\"You must be messing with me... Why would you bring me to such a dangerous place that’s crawling with demons? I’m not you... I won’t last a minute in there!\" she said with teary eyes.","\"If you’re going to be the leader of the Demon Sealing Clan in the future, I want you to know everything about demons—including how they come into existence and the truth,\" Yuan spoke with a solemn expression.","\"You were serious about making me the leader? What about you? The others won’t accept me once they learn that the Divine Paragon has returned.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"The Divine Paragon? He died in the Demon Era.\"","\"Even if you say that...\" Yan Hara sighed.","\"I have much more important things to do than managing the Demon Sealing Clan. I have already decided to make you my successor, so don’t try to convince me.\"","Yan Hara sighed again, this time with more force.","\"I understand... So, what are we going to do about Qian Chu?\"","\"Let me tell you the full story first.\"","Yuan then recounted everything that had transpired between him and Qian Chu—including how Qian Chu had mistaken him for a demon, and how he had used that misunderstanding and the demon sealing treasures to gain Qian Chu’s trust and begin working alongside him.","\"I’ll continue monitoring Qian Chu and let you know if anything unusual happens. In the meantime, keep watching him on your end as well, just enough so he doesn’t grow suspicious.\"","Yan Hara nodded.","\"As for the Demon Realm... I’ll let Qian Chu open it for me.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Now, let’s discuss how we’re going to present the Divine Paragon’s legacy in a way that brings the Demon Sealing Grotto to our side.\"","Meanwhile, the Demon Sealing Grotto turned its attention to handling the aftermath of the invasion. After confirming that nothing else had been stolen from the vault aside from the two Demon Sealing Treasures, they began interrogating the captured traitors and Demon Worshippers. Having been warned by Yuan that the traitors were cursed to die if they revealed anything, the Demon Sealers entered the interrogation fully prepared.","As for the city, since only the outer city had been destroyed, its restoration was postponed until the more pressing matters were addressed."]},{"number":2108,"title":"Chapter 2108: Selfish","paragraphs":["Chapter 2108: Selfish","Armed with the knowledge that the traitors were cursed, the Demon Sealing Grotto wasted no time in forcefully extracting their memories to uncover the truth—even if it meant crippling or killing them in the process.","However, even after forcefully extracting their memories, the Demon Sealing Grotto found themselves empty-handed. The traitors had been afflicted with two powerful curses, one that prevented them from speaking the truth and another that blocked any attempt to delve into their memories.","The moment the Demon Sealing Grotto tried to extract their memories, their Dantian were forcefully destroyed, turning them into powerful bombs. Unable to make further progress, the Demon Sealing Grotto decided to suspend the traitors’ interrogation until a method to bypass the curses could be found. Ordinarily, this would require the assistance of a curse expert.","However, experts in curses are exceedingly rare. Few dare to tread such a dangerous path, one notorious for its high mortality rate and unforgiving nature.","As for the Demon Worshippers, the Demon Sealing Grotto managed to uncover some results. As they had suspected, the red-masked individuals were innocent people who had been forcibly made to consume demon blood. The corrupting influence weakened their mental state, making it far easier for the true Demon Worshippers to seize control of their minds.","Unfortunately, there was no known cure for those who had succumbed to demon blood. Its corrupting influence often drove victims to madness, making them dangerously unstable and violently aggressive.","Thus, the Demon Sealing Grotto made the painful decision to execute all of them—a final act of mercy for those beyond saving.","As for the black-masked Demon Worshipper they had captured, he was subjected to relentless torture and interrogation. Until then, the Demon Sealing Grotto had no lead on the thief who stole their treasures other than the information given to them by Yuan.","After two whole weeks, Zhou Yanfei approached Yan Hara with information on their progress of the situation.","“If handling this alone is too much, why not request help from the Demon Sealing Clan?” Yan Hara suggested.","“Ask the Demon Sealing Clan for help?” Zhou Yanfei scoffed, his tone laced with disdain. “What a joke. What makes you think they can do anything? They’re barely holding themselves together! What could they possibly offer us?”","“Unlike the Demon Sealing Grotto, which specializes solely in Demon Sealers, the Demon Sealing Clan is far more versatile,” Yan Hara replied. “While we may currently fall short in demon sealing expertise, our strength lies in broader experience beyond that field.”","“Even if that’s true, have you forgotten we’re at war?” Zhou Yanfei snapped. “You want me to ask my enemy for help? That’s just begging to be stabbed in the back—just like they did during the Supreme Demon Sealer Qualifications!”","Yan Hara shook her head and sighed, “How many times do we have to have this conversation? You’re at war with Qian Chu and his faction, not the rest of the Demon Sealing Clan. Also, if I were you, I’d be more worried about being backstabbed by my own people. What are you going to do if there are more traitors within the Demon Sealing Grotto?”","Zhou Yanfei gritted his teeth and clenched his fists in frustration, the reminder of possibly more traitors within the Demon Sealing Grotto weighing heavily on him.","After a moment of heavy silence, he finally spoke.","“The Demon Sealing Grotto is already taking steps to address the possibility of more traitors. Since every exposed traitor was marked with curses, we can simply check everyone for them.”","Yan Hara raised an eyebrow at his solution and said, “That’s easier said than done.”","“That’s why we’re going to ask the Master of Curses for his assistance. He’s probably the only expert in the world who can deal with this level of curses. We also can’t touch the traitors we already caught since we are powerless against their curses.”","Yuan then spoke, “Regarding that... I have a way of dealing with the curses.”","“You do?!” Zhou Yanfei looked at him with wide eyes filled with disbelief.","Yuan confirmed, “I can remove their curses.”","“Then we must immediately—”","“That can wait. Let’s talk about the reason you’re here today first.”","“...”","Zhou Yanfei fell silent, but he didn’t disagree.","“Alright. Then let’s talk about the Divine Paragon’s legacy.”","He turned to face Yan Hara with a solemn expression and continued, “Since there may still be traitors within the Demon Sealing Grotto, only I will be present in this conversation, so you don’t have to worry about revealing information to the enemy.”","“I appreciate your consideration,” Yan Hara said in a somewhat sarcastic tone.","The room fell silent once more before Zhou Yanfei broke the stillness, his voice heavy with doubt.","“Did you truly obtain the Divine Paragon’s legacy? Or is this just some elaborate trick?”","“Why don’t you tell me?” Yan Hara replied calmly.","Without another word, she began to display the Divine Paragon’s demon sealing techniques one after another, each one unmistakable. They were techniques well-documented in their records, yet lost to history ever since the Divine Paragon’s disappearance.","“Demon Sealing Zone... Swords of Eternal Torment...” Zhou Yanfei fell to his knees after witnessing the demon sealing techniques one after another, his eyes and mouth agape with shock and disbelief.","“H-How?! How did you obtain the Divine Paragon’s legacy?!” he cried, crawling toward her on his knees, his voice filled with desperation as he begged for an answer.","“Sorry, but I cannot disclose that information.” Yan Hara responded in an adamant tone.","“Do you really intend to keep these techniques all to yourself?!” Zhou Yanfei roared, rising to his feet in anger. “How can you be so selfish, especially now, with everything at stake and the demons on the verge of returning?!”","“If you shared those techniques with everyone, we wouldn’t have to fear the demons at all! We could fight back without hesitation!” Zhou Yanfei shouted, his voice trembling with emotion.","“Do you think you can play the Divine Paragon and use his techniques to control us? This is bigger than you—far bigger!”"]},{"number":2109,"title":"Chapter 2109: Divine Paragon’s Will","paragraphs":["\"Selfish?\" Yan Hara narrowed her eyes at Zhou Yanfei, looking annoyed.","Then, she spoke loudly, \"Zhou Yanfei, you old fart! When the hell are you ever going to let people finish speaking before you jump to conclusions?! I cannot even count how many times you’ve done this already!\"","\"The Divine Paragon taught everyone how to use Demon Sealing Aura and shared some of his demon sealing techniques so humanity could stand against the demons. But there were a few he deliberately chose not to share.\"","She took a step forward, her gaze sharp.","\"Are you calling the Divine Paragon selfish for that?!\"","\"T-That’s...\" Zhou Yanfei took a step back, taken aback by her response.","\"Do you know why he chose not to share those techniques?!\" Yan Hara took another step forward as she questioned him.","Zhou Yanfei also took another step back, and he silently shook his head in response to her question.","\"That’s because these techniques are not something everyone can use! These techniques are incredibly complex and difficult to control, and a single mistake could seal the user instead!\" Yan Hara revealed.","\"Did you know I learned these techniques years ago? And yet, I’ve only just begun to use them properly.\" She clenched her fists, voice rising. \"Even now, I can barely tap into their true potential, and I’ve personally received the Divine Paragon’s guidance through his legacy!\"","\"If I shared these techniques without restraint, it would do more harm than good. Moreover, these techniques are so powerful that they can affect humans and not just demons, and you want me to share it with everyone? You must be out of your mind!\"","Zhou Yanfei was left speechless, but Yan Hara wasn’t done speaking.","\"Naturally, I do not intend to keep these techniques to myself. However, I will only pass them on to those I deem responsible and trustworthy. It doesn’t take more than a few capable individuals with these techniques to deal with any amount of demons—that’s just how powerful they are.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Yanfei lowered his head and sighed, \"I have spoken too soon and offended you. I apologize.\"","Yan Hara added firmly, \"And if you think I’ll hand these techniques over to the Demon Sealing Grotto while you still treat the Demon Sealing Clan as your enemy, you can forget it. I intend to lead the Demon Sealing Clan one day as the Divine Paragon’s successor, and I won’t share such valuable techniques with those who stand against us.\"","\"What...?\" Zhou Yanfei stared at her in stunned disbelief.","But it wasn’t her declaration to one day lead the Demon Sealing Clan that left him speechless—it was her claim to be the Divine Paragon’s successor that truly shook him.","\"Leading the Demon Sealing Clan and being the Divine Paragon’s successor are two entirely different things,\" Zhou Yanfei said, a slight frown creasing his brow. \"You might be able to force your way onto the throne, but you’ll never be recognized as a true successor.\"","Yan Hara sneered, \"Do you think I only received the Divine Paragon’s techniques through his legacy?\"","\"What do you mean...?\" Zhou Yanfei asked for clarification.","Without saying another word, Yan Hara retrieved a peculiar device from her spatial ring and placed it gently on the floor. The moment she infused it with her spiritual energy, a projection shimmered to life—a figure slowly materializing before them in a ghostly, ethereal form.","Zhou Yanfei instantly recognized this figure and fell to his knees.","\"D-Divine Paragon!\"","The figure was none other than Tian Chenyu, the Divine Paragon.","After a brief moment of silence, the figure began to speak.","\"My name is Tian Chenyu—though most of you may know me as the Divine Paragon, or the Bane of Demons,\" he said, his voice calm and resolute. \"I understand that my disappearance may have raised many questions, but that Chapter belongs to the past. My purpose ended with the defeat of the Demon Clan.\"","\"However, I have chosen to leave my legacy behind,\" Tian Chenyu continued. \"Whoever is the first to find it shall inherit all of my knowledge and techniques—and bear the title of my successor.\"","\"If the day comes when the demons return and I am no longer here, place your trust in my successor. They will be the one to carry on my will.\"","Of course, this entire display had been orchestrated by Yuan and Yan Hara just days earlier. All it took was a carefully crafted recording of Yuan posing as Tian Chenyu.","Given that such projection technology had existed since the Demonic Era, it would be nearly impossible to prove the recording was fabricated.","Moreover, the fact that Yan Hara genuinely knew the Divine Paragon’s techniques only added to the illusion, making the deception all the more convincing.","That said, the recording wasn’t entirely a lie. After all, Yuan truly was the Divine Paragon, and he had genuinely chosen Yan Hara as his successor. The only issue was convincing others without revealing his true identity.","Yan Hara retrieved the recording device and said, \"This was left behind where I discovered the Divine Paragon’s legacy. If you still don’t believe me, I have more evidence.\"","Yuan had given Yan Hara his Demon Sealing Ring and a few more cards to play just in case Zhou Yanfei remained skeptical.","Fortunately, they didn’t need to reveal these cards since Zhou Yanfei believed them without any questions.","\"This Junior Demon Sealer greets the Divine Paragon’s successor,\" Zhou Yanfei said as he bowed respectfully, his demeanor shifting completely.","Yan Hara then spoke, her voice firm yet composed.","\"As I said, I intend to challenge Qian Chu and lead the Demon Sealing Clan. While it may be too much to ask for the Demon Sealing Grotto’s full support... Can I at least count on you, Zhou Yanfei?\"","Zhou Yanfei nodded and said, \"Of course, but it won’t just be my support. I will ensure the entire Demon Sealing Grotto supports you—after we clean out all of the traitors, of course.\"","Yan Hara nodded with a satisfied smile, \"Then I’ll count on you.\""]},{"number":2110,"title":"Chapter 2110: Training Yan Hara","paragraphs":["\"Now that we no longer have to worry about the Demon Sealing Grotto becoming our enemy, it’s time to clean up the traitors,\" said Yan Hara as she turned to look at Yuan.","He calmly nodded and said, \"Bring me to the traitors. I’ll remove their curses.\"","\"Of course.\"","Zhou Yanfei proceeded to guide them to where the traitors were being held. Unlike Yuan, nobody in the Demon Sealing Grotto was powerful enough to seal Demon Sealers at their level, so they had to restrict them using other methods, such as treasures and formations.","The traitors were each confined to their own cells within a dungeon-like prison deep underground. The hallways were dimly lit, casting long shadows across the damp stone walls, while the cells themselves were shrouded in complete darkness.","As for the prisoners, each one was bound in black chains that sealed their spiritual energy, rendering them as powerless as ordinary mortals. Their mouths were also forced open and restrained, ensuring they couldn’t even bite their tongues to commit suicide.","With no strength to resist and no means to end their lives, they were left completely at the mercy of their captors.","\"Take as long as you need with them,\" said Zhou Yanfei.","\"I will only need a moment to deal with their curses.\"","Yuan entered one of the cells and retrieved the Sacred Chalice of Purification before feeding it a drop of the traitor’s blood. However, since the treasure was already working fulltime trying to cleanse Yuan’s curse, it took much longer than usual to deal with the traitor’s curse.","\"Sorry, but this will actually take longer than I anticipated,\" he said shortly after realizing this.","\"I understand.\"","Time passed swiftly, and after several days, Yuan finally managed to cleanse the curses that prevented the traitors from speaking.","\"Alright, you can resume his interrogation. I’ll continue to work on the others,\" said Yuan as he made his way to the next cell.","Thus, Yuan continued to cleanse the seals on the traitors while the Demon Sealing Grotto resumed their interrogation.","\"Thank you for your assistance. We should be done with our investigation in a few weeks,\" said Zhou Yanfei.","Yuan then said, \"I don’t really care about the results, so you can forward them to Yan Hara once you’re done.\"","\"Are you leaving already?\" Yan Hara asked.","\"No, I still have a few months, and I am going to use that time to help you improve your Demon Sealing Aura,\" he said.","Zhou Yanfei raised an eyebrow after hearing Yuan’s words. He couldn’t fathom how anyone could teach the Divine Paragon’s successor.","’Just who the hell is this guy? For Yan Hara to respect him so much, he must have an impressive background.’","However, Zhou Yanfei decided not to question it.","\"You can use my private training ground,\" he said to them a moment later.","Thus, Yuan began training Yan Hara’s Demon Sealing Aura, as well as the Divine Paragon’s techniques.","\"Tell me,\" Yuan said as he stood with Yan Hara in the center of the training grounds, \"what must a Demon Sealer do to strengthen their Demon Sealing Aura?\"","\"There are two main methods,\" Yan Hara replied. \"First, through constant use. Second, by enhancing one’s Soul Strength...\"","\"That can be applied to almost everything. There is one way to quickly strengthen your Demon Sealing Aura, and that is through emotions.\"","\"Emotions...?\"","Yuan nodded and added, \"Your anger, or more precisely, your hatred toward demons. That’s how Demon Sealing Aura was born in the first place.\"","He paused briefly, his gaze distant.","\"It’s one of the main reasons Demon Sealers from the Demonic Era were so much more powerful. They had all lived through the horrors and watched their loved ones killed or devoured by demons. That kind of pain... it fuels their Demon Sealing Aura. However, since demons have gone into hiding and rarely show themselves these days, the Demon Sealers of this era lack that hatred and anger.\"","Yan Hara fell into silent contemplation before asking, \"It’s easy to fear demons... or even find them repulsive. But hatred? That’s different. How does one go about truly feeling hatred toward them?\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"It’s easy.\"","Without a word, Yuan suddenly summoned the Demon Devouring Sword into his hand.","\"You just need to experience what it’s like to lose someone you love... to the hands of demons,\" he then said.","\"That sword...\" Yan Hara’s eyes widened in awe as she took in its presence.","\"Isn’t that the Demon Sealing Sword? The Divine Paragon’s strongest treasure? It’s said to be so powerful that even the three Demon Sealing Treasures pale in comparison!\"","\"Its true name is the Demon Devouring Sword,\" said Yuan.","\"Where did you acquire it?\" she then asked.","\"In the Demon Sealing Pagoda.\"","\"What! That treasure had been under our noses this entire time?!\" Yan Hara exclaimed after hearing this.","\"But how are you going to let me experience losing someone I love?\" she then asked.","Yuan smiled faintly, then raised the Demon Devouring Sword, and in the next moment, a demon was summoned before them.","Yan Hara jumped back like a startled cat, her instincts flaring. But it wasn’t the sudden appearance that terrified her—it was the demon’s overwhelming presence. It radiated such terrifying pressure that her entire body went numb.","\"What in heaven’s name is that?!\" she cried out loud.","\"This is one of the Demon Emperors I fought and defeated during the Demonic Era,\" Yuan said calmly.","\"Its name is Demon Emperor Nightmare. It possesses the ability to trap its victims in illusions so vivid that they are indistinguishable from reality.\"","\"I mean, how in heaven’s name did you summon that thing? Is it real?\"","\"Yes, it’s real. The Demon Devouring Sword has the ability to summon demons it has devoured.\" Yuan nodded.","\"And you have complete control over it?\"","\"Yes. It no longer has a soul and is akin to a puppet, so there is no chance it’ll defy me, either.\"","\"If you say so...\" Yan Hara swallowed nervously."]},{"number":2111,"title":"Chapter 2111: Demon Emperor Nightmare","paragraphs":["\"Then I will begin your training now,\" said Yuan a moment later.","\"G-Give me a moment to prepare myself!\" Yan Hara hastily said.","Then, she closed her eyes and took several deep breaths.","A few moments later, she slowly opened her eyes as she declared, \"Okay, I am rea—\"","Before Yan Hara could even finish her sentence, Yuan commanded Demon Emperor Nightmare to activate its unique technique.","A dark crimson light flickered within the Demon Emperor Nightmare’s eyes, and in the next instant, trapped Yan Hara within its illusion.","When Yan Hara fully opened her eyes, she found herself in an unfamiliar place. However, the Demon Emperor Nightmare’s ability could do more than just create illusions. It could even create false memories and implant them into the victim, further selling its illusion.","Within moments after entering the illusion, fabricated memories flowed into her head.","Yuan calmly took a seat on the ground and waited for Yan Hara to finish her training, which could easily take weeks if not months.","\"Demon Emperor Nightmare, huh?\"","Yuan closed his eyes and reminisced about the war between humans and demons, specifically when he had to fight the Demon Emperor Nightmare.","Of all the Demon Emperors the Divine Paragon had faced, Demon Emperor Nightmare was arguably the most dangerous and annoying, as its unique ability had once forced him to relive the most harrowing moment of his life: the death of his childhood friend.","Naturally, Demon Emperor Nightmare was nothing more than a slight annoyance in the Divine Paragon’s eyes, akin to that of a buzzing fly, and it didn’t take him too much effort to defeat it.","While Yuan sat silently, lost in the memories of his past, Yan Hara was plunged into a living nightmare, experiencing misfortune after misfortune as she watched her loved ones fall, one by one, at the hands of demons. Each loss felt painfully real, and with every passing moment, the illusion sank deeper into her heart.","At first, Yan Hara was aware she was trapped in an illusion. But each time one nightmare ended, she was immediately thrust into another, each illusion weaving a different set of memories, a different life, all ending in tragedy.","Over time, the lines between reality and illusion began to blur, and her sense of self slowly unraveled as she was forced to live—and lose—again and again.","Furthermore, time flowed differently within the illusion. For Yan Hara, a single day in Yuan’s world felt like an entire lifetime, and each passing moment was years of love, loss, and pain.","This method of training bordered on torture. It was harsh, relentless, and unforgiving. Yet despite its brutality, the results were already beginning to show within just a few days.","With each passing day, Yan Hara’s Demon Sealing Aura grew noticeably stronger, denser, more refined, and far more intimidating. Alongside it, a fierce killing intent began to radiate from her body.","Time flowed swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, three months had passed since Yan Hara began her training.","By now, Yan Hara was almost unrecognizable. Though her appearance remained the same, her aura and presence were incomparable to before.","After another month, Yuan suddenly opened his eyes when blood began flowing from Yan Hara’s nose. Seeing this, he muttered, \"Looks like it’s time to end her training.\"","He commanded Demon Emperor Nightmare to halt its abilities the very next moment, ending Yan Hara’s seemingly endless nightmare.","However, the moment Yan Hara returned to the real world, her eyes instantly locked onto Demon Emperor Nightmare, and they flared with unfathomable hatred and killing intent.","\"DEMON!\" she roared before shooting herself at it.","Yuan didn’t stop Yan Hara and decided to let her fight Demon Emperor Nightmare.","Yan Hara’s body exploded with immense Demon Sealing Aura. It was so powerful that it leaked out of the training grounds and into the city outside, shocking the nearby Demon Sealers.","\"Heavens! Whose Demon Sealing Aura is this?! I have never experienced such a powerful aura! Even Master Zhou pales in comparison!\"","\"It must be Senior Yan! Only the Divine Paragon’s successor could possibly achieve this level of prowess!\"","While Yan Hara had been training, Zhou Yanfei spread the news of her being the Divine Paragon’s successor throughout the Demon Sealing Grotto, news that sent shockwaves through the entire faction.","Though many members were initially skeptical, they couldn’t forget witnessing Yan Hara wielding the Divine Paragon’s techniques during the invasion. Coupled with Zhou Yanfei’s firm endorsement, it didn’t take long for the faction to accept her as the rightful successor to the Divine Paragon’s legacy.","\"The Demon Sealing Aura is getting stronger!\" The Demon Sealers started gathering around the source, but none of them dared to approach since it was coming from within Zhou Yanfei’s territory.","Eventually, Zhou Yanfei appeared at the training grounds.","Though he was well aware that Yuan and Yan Hara were using the space for their training, curiosity eventually got the better of him, and he decided to step inside for a closer look.","’Heavens! What the hell is a demon doing here?! And that heavy presence... It’s a Demon Emperor!’ Zhou Yanfei was greatly shocked to see a Demon Emperor appearing in the middle of his training grounds, and he wondered if it had snuck inside to try to assassinate Yan Hara.","After a brief moment of contemplation, Zhou Yanfei showed himself and joined the battle with Yan Hara to deal with Demon Emperor Nightmare.","Yuan had already noticed Zhou Yanfei’s presence long before he arrived, but he decided not to stop him, even using it as an opportunity to test his loyalty.","Seeing Zhou Yanfei assisting Yan Hara without hesitation made him give a nod of approval.","After nearly an entire week of fighting, Yan Hara and Zhou Yanfei managed to subdue Demon Emperor Nightmare, sealing it.","\"How... How and when the hell did a Demon Emperor sneak inside? We have people guarding the city’s entrance around the clock ever since the Demon Worshippers’ invasion!\" Zhou Yanfei exclaimed afterward, wondering if someone had purposefully let it inside.","However, Yuan quickly said, \"Relax. This Demon Emperor isn’t real. It’s a puppet I created to help Yan Hara with her training.\"","\"What...?\" Zhou Yanfei stared at him with wide eyes, seeming unable to believe his ears."]},{"number":2112,"title":"Chapter 2112: Leaving the Demon Sealing Grotto","paragraphs":["Zhou Yanfei muttered, his face filled with disbelief. \"The demon was indistinguishable from the real thing! How did you manage to create such a thing?!\"","\"That’s a family secret,\" Yuan responded with a mysterious smile on his face.","Then, he turned to look at Yan Hara, who was standing before him with a dazed look on her face.","\"Are you okay?\" he asked her.","Yan Hara lowered her head to stare at her trembling hands and slowly responded, \"Give me a few minutes... I need to organize my mind for a bit...\"","Yuan silently nodded and returned to Zhou Yanfei.","\"So, anything new during these last few months?\" he questioned.","\"Your trick worked like a charm. We’ve managed to extract the traitors’ memories without any issues after you removed their curses, and we learned from them their background and goal on that day, as well as some information on the thief. Unfortunately, there was very little information about the thief.\"","\"I see. What did you learn?\"","\"These traitors were all orphans trained at a young age to be spies in the Demon Sealing Grotto and Demon Sealing Clan. They hail from a hidden family surnamed Mo somewhere within the Disappearing Mountain Valleys, and that’s all we know about them. We also know about their methods of training as well as their purpose.\"","\"Once they complete their training, they are sent to the Demon Sealing Clan and the Demon Sealing Grotto, where they establish themselves as Demon Sealers and spy on us. Their goal during the invasion was to distract us so the thief, whom they knew as ’Master Mo’, could break into our vault.\"","\"Master Mo, huh?\" Yuan mumbled, pretending to ponder despite already knowing the thief’s true identity.","\"So what is the Demon Sealing Grotto going to do now?\" he then asked.","\"Naturally, we’re going to retrieve the Divine Paragon’s treasures. Once we’re prepared, we’re going to give this Mo Family a visit.\"","\"I would investigate the Mo Family first before approaching them if I were you,\" said Yuan.","\"Don’t worry, we won’t act recklessly, especially knowing that they are working together with demons,\" Zhou Yanfei reassured.","Zhou Yanfei left Yuan and Yan Hara alone a few moments later.","Nearly half an hour after Zhou Yanfei left, Yan Hara finally opened her eyes and said, \"I apologize for the wait.\"","\"That was quick. I wouldn’t have blamed you even if it had taken a few months,\" said Yuan.","Yan Hara sighed and said, \"I have lived a total of 176 different lifetimes, with each and every single one of them ending in tragedy. My loved ones and I have died in every possible way to the demons, from being boiled to being eaten alive. These indescribable experiences... if I had known what I was getting myself into, I would’ve probably refused it, but alas...\"","After a brief moment of silence, she continued, \"At least my mental strength has drastically improved because of it, and my hatred toward demons feels very natural even though I am aware that it all happened in an illusion.\"","Yuan nodded with a smile and said, \"Not only did your Demon Sealing Aura improve significantly, but even your Soul Strength is nearly incomparable to just three months ago.\"","\"I only spent three months inside the illusion? It felt like ages,\" Yan Hara’s eyes widened at this news.","\"If you want to feel better, I have spent several years training in that manner as the Divine Paragon, experiencing thousands of tragic lifetimes. However, since my hatred toward demons was already quite high, it barely improved my hatred for them.\"","\"If you don’t mind me asking, what created the Divine Paragon?\" Yan Hara asked, her eyes flickering with curiosity.","Yuan closed his eyes for a moment before responding, \"I had a childhood friend. Her name was Ai Rong, and she was eaten by demons right before my eyes. At that time, I was a powerless, spineless bastard who could do nothing but watch his loved one be eaten. After that incident, I began to desperately search for a method to deal with demons.\"","\"Back then, the only way to deal with demons was to completely overwhelm them or destroy their crystal. Their regenerative abilities were one of the main reasons for their dominance, so I began researching in that direction.\"","Yuan paused for a moment before continuing, \"Honestly, I don’t remember how I came up with Demon Sealing Aura. It just appeared in my mind during a period of enlightenment.\"","\"That’s just how enlightenment works,\" Yan Hara said. \"It’s how many inventions and cultivation techniques come into existence. It’s called God’s knowledge for a reason.\"","Many cultivators believe that the state of enlightenment is akin to receiving divine insight—knowledge bestowed directly by the God of Knowledge, which explains most of the miracles that come with it.","\"God’s knowledge, huh?\" Yuan muttered.","A moment later, he continued, \"Anyway, what are you going to do now? I will leave soon.\"","\"Well, now that I am aware of the culprit behind the stolen treasures, and I have declared myself as the Divine Paragon’s successor, I can only return to the Demon Sealing Clan and try to take Qian Chu’s position while he’s gone. It won’t be easy, but with the Demon Sealing Grotto now on my side, it’s definitely doable.\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"If anything happens, you have ’that’ thing.\"","Yan Hara smiled and said, \"Of course. Nobody would dare to defy me if I reveal that thing—perhaps except traitors who aren’t true Demon Sealers.\"","\"Then good luck. I’ll come visit you once I am finished with my business. Qian Chu plans on doing something in 20 years, so we’ll likely meet before then.\"","\"You stay safe as well.\"","Shortly later, Yuan left the Demon Sealing Grotto to head to the Rising Phoenix Clan, while Yan Hara remained a little longer to speak with Zhou Yanfei and the rest of the Demon Sealing Grotto to ensure she had their full support in the future."]},{"number":2113,"title":"Chapter 2113: Returning to the Rising Phoenix Clan","paragraphs":["After a month of traveling nonstop, Yuan arrived at his destination, the Rising Phoenix Clan.","Even before he reached their residence, Yuan sensed a change in the atmosphere compared to his last visit. It was much stiffer and heavier, almost as if something grim had occurred recently.","\"I wonder what happened.\" Feng Yuxiang muttered as she appeared beside Yuan.","\"There’s only one way to find out.\"","As Yuan and Feng Yuxiang approached their territory, several powerful presences suddenly appeared to intercept them.","\"Halt right there and identify yourselves!\"","\"I’m Feng Yuxiang, and this is my Young Master. We have an appointment with your leader,\" Feng Yuxiang said calmly.","\"Appointment? We haven’t been informed of any such thing,\" the guard replied with a frown. \"You’ll have to turn around and leave.\"","\"You can ask either Feng Zhenyan or the Grand Elder. They’re expecting us.\" Feng Yuxiang continued.","\"Look here. I don’t care if you have an appointment or not. Unless you’re more important than the Celestial Doctor, you will not see our leader!\" The guard roared.","\"Celestial Doctor?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow upon hearing this, and he asked, \"Is the leader sick?\"","\"Mind your own business. This isn’t something for an outsider to know about.\"","However, the very next moment, they sensed another presence approaching. When the guards saw who it was, they quickly lowered their heads with respect.","\"I thought I sensed your presence, Young Master.\"","This individual was none other than Feng Haoyu.","\"Y-Young Master?\" The guards stared at him with wide eyes filled with disbelief, as none of them could fathom why their young lord would address someone in such a manner.","\"What do you think you’re doing? They’re our esteemed guests.\" Feng Haoyu then said.","\"T-That’s...\"","\"But due to the situation, I won’t blame you guys. Leave. I’ll handle things from here.\"","\"Yes, Young Lord.\"","Once the guards left, Feng Haoyu faced Yuan and said, \"I apologize for that.\"","\"No worries. What’s the situation right now? I heard you’re waiting for the Celestial Doctor.\" \"Please, follow me. This isn’t a subject we should be speaking about out in the open.\"","Yuan nodded and followed Feng Haoyu to a private room.","Once they were seated, Feng Haoyu spoke, \"The situation is quite dire right now, so everyone is on edge. Our leader—my mother—returned two weeks ago, but she returned greatly injured.\"","\"What happened to her?\"","\"We’re still unsure of the situation. She collapsed shortly after returning and hasn’t regained consciousness since, hence why we contacted the Celestial Doctor, who is known as the most experienced doctor in the Nine Heavens.\"","Yuan glanced at Feng Yuxiang and asked, \"What’s the difference between the Celestial Doctor and the Divine Doctor you introduced before?\"","\"Well,\" Feng Yuxiang explained, \"the Divine Doctor mainly treats mortals, while the Celestial Doctor specializes in treating immortals. He’s essentially in a completely different league compared to Li Shizhen.\"","\"When will the Celestial Doctor arrive?\" Yuan then asked.","\"He should arrive next week.\"","\"Do you think I can have a look while we wait?\"","\"Are you also a doctor?\" Feng Haoyu looked at him with wide eyes.","\"Well, I wouldn’t call myself a doctor, but I do specialize in curing poison and curses.\"","\"In that case, please take a look at my mother!\"","Yuan nodded, \"Alright. Bring me to her.\"","Sometime later, Feng Haoyu brought Yuan and Feng Yuxiang to his mother’s private residence, where the Grand Elder and several unfamiliar individuals were gathered.","\"Who are they?\" The people in the room questioned the moment they saw Yuan.","\"Senior Primordial Phoenix!\" The Grand Elder greeted him instead.","\"What? He’s the Primordial Phoenix that you were speaking of?\" The others in the room were utterly shocked to learn this.","Yuan ignored their gaze and approached the woman sleeping on the bed.","However, his path was immediately blocked by someone.","\"What do you think you are doing?\"","\"Step aside, Elder Yikong. The Young Master is an expert with poison and curse, and we already know that she’d been cursed,\" Feng Haoyu said out loud.","\"Can you really trust him? Although you have sworn your loyalty to him, you barely even know him! It’s not too late to stop your nonsense!\" Another elder spoke, criticizing his decision to follow a stranger.","\"I may not know much—if anything—about him,\" Feng Haoyu said calmly, \"but I trust my judgment of people. And my judgment tells me he’s someone who can be trusted.\"","\"Grand Elder! Please say something! The Young Lord is out of his mind!\" The elders turned to look at their eldest and most experienced.","The Grand Elder took a deep breath before speaking.","\"Senior Primordial Phoenix, I ask for your understanding regarding their skepticism. As a phoenix, I possess the ability to read one’s character through their flames. After experiencing your True Primordial Fire firsthand, I can say with certainty that you are not someone of ill intent, but I cannot speak for the others.\"","He then turned to look at the others and continued, \"Senior Primordial Phoenix has no reason to harm the leader. He may be a stranger, but he possesses the Primordial Phoenix’s bloodline, and just from that, we are obligated to give him a chance.\"","The elders fell silent.","\"Relax. I am just going to check her condition and nothing else.\" Yuan reassured them a moment later. \"Of course, if you still refuse to trust me, we can all wait for the Celestial Doctor to arrive. Though it might be too late by then.\"","\"W-What the hell do you mean it might be too late?!\"","\"Do you really think you can scare us with such nonsense?!\"","The elders exclaimed, their faces full of anger.","Yuan shook his head and explained, \"I’ve only been in this room for a few moments, and I can already sense her bloodline weakening significantly. If we wait an entire week, she may not die—but she likely won’t recover properly from whatever’s afflicting her either.\"","Hearing this, the elders turned to look at their leader and swallowed nervously."]},{"number":2114,"title":"Chapter 2114: A Familiar Curse","paragraphs":["\"There’s no way the leader’s bloodline is weakening! Someone get the Golden Phoenix Needle!\" One of the elders shouted, his voice full of nervous skepticism.","Another person there rushed out of the room the next instant, and he returned a few minutes later with a golden needle in his grasp.","Then, using the Golden Phoenix Needle, often used by phoenixes to check the strength of their bloodline, carefully tested the leader’s bloodline through a drop of her blood.","Shortly after testing the leader’s bloodline, the Golden Phoenix Needle emitted a faint crimson glow before a number appeared on the top of the needle’s handle.","\"85.2 percent?! Her bloodline quality has dropped by four whole percent!\" the elder holding the needle exclaimed in a voice laced with terror.","\"FOUR PERCENT?!\"","The others cried out in shock, as if they had just seen a ghost. Even the Grand Elder and Feng Haoyu were visibly shaken. Though four percent might not sound like much, in truth, it was a devastating loss—one that could take generations to recover, even by a single percent.","In the world of phoenixes, only those with a bloodline quality of at least eighty percent were deemed royalty. The leader of the Rising Phoenix Clan possessed a peak bloodline quality nearing ninety percent, placing her among the purest and most exalted bloodlines in all the Nine Heavens.","However, with her bloodline diminished by four percent, her status and standing within the phoenix clan would plummet. Should it continue to fall any further, the Rising Phoenix Clan itself could face the unthinkable—having its title as one of the Royal Phoenix Clans revoked.","\"Her bloodline dropped by four percent, and it’s only been three weeks since her return! If we wait another week, it could drop by another percent!\"","\"What should we do?! We cannot wait for the Celestial Doctor’s arrival!\"","The entire room suddenly fell silent, and everyone in the room slowly turned their heads to look at Yuan.","After a moment of stillness, they all approached Yuan and fell to their knees.","\"Senior Primordial Phoenix! We were wrong for doubting you! Please heal our leader!\"","\"Please, Senior Primordial Phoenix!\"","They abandoned their pride and lowered their heads to beg Yuan.","Feng Haoyu then spoke in a grim voice, \"Four percent... this would take at least four million years to recover. Young Master, is there anything you can do to help my mother?\"","Yuan spoke firmly, \"Calm yourselves. I already said I would examine her condition, but I cannot guarantee I’ll be able to help. As for her weakened bloodline... we can discuss that later.\"","Hearing this, the elders quickly stepped aside, clearing a path to the bed where their leader lay in deep slumber.","Yuan stepped up to the bedside, his gaze falling upon the beautiful woman resting there. At first glance, she appeared to be sleeping peacefully, but every so often, her brows would knit together, as if she were trapped in the grip of a troubling nightmare.","Without a word, he placed a hand on her head and closed his eyes.","The room fell into a tense, uneasy silence. Everyone stood motionless, yet their bodies betrayed them with subtle tremors running through them as they waited in anxious anticipation for Yuan’s response.","A few moments later, Yuan lifted his hand from the leader’s forehead and turned to face the others before speaking, \"She’s definitely been cursed, and I am quite familiar with this curse.\"","His gaze drifted to Feng Yuxiang and continued, \"Feng Feng, you were also afflicted with this curse before.\"","\"Y-You don’t mean...\" Feng Yuxiang’s eyes widened at his words.","Yuan nodded, \"It’s the same curse that restricted your bloodline.\"","\"W-What is going on?\" Unable to contain their curiosity, one of the elders asked.","Feng Yuxiang then explained in a grim voice, \"Shortly after I left the Rising Phoenix Clan to do my own thing, I encountered this bastard who placed a curse on me, which restricted my bloodline and powers, essentially turning me into a human. If it weren’t for the Young Master’s help, I would’ve probably lost all of my powers by now.\"","\"What?! Such a vicious curse exists?! Who the hell is this bastard, and why did he target our leader?!\" The Grand Elder roared in anger.","Feng Yuxiang shook her head and sighed, \"I don’t know.\"","\"We can deal with this bastard later. Right now...\" Feng Haoyu looked at Yuan and asked, \"Since you have already dealt with it once, you can remove the curse again, right?\"","Yuan nodded, \"Naturally.\"","\"Please, save my mother. I beg of you.\" Feng Haoyu fell to his knees and begged.","The elders stared with bewilderment, as this marked Feng Haoyu’s first time begging someone on his knees.","\"Get up. I have no reason not to help her.\" Yuan said.","\"Thank you! Truly!\"","The next moment, Yuan retrieved the Sacred Chalice of Purification and began removing the leader’s curse.","\"This will take some time,\" Yuan warned them.","Yet, not a single soul in the room left.","A week passed quickly, but to the Rising Phoenix Clan, that week felt like an eternity. And although they wanted to urge Yuan to cure the leader faster, none of them dared to utter a word.","Suddenly, someone knocked on the door and spoke, \"Elders, the Celestial Doctor has arrived.\"","\"I’ll go greet the Celestial Doctor.\" The Grand Elder responded before anyone else could even say a word and left the room quickly after.","Upon arriving at the guest room, the Grand Elder greeted a short old woman in green robes.","\"I am the Grand Elder of the Rising Phoenix Clan. Thank you for coming here on such short notice, Celestial Doctor.\"","The Celestial Doctor, who was no taller than 4 feet, calmly spoke, \"Well, your leader is a good friend of mine. How is her condition right now?\"","\"She’s still unconscious, but we have someone helping her right now.\"","The Celestial Doctor frowned at this information and spoke, \"You allowed someone to touch her before I could even arrive?\""]},{"number":2115,"title":"Chapter 2115: Celestial Doctor","paragraphs":["\"Are you out of your mind?! How could you let someone touch her before I arrived?!\" the Celestial Doctor thundered at the Grand Elder. \"What if they made a mistake? It could have cost her life!\"","\"Please, let me explain, Celestial Doctor...\" the Grand Elder said quickly. \"This man is no ordinary healer. He’s an expert in curses and poison—and our leader has been cursed, which caused her bloodline purity to drop! In just three weeks, it’s fallen by four percent! If we had waited for you, her bloodline might have weakened far more than necessary!\"","\"Four percent?!\" The Celestial Doctor’s eyes widened at this information.","The Grand Elder nodded with a solemn face.","\"As a beast yourself, you should understand why we’re panicking and why we acted so hastily,\" he sighed.","\"Who the hell are you calling a beast? I am a Celestial Spirit! We’re nothing alike!\" the Celestial Doctor shot back.","Celestial Spirits were entities born naturally from Celestial Qi, often formed when vast concentrations of it gathered and condensed over time. They’re akin to treasures but have their own consciousness and soul.","However, because of the immense amount of Celestial Qi required to give them form, Celestial Spirits were exceedingly rare—so rare, in fact, that perhaps only one would be born in an entire era.","As for their appearance, since their bodies were composed entirely of Celestial Qi, they could assume any form they desired. The Celestial Doctor’s short, elderly visage was simply a matter of personal choice, adopted for reasons known only to her.","\"Anyway, enough yapping. Let me see your leader and this ’expert’ you speak of.\"","The Grand Elder nodded and led her to the leader’s room, where the leader was still being treated.","\"That’s the expert?\"","The Celestial Doctor raised an eyebrow after seeing the situation inside. Since Yuan only needed the Sacred Chalice of Purification to cleanse the leader’s curse, he didn’t need to do anything after feeding it her blood, so he was just sitting beside her like a spectator.","\"Move aside.\" The Celestial Doctor said to the elders in the room as she approached the bed.","The elders didn’t say anything and quickly moved aside for her.","Once the Celestial Doctor stood beside Yuan, where she could see his face, her eyes widened with shock and disbelief.","\"Y-You! Tian Yingzhe?! What the hell are you doing here? I thought you were dead!\" she exclaimed, sounding as if she’d just witnessed a ghost.","Yuan turned to look at the short old lady with a puzzled face and asked, \"Tian Yingzhe? Who’s that?\"","Of course, Yuan recognized the name Tian Yingzhe, as he was the founder of the Celestial Overlords. However, he had no recollection of the Celestial Doctor himself, so he simply feigned ignorance.","\"Who the hell do you think you are trying to fool?\" The Celestial Doctor frowned, looking offended.","\"In case you have forgotten, I am a Celestial Spirit, and I have the ability to look directly at your soul,\" she said.","Yuan immediately fell silent. Though the Celestial Doctor claimed she could see his soul, Yuan wasn’t quick to take such a statement at face value.","\"Why don’t we talk somewhere else?\" Yuan then said.","\"Sure.\"","As Yuan stood up and approached the exit, one of the elders asked, \"What about the curse?\"","He was worried that the treatment might be delayed because of this.","However, Yuan pointed at the chalice on the ground and said, \"That doesn’t require any management. It won’t stop working just because I am out of the room, either, so you can relax.\"","\"If you say so...\"","Sometime later, Yuan and the Celestial Doctor left the room. Feng Yuxiang decided to stay behind so she wouldn’t disturb their conversation.","A few moments later, standing in an empty courtyard not far away, the Celestial Doctor faced Yuan and asked, \"What the hell is going on, Tian Yingzhe?\"","\"I wasn’t joking when I said that I am not Tian Yingzhe,\" he calmly responded.","\"Still trying to fool me? What are you trying to achieve with this?\" she narrowed her eyes at him.","\"Before I explain myself, what is your relationship with Tian Yingzhe?\"","\"My relationship? Fine, I’ll entertain your nonsense for a bit.\" The Celestial Doctor gave a quick sneer before retrieving an azure-colored medallion from her spatial ring that read ’Celestial Overlords’.","\"Tian Yingzhe and I go way back,\" the Celestial Doctor began. \"I knew him long before I even became a full-fledged Celestial Spirit. In my immature state, I was no different from a living treasure—something that could grant immense benefits to a cultivator. Because of that, I was constantly hunted by humans and beasts alike.\"","\"I met Tian Yingzhe when he saved me from being captured, and he continued to protect me until I became an adult Celestial Spirit. If it weren’t for him, I wouldn’t be here right now. Anyway, to repay him, I decided to follow him and help him build the Celestial Overlords. I am essentially its co-founder.\"","Yuan’s eyes widened upon hearing this, but before he could even respond, the Celestial Doctor’s figure suddenly shifted, transforming herself into a tall and slender beauty.","\"Do you remember me now?\" she asked.","\"Uhh...\"","Yuan was speechless for a brief moment.","Then, he explained his situation, \"To tell you the truth, Tian Yingzhe died long ago.\"","\"WHAT?!\" The Celestial Doctor exclaimed, not daring to believe her ears.","\"Let me finish. Anyway, he died and reincarnated.\"","\"Are you saying that you are...\"","He nodded.","\"Yes, I am Tian Yingzhe’s reincarnation. Although I don’t have all of his memories right now, I’ll eventually regain them.\"","\"Unbelievable... but that explains the state of your soul...\" The Celestial Doctor sighed, even rubbing her eyes in a somewhat stressed manner.","After a moment of silence, she asked, \"So, about the Celestial Overlords... have you heard about their situation?\"","\"If you’re talking about their internal struggle, yes, I am well aware of it. At least the surface stuff,\" he said."]},{"number":2116,"title":"Chapter 2116: Celestial Doctor(2)","paragraphs":["\"Internal struggle... that’s putting it lightly,\" the Celestial Doctor said, shaking her head. \"The Celestial Overlords quickly went to shit after you disappeared. It’d gotten so bad that I decided to leave.\"","\"Now that you’ve returned, are you going to take control again? Otherwise, I don’t see myself ever returning.\"","\"We’ll see how things go. The Celestial Overlords is a thing of the past, so I don’t really have much attachment to it, especially since I don’t have most of Tian Yingzhe’s memories. However, that might change when I recover his memories.\"","\"Is that so? I guess I’ll remain as a wandering doctor for a little longer then.\"","The Celestial Doctor retrieved a jade slip before casually tossing it into the air toward Yuan, who quickly caught it.","\"You can use that to communicate with me directly. If you ever need my help, don’t hesitate to call,\" she said. \"I don’t want to brag, but as the Celestial Doctor, I’m one of the most influential individuals in the Nine Heavens. There’s hardly a sickness or injury I cannot heal, and I have treated countless people throughout the years.\"","\"In that case, I’ll contact you if I ever get hurt.\" Yuan chuckled.","The Celestial Doctor nodded before falling into a brief moment of silence.","\"By the way, have you met that mischievous little girl yet?\" she suddenly asked.","\"Mischievous little girl? Who are you talking about?\" Yuan asked with his eyebrows raised.","\"You know... that little girl who used to follow you everywhere. She’s one of the four Celestial Overlords in your faction.\"","\"Oh, you mean Xu Jiaqi? Yeah, I have met her. In fact, she is convinced that I am Tian Yingzhe’s reincarnation—not that I have told her the whole truth, yet.\"","\"Why not? Do you not trust her? You told me about your identity quite easily, even though you don’t even remember me,\" she said with a somewhat puzzled face.","\"No, that’s not it. I met her long before I even began recalling any memories, so I am just waiting for the right time to tell her. She’s also quite busy right now with the Celestial Overlords, and I do not want to distract her. Regardless, she already knows that I am Tian Yingzhe’s reincarnation.\"","\"But she doesn’t know you’ve retained Tian Yingzhe’s memories,\" the Celestial Doctor said. \"Still, that’s not surprising, considering it’s almost unheard of for a reincarnator to keep the memories of their past life. Such a thing would be beyond defying the heavens.\"","\"Anyway, as much as I’d like to keep talking about the past and catching up, I still have a job to do—and my friend’s life is at risk. Can you tell me about the leader’s condition?\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"Let’s catch up another time. The leader was cursed with a vicious curse that sealed her bloodline. However, that’s already being taken care of. Since I am not a real doctor, I don’t know if there’s anything else wrong with her.\"","\"I understand. Then I will have to examine her. Let’s return.\"","Some time later, Yuan and the Celestial Doctor returned to the room.","\"I’m going to examine the leader now,\" declared the Celestial Doctor.","Yuan quickly reassured the elders, \"Don’t worry, it won’t affect the curse-cleansing process.\"","The Celestial Doctor went to examine the leader shortly later.","\"She has some minor internal injuries. However, it’s nothing serious, and they will heal by themselves,\" she said a moment later.","\"Do you know where she went before returning?\" she then asked the elders.","\"Well, she had some business with another Royal Phoenix Clan, but I can’t imagine they’d do something like this to her—we’ve always been on good terms. She was probably attacked on her way back or something. We won’t know for sure until she wakes up,\" explained one of the elders.","The Celestial Doctor then said, \"In any case, since I have examined her and determined there’s nothing I can do for her, I’ll be taking my leave now.\"","\"W-What about her weakened bloodline? Is there a fix for that?\" One of the elders suddenly asked.","The Celestial Doctor responded without hesitation. \"Of course, but it’s going to be very costly. I can already think of a few treasures that could restore her bloodline, but each one is incredibly rare and utterly priceless.\"","\"That’s...\"","Naturally, the elders knew of such treasures even without needing the Celestial Doctor to name them, but they were far beyond the reach of even the Rising Phoenix Clan. Even if they somehow managed to acquire these treasures, they wouldn’t dare to use them so carelessly.","\"Aside from using such treasures, the only option is for her to slowly restore her bloodline over time,\" the Celestial Doctor said.","\"That will take millions of years...\"","\"It’s unfortunate, but there is no shortcut.\"","Yuan then spoke up, \"I may have a way to improve her bloodline.\"","\"Really?!\" The elders looked at him with skepticism written all over their faces, but none dared to voice their doubts.","Feng Haoyu stepped forward and said, \"Have you all forgotten that he carries the Primordial Phoenix’s bloodline?\"","\"That’s right! Primordial Phoenixes can enhance the bloodline of other phoenixes!\" the elders exclaimed, trembling with excitement as they remembered Yuan’s identity.","But before they could celebrate, Yuan’s calm voice cut in.","\"Removing your leader’s curse and restoring her bloodline are two entirely different matters. I won’t ask for anything to lift the curse, but if you want me to restore her bloodline, you’ll have to do something for me in return.\"","\"What do you want us to do?\" One of the elders asked.","\"We can talk about that once your leader wakes up,\" he said.","\"Okay...\"","\"Then I’ll take my leave for real now. Until next time.\" The Celestial Doctor said to Yuan before leaving the Rising Phoenix Clan.","Three days after the Celestial Doctor’s departure, the Sacred Chalice of Purification completed its work, fully cleansing the leader’s curse. Just a few hours later, she finally awoke from her long slumber."]},{"number":2117,"title":"Chapter 2117: Fate Maniac","paragraphs":["\"Leader! You’re awake! Thank the heavens!\" The elders immediately rushed to her side after noticing her open eyes.","The leader, a beautiful woman with flowing red hair and sharp facial features, slowly sat up on the bed and turned to look at the group with a puzzled face.","\"Where... where am I?\"","\"You’re back at the Rising Phoenix Clan, mother.\" Feng Haoyu said, pushing the elders aside so he could see her.","\"I see... I made it back...\" she muttered in a low voice.","\"What happened out there, mother? Why did you come back injured? Who attacked you?\"","The leader gritted her teeth and clenched her fists in frustration as she responded, \"It was that damn freak, the Fate Maniac!\"","\"Fate Maniac?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow upon hearing this weird nickname.","The leader continued, \"That bastard attacked me out of the blue, claiming he was merely following fate’s command! I don’t know what he did to me, but he left after placing some curse on me, and I was barely able to make it back!\"","The room fell silent after everyone learned the identity of the attacker.","\"The Fate Maniac... what a troublesome individual.\" The Grand Elder muttered in a stressed tone.","\"Who is this Fate Maniac?\" Yuan asked.","The Grand Elder explained, \"We don’t know the Fate Maniac’s true identity, only that he’s a madman obsessed with fate—constantly proclaiming himself a servant of it. He’s incredibly elusive; you can’t seek him out, only be sought out by him. And on top of that, his strength is unfathomable.\"","\"Servant of fate...?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at the familiar description, his thoughts drifting back to his time in the lower heavens, when he had encountered an unusual man named Jia Chong in the Demons’ Valley.","\"Wait a second. Who are you?\" The leader suddenly questioned Yuan’s identity as she finally noticed his presence.","\"This is—\"","\"My Young Master.\" Feng Yuxiang stepped forward and interrupted Feng Haoyu.","The leader’s eyes widened at her familiar face.","\"You are... Feng Yuxiang? Why are you here? I thought you’d left. Have you decided to return to us?\"","Feng Yuxiang shook her head. \"No, I’m still not affiliated with the Rising Phoenix Clan. I’ve returned because my Young Master has business with you.\"","\"Sorry for the late introduction. I am Yuan, a Primordial Phoenix.\"","\"What?! That’s impossible!\" the leader exclaimed, abruptly rising from her bed.","Yuan didn’t waste time arguing. Instead, he simply summoned his True Primordial Fire, letting its invisible presence speak for his identity.","\"Invisible flames... True Primordial Fire...\" The leader fell to her knees in shock.","\"It was also the Young Master who removed the curse from you, or you would still be bedridden right now, and your bloodline would’ve continued to decline,\" said Feng Haoyu.","The leader’s entire body froze at his words. Then, she turned to look at him with stiff movements.","\"W-What did you just say?\" she asked in a trembling voice.","\"The Young Master removed the curse—\"","\"No! Not that! What about my bloodline?!\" she shouted in a panicked voice.","The room instantly fell silent, and the atmosphere became heavy.","\"Someone speak to me, damn it!\" the leader snapped, stomping her foot with such force that the entire chamber trembled.","The Grand Elder stepped forward, his voice solemn as he said, \"The curse placed upon you has weakened the purity of your bloodline. In just three weeks, it has fallen to 85.2 percent.\"","Upon hearing that her bloodline purity had dropped by a full four percent, the leader’s expression froze. Before she could even speak, her body gave way, and she collapsed once more, overcome by shock and despair.","\"Leader!\"","\"Mother!\"","Those nearby hurried forward to catch her, gently laying her back onto the bed.","Even as a God Ascension cultivator, with a mind and soul tempered to extraordinary resilience, the blow to her bloodline was too heavy a burden for her to endure.","A few minutes later, the leader’s eyes fluttered open, and she slowly sat up. Turning to the others with a strange smile, she said, \"I just had the most unbelievable nightmare... In it, my bloodline purity dropped by four percent. Please, tell me it was just a dream.\"","The elders’ faces turned pale once more, and not one of them could find the words to comfort her.","\"Sorry, but it wasn’t a dream,\" Yuan said calmly. \"The curse truly did weaken your bloodline. But look on the bright side. It could have been far worse. For instance, Feng Feng—Feng Yuxiang, endured this same curse for thousands of years before she met me.\"","\"Also, it’s not impossible to help you recover your weakened bloodline.\"","\"T-That’s right! You’re a Primordial Phoenix! You can help my bloodline recover, perhaps even strengthen it!\" The leader’s eyes began glowing with hope again.","\"It’s possible, yes. However, it’s not going to be free.\"","\"What do you want? Money? Treasures? Just name your price!\" The leader said.","\"I have no shortage of treasures. That said, there is something that I want from the Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, the leader spoke, \"Clear the room for us. I would like to speak with him in private.\"","The elders in the room immediately left without uttering a sound.","Once only Yuan, Feng Yuxiang, and the leader remained in the room, Yuan spoke plainly.","\"I’ll get straight to the point—I want the Ancient Seal in your possession.\"","The leader’s eyes narrowed with skepticism.","\"I won’t even ask how you learned the Ancient Seal is in our possession, but why are you after it? What would a Primordial Phoenix want with it—if you’re even a real Primordial Phoenix?\"","Yuan shook his head.","\"Sorry, but I cannot tell you that.\"","\"You do realize the Ancient Seals were entrusted to us by the Celestial Emperor, right? Handing it over would be akin to betraying him outright. And with the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans having recently allied themselves with him, our clan would have to answer not only to the Celestial Emperor, but to every other Royal Phoenix Clan as well. You’re basically asking us to die with that request,\" she said."]},{"number":2118,"title":"Chapter 2118: The Celestial Emperor’s Offer","paragraphs":["\"The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans have allied themselves with the Celestial Emperor?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, her voice tinged with disbelief. \"That’s hard to believe. Why would they—who have always prided themselves on their independence—choose to work with the Celestial Emperor, of all people?\"","The leader looked at Yuan and calmly responded, \"Because the Celestial Emperor has a phoenix on his side—a Primordial Phoenix, that is.\"","\"What?\" Feng Yuxiang muttered with wide eyes.","\"The Celestial Emperor has a Primordial Phoenix?\" she repeated just in case she misheard.","The leader nodded, her expression serious.","\"Yes. He promised to elevate all of our bloodlines by at least three percent, regardless of our current bloodline purity, if we agree to work with him for ten million years.\"","Though ten million years might sound like an eternity, even the Royal Phoenix Clans considered it an incredible bargain. For those whose bloodline purity was already exceptionally high, gaining even a single percent could take millions of years, making the Celestial Emperor’s offer nearly irresistible.","The Rising Phoenix Clan’s bloodline purity ranged between 80 and 85 percent, with their leader being the highest at 89 percent before it was weakened, and they were ranked sixth amongst the ten Royal Phoenix Clans.","The Royal Phoenix Clans above them ranged between 85 and 88, with the top three ranging between 90 and 92 percent.","The phoenix with the current highest purity has a 94 percent bloodline purity, with no phoenix in history besides the Primordial Phoenix achieving a bloodline purity of over 95 percent, hence why the Celestial Emperor’s offer was extremely enticing and almost impossible to reject.","\"This is also why I doubt your identity as a Primordial Phoenix. I appreciate that you helped cure my curse, but I cannot give you the Ancient Seal, as that would spell the end of my life and of this clan.\"","A Primordial Phoenix had not appeared in the world for millions of years, so for two to emerge within the same era was something almost impossible to believe.","Naturally, Yuan did not blame her for not believing him.","\"How can you be so sure the other Primordial Phoenix is genuine?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Because we tested their bloodline purity—it was 96.5 percent,\" the leader replied. \"Only a Primordial Phoenix can naturally surpass 95 percent. And that phoenix also displayed the True Primordial Fire.\"","In the end, Yuan decided to deactivate his phoenix transformation and said, \"You’re right. I am not a phoenix, much less a Primordial Phoenix.\"","\"Y-You...\" The leader’s eyes widened with shock and disbelief.","\"You’re a human?! How in heaven’s name is that even possible?!\"","\"I’ll tell you if you do me a favor.\"","\"What is it? And don’t even bother opening your mouth if you’re going to ask for the Ancient Seal.\"","\"I would like you to help me set up a meeting with the Royal Phoenix Clans,\" he said.","\"Are you serious? I may be the leader of the Rising Phoenix Clan, but my authority is limited. I can’t summon the others whenever I feel like it. There must be a real reason. Unless you’re a Primordial Phoenix, you can forget about it.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"While it is true that I only pretended to be a Primordial Phoenix, it is also true that there is a Primordial Phoenix present right now.\"","\"You can’t mean...\"","The leader slowly shifted her head to look at Feng Yuxiang.","Noticing her gaze, Feng Yuxiang placed her hands on her hips and lifted her chin slightly.","\"That’s right—I am a Primordial Phoenix,\" she declared, her voice brimming with pride.","The leader’s expression darkened into a frown, looking offended.","\"Do you really expect me to believe that? Have you forgotten we tested your bloodline when you first joined us? It was only 83.2 percent back then. How could you be a Primordial Phoenix with that level of purity? You may qualify as a royal phoenix, but that’s it! Are you mocking me right now?\"","Feng Yuxiang quickly replied, \"That was before I awakened my bloodline and before I met the Young Master.\"","\"You were also cursed, weren’t you?\" the leader pressed. \"Wouldn’t that have lowered your bloodline, too? In fact, I’m starting to doubt you were cursed at all. How did you manage to survive thousands of years with it, while I lost four percent in just three weeks?\"","\"Maybe because my bloodline is much harder to weaken? After all, I am a Primordial Phoenix,\" she said.","Yuan then stepped in, his tone calm but decisive. \"Rather than wasting time with words, why don’t we settle this with the Golden Phoenix Needle?\"","He turned around and walked outside, where the elders were waiting.","\"Is the conversation finished?\" They asked.","\"No. I need to borrow the Golden Phoenix Needle for a moment,\" he said.","The elder with the needle quickly handed it to him.","\"Thanks.\"","Yuan returned to the room and closed the door behind him.","\"You can do the honor.\" Yuan handed the Golden Phoenix Needle to the leader, who wasted no time testing Feng Yuxiang’s bloodline.","Moments later, the needle emitted a bright golden glow, followed by a number.","\"This can’t be... this is impossible!\" The leader mumbled to herself after reading the numbers.","Not daring to believe her eyes, she rubbed them and looked again. Yet, the number remained the same.","\"97.9 percent!\" she exclaimed after confirming the number.","However, Feng Yuxiang frowned and said, \"Only 97.9 percent? I was expecting 100 percent!\"","\"W-What about True Primordial Fire? Can you use it?\" The leader asked after snapping out of her daze.","Feng Yuxiang nodded and casually summoned some True Primordial Fire.","\"There are currently two Primordial Phoenixes existing in this era? Truly unbelievable...\" The leader muttered.","\"So, about the gathering... can you do it?\" Yuan asked after a brief pause. \"If that’s not enough to draw them in, tell them we have an offer even better than what the Celestial Emperor is promising.\"","The leader could only stare at Yuan in silence, as if struggling to believe there could be an offer surpassing even the Celestial Emperor’s."]},{"number":2119,"title":"Chapter 2119: The Royal Phoenix Clans’ Response","paragraphs":["After a moment of silence, the leader slowly nodded her head and said, \"I’ll bring it up with the other leaders. It’ll probably take a few days to receive an answer.\"","\"We can wait.\"","The leader retrieved a communication jade slip from her spatial ring and began sending messages, notifying each and every leader of the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans about the situation.","She had expected it would take several days for them to reply, but to her surprise, many of the leaders responded within mere minutes.","\"Six of the other nine clans have responded and agreed to attend the meeting. However, three have refused,\" she informed Yuan.","\"Who refused?\" Yuan asked.","\"The Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan, Immortal Ember Phoenix Clan, and the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan. They’re ranked 8th, 4th, and 1st in the Royal Clans,\" she explained. \"So, do you still want to have this gathering?\"","He nodded, \"Yes, I don’t need all of the Royal Clans on my side—just enough to convince you to give me the Ancient Seal.\"","The leader’s mouth dropped.","\"You’re seriously doing all of this just for the Ancient Seal? Why do you even want it? Besides being a key that opens the Primordial Realm, I don’t think it has any other uses,\" she said.","\"I’ll tell you after I acquire the Ancient Seal,\" he said with a calm smile.","\"Fine. Then, when do you want the gathering to happen? What about the location?\"","\"As soon as possible. As for the location, I’ll let you decide.\"","\"I understand. Give me a moment to think.\"","A few minutes later, she said, \"I can’t really think of anything, so let’s just hold it where we usually do—at the Undying Fiery Summit. Since this topic is too sudden, it’ll take at least a month or two for everyone to be prepared. Let’s hold the gathering three months from now just to be safe.\"","\"Sounds good.\" Yuan agreed.","\"Then I’ll let the others know.\"","The leader immediately notified those who agreed to the gathering of the location and time. Soon, they responded with acknowledgement.","\"Alright. It’s done.\"","\"Thank you. Now, let’s talk about the Rising Phoenix Clan. Although this could wait until the gathering, we might as well do it now since we’re already here.\"","\"What do you want from the Rising Phoenix Clan?\" she asked, a faint frown of worry creasing her brow.","\"Nothing material,\" Yuan replied. \"I want the Rising Phoenix Clan to serve me. Or, if you prefer a better phrasing, I want you to work with me.\"","\"That’s—\"","Yuan quickly interrupted the leader as she opened her mouth, \"Listen to my offer before you give me an answer.\"","The leader slowly closed her mouth and silently nodded.","\"Not only will we improve the Rising Phoenix Clan’s bloodline purity, but we’ll also help your bloodline evolve into a superior one—if it’s possible.\"","\"What... did you just say?\" The leader’s eyes widened so far that it seemed her eyeballs might pop out.","\"Primordial Phoenixes like Feng Yuxiang have the ability to improve other phoenixes’ bloodline purity, but I can do that and evolve it.\"","\"How can a mere human have the ability to—\"","The leader abruptly cut herself off as a thought struck her. The possibility of it being true was almost nonexistent. Yet, it was not entirely zero.","She wanted to voice the question lingering in her mind, but the courage to ask it never came, so she held her tongue and remained silent.","Yuan noticed her weird facial expression and could guess what she was thinking, but he didn’t say anything, only offering a mysterious smile on his face.","\"If... If you really have that ability, then the Rising Phoenix Clan will serve you,\" she said. \"However, how are you going to prove your ability? Surely, you’re not expecting me to just take your word for it.\"","\"Of course not. As for the evidence... I’ll prove it to you during the gathering.\"","\"In that case, I’ll wait until then to provide you with my answer.\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Fair enough.\"","\"Anything else you want to talk about?\" The leader then asked.","\"No. We’ll leave for now. See you again in three months at the Undying Fiery Summit.\"","\"Okay.\"","Yuan and Feng Yuxiang left the room shortly after.","\"Where are you going, Young Master?\" Feng Haoyu asked them.","\"I’m going to leave for three months.\"","\"Leave? Why?\"","\"Your mother will tell you everything.\"","\"I understand...\"","Though he still had many questions, Feng Haoyu decided to wait until later.","Once Yuan and Feng Yuxiang departed from the Rising Phoenix Clan’s territory, Feng Haoyu and the elders immediately approached the leader for answers.","She did not withhold anything, openly recounting the entire situation to them—including the revelation that Yuan was not the true Primordial Phoenix, but that title belonged to Feng Yuxiang.","\"What?! Feng Yuxiang was the Primordial Phoenix?!\" The Grand Elder exclaimed.","\"That’s impossible! How did that man use True Primordial Fire, then?!\"","\"Hmph. It was probably some trick. I bet he was only acting like he could use it when, in reality, it was Feng Yuxiang who was using it,\" remarked one of the elders.","\"Although we were tricked, it doesn’t change the fact that they have a Primordial Phoenix, and Feng Yuxiang’s bloodline purity is even above that of the one with the Celestial Emperor.\"","\"They already fooled us once. What’s to say they aren’t still deceiving us? What if Feng Yuxiang isn’t truly a Primordial Phoenix either?\" another elder asked, his voice thick with skepticism.","\"That’s very unlikely,\" said the leader, backing Feng Yuxiang. \"Not only is it impossible to trick the Golden Phoenix Needle, but it’s impossible to fake her True Primordial Fire, too.\"","Suddenly, someone spoke up.","\"Young Lord, what are your thoughts on this matter? You swore loyalty to that man, yet he turned out to be a fraud. He’s not even a phoenix, let alone a Primordial Phoenix.\"","Everyone turned their attention to Feng Haoyu, who was deep in thought.","\"What? You swore loyalty to him?\" the leader asked, her frown deepening as she heard this for the first time."]},{"number":2120,"title":"Chapter 2120: Abyssal Underground","paragraphs":["Under the weight of many gazes, Feng Haoyu let out a heavy sigh before speaking.","\"Honestly, I don’t know what to say or even feel. Betrayed? Not necessarily. I swore my loyalty to him not because of his bloodline, but because of his ability and something else. So even if he isn’t truly a Primordial Phoenix, as long as his abilities are real, I have no reason to complain. And... there’s just something about him—something that makes me attracted to him. I can’t explain it.\"","He then turned to his mother and continued, \"I’m sorry, Mother, for making such a decision without consulting you. I acted on my instincts.\"","\"Since it’s your decision, I will respect it,\" she replied. \"However, now that you know he might be a fraud, what will you do? Unless you’ve performed a ritual, you can still withdraw your allegiance, as a verbal declaration isn’t technically binding.\"","\"Just like you, I’ll wait until the gathering before making my decision. There must be a good reason why Feng Yuxiang—a true Primordial Phoenix—would follow someone like him,\" he said.","Hearing this last remark, the elders couldn’t help but agree. It was indeed strange. They could understand why someone might follow the Celestial Emperor, the most influential figure in the Nine Heavens—but Yuan? No one present even knew his true identity.","In their eyes, he was just a human who could somehow transform into a phoenix.","\"...\"","While everyone in the room pondered deeply yet failed to find a convincing reason, the leader’s mind settled on one possibility. However, she kept it to herself, as voicing it aloud might make her sound utterly insane.","Meanwhile, after leaving the Rising Phoenix Clan for the second time, Feng Yuxiang asked Yuan, \"What are we going to do for the next three months?\"","\"How far away is the Undying Fiery Summit?\" he asked.","She pondered for a moment before responding, \"If we take the teleporters, it’ll only take twenty days to get there.\"","\"Are there any good hunting grounds near that place? I want to spend this time hunting magical beasts.\"","\"Hunting magical beasts?\" Feng Yuxiang raised an eyebrow at the unusual activity. \"If you’re looking for strong ones for training, I’d recommend—\"","\"No,\" Yuan cut in abruptly. \"I don’t care how strong they are. I only care about numbers. I need to kill around a hundred million, after all.\"","\"A hundred million?!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed after hearing this astronomical number.","\"Why in heaven’s name do you need to kill so many magical beasts?\" she couldn’t help but ask.","\"It’s for a quest.\"","\"...\"","Feng Yuxiang fell silent for a moment to ponder. Then, she spoke, \"If you want numbers, you should visit the Abyssal Underworld. All sorts of insect-type magical beasts dwell there, and they typically come in massive numbers, such as the Abyssal Crystal Ants.\"","\"Sounds like just the place I want to go. How far is it?\"","After some calculations in her head, Feng Yuxiang replied, \"A month, but it’s quite close to the Undying Fiery Summit.\"","\"Alright. Lead the way.\"","Feng Yuxiang summoned her flying treasure, and the two sped away.","After several teleportations and a month of travel, they finally arrived at their destination.","The entrance to the Abyssal Underworld yawned before them. It was a colossal hole in the earth, vast enough to swallow an entire mountain whole. From the outside, it appeared as nothing more than an abyss of pitch-black darkness, its depths concealing whatever lay within.","\"There are a lot of people here,\" Yuan said in a somewhat surprised tone.","\"The Abyssal Underworld is vast, with countless areas still unexplored. Mapping it can be extremely profitable. And in places untouched by cultivators, treasures are often abundant, making it a hotspot for treasure hunters as well.\"","\"How strong are the magical beasts inside?\" Yuan then asked. \"Many of the cultivators here are Bronze and Silver Immortals.\"","\"The deeper you go, the stronger the magical beasts. The weakest magical beasts inside are the ones by the entrance, and they have a cultivation of Divine King.\"","\"How deep do I have to go for the Abyssal Crystal Ants?\"","\"I’m not sure since I’ve never entered this place before. However, the Abyssal Crystal Ants are only around Divine Ancestor, so they shouldn’t be too deep.\"","Yuan nodded.","\"I should probably buy a map before I enter, right?\"","\"Or hire a guide who knows where to find the Abyssal Crystal Ants.\"","Yuan used his divine sense to look around the place, where many people were camped around the entrance.","Very quickly, he found several people selling maps of the Abyssal Underground, as well as a few people with a sign that read ’guide for hire’.","Since it would be more convenient to just hire a guide to lead him to his destination, Yuan approached one of the guides.","\"Good day, Young Master. Are you looking for a guide? Where are you trying to go?\"","The middle-aged man greeted Yuan, who was wearing a mask at the moment.","Yuan nodded and said, \"I’m looking for the Abyssal Crystal Ants.\"","At his words, the middle-aged man’s expression visibly stiffened, a flicker of unease crossing his face.","\"What’s wrong?\" Yuan asked.","\"Well... I don’t have what it takes to take you to the Abyssal Crystal Ants. I’m sorry,\" he said.","\"But you’re a Silver Immortal,\" Yuan remarked with raised eyebrows. \"The Abyssal Crystal Ants are only Divine Ancestor, so they shouldn’t be too deep.\"","\"This must be your first time at the Abyssal Underworld. Although the Abyssal Crystal Ants are quite weak, they actually live deep within the tunnels, where insects at the Golden Immortal level roam.\"","\"I see. I’ll find someone else, then. Thanks for your time.\"","Just as Yuan turned around, the middle-aged man said, \"Just a moment, Young Master. I may not be able to assist you, but I know someone who can help you.\"","Yuan halted his movements at such words.","\"I can take you to him if you’d like.\"","\"Sure.\" Yuan calmly nodded."]},{"number":2121,"title":"Chapter 2121: Abyssal Underground(2)","paragraphs":["\"Please, follow me.\" The middle-aged man led Yuan to a beautiful woman with emerald- colored hair and brown eyes at the other side of the entrance.","Unlike the middle-aged man, who was only a Silver Immortal, this woman had the cultivation of a True Immortal.","“Senior Zeng, I have brought you a potential customer. This is his first time here.\"","The woman looked at Yuan with a gentle smile and spoke, \"Hello, esteemed guest. I'm Zeng Guoquan, also known as the Jade Guide around here. I have over a thousand years of experience with tens of thousands of satisfied customers. If you're looking for a reliable and experienced guide for the Abyssal Underground, you have found the right person.\"","Yuan nodded and said, “I'm Xiao Yang, and I'm trying to reach the Abyssal Crystal Ants.\" “The Abyssal Crystal Ants are located between underground levels 250 and 300, where most Golden Immortal realm creatures roam. I can take you there for 500,000 spirit stones. 750,000 spirit stones if you want me to guide you back. I can even act as your bodyguard, but that will cost an additional 1 million spirit stones.”","“I just need you to bring me there,\" Yuan said.","“I understand. When would you like to depart?\"","“Immediately, if possible. Otherwise, as soon as possible.”","“We can depart immediately then.” Zeng Guoquan said.","\"Stay close to me.\"","Yuan nodded and followed Zeng Guoquan into the entrance to the Abyssal Underground.","From the outside, the Abyssal Underworld appeared to be an endless void of pitch black, but once Yuan crossed a certain threshold, a dim light seeped through the darkness. It wasn't nearly as bright as the surface, more akin to the faint glow of a nightlight in a dark room. Still, for a cultivator like Yuan, the low light made little difference; he could see through the darkness with ease.","\"How deep does the Abyssal Underworld go?\" Yuan asked as they ventured further into the tunnels.","\"No one can say for certain since nobody has ever reached the end. The furthest anyone has descended is to underground level 1,290, where peak God Ascension beings roam,\" Zeng Guoquan replied.","\"Peak of God Ascension? There are beings that strong within the Abyssal Underworld?\" Yuan was surprised to hear this.","“This world is filled with unfathomable beings, after all.\" Zeng Guoquan calmly remarked.","The tunnels of the Abyssal Underworld stretched wide and spacious, their ceilings soaring nearly ninety-five meters high, allowing for effortless movement through their vast expanse.","As Yuan and Zeng Guoguan made their way through the tunnels, they came across a myriad of insects and subterranean creatures, each native only in the Abyssal Underworld.","Two days later.","\"We're at underground level 100 right now. We should arrive at our destination in a few more days.\"","\"Okay.\"","“If you don't mind me asking, why are you looking for the Abyssal Crystal Ants?\" Zeng Guoquan suddenly asked.","“For training: Yuan gave a generic answer.","“I see. Where are you from? I used to be a disciple at the Verdant Rivers Pavilion before coming here to work as a guide,” Zeng Guoquan continued to make small talk as they traveled.","“I grew up as an orphan, so I don't have any background.\"","“Wow. You managed to reach that level as an orphan? You must be very talented.\"","“I wouldn't say that. However, I did get lucky with a few fortunate encounters.”","“Well, some say that luck is even more important than talent.\"","They passed the time with light conversation, and after two days of unhurried travel, they reached the 200th floor. Thanks to their overwhelming cultivation, none of the creatures dared to approach, allowing their journey to remain calm and untroubled. However, once they reached the 200th floor—where even the weakest beings were at the Silver Immortal realm—the monsters finally began to launch attacks against them. “Just ignore them,\" Zeng Guoguan instructed. \"If you have a technique to mask your presence, use it.\"","With that, she activated a technique that suppressed her aura just enough to slip past unnoticed.","Yuan followed suit, though he deliberately left a trace of his presence unconcealed. Several days passed in silence, Zeng Guoquan uttering not a single word, her attention seemingly fixed solely on guiding Yuan to his destination.","“How much further until we arrive?\" Yuan eventually asked.","“We're only a few hours away,\" she calmly responded.","Yuan didn't say anything else and continued to follow her.","Two hours later, Zeng Guoquan came to a halt and said, \"We have arrived at our destination.\"","Yuan used his divine sense to sweep the place, but he couldn't find any Abyssal Crystal Ants.","\"Are you sure we're in the right place?” he asked.","“Yes, I am sure.\"","Yuan closed his eyes and sighed.","While he didn't find any Abyssal Crystal Ants, he did find something else—several powerful presences.","\"So much for being a reputable guide,\" he sighed out loud.","In the next moment, the presences he had sensed revealed themselves, grinning broadly. Four figures stepped into view—human cultivators, each at the True Immortal realm.","“I didn't lie to you,\" Zeng Guoquan said. “I really am a reputable guide, and almost everyone knows me. But they only know what I choose to show them.”","Unfazed, Yuan asked, \"So, how often do you trap your customers?\"","\"Not often. Only when they're nobodies who won't be missed... orphans with no background like you,\" she replied with a peal of laughter.","The four cultivators joined in her laughter, their voices reverberating through the tunnel in mocking echoes.","“These idiots have no idea what they've gotten themselves into.\" Feng Yuxiang shook her head as she watched everything unfold within Yuan's Dantian.","Yuan then spoke, \"So, what are you going to do to me? Kill me and rob my corpse?\"","“It won't be considered robbing if the treasures owner is already dead,\" remarked one of the cultivators.","“In that case, hurry up and get it over with,\" Yuan said, his voice devoid of even the slightest trace of concern."]},{"number":2122,"title":"Chapter 2122: Abyssal Underground(3)","paragraphs":["\"Since you're so eager to die, allow me to grant your wish!\" one of the True Immortals snarled before suddenly lunging at Yuan.","\"Supreme Spear Arts, Grand Thrust!\"","The cultivator drew his arm back before hurling the spear in his grasp toward Yuan. His aim, however, deliberately avoided any vital organs, as though he wished not to end Yuan's life too quickly, but to let him suffer a slow, agonizing death.","Yet the instant the spear touched Yuan's body, it stopped cold against his skin, unable to pierce even a fraction deeper. To the wielder, it was as if he had struck an unyielding wall of steel.","“W-What...2\"","The man's eyes widened in disbelief, refusing to accept what he was seeing. He subconsciously began channeling more Immortal Qi into his strike, pushing with all his strength. Yet, the spear remained frozen in place, unable to advance an inch.","Yuan calmly looked at the spearman and said, \"How are you going to kill me if you cannot even harm me?\"","\"AHHHH!\"","The spearman let out a furious shout, unleashing the full force of his cultivation. A moment later, he felt the spear inch forward and allowed himself a brief smile—only for it to vanish when he realized the truth. Yuan had merely moved back ever so slightly, creating the illusion that the weapon was piercing his body.","\"Fuck! What the hell are you doing? Stop fooling around!\"","Unable to bear watching any longer, another True Immortal roared in frustration and charged forward, swinging a massive mace—twice the size of his own body—straight at Yuan's head.","BOOM!","A violent shockwave tore through the area as the mace slammed down on the crown of Yuan's head, hurling him into the ground. The impact shattered the earth, leaving a massive crater in the ground.","“That's how you do it, Third Brother!” laughed the man wielding the mace.","“Damn it! That was unnecessary, Third Brother! I could've killed him myself if you had given me a little more time!\"","“Enough yapping and go search his body! He reached the Golden Immortal realm as an orphan, and he's mentioned having fortuitous encounters. He's bound to be carrying something valuable,\" Zeng Guoquan barked.","“Yes, Elder Sister!\" they replied in unison.","But just as they moved toward the crater where Yuan had fallen, one of the other two brothers suddenly shouted in alarm, \"Watch out!\"","The Third Brother barely reacted just in time, but the Fourth--spear in hand--was a split second too slow. A sword flashed toward his face, the gleam of its edge being the last thing he saw before his consciousness was swallowed by darkness.","Though the Fourth Brother never realized how he died, the others were gripped by a surge of sorrow and fury at the sight of a sword driven straight through his face. \"FOURTH BROTHER!\"","The other three brothers shouted.","\"So loud,\" Yuan remarked as he emerged from the crater without even a scratch on his body.","“You bastard! You killed our Fourth Brother!\" the remaining three brothers roared, weapons leveled at Yuan as their eyes blazed and Killing intent flooded the area.","\"Okay... and?\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Did you really expect me to stand here and let you kill me without resistance? Did you think I wouldn't fight back? You should be thankful that I gave him a swift and painless death.\"","“Kill him! No! Tear him from limb to limb! Make him regret ever being born!\" Zeng Guoquan suddenly shouted.","The next moment, all three remaining brothers rushed at Yuan. While the Third Brother wielded a large mace, the other two wielded a sword and a heavy axe.","Of course, no matter what kind of weapon they wielded or how many there were, none of them could get through Yuan's physique with their Ancient-grade weapons.","“Elder Sister! Something is wrong! We cannot touch him with our weapons for some reason! Help us!\"","“You brainless idiots! If weapons don't work, use your martial techniques!\"","At her urging, the three brothers swiftly stowed their weapons, opting to unleash their martial techniques instead.","The tunnel shook violently as they executed their most powerful techniques. Yet, Yuan remained utterly unfazed, even letting out a casual yawn.","“Impossible! Even our martial techniques can't touch him!\" the brothers exclaimed in disbelief as Yuan emerged without a single scratch.","This time, even Zeng Guoquan stood frozen, utterly dumbfounded.","“I'd let you have some more fun before I end your lives, but seeing how I am short on time, I'll end things here,\" Yuan said a moment later.","“You—*","Just as Zeng Guoquan opened her mouth to speak, Yuan released his Supreme Sword Aura. In an instant, the True Immortals were smothered beneath its razor-sharp pressure, every breath laced with the threat of being cut to pieces should they dare to move.","“W-Who... who the hell are you?\" Zeng Guoquan cried out loud, forcing the words out with as little movement as possible, her voice strained and uneven under the crushing aura.","“I'm just a nobody,\" he calmly responded.","As his words faded, Yuan's Supreme Sword Aura struck the three brothers at once. Yet he deliberately avoided their vital organs, ensuring they would bleed out slowly, writhing in agony as death crept upon them.","\"How can a mere Golden Immortal possess such power...\" Zeng Guoquan muttered, her expression dazed.","Yuan stepped toward her at an unhurried pace and said, “I'm actually glad you revealed your true colors. Otherwise, I wouldn't have had the chance to rid myself of trash like you today.\"","\"Please... spare me... Il do anything you want!\" Zeng Guoquan begged, her voice trembling as she tugged down her upper robes, shamelessly revealing her alluring figure in a desperate bid for mercy.","\"Anything?\" Yuan asked.","\"Anything!\" she confirmed.","“Then die for me.\"","Yuan seized the Fourth Brother's fallen spear with his spiritual energy and, without hesitation, drove it into Zeng Guoquan's stomach, pinning her to the ground.","Zeng Guoquan let out a piercing scream, yet she refused to yield. In a flash, she produced a treasure from her spatial ring and pointed it at Yuan, shouting, \"Even if I die today, I'll make sure to take you with me!\""]},{"number":2123,"title":"Chapter 2123: Rod of Destruction","paragraphs":["\"Die, you bastard!\" Zeng Guoquan roared, flooding the treasure with her spiritual energy the instant she drew it, and the treasure began to glow ominously.","“Did you really think I'd let you use it?\" Yuan sneered, using the Heaven Sealing Technique on her. In a heartbeat, Zeng Guoquan's cultivation was sealed, cutting off the flow of spiritual energy and with it, any hope of activating the treasure.","Yuan then plucked the treasure from her grasp and examined it with mild interest. It resembled a wand, yet was forged entirely from some unknown crystal, its core brimming with an immense, destructive energy.","The energy within was so immense that, had Zeng Guoquan managed to activate it, the resulting devastation could have reshaped the very landscape of the Abyssal Underworld.","“What a dangerous item you have here. Where'd you get something like this?\" Yuan asked her, as he'd never seen anything like it before.","“I'l tell you if you let me live,\" she quickly replied.","\"Sure. I won't touch you if you tell me.\" Yuan nodded.","“Swear on your soul!\" she demanded.","“If you do the same.\"","With no choice but to obey, Zeng Guoquan began swearing on her soul with clenched fists, “I swear on my soul that I will tell you where I acquired the Rod of Destruction—the treasure in your hands if you let me live.\"","Yuan then swore, \"I swear on my soul that I won't touch you if you tell me everything you know about this treasure.\"","Once they had both completed their oaths, Zeng Guoguan began divulging everything she knew about the Rod of Destruction.","“The Rod of Destruction is an artificial treasure forged by the Nameless Society—a cabal of madmen united by a single goal: to create a weapon capable of unleashing the greatest destruction imaginable. I acquired it through a friend who had close connections with them. That's all I know.\"","“The Nameless Society, huh?\" Yuan mumbled.","“Who's your friend?\"","“You already met him. He's the one who brought you to me.\"","I see","“I've told you everything I know, so I'll be taking my leave now.\"","Without waiting for Yuan's reply, Zeng Guoquan wrenched the spear from her body, causing her blood to flow like a waterfall.","\"Wait.\"","Just as she began flying away, Yuan stopped her.","\"Are you going to break your oath? The heavens will destroy your soul if you do!\" she shouted with a deep frown on her face.","\"No, I won't do anything to you.\"","“But I will.\"","An unfamiliar voice suddenly resounded, startling Zeng Guoquan.","In the next instant, Feng Yuxiang emerged from Yuan's Dantian. Without a word of warning, she leveled a finger at Zeng Guoquan, summoning her True Primordial Fire. invisible flames erupted around Zeng Guoquan, consuming her body in an instant. \"Aaaah! You tricked me, you wicked bastard!\" Zeng Guoquan screamed, collapsing to the ground as agony tore through her body.","Yuan remained silent, his gaze fixed on her as she was slowly reduced to ash in Feng Yuxiang's flames.","“I curse you! Curse you! Curse you! I curse youll\" Zeng Guoquan screamed relentlessly, but her cries soon faltered.","Mere moments later, her voice fell silent altogether.","With the offenders dealt with, Yuan calmly gathered their spatial rings, transferring all their treasures into his own.","Among the items he discovered within their spatial rings was a map of the Abyssal Underworld, containing detailed information up to the 500th level.","Then, using this map, Yuan made his way to the actual location of the Abyssal Crystal Ants.","A day later, Yuan arrived at his destination.","\"So this is the Abyssal Crystal Ants' colony.\"","A faintly excited smile curved Yuan's lips as hundreds of Abyssal Crystal Ants came into view, scurrying through the depths and tirelessly carving new tunnels into the Abyssal Underworld.","Though they were ants in form, each was the size of a minivan, radiating the aura of the Divine Ancestor realm, while a few among them had reached Immortal Ascension. Without hesitation, Yuan revealed his presence and began slaughtering the Abyssal Crystal Ants. Though famed for their durable exoskeletons that were harder than refined metal used to craft Divine-grade treasures, they were utterly helpless before him, their bodies shattering beneath a single blow of his fist.","After killing several ants with nothing but his fists, Yuan unleashed his Supreme Sword Aura, cutting down many in a single sweep, as it would simply take too long to kill them one by one.","In the blink of an eye, hundreds of ants lay dead. Yet Yuan felt no satisfaction. Because at this rate, completing his quest of a hundred million kills would still take an eternity. Unfortunately, less than two months remained before he was due to depart for the Undying Fiery Summit.","As he continued cutting down hundreds of ants every few minutes, Yuan pondered a faster method to hasten the slaughter.","Suddenly, an idea surfaced in his mind—one that could drastically accelerate his grind, yet was both dangerously risky and downright devious.","\"Feng Feng, Yu Ning, Yingying. Hear me out.\"","Yuan then laid out his idea to them, seeking their thoughts.","“Young Master... that's insane—but brilliant at the same time,\" Feng Yuxiang said.","“It might not affect you, but it will definitely impact everyone else,\" Yu Ning added.","“It sounds good in theory, but it could easily go out of control, and innocent people could die as a result.\" Lan Yingying said in a worried tone.","“I'll make sure to seal off this entire area before I do it, so there won't be any innocent casualties,\" said Yuan.","After discussing the plan in detail and refining it to ensure nothing spiraled out of control, Yuan readied himself to set it into motion.","First, he moved through the surrounding area, sealing every tunnel leading out of the Abyssal Crystal Ants' territory with formations through Yu Ning's help, effectively trapping them in one place. However, the territory was so vast that it took Yuan nearly an entire month to complete the task.","Once he was certain that there was no place for them to escape, Yuan retrieved the Baneful Abyss and approached the nearest ant."]},{"number":2124,"title":"Chapter 2124: Mark of the Baneful","paragraphs":["With the Baneful Abyss in hand, Yuan calmly approached the nearest Abyssal Crystal Ant.","The moment it sensed his presence—and the ominous aura radiating from the dagger— the creature let out an inaudible cry before turning to flee.","“You can run, but you can't hide.\"","Yuan made no move to chase the ant. In fact, he came to a complete stop.","Then, when it had fled far enough, he drew his arm back and hurled the Baneful Abyss, sending it streaking through the air like a deadly missile.","In the span of a heartbeat, the Baneful Abyss reached its target, striking the Abyssal Crystal Ant's body—a mass of semi-transparent, greyish crystal.","The blade of the Baneful Abyss pierced the ant's crystal body as effortlessly as a sharp knife through paper, instantly poisoning it and branding it with the Mark of the Baneful. The venom was so potent that the Abyssal Crystal Ant was brought to the brink of death in an instant.","Then, with the mark's activation, the dagger's second ability triggered, and its corpse erupted violently, releasing a dense poison mist that spread in a hundred-meter radius. The nearby Abyssal Crystal Ants were instantly afflicted with the Mark of the Baneful, each one detonating in turn. The chain reaction swept through their ranks without pause, continuing until every nook and cranny of their vast territory was shrouded in the deadly poison mist.","Hundreds... thousands... tens of thousands of ants perished within seconds, and in mere minutes, Yuan's quest progress had surged by millions of points.","in fact, the Baneful Abyss proved so devastating that it wiped out the entire Abyssal Crystal Ant population in the area.","Pleased by the method's efficiency—and with ample time still remaining—Yuan decided to expand his hunting grounds.","However, before using the Baneful Abyss, Yuan first ensured that no one else was nearby, as he had no intention of harming innocents.","Then, with the time remaining before his departure for the Undying Fiery Summit, he steadily expanded his hunting grounds, filling vast stretches of the Abyssal Underworld with the spreading poison mist.","Before long, people began to sense that something was amiss. Creatures within the Abyssal Underworld were behaving strangely, appearing in places they were never known to roam. Even powerful beings that should have existed only in the deepest levels were now being spotted in the upper floors, leaving the explorers utterly dumbfounded. Of course, this was because they were desperately fleeing from the poison mist unleashed by Yuan. With him relentlessly terrorizing through the lower levels, their only option was to escape toward the upper floors, which led to the entrance.","\"Everyone, watch out! Something strange is happening inside the Abyssal Underground!\" Someone shouted as soon as they left the underground, warning the people camping near its entrance.","“What's happening?\"","“The creatures that are usually found only within the deeper levels are rushing towards the entrance! I have never seen or heard of anything like this before!\"","\"Do you know the cause of this phenomenon?\"","\"No, but there are already people who went down to investigate.\"","A few days passed as word of the strange phenomenon spread far and wide. Eventually, reports began to arrive from those who had ventured out to investigate.","\"According to the investigators, the lower levels are shrouded in some kind of poison mist. They tried to probe deeper, but formations blocked their path, preventing them from getting any closer,” someone reported.","“Formations? Did someone put them up to prevent the poison from spreading?\"","“That's very likely.\"","“Where did this poison even come from? Was it released by some creature, or created by something else?\" another person mused aloud.","“There's no way to know unless we deactivate the formations and search deeper—but doing that could spread the poison even further. And we still have no idea how potent it truly is,\" someone remarked.","A debate soon broke out over whether they should deactivate the formations to investigate or keep the poison contained until it dissipated on its own.","Logically, the poison should be left alone to avoid unnecessary trouble and risk. However, the vast territory it now occupied severely hindered exploration, which in turn meant significant losses in revenue.","Moreover, many believed the poison wasn't particularly lethal and could be bypassed with the aid of poison-resistant pills.","“We should just let the poison spread. That way, itll thin out and disappear much quicker.”","\"Since we don't know where it's coming from, we can't say for certain the poison will disappear so easily.\"","“I'm actually a master of poisons. I'll check out the poison first and give you my input.\" “I'll go with you since I also have some experience with poison.”","\"Me, too.\"","Before long, an expedition was organized, with numerous experts setting out to examine the poison for themselves.","Some time later.","\"So, what do you think? How deadly is it?\"","“It's hard to say without experiencing it firsthand, but even so, I can tell it's unlike any poison I've ever encountered. That said, it's probably not too deadly since its color is only green, which is the most common and weakest color of poison out there.\"","“This poison resembles the Jade Poison,” remarked one of the poison experts there. “Though it's powerful, it's only strong enough to threaten mortals.”","“If that's the case, why are even Immortal-level creatures running away from it?\"","\"Poison doesn't affect everyone the same way. It's possible the creatures in the Abyssal Underworld are simply more vulnerable to it by nature.”","“Why don't we deactivate the formation briefly--just long enough for me to test the poison?\"","\"Are you sure?\"","The poison master nodded. \"Truth be told, I'm not doing this out of goodwill. I'm simply very interested in studying this poison.\"","“Let's get an Array Master down here then.\"","A few days later, a Level 8 Array Master was brought to the Abyssal Underground to deal with the formations.","When the Array Master arrived and saw the formations, he exclaimed with surprise, \"Heavens! This type of formation is incredibly ancient and dates back to the Primordial Era! There are only a few Array Masters in this world who would be knowledgeable enough to create something like this!\""]},{"number":2125,"title":"Chapter 2125: A Deadly Mistake","paragraphs":["\"I never imagined I'd lay eyes on such an ancient formation...\"","The level 8 Array Master was left in awe of the formations crafted by Yu Ning, an Array Master from the Primordial Era. With the passage of countless years, most formations from that era had been lost to time.","\"So, can you deactivate it or not?\" one of the cultivators there asked the Array Master. The Array Master coldly scoffed, \"Of course, I can. However, it's going to take a little longer than usual since formations from the Primordial Era are much more complex.” Although formations from the Primordial Era were far more intricate in design, they were not necessarily stronger than modern ones. Over time, advancements in array symbols and formations had reduced unnecessary complexity while retaining their power, and in some cases, even enhancing it.","After taking another moment to admire the formation, the Array Master began working on deactivating it.","Somewhere in the Abyssal Underground, Yu Ning instantly sensed something was wrong with her formation and warned Yuan, \"Young Master, someone is trying to deactivate one of my formations.\"","However, Yuan wasn't surprised to hear this. In fact, he'd anticipated someone would try to release the poison, as it was in human nature to mess with things they shouldn't. “Which one?\" he asked Yu Ning.","“The formation on the 220th level.\"","Hearing this, Yuan immediately began moving in that direction. Though he could get rid of the poison if these people were afflicted with it, he had to be close enough to do so.","A day later, Yuan arrived just in time, as the level 8 Array Master was only minutes away from breaking the formation.","He approached them and spoke out loud, \"I wouldn't do that if I were you.\"","\"What?\"","Everyone there turned to look at him with raised eyebrows.","\"And who are you?\"","“The one who put up that formation,\" said Yuan.","“What? You're the one who set up these ancient formations?\" The Array Master paused his work, staring at Yuan with wide eyes, but he didn't recognize him at all. After all, every Array Master known to possess the skill to create such formations was a renowned individual.","“I put up the formation for a reason, you know? Don't you see the poison mist on the other side? Or is everyone here blind?\" Yuan mocked them.","The people there quickly frowned, and one of them responded, \"While I appreciate your concern for others, do you know how much traffic your formations are blocking in the Abyssal Underground? Even if there is a little poison, it can easily be negated with poison-resistant pills.\"","“A little poison? Do you know what kind of poison that is?\" Yuan then asked.","“No, but according to the experts, it's nothing too dangerous.”","Yuan couldn't help but chuckle at such a response and said, \"Nothing too dangerous? Alright. If you truly think that, go ahead and release the poison. I already warned you, so don't blame me for whatever happens afterward.\"","The frowns on their faces deepened after hearing Yuan's ominous words.","Since everyone present was at least a Bronze Immortal, Yuan wasn't too worried the poison would kill them instantly, and he could definitely remove the poison in time. However, these cultivators will suffer immense pain for a bit.","“The best way to learn is through pain, after all.\"","“What should I do?\" The Array Master asked the others for their opinion. “I can continue to remove the formation, or I can stop here.\"","The cultivators there began to ponder.","Eventually, one of the poison experts spoke, \"If you're that afraid, you can all stay back and let me prove to you that there's no need to be afraid of this level of poison.”","The cultivators nodded.","“In that case, let's do it.\"","\"Right? That guy probably doesn't even know anything about poisons and is just paranoid.\"","Yuan didn't try to convince these people and silently watched them remove the formation.","A few minutes later, the Array Master completed his preparations and began dismantling the formation.","The instant it was deactivated, the sealed poison surged outward like an unrelenting wave.","The Array Master immediately retreated, while the poison expert stepped forward, allowing the toxic mist to wash over him.","The others looked on in tense silence.","\"See? There's absolutely nothing to be worried abo—\"","The poison master broke off mid-sentence, his once-calm expression twisting suddenly into one of sheer terror and shock.","\"A-Are you okay?!\" the cultivators cried out.","\"H-Help... me...\" the poison expert gasped, collapsing to the ground and reaching toward them in desperation as blood poured from his eyes, nose, mouth, and ears.","Panic surged through the cultivators, and they turned to flee—but the poison mist spread far faster than they had anticipated, engulfing them before they could escape. Soon, they were all on the ground, writhing in agony and gasping for breath as the poison's excruciating pain tore through their bodies.","“What did I tell you? A bunch of idiots.\"","Yuan shook his head.","Once a few seconds had passed, and right before the poison claimed their lives, Yuan retrieved the Baneful Abyss and collected the poison with it. Then, with Yu Ning's help, reactivated the formation.","“This is my last warning to all of you—if you tamper with my formation and release the poison again, I won't be here to save you.\"","Without another word, Yuan turned and vanished into the darkness. Even with the poison purged from their bodies, the cultivators remained unable to move, the damage it had wrought requiring time to heal.","After their near-death experience, the cultivators quickly spread word to the others, warning them not to release the poison.","“That poison was unlike anything I have experienced before as a poison expert! Despite my poison resistance, it was able to completely immobilize me within seconds! If it weren't for that mysterious expert, I would've perished on that day!\" The poison expert recalled his experience.","And so, the people at the Abyssal Underground abandoned any further attempts to dismantle the formations, choosing instead to navigate around them—no matter how inconvenient it might be."]},{"number":2126,"title":"Chapter 2126: Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Gathering","paragraphs":["After the incident with the cultivators deactivating his formation, Yuan continued to spend every moment spreading the poison mist until it was almost time for the gathering at the Undying Fiery Summit.","In just over a month, Yuan had already slaughtered more than seventy million beings within the Abyssal Underworld, leaving him with fewer than thirty million to complete his quest. Of course, he still needed to break through to the True Immortal realm.","Once it was almost time, Yuan retrieved all of the poison mist with the Baneful Abyss before leaving the Abyssal Underground.","Although he could've left the poison there to passively grind kills, he didn't want to risk people deactivating his formation while he was gone, as he wouldn't be able to save them in time.","Moreover, he could easily return to this place to finish his quest in the near future, and since he still had to reach True Immortal, he was in no rush to complete it.","After emerging from the Abyssal Underworld, Yuan lingered near the entrance for several moments, his divine sense spread wide as though searching for someone. Moments later, he flew off in a particular direction and descended before a familiar middle-aged man.","“Y-You! Why are you here?!\" The middle-aged man exclaimed in shock, surprised to see Yuan standing before him, almost as if he was looking at a ghost.","“What's wrong? You look as if you'd seen a ghost\" Yuan remarked, snapping the middle-aged man out of his daze.","“What happened to the Senior Zeng?\" The middle-aged man immediately asked about her.","“Oh, it was horrible.\" Yuan quickly responded, his voice filled with anguish. \"We made it to the 300th floor without any problem, but as we neared the Abyssal Crystal Ants’ territory, the ground beneath us exploded, releasing a bunch of poison mist. Fortunately, I have poison resistance. However, the guide... she was not so lucky, and she perished from the poison.”","\"WHAT?! SHE'S DEAD?!\" The middle-aged man exclaimed, his face filled with disbelief. “I'm sorry for your loss.\" Yuan sighed.","“That can't be! There's no way she's dead!\"","Yuan shrugged, \"I don't know what else to tell you. If you don't believe me, you can go see her corpse for yourself. However, I don't know if itll still be there by the time you get there.\"","The middle-aged man fell to his knees with a blank expression on his face.","Yuan said nothing more and simply turned to leave. Though the man might have been colluding with Zeng Guoquan, Yuan lacked the proof to act. And even if he had it, killing the man in front of so many witnesses would only make him appear the villain, not to mention he needed to convince everyone there about Zeng Guoquan's true character. After departing from the Abyssal Underworld, Yuan followed Feng Yuxiang toward the Undying Fiery Summit.","Their destination lay within a land of eternal flame—a vast expanse wreathed in undying fire. For thousands of miles, the flames stretched unbroken, growing ever more intense the deeper one ventured, their power marked by a gradual shift in color.","“What's the story behind this place?\" Yuan asked.","Feng Yuxiang replied, \"According to legend, a Primordial Phoenix was born here. At its birth, the flames you see now were ignited, and they have burned ever since. It's said that even a great flood once tried and failed to extinguish them—hence the name, the Undying Flame Valley.\"","“This is also a revered place where phoenixes come to cultivate, considered both popular and sacred among them. Humans, however, are strictly forbidden to enter, and any who are discovered will be executed on sight by the phoenixes who train here.\"","\"So I am in danger?\" Yuan chuckled.","“Well, you're a different story. Also, humans can enter if they received a phoenix's approval, and with me here, nobody would dare to cause you any trouble,\" she said. After two more days of travel, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang finally beheld a colossal solitary mountain in the distance—its entire form wreathed in roaring flames.","When they got close enough, they could see guards surrounding the entire place, treating it like a treasure vault.","“Identify yourselves.\"","The guards commanded when Yuan and Feng Yuxiang got close enough.","“We're the ones who called for this gathering,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","“Then you must be the Primordial Phoenix! Please, follow me. The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans are already present and waiting for your arrival.\"","And so, Feng Yuxiang and Yuan followed the guard up the mountain's fiery slopes until they arrived at its summit, where a colossal colosseum-like structure stood. Within its walls lay a grand hall arranged much like a conference chamber.","Within the conference chamber were ten distinct sections, each clearly designated for one of the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans.","\"Hm?\" Both Yuan and Feng Yuxiang raised their brows at the sight before them.","“What's going on? I thought only seven of the Royal Phoenix Clans had agreed to participate. So why does it look like all ten are here?\" Feng Yuxiang asked as they stepped into the chamber, noting that each section was occupied by groups clad in their own distinct attire.","Noticing their arrival, the leader of the Rising Phoenix Clan spoke up.","“Welcome to the Royal Phoenix Chamber. As for your question, though three clans had initially declined to participate, they changed their minds at the last moment and chose to join the gathering after all.\"","Feng Yuxiang glanced at Yuan, who wore a faint smile behind his mask.","Stepping into the spacious center of the chamber, Yuan raised his voice and asked, \"Did you come here under the orders of the Celestial Emperor?\"","The room fell silent, and the atmosphere instantly became stiff and heavy.","“That's right,” someone suddenly replied. \"Is there a problem with that?\"","Yuan turned his gaze toward the phoenix who had spoken and said calmly, \"No, not at all. In fact, I'm glad you're all here. It will make this meeting far more interesting, and it spares me the trouble of hunting you down later.\""]},{"number":2127,"title":"Chapter 2127: Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Gathering(2)","paragraphs":["Shortly after the Rising Phoenix Clan's leader informed the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans of the gathering, the others promptly contacted the Celestial Emperor to report the situation, since failing to do so might have been seen as acting behind his back. Naturally, the Rising Phoenix Clan had done the same. That said, the Royal Phoenix Clans had contacted the Celestial Emperor largely as a formality, and few of them truly regarded the matter as treacherous.","When the Celestial Emperor learned of the existence of a second Primordial Phoenix, he was just as surprised and intrigued as the Royal Phoenix Clans. Thus, he suggested that everyone take part in the gathering. Since seven of the ten had already agreed to participate, he was mostly speaking to the three who initially declined.","\"Before we even begin, I would like to confirm something.\" Another phoenix suddenly spoke out loud. \"To not waste anyone's time, I want to see for myself the evidence that you are a Primordial Phoenix.\"","Though nobody else said anything else, many of the phoenixes present could be seen nodding their heads in agreement, as they all shared the same sentiment.","\"Sure.\" Feng Yuxiang agreed without hesitation.","One of the phoenixes in the chamber produced a crimson needle crafted from a crystal- lie material and spoke loudly, “Instead of the Golden Phoenix Needle, we'll be using the Celestial Phoenix Needle. It was crafted from a Primordial Phoenix's feather and blood. Not only is it more accurate than the Golden Phoenix Needle, but it will also produce a distinct reaction upon sensing the Primordial Phoenix bloodline. The other Primordial Phoenix also used this needle to test their bloodline, so it would only be fair to test your bloodline with it as well.\"","“Use whatever needle you want. The results won't change.” Feng Yuxiang responded with full confidence.","The phoenix holding the Celestial Phoenix Needle rose to his feet and approached Feng Yuxiang, needle in hand. Moments later, he drew several drops of her blood and waited. Within seconds, the needle began to tremble before bursting into a brilliant crimson flame, the fire taking the form of a phoenix with wings outstretched.","“It's true! She's a genuine Primordial Phoenix!” the man exclaimed, awe written across his face.","The others in the chamber echoed his astonishment, their expressions a mix of shock and delight. No matter their personal feelings, the appearance of two Primordial Phoenixes at the same time was nothing short of a miracle—an event worthy of celebration.","“That's not all!\" The man with the Celestial Phoenix Needle continued. \"The purity of her bloodline is at 98.8 percent! It's much higher than the other Primordial Phoenix's bloodline!”","\"What?!\" the leader of the Rising Phoenix Clan exclaimed, leaping to her feet in shock. \"I tested her bloodline only three months ago, and it was at 97.9 percent! Are you telling me it's risen by nearly a whole percent in that short time?!\"","\"Perhaps the Golden Phoenix Needle failed to measure her bloodline accurately,” one of the phoenixes suggested.","However, Feng Yuxiang dismissed that notion and said, \"I don't know if she mentioned it, but my bloodline was cursed for thousands of years and only began recovering a few years ago. I believed I had already fully recovered, but clearly, that wasn't the case. I'm willing to bet that my bloodline will reach 99 percent sooner or later.\"","The chamber fell into silence, as none of the phoenixes present could truly fathom what it meant to possess a bloodline purity of ninety-nine percent.","“Is there anything else you need to verify before we begin the meeting?\" Yuan asked, breaking the silence.","“What about you?\" Someone responded a second later. \"Who are you, and what qualifications do you have to stand before us, much less speak with us?\"","\"Do I qualify to be here?\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly asked.","\"Of course. You're a Primordial Phoenix with near 99 percent bloodline purity,\" the phoenix quickly responded.","“Then he, my master, definitely qualifies to stand before you.\"","“Outrageous! How can a Primordial Phoenix like you serve as a mere human's servant?!\" someone exclaimed, their voice brimming with indignation.","“Why not? The other Primordial Phoenix serves the Celestial Emperor, and as far as I know, the Celestial Emperor is human as well,\" Feng Yuxiang replied.","“I-That's a different story! The Celestial Emperor is the most powerful human in the Nine Heavens!\"","“Well, I beg to differ. My Young Master is unquestionably superior to the Celestial Emperor,’ Feng Yuxiang declared calmly, not a trace of hesitation in her voice. Her words left the room dumbfounded.","A little over twenty phoenixes were present, with two to three representatives from each of the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans.","“Let's calm down,\" Yuan said after a brief silence.","He went on calmly, \"I was the one who summoned this gathering—not you, nor anyone else in this chamber. If you believe I am unqualified to be here, then you are free to leave.\"","The phoenixes narrowed their eyes at Yuan's boldness, but despite their displeasure, they all remained in their seats.","“Now with that settled, let's begin the meeting, shall we?\"","The phoenixes nodded.","“Let's begin with a quick introduction. My name's Yuan.\"","“I'm Feng Yuxiang.\"","Despite giving his real name, none of the phoenixes recognized it. Although his name had spread during the Sword Emperor's Qualifications, most beasts held no interest in matters irrelevant to them and hadn't bothered to watch. Even in the wider world, the number of people who had witnessed the event was insignificant when compared to the grand scale of the populace.","The leader of the Rising Phoenix Clan introduced themselves next.","\"Feng Lingyang of the Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"Feng Niepan of the Nirvana Phoenix Clan.\" The phoenix seated beside the Rising Phoenix Clan went next.","\"Feng Qiongyao of the Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan.\"","\"Feng Yushan of the Heavenly Phoenix Clan.\"","One by one, the leaders of the Royal Phoenix Clans introduced themselves.","By the end, Yuan had learned the names of every clan."]},{"number":2128,"title":"Chapter 2128: Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Gathering(3)","paragraphs":["After the introduction ended, Yuan spoke, \"I know your time is very precious, so I will get straight to the point.\"","“You've allied yourselves with the Celestial Emperor because he promised to help you improve your bloodline by three percent. However, the Celestial Emperor and I are... let's just say we're not very friendly with each other, and I want you to serve me instead of the Celestial Emperor.\"","The phoenixes in the chamber stared at Yuan with wide eyes, as though unable to believe what they had just heard.","After a moment of silence, they burst out laughing.","“You want us to serve you instead of the Celestial Emperor?! Hahaha! That's the funniest joke I've heard all decade long!\"","Once the laughter calmed down a little, the leader of the Crimson Rebirth Phoenix spoke in an offended tone, \"First of all, we don't “serve’ the Celestial Emperor. In fact, we don't serve anyone. We are working with him. That's completely different from serving him.\" The leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan then spoke, \"I don't know how you managed to coax the Primordial Phoenix into becoming your servant, but it won't work on the rest of us. Regardless of your offer, we won't serve you.\"","“Why don't you hold onto that thought until after you hear my offer? I did mention that I have an offer even better than the one the Celestial Emperor gave you, hence why some of you even bothered to show up here.\"","The room fell silent as the phoenixes began talking with each other through voice transmission.","Yuan couldn't care less about what they were talking about and patiently waited for them to be done.","Several minutes later, the leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan finally spoke. “Very well—we'll entertain you for now. Let's hear your offer.\"","Yuan's voice was steady and deliberate as he spoke loudly, \"Not only will I raise your bloodline purity by more than three percent, but I will also grant the first three phoenix clans that agree to serve me the chance to evolve their bloodline.\"","“What?! Evolve our bloodline?!\" Several clan leaders shot to their feet in shock.","However, a few immediately dismissed his claim, sneering with disdain and anger. \"You expect Us to believe such nonsense? Is that the same trick you used to deceive the Primordial Phoenix?\"","“What good would come from deceiving the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans? I'm not that foolish,\" Yuan said with a shake of his head. \"While I cannot promise success in evolving your bloodline, I can guarantee that I will raise its purity to its utmost potential. There are also other benefits for serving me, but I will save those for later.\"","“Even if you are telling the truth, are you really expecting us to just take your word for it? Just like how we confirmed the Primordial Phoenix's bloodline, we'll need evidence for your claims.”","\"Of course, I'l prove it.\"","Yuan scanned the room with a sharp gaze before stopping at a certain individual.","\"Feng Haoyu, come over here.\"","\"Me?\" Feng Haoyu, who had shown up to the gathering with his mother and the Grand Elder, wore a dumbfounded look on his face after being called out.","Yuan silently nodded.","Feng Haoyu stood up and approached the center of the room.","Then, Yuan asked him, \"Before we begin, I would like to apologize for fooling you while pretending to be a Primordial Phoenix. I also won't blame you if you no longer wish to serve me.\"","\"That's...\" Feng Haoyu began, but finding himself at a loss for words, he quickly closed his mouth.","\"Regardless of your decision, I will permanently improve your bloodline as an apology.\" Yuan turned to look at the phoenix who tested Feng Yuxiang's bloodline and said, \"You should test his bloodline before I begin so you can see the results.\"","The phoenix, who was from the Graceful Phoenix Clan, nodded and approached Feng Haoyu with the Celestial Phoenix Needle in hand to collect his blood.","A few moments after collecting Feng Haoyu's blood, the Celestial Phoenix Needle revealed his bloodline's purity.","\"86.4 percent.”","“Not bad.\" Feng Lingyang, his mother, nodded with a satisfied expression on her face. Due to her weakened bloodline, Feng Haoyu's bloodline had also suffered, dropping from its original 87 percent.","\"86.4 percent, correct? Keep that number in mind.\"","As Yuan spoke, he retrieved the Baneful Abyss and, before everyone's eyes, pricked the tip of his finger with it, drawing several drops of his blood. Though he still had some preprepared blood in his possession, he needed to show the phoenixes evidence that it belonged to him.","The instant Yuan's fresh blood touched the air, a unique aroma spread throughout the chamber. The moment the phoenixes sensed it, they began to salivate unconsciously. After collecting his own blood, Yuan held it before Feng Haoyu and commanded, \"Drink it","\"Excuse me?\" Feng Haoyu's eyes widened at his command.","“If you want to improve your bloodline, drink it. If you don't want to, I'l give it to someone else,\" said Yuan.","Feng Haoyu fell into deep thought over Yuan's offer. For a divine beast, drinking the blood of a human was deemed disgraceful—an act befitting only wild magical beasts who reveled in such savagery.","Yet, despite his distaste for the notion of drinking a human's blood, Feng Haoyu couldn't shake the feeling that refusing would lead to immense regret, especially when he noticed Feng Yuxiang staring at the blood with a ravenous gleam in her eyes.","“Okay, I'll drink it.\"","With resolute determination, Feng Haoyu accepted the blood and downed it in a single quip.","“Delicious!” he exclaimed involuntarily, the taste unlike anything he had ever known— refined and divine, as though crafted by the heavens themselves.","Then, a familiar sensation swept through his body, one strikingly similar to the feeling he had experienced when Yuan bestowed his blessing over a year ago.","Just to be safe, Yuan gave Feng Haoyu the Immortal Monarch's Blessing.","\"Alright, you may test his bloodline again,” Yuan said as he turned to the phoenix holding the Celestial Phoenix Needle."]},{"number":2129,"title":"Chapter 2129: Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Gathering(4)","paragraphs":["\"What? You want me to test his bloodline already? It hasn't even been a full minute since whatever you did to him! Do you think our bloodline can be improved so easily?\" The phoenix with the Celestial Phoenix Needle remarked with a frown on his face.","“You'll know once you test his bloodline,\" Yuan replied with confidence.","\"...Whatever. If you say so.\"","The phoenix proceeded to test Feng Haoyu's bloodline again.","A moment later, when the phoenix saw the results, he dropped the Celestial Phoenix Needle onto the ground, his face frozen with shock and disbelief.","\"Well? What's the result?\" the other phoenixes pressed, their voices brimming with curiosity and anticipation.","The phoenix swallowed nervously before responding in a dazed voice, \"86.9 percent...\" “What?! His bloodline purity has improved by half a percent in just a minute?! Impossible! Test his blood again!\" The phoenixes urged.","Picking up the Celestial Phoenix Needle, the phoenix looked at Feng Haoyu, who was just as dazed by the result, and said, \"Excuse me...\"","He tested Feng Haoyu's bloodline again.","“Impossible!” The phoenix exclaimed a moment later.","\"H-His bloodline is now at 87.3 percent!\"","The entire chamber fell silent as the phoenixes struggled to comprehend what they were witnessing. In just a minute or so, Feng Haoyu's bloodline purity has improved by nearly an entire percent, something that normally requires hundreds of thousands of years. “What in heaven's name is going on?! How can consuming a human's blood strengthen his bloodline?!\" The leader of the Radiant Phoenix Clan exclaimed.","Though they wanted to believe it was some kind of trick, they knew that was impossible, as the Celestial Phoenix Needle could not be deceived. Yet, a few of them soon reached a startling thought.","“Wait... a human's blood capable of strengthening a divine beast's bloodline? That sounds exactly like the Immortal Monarch's power...","None dared to voice such a notion aloud, for it bordered on madness. The Immortal Monarch had perished many eras ago, after all. And yet, the more they turned the thought over in their minds, the more plausible it began to feel.","“Well, are you satisfied? Or do you need more evidence?\" Yuan suddenly said, breaking the brief moment of silence in the chamber.","“One... one more time. Let me test your bloodline again!\" the phoenix with the Celestial Phoenix Needle demanded, his eyes fixed on Feng Haoyu.","Feng Haoyu quickly nodded in approval, as he, too, was eager to know if his bloodline had strengthened further.","The other phoenixes swallowed nervously.","A moment later, the results came back.","\"8...89.3 percent! His bloodline has improved by yet another entire percent!”","\"Heavens! Another percent?! Even if the improvements stopped at this point, his bloodline still improved by two percent in just a few minutes! This level of progress is unheard oft\"","\"How much more will his bloodline improve?\" The leader of the Etheral Phoenix Clan asked Yuan.","He shrugged,”Honestly,! have no clue.If you really want to know, you'll have to wait a few days for the final results-weeks to be safe.\"","Very well, I'll acknowledge your ability to enhance our bloodline.But what about your second claim? If true, it would be an","“Unfortunately, I cannot provide proof at this moment, as I currently lack the ability to do so,\" Yuan said. \"However, once I regain more of my strength, I will be able to begin attempting it. For now, you'll have to take me at my word.\"","\"Regaining your strength...? Just who are you?\" The leader of the Jade Phoenix Clan questioned.","“Who am I? I think many of you already have a clue about my identity, so why don't you try to confirm it?\" Yuan responded with a smile on his face.","Feng Lingyang of the Rising Phoenix Clan was the first to stand up and open her mouth, “Then if you don't mind me asking... Are you related to the Immortal Monarch?\"","“What?! The Immortal Monarch?!\" Those who did not connect the dots exclaimed in shock after hearing his name.","The atmosphere in the chamber quickly shifted, becoming heavier as the phoenixes anxiously awaited Yuan's response.","“You can say that.\" Yuan acknowledged.","\"W-What is your relationship with the Immortal Monarch? Is he still alive?” Feng Lingyang continued to question.","“Yes, the Immortal Monarch is alive. As for my relationship with him...\" After a brief pause, Yuan continued, *I am the Immortal Monarch.\"","The phoenixes in the chamber leapt to their feet, their eyes widening so much it seemed they might fall from their sockets.","The revelation was so staggering and confusing that silence blanketed the chamber for several long moments.","Then, the stillness was shattered with the sound of laughter.","\"Hahaha! I can't hold it in any longer! You're the Immortal Monarch? That's hilarious!\" scoffed a handsome young man seated beside the leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan.","Yuan turned his gaze to the young man, who had risen to his feet and was now striding toward the center of the chamber, closing the distance between them.","The young man stopped right before Yuan and spoke, “If you're really the Immortal Monarch, you should be able to make me kneel with just your words, right? Try it.\"","\"Are you sure you won't mind the humiliation?\" Yuan asked.","“Don't worry, I won't be humiliated,\" he confidently responded.","\"Why? Because you're a Primordial Phoenix?\"","The smile on the young man's face instantly disappeared.","\"Oh? How did you figure it out? I purposefully suppressed my aura to hide it.\"","“Just a guess,\" Yuan said. \"I figured that if the Celestial Emperor wanted the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans present at this gathering, he would also want the Primordial Phoenix to attend. Also, while you can hide your aura, you can't stop the others from giving you glances.\"","“I see... so the others sold me out.\"","Realizing his cover had been exposed, the young man released the restraint on his aura, letting it surge forth and flood the entire chamber."]},{"number":2130,"title":"Chapter 2130: Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Gathering(5)","paragraphs":["\"So, you want me to prove my identity as the Immortal Monarch by forcing you to kneel, is that it?\" Yuan asked.","“That's right. Do you have any issues with my request?\" The Primordial Phoenix said. \"Honestly, that's far too boring, as it would take no effort at all. Besides, I've no desire to humiliate the Celestial Emperor's lapdog and give him yet another reason to hate me.\" The Primordial Phoenix trembled after hearing Yuan's words, and he muttered, \"What did you just call me? A lapdog? I am nobody's lapdog, you bastard!\"","“Oh? If you're not the Celestial Emperor's lapdog, what are you? His slave?\"","Flames erupted from the Primordial Phoenix's body, weaving around him as they formed an armor of pure fire.","“You know what? I don't care if you're the Immortal Monarch or not. You're not going to leave this place until I teach you how to respect a superior being.\"","\"So quick to resort to violence? Your temper is quite short-even by phoenix standards,” Yuan said with a light chuckle.","“I will not be mocked by a mere human!\" the Primordial Phoenix roared, thrusting his right hand-wreathed in True Primordial Fire-toward Yuan's neck.","Young Master!\" Feng Yuxiang cried, instinctively seizing the Primordial Phoenix's arm. Her eyes burned with killing intent as she snapped, \"How dare you lay a hand on my Young Master! Do you have a death wish?!\"","The Primordial Phoenix sneered at her. \"This doesn't concern you.\"","\"Of course, it concerns me! You're attacking my—\"","“It's okay.\" Yuan interrupted. \"His flames are too weak to harm me, anyway.\"","“Not only did you insult me, but you dare to look down on my fire?\" The Primordial Phoenix trembled in anger.","In the very next moment, his entire body erupted with invisible flames, so intense they warped the surrounding space.","The True Primordial Fire instantly engulfed the chamber's center and swallowed both Yuan and Feng Yuxiang within its blaze.","Just as dragons possess reverse scales that drive them into madness when touched, phoenixes, 100, have their own reverse scales—their flames, which are their identity and pride. For many phoenixes, their flames are more precious than life itself. To have them insulted is an offense most people cannot fathom.","“Senior Feng Danyu, please calm yourself! We're still at the Undying Fiery Summit, which, regardless of your bloodline, forbids violence! This is a sacred rule passed down by our ancestors!\" The other phoenixes quickly warned him.","Though Feng Danyu, the Primordial Phoenix, was seething with rage, he had not lost all reason. Regaining control, he swiftly withdrew his True Primordial Fire. Yet the damage was already done, and the phoenixes could only pray for Yuan—for no human could possibly withstand the True Primordial Fire.","“What?! He's completely unscathed!\"","When the phoenixes looked closer, their shock deepened, as Yuan bore no wounds at all, not even the faintest trace of a burn.","\"How is that possible...? Could he have achieved Fire Harmony? No... even that wouldn't grant complete protection against True Primordial Fire since it bypasses all fire resistance!\"","Yuan ignored the shocked phoenixes and focused solely on Feng Daoyu.","“Since you attacked me first, I finally have a reason to mess with you.\"","“What are you—\"","Feng Daoyu opened his mouth to speak, but before he could utter more than a few words, Yuan cut him off. \"Shut up.\"","2m","In that instant, Feng Daoyu's mouth closed. When he tried to open it again, he found he had completely lost control. He tried forcefully opening his mouth with his hands, but such efforts were also futile, almost as if his lips had been glued shut.","The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans swallowed nervously upon seeing this, but they continued to watch in silence.","Yet Feng Daoyu refused to relent. In his struggle, he suddenly unleashed his cultivation base, revealing himself to be at the 7th level of the God Ascension realm.","The moment he unleashed his cultivation, Feng Daoyu broke free from Yuan's command.","“That doesn't prove anything!\" he shouted.","“Then how about this?\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes and commanded in a stern tone, his voice amplified by Immortal Qi.","“Lie on the ground and crawl around like a worm,\" he commanded.","“What are you—\"","Feng Daoyu was cut off once more as his body suddenly crumpled to the ground, thrashing and writhing like a worm dragged from the soil.","Of course, Feng Daoyu managed to break free within seconds, but by then, the damage had already been done.","“Is that still not enough to prove my identity? If not, then I know only one other way—and that is to forcibly extract your blood essence,’ Yuan said in a somewhat threatening tone.","“You wouldn't dare!” Feng Daoyu exclaimed as he subconsciously backed away from Yuan.","Yuan shrugged, \"You're right. Even if you are the Celestial Emperor's pet, I am not cruel enough to use such a vicious technique on you.\"","“For the last time, I am not the Celestial Emperor's lapdog, slave, or pet! Just like the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans, I merely agreed to assist him!\"","\"Oh? In exchange for what? I doubt you'd be willing to work for free.\"","“T-That is none of your business!\"","“If you don't want to tell me, I won't pry,\" Yuan said.","“Then, do you believe that I am the Immortal Monarch?\"","Feng Daoyu clenched his fists tightly and growled, \"I believe you—but so what? Even if you are the Immortal Monarch, don't think that alone will make me respect or revere yout\"","Yuan smiled behind his mask and said, \"I couldn't care less about how you treat me. I am only trying to prove my identity so the Ten Royal Phoenix Clan won't have to worry about me being a fraud.\"","\"Why?\" one of the clan leaders suddenly asked. \"Why are you trying to make us choose you over the Celestial Emperor? Can we not work with both sides?\"","\"Because the Celestial Emperor and I are enemies, and we'll likely clash with each other in the future,” Yuan revealed calmly, dumbfounding everyone in the room."]},{"number":2131,"title":"Chapter 2131: End of the Meeting","paragraphs":["\"W-Wait a second! I must've misheard you... Did you just say you're enemies with the Celestial Emperor?\" the leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan asked aloud, snapping out of her daze.","Yuan calmly nodded, \"That's exactly what I just said.\"","“You're essentially asking us to fight the Celestial Emperor with you! This is much more than just being your follower! Do you have any idea what you're asking of us?\" Another leader exclaimed.","“I am aware, but I want to clear up one thing,\" said Yuan. \"I am not asking you to fight the Celestial Emperor. I wanted to let you know that he and I will be fighting in the future, so you know what you're getting yourselves into. I'm not going to ask you to fight for or with me.\"","\"Are you serious? Why would you even share this with us? What if we refuse to help you and side with the Celestial Emperor instead?\" asked the leader of the Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan.","Yuan replied, \"Because now you also know that siding with the Celestial Emperor may put you in direct conflict with me in the future. I won't force you to choose. If everyone here decides to support the Celestial Emperor, then so be it.\"","\"And I'm not asking you to decide right this moment. I'l give you one year to choose whose side you'll stand on.\"","\"Hahaha!\" the Primordial Phoenix suddenly burst into laughter.","“What's so funny?\" Yuan asked him.","“It's funny because the answer is obvious!\" he said.","\"Oh? Enlighten me.\"","“Why would we ever choose you over the Celestial Emperor? So what if you're the immortal Monarch? You're nowhere near as powerful as you once were.\"","\"And what makes you say that?\" Yuan asked calmly.","The other phoenixes listened with curiosity as the Primordial Phoenix sneered.","“I know more about you than you realize, Immortal Monarch. I know that most of your reputation was built on the Nine Divine Supremes and that most of your strength came from them. But now that they're gone, you're just another human cultivator! Sure, you might command beasts and enhance our bloodlines, but on your own, you're weak!\" Hearing the Primordial Phoenix's reasoning, the other phoenixes found his logic sound and began nodding in agreement.","\"He's right, Immortal Monarch. You were a nobody before you gained the Nine Divine Supremes’ support,\" said the leader of the Immortal Ember Phoenix Clan.","“That's why he wants us to serve him. He's desperately trying to replace the Nine Divine Supremes!\" Another phoenix remarked.","“I don't need a year to decide. I will continue being by the Celestial Emperor's side,\" said the Primordial Phoenix.","Yuan smiled faintly and said, \"You're right—my reputation spread far and wide largely because of the Nine Divine Supremes. But even if some of them are no longer here, their seats will not remain vacant forever. In fact, I have already begun looking for more comrades.\"","\"And you're looking at one right now.\" Feng Yuxiang said with a prideful expression on her face.","“Wait... the way you said that... it almost sounds like some of the Nine Divine Supremes are still alive,” remarked Feng Yushan of the Heavenly Phoenix Clan.","“Is that so hard to believe? If I, the Immortal Monarch, am standing right before you, why couldn't the others still be alive?\"","The room fell into silence. If even one of the Nine Divine Supremes still existed in this era, it would be enough to shift the balance of the world.","“Wait! I just remembered—there's a rumor that the Dragon Goddess Yeyou has returned!” someone suddenly exclaimed. \"I dismissed it as nonsense before... but given the circumstances, it might actually be true!”","“I also heard of this rumor!\" Another remarked.","\"Me too!\"","“Is it true? That Dragon Goddess Yeyou is still alive?!\" One of them asked Yuan.","Dragon Goddess Yeyou was the strongest of the Nine Divine Supremes. If she were truly alive, she alone would be enough to handle the Celestial Emperor.","However, Yuan shrugged and said, *I don't know.\"","“What...2\" The phoenixes looked at him with wide eyes.","He continued, *I have already said enough. Unless I am certain that you're going to be my ally, I won't reveal any more information.\"","“With that said, I am going to end the meeting here. And just a reminder. The first three clans to swear their loyalty to me will have their bloodlines improved—possibly upgraded—as well as other benefits. Those who do so afterward wil still have their bloodlines improved, but that's all. You have one year to decide.\"","Without another word, Yuan left the Undying Fiery Summit.","“What are you going to do for a whole year?\" Feng Yuxiang asked him.","“I'm going to consume the Dragon Ancestor's blood essence to prepare for the Primordial Realm,\" he calmly replied.","“What if the Rising Phoenix Clan refuses to hand over the Ancient Seal and sides with the Celestial Emperor?\"","“If they side with the Celestial Emperor and become our enemy, we can only forcefully take the Ancient Seal from them. That said, I have a good feeling they'll side with us.\" Meanwhile, shortly after Yuan left, the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans remained at the Undying Feiry Summit and began another meeting.","\"So, what do we think about the Immortal Monarch's offer?\" The leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan asked.","“It's a tempting offer, and I would've definitely accepted it without a heartbeat if he hadn't mentioned being the Celestial Emperor's enemy.\"","“Well, he did say that he won't make us fight the Celestial Emperor if we don't want to.\" “Then why is he even trying to gain our loyalty if not to use us against the Celestial Emperor?\"","\"Perhaps it's so that he won't have to deal with us alongside the Celestial Emperor?\" “That actually makes sense. He's already fighting the Celestial Emperor. If I were in his shoes, I wouldn't want to fight our Ten Royal Phoenix Clans, either.\"","“You lot can stay here and continue wasting your time. I'm going to return to the Celestial Emperor to report to him about our situation,\" said the Primordial Phoenix as he began walking toward the exit."]},{"number":2132,"title":"Chapter 2132: Consuming the Dragon Ancestor’s Blood Essence","paragraphs":["\"You're leaving already? You don't care about who will choose to side with the Immortal Monarch or not?\" The leader of the Etheral Phoenix Clan asked, halting the Primordial Phoenix's movement. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)","\"Honestly? I couldn't care less. If you're foolish enough to side with the Immortal Monarch and go against the Celestial Emperor, then you deserve whatever fate awaits you,\" he sneered.","Then, without waiting for their response, the Primordial Phoenix continued walking toward the exit, leaving the chamber shortly later.","Just as he left the building, the Primordial Phoenix noticed a certain figure approaching the summit. It was Feng Yuxiang.","\"What are you doing back here? Forgot to say something?\" The Primordial Phoenix asked her in a somewhat sarcastic tone.","\"Well, someone has to stay behind for those who want to swear their loyalty before the one-year deadline,\" she said.","\"Is that so? You're wasting your time. The Royal Phoenix Clan will not side with the Immortal Monarch.\" \"You sound certain. Where's your confidence coming from?\"","The Primordial Phoenix smiled and said, \"The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans may have ten different clans, but in the end, they all listen to the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan. As long as the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan chooses the Celestial Emperor, the others will follow.\"","\"Even if that is true, there's no guarantee the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan won't choose the Immortal Monarch,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","\"No, it's guaranteed that they won't.\"","Feng Yuxiang narrowed her eyes at him. The Primordial Phoenix was showing such confidence that she couldn't help but worry.","\"I would tell you more, but I am not foolish enough to reveal sensitive information to an enemy. However, if you leave the Immortal Monarch's side-\"","\"Are you mocking me?\" Feng Yuxiang interrupted, her eyes flickering with killing intent. \"There's no reality where I will abandon my Young Master. Frankly, I'm insulted that you think there's even a chance of that happening.\"","The Primordial Phoenix shrugged, \"Then stay with him. I'd much rather be the only Primordial Phoenix in existence, anyway.\"","Without another word, the Primordial Phoenix disappeared from the summit.","Feng Yuxiang entered the building and returned to the chamber moments later.","\"Did you forget something?\" The phoenixes asked her.","\"No, I am here for those who have already decided and want to be the first three to serve my Young Master,\" she said. \"I can also answer any questions you may have.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan made his way to Feng Yuxiang's Immortal Cave, where he prepared to consume the Dragon Ancestor's blood essence.","Before consuming the Dragon Ancestor's blood essence, Yuan activated True Dragon Awakening to assist with the process.","Once he was prepared, Yuan poured the blood essence into his mouth and immediately closed it. However, he opened his mouth again the very next moment and released a dragon-like roar that shook the entire dimension.","<You have consumed the Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence>","<Immortal Monarch's Bloodline is reacting to Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence>","<Nine Dragon Symbols has activated>","<Nine Dragon Symbols has begun refining the Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence, enhancing its potency>","The blood essence surged with such immense energy that Yuan felt his body swelling like an overfilled balloon. As always, it came hand in hand with unbearable pain-but by now, Yuan was accustomed to it. His tolerance had grown to such extremes that even having his limbs torn from his body would hardly faze him.","While Yuan absorbed the Dragon Ancestor's blood essence, the Primordial Phoenix returned to the Supreme Heaven to report the situation to the Celestial Emperor.","\"The Immortal Monarch, huh?\" The Celestial Emperor was not surprised by the Immortal Monarch's return.","\"That man claimed to be your enemy. Is that true?\" The Primordial Phoenix suddenly asked.","The Celestial Emperor fell silent for a moment before responding, \"Honestly, I don't consider him an enemy.\"","\"Excuse me?\" The Primordial Phoenix raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","The Celestial Emperor continued, \"I have never met him personally, much less spoken to him, so I don't have any feelings or hatred toward him. However, he is someone that shouldn't exist someone that I must get rid of.\"","\"May I ask why?\" asked the Primordial Phoenix.","\"It is just one of my many duties as the Celestial Emperor,\" he calmly replied, offering a vague answer.","\"In that case, should I eliminate him?\" the Primordial Phoenix asked.","The Celestial Emperor shook his head.","\"No... not yet. He's like an explosive with an overly sensitive trigger, and the slightest touch could set off a catastrophic detonation. Wait for my orders. I'll let you know when it's safe.\"","\"I understand. What about the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans? Although I'm very confident they won't leave our side, there's always a chance for something to go awry.\"","\"While the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans are very useful, they won't pose any threat even if they were to join the Immortal Monarch's side. That said, I won't tolerate any betrayal, especially if it's to help that","calamity.\"","\"I can eliminate those who betray us, right?\" The Primordial Phoenix asked.","The Celestial Emperor calmly nodded.","\"Very well.\" A cold smile appeared on the Primordial Phoenix's face.","Sometime later, after the Primordial Phoenix left, the Celestial Emperor made his way to his private world, where he'd spend the next several days staring at a screen that displayed several slumbering entities.","\"The Immortal Monarch... the bastard who dared to lay his filthy paws on you has returned. And as much as I want to rip his throat out, I cannot directly touch him, as my lack of influence could ruin your revenge...\"","The Celestial Emperor's body suddenly stiffened as his eyes caught something in the display.","\"It can't be...\" he muttered, his frame trembling.","Though subtle, one of the entities had stirred ever so slightly-a sign that it was beginning to awaken.","Time passed quickly, and in the blink of an eye, six months had passed since the meeting. After the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans' discussion with each other ended, they left the Undying Fiery Summit to return home and continue discussing Yuan's offer with the rest of their family."]},{"number":2133,"title":"Chapter 2133: A Month Before the Deadline","paragraphs":["\"It's already been half a year, and not a single clan has sided with the Young Master...\" Feng Yuxiang sighed, her voice echoing softly through the empty chamber.","The words of the Primordial Phoenix still lingered in her mind, gnawing at her optimism day after day.","She couldn't help but wonder what would happen if none of the Royal Phoenix Clans chose to side with Yuan and instead continued their allegiance to the Celestial Emperor.","A few days later, the chamber doors creaked open, and a lone figure stepped inside.","Feng Yuxiang turned, expecting to see one of the clan leaders-only to be disappointed.","\"Oh... It's just you,\" she muttered, her tone tinged with disappointment. \"What do you want?\"","Feng Haoyu bowed slightly and said, \"I wish to swear my allegiance to the Immortal Monarch-or rather, to reaffirm my loyalty to him.\"","\"That's cool and all, but what about your family? Where are they?\"","Feng Haoyu let out a heavy sigh. \"It's complicated. While most of my clan wishes to follow the Immortal Monarch, they can't simply pledge loyalty without first seeing what the others decide. In other words... they're waiting.\"","\"That's bullshit,\" Feng Yuxiang said with a deep frown. \"Why should it matter what the others do? The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans are separate clans, not one united background.\"","Feng Haoyu shook his head. \"You probably don't know this since you were barely with us, but despite the name, the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan holds the most authority. In the end, their word is what carries the most weight.\"","\"Why is it that way?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Because originally, there was only one Royal Phoenix Clan-the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan. But after the Ten Royal Dragon Clans were established, they chose to expand their influence by mirroring the dragon clans, creating the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans.\"","The dragon and phoenix clans had been rivals since ancient times. Unwilling to fall behind the Ten Royal Dragon Clans, the phoenixes established their own Royal Clans, selecting the most qualified among them to rise to that position.","\"So you're telling me that unless the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan sides with the Young Master, the others will not do so?\"","\"Well, it's not impossible, but it's very unlikely.\"","\"I cannot fathom why they would choose the Celestial Emperor over the Immortal Monarch. Yes, the Celestial Emperor is powerful and influential, but their bloodlines would benefit far more under the Immortal Monarch,\" Feng Yuxiang said with a sigh, shaking her head in frustration.","\"Honestly,\" Feng Haoyu replied, \"while the Immortal Monarch was a legendary figure in the past, countless years have passed since then. To the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans, who never had any direct ties to him, he doesn't really hold a place in their eyes.\"","Hearing this, Feng Yuxiang fell silent.","Unlike the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans shared no ties with the Immortal Monarch. The Heavenly White Tiger Clan's ancestor had been one of the Nine Divine Supremes, so their reverence was only natural.","While the Immortal Monarch did have Feng Yuming, another Primordial Phoenix, she held no direct connection to the other phoenix clans and had spent most of her life wandering alone.","Feng Yuxiang had to admit that, although the Immortal Monarch was immensely influential, his era had long since passed and even during the height of his reign, not everyone chose to respect or revere him. \"What will you do if your family refuses to side with the Young Master?\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly asked. Feng Haoyu fell silent, his expression solemn as he pondered. After a moment, he replied, \"Honestly, I don't know. I may be the eldest son, but my influence in the clan is limited. There's no realistic chance I could convince them to follow the Immortal Monarch. And unless they exile me for my decision, it's not as if I could simply abandon them, either.\"","\"While we're on the subject... do you mind if I ask you a question?\"","Feng Yuxiang nodded.","\"What will the Immortal Monarch do if the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans-if my clan refuses to side with him? Will he go to war with them, too?\"","\"I cannot tell you what he might or might not do because I am not the Young Master. That said, he's a very reasonable individual, and he's not someone who will attack the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans without a good reason. Even if we do end up fighting them, I can guarantee you that he won't make you fight your family.\"","\"That's good enough for me.\" Feng Haoyu nodded.","'If we do end up fighting my family... what will I do?' he wondered inwardly.","Another five months slipped by.","Yet, with only a single month remaining before the deadline, not one of the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans had appeared at the summit-let alone to contend for the first three positions.","Meanwhile, at the Rising Phoenix Clan, the Grand Elder approached Feng Lingyang.","\"Clan leader... have you come to a decision yet? There's only one month left, and as far as I am aware, none of the other clans have sided with the Immortal Monarch yet.\"","\"No, not yet...\" she sighed. \"I apologize for being indecisive. I am such a useless leader.\"","\"I want to side with the Immortal Monarch, but doing so will definitely paint a target on my back for the others to aim. However, if I don't side with him, we would not only have to deal with the Immortal Monarch and his powerful allies, but we'll also have to fight my son.\"","\"Grand Elder, if you were in my position, what would you do?\" she asked, gazing at him intently.","\"I would side with the Immortal Monarch,\" the Grand Elder replied without the slightest hesitation, leaving Feng Lingyang utterly dumbfounded.","He smiled and continued, \"Honestly, if it weren't for my position, just like the Young Lord, I would've already sworn my loyalty to him.\"","\"T-That was a quick response... almost as if you were ready to say it at any moment. Can you explain your reasoning?\" she asked. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2134,"title":"Chapter 2134: The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Decision","paragraphs":["\"My reasoning, huh? It's actually quite simple. I know you're worried about the other Royal Phoenix Clans, but once we side with the Immortal Monarch, their stance won't matter anymore. In fact, even the title of 'Royal Clan' will lose its weight,\" said the Grand Elder.","\"What...?\" Feng Lingyang's eyes widened. His reasoning wasn't what she expected, yet the more she considered it, the more sense it made.","The Grand Elder continued, \"Even if we're the only clan to follow the Immortal Monarch, the others won't dare touch us with him behind us. But if we side with the Celestial Emperor, we'll inevitably end up clashing with the Immortal Monarch-and if you ask me, I believe his strength surpasses the Celestial Emperor's.\"","\"Is it because of Dragon Goddess Yeyou?\" Feng Lingyang asked.","\"Not just her,\" he replied. \"Though he didn't state it outright, I believe-based on his words-that other Divine Supremes have also survived. And if the Immortal Monarch defeats the Celestial Emperor, our Rising Phoenix Clan will undoubtedly soar to the top, where we won't even need the title of 'Royal Clan.\"\" \"That's just pure speculation, and you can say the same thing for the others. If the Celestial Emperor defeats the Immortal Monarch, that would undoubtedly spell the end for our Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"It all comes down to whether you want to believe in the Celestial Emperor or the Immortal Monarch.\" The Grand Elder sighed.","Feng Lingyang didn't give a response. Instead, after a long moment of silence, she said, \"I'm going to the Undying Fiery Summit.\"","\"I'll come with you.\"","Sometime later.","\"Mother? Grand Elder?\" Feng Haoyu's face lit up as he saw the two enter the chamber.","Feng Lingyang's gaze swept across the room before settling on Feng Yuxiang.","\"Where is the Immortal Monarch?\" she asked.","\"He hasn't returned yet. If you have any questions, I'll be more than willing to answer them.\"","\"I would like to know why the Celestial Emperor and the Immortal Monarch are enemies. What started the feud between them?\"","\"That's...\" Feng Yuxiang began, only to close her mouth again, realizing she had no answer to give.","\"I'm sorry-I don't know the exact cause. But what I can say with certainty is that it was the Celestial Emperor who showed hostility first. He cursed my Young Master even though they've never met each other before.\"","Feng Lingyang raised her eyebrows and replied in a doubtful tone, \"The Celestial Emperor cursed the Immortal Monarch even though they've never met before? That's hard to believe and completely irrational.\"","\"I understand your skepticism, and I am just as puzzled, but it's the truth. Have you heard about the incident at the Dragon Spiral Mountain recently?\"","\"You mean when the Celestial Emperor attacked the Holy Dragon Clan? I am aware of the incident, but nobody knows the reasoning behind his action.\"","\"It's related to my Young Master,\" Feng Yuxiang revealed.","\"Seriously...?\" Those present stared at her with wide eyes.","\"If you want to know more, you'll have to ask my Young Master himself.\"","Feng Lingyang nodded, \"Okay.\"","While they waited for Yuan to return, Feng Haoyu approached Feng Lingyang and asked, \"Mother, has the clan reached a decision yet?\"","\"As you know, the majority of the clan are in support of siding with the Immortal Monarch, but in the end","\"It's all up to you,\" Feng Haoyu interrupted.","\"I have also made a decision, but I want to know the reasoning behind their enmity first.\"","Time continued to pass, and in the blink of an eye, an entire year had passed since the end of the meeting.","A few days before the deadline, the other Royal Phoenix Clans returned to the Undying Fiery Summit.","\"Where's the Immortal Monarch?\" They asked upon their arrival.","\"He's not here yet, but he should arrive soon,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","\"Feng Lingyang, did the Rising Phoenix Clan swear their loyalty to the Immortal Monarch already?\" The leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan questioned her after seeing that she'd arrived before them.","\"No.\" Feng Lingyang replied with a simple and straightforward answer.","\"Are you sure? I heard that you arrived a month early,\" pressed the leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan.","\"So what?\"","The atmosphere in the chamber grew heavy, tension pressing down on everyone present.","But it shattered the moment the door opened and a lone figure stepped inside, drawing every gaze in the","room.","However, it wasn't Yuan.","\"What are you doing here? Weren't you clear about siding with the Celestial Emperor? Or have you changed your mind?\" Feng Yuxiang asked the Primordial Phoenix, who had just entered the chamber.","The Primordial Phoenix sneered. \"In your dreams. I'm only here to watch the show-and to savor the disappointment on the Immortal Monarch's face when he realizes that he's no longer relevant in this day and age.\"","He looked around the room and continued, \"So, where's the Immortal Monarch?\"","\"He'll arrive as soon as he's done with his business.\"","\"He's the one who made the deadline, yet he's the last to show up? It's almost like he doesn't even care.\" \"Calm down, little bird. It's not like I am late.\"","A calm voice suddenly resounded.","\"What?\" The Primordial Phoenix and everyone else in the chamber turned toward the entrance-only to see Yuan standing there, having appeared out of thin air.","\"The hell? How long has he been there? I didn't sense a thing until he spoke!\"","Everyone in the chamber was shaken by his complete lack of presence.","\"This bastard... what has he done in the past year? He feels like an entirely different person!\"","Though none of them could explain it, they all felt it. Something within Yuan had changed drastically, and he was vastly different from when they last saw him a year ago.","Yuan ignored their stares and strode unhurriedly to the center of the chamber.","His eyes swept across the gathered phoenixes as he spoke in a calm, clear voice, \"So, have you reached","a decision? Will you continue to serve the Celestial Emperor, or will you stand beneath my banner?\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2135,"title":"Chapter 2135: The Ten Royal Phoenix Clans’ Decision(2)","paragraphs":["\"Before we begin, I would like to ask you something.\"","Feng Lingyang suddenly stepped forward.","\"Go ahead.\" Yuan calmly nodded.","\"Why are you enemies with the Celestial Emperor?\"","\"A good question. Unfortunately, I do not know the answer to that question.\"","\"What? You don't know why you're enemies with the Celestial Emperor? How's that even possible?\" said the leader of the Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan.","\"I bet you he's making it up,\" said the Primordial Phoenix.","\"What would I gain from making this up? I've never even met the Celestial Emperor. Yet, he placed a curse on me for some reason.\"","\"Are you trying to claim that the Celestial Emperor showed you hostility for no reason? Sorry, but I don't believe that,\" said the leader of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan.","The Primordial Phoenix burst into laughter. \"You're so desperate to paint the Celestial Emperor as a villain, but all you're doing is making yourself look like a fool!\"","He turned to face the others and spoke loudly, \"Is this really someone you want to serve?! A jealous, arrogant, and foolish human like him?\"","The room fell into silence.","But it did not last long, for it was soon broken by the leader of the Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan, who declared firmly, \"The Crimson Rebirth Phoenix Clan rejects your offer, Immortal Monarch. We will continue to stand with the Celestial Emperor.\"","Then, like a chain reaction, the others began voicing their decisions.","\"The Immortal Ember Phoenix Clan refuses your offer, Immortal Monarch.\"","\"The Burning Lotus Phoenix Clan also refuses.\"","\"The Radiant Phoenix Clan refuses...\"","One after another, the rejections echoed through the chamber, pouring in without pause.","\"My Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan rejects your offer.\"","\"Looks like no one's willing to side with you, huh? Just as I predicted,\" the Primordial Phoenix mocked.","Yet despite the wave of rejections, Yuan remained calm and composed.","Eventually, only a single clan had yet to respond-the one clan that still hadn't refused Yuan's offer.","\"Mother...\" Feng Haoyu looked at his mother, his face tight with worry.","The others in the chamber turned their glares upon her, and under the crushing weight of their stares, Feng Lingyang swallowed hard, her body trembling.","\"What's wrong, Feng Lingyang? We're all waiting for you,\" said Feng Tianhuang, the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan's leader.","Feng Lingyang closed her eyes and took several deep breaths. When she opened her eyes again, they flickered with resolution.","\"The Rising Phoenix Clan will accept your offer, Immortal Monarch,\" Feng Lingyang declared.","Feng Haoyu and the Grand Elder's faces lit up with joy at her words, while the other clans openly displayed their disappointment and disdain, making no effort to conceal it.","\"What is the meaning of this, Feng Lingyang?\" Feng Tianhuang stepped forward, her body radiating oppressive pressure.","\"Explain yourself!\" she demanded.","Feng Lingyang met her gaze steadily. \"Why should I need to explain myself? While I am grateful to the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan for allowing us into the ranks of the Royal Phoenix Clans, you do not own us-nor do we owe you an explanation. Still, as a courtesy, I'll tell you. As clan leader, I have an obligation to heed the will of my people, and the vast majority wish to follow the Immortal Monarch. Quite simple, isn't it?\"","\"You will regret your decision.\"","\"I'll deal with it when that time comes.\"","Feng Tianhuang sneered. \"As much as I'd like to expel the Rising Phoenix Clan from the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans right this moment, protocol must be followed. That said, it will take little effort to see you removed.\"","\"Then allow me to save you the trouble,\" Feng Lingyang declared. \"From this moment onward, the Rising Phoenix Clan renounces its title and withdraws from the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans. From now on, we shall stand as an independent clan once more.\"","The room fell into stunned silence, the atmosphere growing oppressively heavy. None of the other phoenix clans had ever anticipated such an outcome.","Though none of them spoke aloud, a few secretly admired Feng Lingyang's courage. She had dared to stand up for herself when they could not. In truth, some among them also wished to side with the Immortal Monarch-but fear of the Imperial Vermilion Phoenix Clan and the Primordial Phoenix kept them silent.","\"You will not regret your decision,\" Yuan's voice suddenly rang out, shattering the silence.","\"From this moment on, the Rising Phoenix Clan is under my protection. Should anyone dare to harm them, -the Immortal Monarch-will unleash my full power to destroy the offender.\"","Yuan's words were not merely a welcome to the Rising Phoenix Clan. They were also a warning-if any dared to retaliate against them for their choice, he would personally see to their destruction.","\"Let's go. We've already wasted enough time here,\" Feng Tianhuang declared coldly before turning on her heels. Her robes flared as she strode toward the exit, her aura sharp enough to cut the air.","Without another word, the remaining phoenix clans, their expressions ranging from disdain to unease, silently followed her out of the chamber.","\"So you've managed to deceive one clan to your side, huh?\" The Primordial Phoenix, who decided to linger a little longer, remarked.","Yuan looked directly at the Primordial Phoenix and asked, \"So, are you going to attack us now?\"","The Primordial Phoenix smirked. \"Why would I do that?\"","\"I wouldn't be surprised if the Celestial Emperor had ordered you to 'take care' of us.\"","A scoff escaped the Primordial Phoenix's lips. \"Still trying to make the Celestial Emperor look like a villain, huh? Sorry, but it won't work. Although you've stirred up trouble for the Royal Phoenix Clans, you've done nothing that warrants punishment. Clans breaking ties or shifting allegiance are things that happen constantly in the cultivation world. It's nothing new or illegal.\"","His tone was dismissive, but the cold gleam in his eyes made it clear that he wasn't very pleased about the outcome, as he'd expected a complete victory. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2136,"title":"Chapter 2136: Immortal Monarch’s Grand Blessing","paragraphs":["After a brief silence, the Primordial Phoenix finally spoke, \"Though I cannot punish you for luring the Rising Phoenix Clan to your side, I can certainly punish you for slandering the Celestial Emperor's name.\"","\"Just because you refuse to believe it doesn't make it slander,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Still, if you wish to fight, I'll be more than willing to oblige.\"","The Primordial Phoenix silently swept his gaze over Yuan and the others in the chamber. Alongside Yuan and Feng Yuxiang stood Feng Lingyang, Feng Haoyu, and the Grand Elder. Though his cultivation surpassed them all, he ultimately chose not to act.","\"You should be grateful the Celestial Emperor forbade me from touching you,\" the Primordial Phoenix said. \"At least, for now.\"","Yuan raised his brows in surprise.\"Oh? The Celestial Emperor told you not to fight me? How unusual... or perhaps he intends to deal with me personally?\"","\"The Celestial Emperor has far more important matters than wasting time on an insect like you.\" The Primordial Phoenix sneered, then turned and strode toward the exit.","\"Of course, the same goes for me.\"","After saying that, the Primordial Phoenix left the room and disappeared from the summit shortly after.","\"So... what now?\" Feng Yuxiang turned to look at Yuan and asked.","\"Let's return to the Rising Phoenix Clan for now,\" he said.","\"Alright.\"","As they traveled, Yuan said, \"I will fulfill my promise to you and strengthen the entire Rising Phoenix Clan. Once we arrive, can you gather everyone for me?\"","Feng Lingyang immediately nodded in agreement.","Before long, they returned to the Rising Phoenix Clan's territory. At Yuan's request, Feng Lingyang swiftly summoned every member of the clan. Yet even before she could announce the results of their journey, the clan members already understood the outcome, as Yuan's very presence within their grounds spoke louder than words.","\"As you may have already realized, your leader has accepted my offer. From this day forward, the Rising Phoenix Clan stands under my command.\"","\"If you are unwilling to follow me, I will grant you the chance to leave now,\" Yuan declared. \"There is no need for words or explanations-simply depart in silence, and no punishment will follow.\"","He then stood in patient silence, giving time to those who wished to go. After several minutes, a handful of figures quietly took to the skies, vanishing into the distance without a trace. Yet, despite their departure, the overwhelming majority of the clan remained.","\"Anyone else?\" he asked.","When the remaining members shook their heads, Yuan nodded. \"Very well. As a reward for choosing to stand with me, I will bestow upon you all a blessing.\"","With a single gesture, Yuan directed his will toward the gathered clan members. At once, the heavens above bloomed with radiant golden symbols, each one pulsing with profound might.","\"Those who choose to serve me, accept the Immortal Monarch's symbol. From that moment forth, you shall be my followers, and my decree shall be your law.\"","One by one, the clan members reached out to the golden symbols, allowing them to sink into their bodies and fuse with their Dantians.","Once everyone had accepted his symbol, Yuan activated another skill.","<Immortal Monarch's Grand Blessing has been activated>","In the blink of an eye, a wave of radiant power swept across the Rising Phoenix Clan. Unlike an ordinary blessing, the Grand Blessing etched its effects permanently into the bodies of all who had accepted his symbol.","\"This feeling! My body... It's overflowing with power!\"","Cries of astonishment echoed as the clan members suddenly felt their strength rising beyond imagination. \"This is the Immortal Monarch's power...? Feng Lingyang mumbled, her voice filled with awe. However, Yuan shook his head and said, \"This is just a simple blessing. The real thing begins now.\" Yuan pricked his fingertip, letting a stream of blood flow forth. It quickly condensed into a sphere the size of a fist, hovering in his palm. With a firm clench, the sphere burst apart, scattering into countless drops of crimson light. Guided by his will, one drop entered the mouth of every clan member present.","The clan members shuddered in ecstasy, their senses overwhelmed by the peerless taste of his blood, a flavor surpassing every delicacy they had encountered in their lives.","\"I just fed each of you a drop of my blood. Soon, your bloodline purity will improve,\" he said to them a moment later.","\"Just like that?!\"","\"If you can't believe it, you can test your bloodline,\" Yuan remarked.","\"Hand me the Golden Phoenix Needle!\" Feng Lingyang commanded loudly.","The next moment, one of the elders approached her with the needle in hand.","Feng Lingyang immediately tested her bloodline while everyone watched in anticipation.","When the results appeared seconds later, Feng Lingyang's hands went limp. The Golden Phoenix Needle slipped from her grasp and clattered to the floor as she stood frozen, her face blank with shock.","\"Clan Leader?! What's wrong?!\" the Grand Elder cried, his voice laced with worry.","\"M-My bloodline...\" she whispered in a daze. Too shaken to form her thoughts into words, she simply lifted her trembling fingers and pointed toward the fallen needle.","The Grand Elder bent down and picked up the fallen Golden Phoenix Needle, his gaze fixed upon the results.","\"By the Heavens!\" he exclaimed, his voice trembling as his eyes grew wide with disbelief.","The other elders hastened to gather around him. When their eyes fell upon the results, their expressions froze, as though their very souls had been shaken.","\"91.2 percent?!\" one of the elders revealed.","\"What?!\" Gasps rippled through the crowd as the rest of the members heard the result, their surprise mirroring the elders' reactions. None of them, however, knew the hidden truth-that Feng Lingyang's bloodline had long been weakened by a curse, a secret known only to the elders and a select few.","Therefore, in their eyes, Feng Lingyang's bloodline had only increased by two percent, not six percent, as her bloodline had weakened to 85.2 percent. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2137,"title":"Chapter 2137: Acquiring the Final Ancient Seal","paragraphs":["\"M-My blood! I must test my bloodline!\" the Grand Elder stammered, quickly seizing the Golden Phoenix Needle after snapping out of his daze.","Moments later, his eyes widened, and he exclaimed with unrestrained joy, \"90.9 percent! My bloodline purity has surpassed ninety percent! This is a miracle!\"","Stirred by his words, the other elders hastily tested themselves as well. Sure enough, nearly all of them discovered that their bloodline purity had risen by four to five percent.","\"My lord! With only a single drop of your blood, our bloodlines have undergone unimaginable growth! And to think the Celestial Emperor only offered us no more than three percent!\" one of them exclaimed.","Yet even in their excitement, unease gnawed at their hearts, as the results seemed almost too good to be true.","\"Immortal Monarch, forgive my boldness, but... what kind of drawbacks should we expect from this?\" someone finally asked, instantly silencing the place.","The clamor of celebration died down at once, and every gaze there shifted to Yuan, their faces full of worry and realization. They all knew that although innumerable treasures existed beneath the heavens, many of them had effects that were more detrimental than beneficial.","Now that their excitement had died down and their minds had cleared up, they began wondering what sacrifices must be made for such a powerful boost to their bloodline.","However, what came out of Yuan's mouth in just a moment left them all stunned again.","\"Drawbacks? There are none. You can enjoy your improved bloodline without such needless worry.\"","\"Are you serious?\" Even Feng Lingyang couldn't believe it.","Yuan smiled and said, \"If you think I am lying, I can swear on my soul.\"","\"T-That won't be necessary! We believe you. It's just... I didn't expect such an overpowered ability to exist... Maybe that's why the Celestial Emperor is trying to get rid of you.\"","Yuan chuckled. \"If you think this is overpowered, just wait until I fully recover my strength.\"","\"Recover? Are you injured?\" Feng Haoyu asked in surprise.","\"No,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"I only reincarnated recently, so much of my power has yet to return.\"","\"I see...\" Feng Haoyu murmured.","\"Anyway, I have fulfilled the first part of our agreement. As for evolving your bloodline, you'll need to wait until I recover more of my strength, as I currently lacks the ability to do so.\"","Feng Lingyang nodded. \"Don't worry. We never expected you to improve our bloodline so quickly in the first place, much less evolve it.\"","\"Thank you for your understanding.\"","\"So... what is the plan now? What do you want the Rising Phoenix Clan to do?\" Feng Lingyang asked.","Yuan's expression grew solemn. \"For now, focus on training and familiarizing yourselves with your newfound strength. I cannot say when, but I am certain the Celestial Emperor and the other Royal Phoenix Clans will not stay still and will soon act.\"","Feng Lingyang sighed at his words, but she was not surprised. In fact, she anticipated something like this would happen and had already mentally prepared for it.","\"I don't know about the Celestial Emperor, but the Royal Phoenix Clans will definitely come after our clan for humiliating and defying them. However, I doubt they will come after us anytime soon-at least not until they figure out your prowess and whether or not they would be able to get away with it.\"","\"In that case, I'll leave the Phoenix Rising Clan for now and return later,\" said Yuan.","\"I understand.\"","\"Before I go...\" Yuan looked at Feng Lingyang and made a beckoning gesture with his hands.","Feng Lingyang stared at his hand with a puzzled face for a moment before she finally realized what he wanted from her.","\"G-Give me a minute! I'll grab 'that' for you now!\"","Without another word, Feng Lingyang flew away, disappearing deep into their territory.","About half an hour later, Feng Lingyang returned with a spatial ring in her grasp.","\"I'm sorry it took so long, but here is the thing you wanted,\" she said as she offered the ring to him.","Yuan accepted it and looked inside. Sure enough, the Ancient Seal was inside.","\"Thank you.\"","With the fourth and final Ancient Seal in his grasp, Yuan could finally enter the Primordial Realm and meet with Xiao Hua's family-the Asura Clan.","\"Can you tell me why you want the Ancient Seal now?\" Feng Lingyang asked.","Yuan smiled and said, \"The Ancient Seals only serve one purpose. What else am I going to do with it?\"","Feng Lingyang swallowed nervously.","'I knew he wanted to open the Primordial Realm, but I wanted to believe the Ancient Seal had other purposes...' she sighed inwardly.","\"Can I ask why you're trying to open it?\"","\"Some of my friends from the past are imprisoned within, and I intend to free them,\" Yuan said.","\"But the Primordial Realm is filled with...\" Feng Lingyang began, but she stopped herself before uttering","the word 'criminal'.","\"I know what you want to say, but not everyone inside the Primordial Realm is a criminal. The previous Celestial Emperors have imprisoned innocent people inside just for standing up to him.\"","\"Alright. I won't question it anymore. I'm sure you have your reasons.\"","Sometime later, before Yuan left the Rising Phoenix Clan's territory, he said to Feng Lingyang, \"If anyone dares to mess with your clan, don't hesitate to contact me.\"","Feng Lingyang nodded with a smile and said, \"Don't worry. Our Rising Phoenix Clan isn't so weak that anyone could bully us. We didn't earn the title Royal Phoenix Clan by luck, after all. However, if we do encounter a situation we cannot handle, we will definitely request your help.\"","\"Even if nothing happens, I'll visit once I regain enough power to evolve your bloodline.\"","\"What about me, Young Master? Is there anything I can do for you?\" Feng Haoyu asked.","\"Continue doing what you normally do. I'll contact you if I ever need your help.\"","\"As you command.\"","With that, Yuan left the Rising Phoenix Clan.","\"Are we going straight to the Primordial Realm?\" Feng Yuxiang asked Yuan shortly later.","He shook his head and replied, \"No, I still need to prepare some more.\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2138,"title":"Chapter 2138: A Hundred Million","paragraphs":["After leaving the Rising Phoenix Clan, Yuan traveled straight to his next destination to prepare for the Primordial Realm.","\"The Abyssal Underground? You wanted to come back here?\" Feng Yuxiang quickly realized where he was trying to go.","He nodded and explained, \"I still need a few more million kills to complete my quest, so I might as well finish it up before I head to the Primordial Realm.\"","The Primordial Realm was filled with dangerous Immortals and even God Ascension realm cultivators. If he wanted to traverse it safely, he needed to prepare properly for it.","Some time later, Yuan returned to the Abyssal Underground. This time, instead of looking for a guide, he flew straight into the entrance, disappearing into the void.","However, instead of starting his hunt at the 300th level, Yuan went as far as the 500th level, where the creatures were all between the 1st and 2nd level of God Ascension.","Once he ensured there was nobody nearby, he retrieved the Baneful Abyss and began spreading the poison mist, quickly gaining kills again.","As Yuan remained inside the Abyssal Underground, word of the Immortal Monarch's return surged through the Nine Heavens like a tempest, shaking every beast clan to its core. Though everyone was skeptical in the beginning, the moment it was revealed that the Royal Phoenix Clans themselves had spread the news, every shred of doubt was dispelled.","\"From what I heard, the Immortal Monarch vanished without a word after the Divine Heaven split, becoming the Nine Heavens. Where do you think he'd been this entire time?\"","\"I think only the Immortal Monarch will be able to answer that question.\"","\"The Immortal Monarch's return has serious implications. I can imagine things will get chaotic very soon, especially with the beast clans.\"","\"What do you think he's going to do now that he returns? Continue what he did in the past?\"","\"His goal in the past was to unify humans and beasts. Since we're co-existing with each other properly now, I bet he'll find other things to do.\"","As word of the Immortal Monarch's return spread to every corner of the world, it seemed as though the very heavens and earth resounded with his name, and for the next several months, one would not be able to go anywhere without hearing his name at least once.","Of course, in the realm of the beast clans, his name was uttered with even greater frequency, for the Immortal Monarch's legacy carried unparalleled weight among them.","\"The Immortal Monarch may have returned, but the Nine Divine Supremes are still gone...\"","\"Haven't you heard? Dragon Goddess Yeyou has also returned.\"","\"That's just one out of nine, though.\"","\"The Eater of Stars is also alive at least according to someone who last saw it wandering the Starry Sky several hundred years ago.\"","\"Isn't this an opportunity for us to replace those who are gone, though?\"","\"Replace them? You're delusional if you think you have the capability to become one of the Nine Divine Supremes.\"","\"I know that, you idiot. However, it doesn't change the fact that their positions are now open, and we may see new ones soon.\"","\"That is assuming the Immortal Monarch wants to replace them.\"","\"Haven't you heard? The Immortal Monarch has already begun recruiting people to his side, and the Rising Phoenix Clan has already offered its loyalty to him.\"","\"Huh? Isn't the Rising Phoenix Clan one of the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans?\"","\"Not anymore. They left the Royal Clans to join the Immortal Monarch.\"","Beast clans from every corner of the world began dispatching envoys to seek out the Immortal Monarch, knowing full well he would never come to them and that they would have to approach him themselves if they wished to stand by his side.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the Nine Heavens, a powerful pressure enveloped a vast area when a certain individual learned of the Immortal Monarch's return.","\"What?! That bastard is still alive and has returned?!\" The Great One roared, his voice loud enough to crack the space around him.","\"I swear, if you're messing with me, I'll fucking rip you limb from limb!\"","The messenger quickly replied, \"I swear on my soul that it's true! The entire world is talking about it!\"","\"Damn it! Why now of all time?\" The Great One gritted his teeth in frustration.","Just when he thought he could pursue Dragon Goddess Yeyou in peace, his biggest competition made a return.","\"Where?! Where is this bastard?\"","\"He was last seen at the Rising Phoenix Clan's territory, but nobody has seen or heard from him in a few weeks. Are you going to give them a visit?\"","The Great One narrowed his gaze. Then, after a moment of silence, he responded, \"Are you insane? Why would I seek him out when I don't even want to see that bastard? Get lost!\"","\"M-My apologies! This lowly subordinate will leave immediately!\" The messenger hurriedly disappeared from his presence.","\"Immortal Monarch... looks like the heavens are on my side and want to see me defeat you!\" The Great One laughed out loud, his voice causing the air to tremble.","Two months have passed since Yuan entered the Underground Abyssal.","[Progress: 100,000,000/100,000,000]","<You have fulfilled a requirement for the Unique Quest '???'>","\"Thank goodness for the Baneful Abyss's poisonous abilities. Without them, this quest would have taken far longer.\" Yuan shuddered at the thought of facing a hundred million foes without its convenient ability.","Having completed this requirement, Yuan now faced but a single remaining trial before he could resume the use of Heaven's Supremacy.","\"I will need to evolve my physique again before I can enter the True Immortal Realm.\"","He thought he would be able to force his way to the True Immortal Realm by consuming the Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence, but it didn't happen. However, he did gain several new abilities as a result.","\"Next stop, White Hell.\"","With his next destination decided, Yuan cleaned up the poison mist before leaving the Abyssal Underground. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2139,"title":"Chapter 2139: White Hell","paragraphs":["White Hell-a place so perilous it earned the name Gateway to Hell. There were four such forbidden lands within the Nine Heavens, and Yuan had already explored one of them, the Vanishing Valley.","Being one of the coldest places in the Nine Heavens, White Hell is a vast expanse of endless snow and towering mountains, shrouded in extreme cold. The chill is so severe that even those with strong cold resistance struggle to survive in its outer regions, let alone venture into its depths.","And yet, in spite of its peril and the countless lives it claims, White Hell draws thousands of cultivators every year-some to hone their strength, others to pursue the treasures buried within its icy depths.","All of this was made possible by the Sun God's Temple, a unique sanctuary where cultivators gathered to cultivate their Yang Qi. They also possessed a powerful treasure that, while unable to eliminate the cold of White Hell, granted enough resistance for cultivators to endure its frost and traverse its perilous lands. This treasure was known as the Sun God's Lake, a small yet extraordinary lake within the Sun God's Temple's territory. Not only was it one of the most sought-after training areas in the world, but it could even evolve one's physique. Naturally, it could not be taken into White Hell itself. Instead, it was used to imbue Sun Stones, small rock-like objects that shielded their bearers from the cold.","However, the Sun Stones carried limited power, losing their effectiveness after a certain period of time. To obtain one, cultivators had to approach the Sun God's Temple and make an offering in exchange, whether it be spirit stones or treasures.","Right outside the White Hell's entrance, several individuals wearing the Sun God's Temple's outfit could be seen talking to a group of female cultivators.","\"This here is the One-Year Sun Stone, which you will need to traverse White Hell safely.\"","In one member's hand rested a glowing pebble, radiating such immense Yang Qi that it warmed the air around them, even in the freezing cold.","\"It has soaked in the Sun God's Lake for a year, and it will last for ten years while inside White Hell.\"","Then, he produced another glowing stone, pulsing with even more intense Yang Qi. \"And this,\" he said, \"is a Hundred-Year Sun Stone. It will last for a hundred years in the outer regions, and its might is sufficient to defy the cold of the second region, reaching even into the third.\"","White Hell was divided into nine regions, beginning with the outer region. The deeper one ventured, the colder and more perilous it became. As for the Sun Stone, the most refined ones could allow a cultivator to venture safely into the fifth region. However, each stone needed to be immersed in the Sun God's Lake for over a million years, making them unimaginably expensive.","One might assume the Sun God's Temple could simply throw countless Sun Stones into the lake to satisfy demand. However, doing so would drain the lake's power, and since its primary purpose was as a training ground, the temple was unwilling to create too many.","\"I would like to venture into the fourth region,\" one of the female cultivators said.","\"Then you will need a Ten-Thousand-Year Sun Stone, and it will only last you ten years in the third region,\" said one of the Sun God Temple's disciples.","The female cultivator nodded and calmly handed a spatial pouch to the man.","\"Is this donation enough?\" she asked.","The disciple peeked into the spatial pouch and nodded, \"Yes, this is more than enough. Thank you for your donation. Here is a Ten-Thousand-Year Sun Stone.\"","He handed her the Sun Stone.","\"The Sun Stone will begin to lose its glow when it's near its limit, so make sure you leave White Hell the moment you see it.\"","\"I understand.\"","One by one, the female cultivators purchased a Sun Stone before stepping into White Hell.","A few hours later, another group of female cultivators arrived, their matching attire revealing that they belonged to the same sect.","\"I'd like to purchase 23 Hundred-Year Sun Stone.\"","The woman leading the group handed a spatial ring to one of the disciples, who then quickly checked the ring and handed the Sun Stones to them.","Minutes after they departed, another figure appeared at the entrance. This time it was not a beautiful female cultivator but a strikingly handsome man.","The disciples of the Sun God's Temple watched as he approached, expecting him to purchase a Sun Stone. To their surprise, however, the handsome man ignored them entirely and strode straight past.","\"W-Wait a second! Where are you going?\" One of the disciples subconsciously called out to him in a surprised tone.","The handsome man stopped walking and turned to look at him.","\"Where does it look like I am going?\" he calmly responded.","Another disciple spoke, \"Do you already have a Sun Stone?\"","\"A what?\"","The disciples were baffled by this man's ignorance. How could one even think about entering White Hell without their Sun Stone?","\"You don't even know what a Sun Stone is, and you're attempting to challenge White Hell? Are you courting death?\"","\"Listen here. The White Hell is a place where even cultivators with Cold Immunities are helpless. The only way you can traverse White Hell is with the help of the Sun God Temple's Sun Stone.\"","The handsome man smiled and asked, \"So, the Sun Stone keeps me safe from the cold within White Hell, is that correct?\"","\"That's right.\"","\"If you want-\"","The man interrupted and said, \"In that case, I don't need it.\"","\"Excuse me?\"","The disciples' eyes widened with surprise, wondering if they'd misheard him.","\"I came to White Hell to train, so the Sun Stone will only hinder me. Now, if you will excuse me.\"","Before the disciples could even open their mouths again, the handsome man turned around and continued moving toward White Hell, quickly vanishing into the snowstorm. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2140,"title":"Chapter 2140: White Hell(2)","paragraphs":["\"What a fool. What can he do without the Sun Stone? Even if he has Cold Resistance, he won't be able to withstand the cold enough to train properly.\" The disciples of the Sun God's Temple shook their heads at the handsome man who refused to heed their warning.","\"Forget it. There will always be arrogant people like that.\"","\"I doubt we'll ever see him again.\"","Unbeknownst to the disciples, the handsome man-Yuan-had no need for their Sun Stone. With the power of the Primordial Phoenix flowing within him, the cold of White Hell posed no threat. No matter how frigid its depths, his True Primordial Fire could easily protect him.","As Yuan crossed into the first region, he officially stepped into White Hell. The outer region stretched out as endless white plains buried beneath layers of snow. The drifts were so deep that walking on the ground was impossible, and only by flying through the skies could one traverse the land.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved slightly>","Despite possessing Supreme Cold Immunity-enough to remain unaffected even by the Extreme Yin Lake near the Frozen Cloud Ethereal Sect-the cold of White Hell was so intense that it had already begun tempering his resistance further.","\"This place sure is great. I'd just stepped into it, and my cold resistance is already improving with every passing second.\" Yuan mumbled with a satisfied smile on his face.","\"White Hell... it's been a long time since I last heard that name,\" Yu Ning remarked. \"I had nearly forgotten this place even existed until you mentioned it.\"","\"What was it like during the Primordial Era?\" Yuan asked.","\"I doubt much has changed,\" Yu Ning replied. \"White Hell has been infamous for as long as I can remember. Back then, during the Primordial Era, the deepest anyone managed to reach was the third region.\"","\"I've never been here before, so I don't know how impressive that is, but according to what those disciples from the Sun God's Temple said, their Sun Stones could help one survive even the fourth region.\"","Yuan had been listening to the disciples marketing the Sun Stones and only pretended to be ignorant.","\"Sun God's Lake, huh? I would like to visit it in the future when I have the chance.\"","After reaching the midway point of the first region, Yuan noticed a group of cultivators slightly ahead of him. Though the snowstorm blanketed the world in white, his divine sense cut through it with ease.","Since he wasn't hiding his presence, the group ahead also noticed him.","\"Am I seeing things, or is that man really traveling through White Hell without Sun Stone?\" one of the women asked aloud, clutching the glowing stone in her hand.","\"Even if he has Cold Immunity, what a reckless thing to do.\"","\"He's probably just lingering in the first region.\"","In truth, every woman in the group possessed some degree of Cold Immunity. Had they not intended to enter the deeper regions, they wouldn't have needed to rely on Sun Stones at all.","However, as they drew closer to the second region, the group was astonished to see Yuan still right behind them, almost as if he intended to enter the second region as well.","Yet, they still believed that Yuan would not venture into the second region.","A week later, they arrived at the threshold of the second region, where the snowstorm transformed into a barrage of hail. Razor-sharp ice shards constantly rained down, and without the protection of spiritual energy, they could pierce flesh as easily as ordinary Sword Aura, riddling one's body with holes.","Naturally, the cold within the second region was far more severe, being at least two to three times harsher than that of the outer region. Mountains also began to emerge, though only one appeared every few days along their path.","\"Heavens! Look over there! That man actually stepped into the second region without a Sun Stone, and he isn't even protecting his body with spiritual energy!\"","The group stared in shock, their curiosity toward him rapidly intensifying.","\"Is he just trying to show off to impress us or something?\" one of the women muttered.","\"That's likely.\"","\"How typical.\"","\"Let's see how long he'll last.\"","While the others chuckled at their own misunderstanding, the one leading them in the front remained silent, quietly observing Yuan through her divine sense to ensure he wasn't up to anything suspicious.","As they ventured deeper into the second region, magical beasts began to appear, many concealed beneath the snow, striking from ambush. With danger lurking at every step, the women soon stopped paying attention to Yuan, turning their focus entirely to their own safety.","Of course, a few of them couldn't resist sneaking glances at Yuan, who trailed behind in silence, almost like a stalker. That said, there were still thousands of miles separating them.","Eventually, one of them realized that no magical beasts had attacked Yuan for several days, even though their own group was assaulted constantly.","This left them greatly puzzled. Yuan made no attempt to conceal his presence, nor employed any special means, yet for reasons beyond their understanding, the magical beasts left him untouched.","\"Why aren't the magical beasts attacking him?\" one of them finally asked.","\"What if... he's not trying to impress us, but instead using us as bait?\" another suggested cautiously.","\"Elder, should we question him? He's only a Golden Immortal, so I doubt he can do anything to us, but I have a bad feeling about him.\"","The woman leading them said calmly, \"We've been moving in a straight line since entering White Hell-it might just be a coincidence. If you're that concerned, we can stop and let him pass us.\"","The others agreed with her suggestion and chose to rest. They carved out a massive crater in the snow before settling down inside it.","A few minutes later, Yuan had caught up to them. They silently hoped he would keep flying past, but their expressions darkened when he suddenly stopped directly above them.","\"I knew it! He's up to no good!\" one of the ladies hastily exclaimed. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2141,"title":"Chapter 2141: White Hell(3)","paragraphs":["When the group of ladies noticed Yuan stopping right above them, they hastily retrieved their weapons and prepared to fight him.","\"What do you want from us, you stalker?\" one of them shouted at him.","Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Stalker? Just because we're heading in the same direction doesn't mean I am stalking you. It's just a coincidence,\" he calmly replied.","\"Then why did you stop? If you're not here for us, then hurry up and get lost!\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan responded, \"In that case, I'll stop bothering you and be right on my way. Sorry for the disturbance.\"","Without another word, Yuan flew away.","\"What a creepy fellow.\"","\"Right?\"","Only after Yuan's presence vanished entirely did the group allow themselves to breathe freely, settling back into their rest. However, their rest was short-lived, as the earth beneath them quaked without warning, sending a jolt of alarm through the group.","\"W-What's going on?!\"","The leader's voice rang out sharply, \"An ambush! Take to the air!\"","At that instant, the ground split wide, and from its depths burst a colossal serpent, its body clad in translucent scales that gleamed like sculpted ice.","\"It's a White Hell Glacial Serpent! The strongest magical beast in the second region! Run! We don't stand a chance against a monster like that!\"","\"S-Scatter!\"","The group quickly scattered in different directions, hoping to confuse the serpent. But the beast was swift and decisive, striking immediately at the weakest among them.","Unfortunately, there was nothing anyone could do for her. After several moments of desperate struggle, the female cultivator was devoured by the beast.","However, the beast was not satisfied and immediately chased after its next prey.","In truth, Yuan had noticed the magical beast and wanted to warn them, but they chased him away before he could do so, even calling him a stalker.","A few days later, Yuan stepped into the third region. Here, the hail grew even more violent, its force great enough to pierce through ordinary spiritual energy. To withstand it, one needed Immortal Qi-making this region accessible only to Immortal cultivators.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved>","Though his Cold Immunity was progressing much faster than the second region, it was hardly enough to satisfy Yuan, so he continued going deeper.","As Yuan traversed the third region, magical beasts at the Golden Immortal level would constantly attack him. Unlike the second region, the beasts in the third region did not fear his aura.","Naturally, none of them posed even the slightest threat to him, and all it took was a single attack with Supreme Sword Aura to one-shot the beasts.","Since he had come to train, Yuan didn't bother using Immortal Qi to shield himself from the hail. Though the ice shards couldn't pierce his skin, each impact left a layer of frost, freezing his flesh on contact.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved>","In the blink of an eye, a month had passed, and Yuan stepped into the fourth region. Here, the hail had ceased, and the skies were clear, yet the temperature had dropped even further. The cold was so intense that Yuan's body was continuously being frozen just by existing within it.","\"Still not enough,\" Yuan muttered as he proceeded to make his way toward the fifth region.","Although his Cold Immunity had been pushed to its limit after consuming the Tear of the Azure Heavens, it still had not reached the realm of Cold Harmony.","A few hours into his journey toward the fifth region, Yuan spotted a lone figure locked in battle with a mammoth-like magical beast. The creature was nearly the size of a small mountain, and a gleaming blue crystal was embedded between its brows.","The cultivator was at the 1st level of God Ascension, while the beast was only at the True Immortal realm. Yet the extreme cold rendered her movements stiff, and much of her focus was spent maintaining a shield of Immortal Qi to protect her body.","Not wishing to disturb her, Yuan quietly flew past without stopping.","Some time later, Yuan finally reached the border of the fifth region. Even without stepping inside, he could sense that his Cold Immunity would be useless there.","Unlike the previous four regions, the fifth was a mountain valley, where a raging snowstorm howled between towering peaks in every direction.","After mentally preparing himself, Yuan entered the fifth region.","The instant he entered the fifth region, Yuan's body began turning into an ice statue.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved greatly>","Still not content with the progress speed, Yuan chose to advance toward the sixth region. Yet without a Sun Stone or other protective treasure, his body froze solid the instant he attempted to proceed. Thus, he summoned forth his True Primordial Fire, engulfing himself in its blaze as though donning a fiery armor, to withstand the frigid domain.","With the True Primordial Fire shielding him, Yuan's body instantly thawed, granting him freedom of movement once more. In fact, the fire's power was so overwhelming that he couldn't even feel the cold in the slightest.","Without hesitation, Yuan flew straight into the sixth region. The deeper one ventured into White Hell, the smaller each region became. While it had taken him nearly three months to travel from the outer region to the fifth, it required only a single week to reach the sixth.","Upon entering the sixth region, Yuan began searching for a suitable place to cultivate. After a few minutes of wandering, he settled on a random cave and stepped inside.","Once he was ready, Yuan extinguished the True Primordial Fire. The warmth vanished in an instant, and his body was immediately overwhelmed by the immense cold, freezing him solid like a statue and turning his very blood to ice.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved drastically>","Despite every inch of his body-even his organs and blood-being frozen solid, Yuan remained alive, forced endure the endless agony.","Time flowed swiftly, and before long, a year had passed. Throughout it all, Yuan remained encased in ice, an unmoving statue in the heart of the sixth region. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2142,"title":"Chapter 2142: White Hell(4)","paragraphs":["One year... two years... three years slipped by since Yuan began his cultivation in White Hell's sixth region. For all that time, he remained a frozen statue within an unremarkable cave, one among countless others scattered through the land.","While he had spent most of that time alone, sometime during his second year, he received an unexpected visitor.","It happened one seemingly ordinary night, when a lone figure suddenly flew into his cave and crashed to the ground.","The intruder was a woman, her body battered with wounds and stained with frozen blood.","However, having fallen unconscious shortly after entering the cave, she remained unaware of Yuan's presence. For the next few days, she lingered in a fragile slumber, surviving only thanks to the Sun Stone clutched tightly in her grasp.","Upon awakening, her eyes fell upon Yuan, and for a moment she was startled. However, she quickly calmed once she mistook him for nothing more than a frozen corpse.","\"Damn it, you scared me for a moment,\" she muttered, sitting up and leaning her back against the wall. For the next several days, she kept her eyes fixed on the cave's entrance with unwavering vigilance, as though expecting someone to appear.","\"I doubt they would be foolish enough to follow me to the sixth region...\" she muttered.","The next moment, she retrieved several recovery pills and swallowed them, beginning the process of healing her injuries. Although she could have hastened the process through cultivation, she chose not to risk exposing her presence and relied solely on the pills for recovery.","A few weeks passed, during which the female cultivator stayed inside the cave without once stepping outside.","\"At this rate, I should fully recover in about a year...\" she muttered as she looked at the Sun Stone in her grasp.","\"I'm glad I bought this Million-Year Sun Stone after all... otherwise, I wouldn't have been able to hide in the sixth region at all,\" she sighed.","Though the Million-Year Sun Stone was considered most effective only up to the fifth region, it could still aid entry into the sixth if the cultivator possessed other advantages, such as unique physiques or powerful treasures. In her case, she had a heaven-defying physique that granted her powerful resistance to the yin element, naturally giving her cold immunity.","\"Those hateful bastards... Once I recover from my injuries, I'll tear them limb from limb!\"","Once the female cultivator was certain her pursuers would not suddenly appear, she turned her full focus to recovery.","After ten months had passed and the majority of her wounds had mended, the female cultivator's eyes snapped open. A sound unlike any she had heard in this cave reached her ears-the sharp crack of ice breaking. Until now, only the endless howling of the snowstorm had filled the silence.","Startled, she stood and turned toward the sound reverberating from the cave's depths. But bewilderment followed, for the only thing at the far end was the frozen corpse, unmoving since the day she had first stumbled upon it nearly a year prior.","It had never crossed her mind that the frozen figure might still live. After all, it was completely unprotected, and not even a God Ascension cultivator could survive in this region without some form of protection.","When the noise ceased, the female cultivator cautiously approached its source. A moment later, upon reaching the end of the cave, her eyes widened in shock and disbelief. The ice statue she had long assumed to be a corpse was no longer frozen, and standing before her was a man, very much alive.","\"Hm? Who are you?\" Yuan asked with mild surprise, not expecting company the moment he awoke from cultivation. During his training, he had entered a trance-like state of enlightenment, fully immersing himself and remaining unaware of the female cultivator's presence until he broke free from the ice.","The woman could not bring herself to answer. She simply stood there, eyes wide and lips parted in shock, unable to comprehend how this man had endured the merciless cold of the sixth region without the slightest protection.","However, the woman quickly snapped out of her daze and stammered, \"S-Sorry, I didn't realize you were alive. I hope I haven't disturbed your training.\"","\"No, it's fine. I didn't even realize you were here until I woke up,\" Yuan said calmly, waving his hand in a dismissive gesture.","He then noticed her blood-stained body and asked, \"Are you okay?\"","\"I... I will take my leave now.\"","Without another word, the woman turned around and quickly left.","Yuan silently watched her depart, making no attempt to stop her.","<You have achieved Cold Harmony>","His attention shifted to the notification.","<Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has begun to evolve>","<Progress: 5%>","\"How long have I been cultivating?\" Yuan asked the others.","\"Three years.\" Yu Ning calmly responded.","\"Three years, huh? Not bad, but my training is not finished.\"","Although he had attained Cold Harmony, it had yet to reach its full potential. Thus, Yuan left the cave shortly after and began making his way toward the seventh region, determined not to leave White Hell until he achieved the highest attainable realm of Cold Immunity.","Over the course of five days, as Yuan made his way toward the seventh region, he encountered only one magical beast. The sixth region's environment was so merciless, so inhospitable, that only the rarest of creatures could exist within its bounds.","As Yuan stood at the border of the seventh region, his eyes widened at the sight ahead. On the horizon, a titanic beast, mammoth in form, loomed, its massive frame so towering it rose above the tallest mountains themselves.","However, what truly caught his attention was not the mammoth itself, but the faint silhouette of a human, barely visible, seated upon the beast's head.","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the distant figure. Though he could not make out their features, he could clearly feel the weight of their gaze fixed upon him.","However, the gaze did not linger, and a moment later the mammoth disappeared into the horizon. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2143,"title":"Chapter 2143: The Demon Sealing Faction’s Return","paragraphs":["Once the colossal mammoth and the silhouette disappeared, Yuan entered the seventh region before looking for a random cave.","The seventh region was so frigid that even with Cold Harmony, Yuan needed to cloak himself in True Primordial Fire just to move. Without it, he would be frozen instantly, reduced to an ice statue.","Some time later, Yuan sat cross-legged within a cave and withdrew the True Primordial Fire, allowing the cold to engulf him—thus beginning his training anew.","Normally, it would take thousands, if not millions, of years to advance Cold Harmony to the next level. But Yuan was forcing his body to the extreme. What truly accelerated his progress, however, was his heaven-defying physique.","The Heaven Refining Physique was a one-of-a-kind existence, so rare that most cultivators had never even heard of it. It first appeared in the Primordial Era, when Tian Yang stumbled upon the Heaven Refining Crystal that granted him this physique. Yet, even after countless years and many reincarnations, Yuan still could not uncover the true origin of that crystal.","Stil, despite possessing the Heaven Refining Physique, Yuan would continue his seclusion in the cave for no less than a decade.","Meanwhile, in the Seventh Heaven, the members of the Demon Sealing Faction returned to the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect after spending over a decade training in the outside world, gaining experience as cultivators.","Once everyone had returned safely to the sect, they gathered to share their experiences. “It's been a while,\" Wang Ming said with a smile. \"How was your journey?\"","“It was a pain in the ass,\" Chu Liuxiang sighed. \"No matter where we go, people are always trying to hit on us. And when we brush them off, it somehow always turns into a fight. Thanks to that, my combat experience is now through the roof.\"","“Fortunately, my group was made up entirely of men, so we didn't have to worry about anyone hitting on us,\" Shi Lang said. \"Even so, we still ran into plenty of trouble—mostly cultivators trying to take advantage of us.\"","“You guys are getting into fights? Pretty much all of my encounters back away after learning of my background,” said Wu Zao.","The others looked at Wu Zao and sighed, \"You're using Kelan's name as a shield? How are you going to gain experience if you avoid everything?\"","“It's not like I avoided every fight. I just avoid the ones I find a pain in the ass.\"","Once they finished talking about their journey and experiences, Wang Ming asked, \"Hey, have you heard anything from Yuan? It's been a while since we last heard from him.\" Meixiu shook her head and said, \"No, he hasn't contacted us since he went to this place called \"White Hell’ for training.\"","Before they parted ways, Yuan gave Meixiu, Chu Liuxiang, and Yu Rou a communication jade slip, allowing them to speak with each other even across great distances. Still, not wanting to interrupt his cultivation, it was usually Yuan who initiated the conversations. “It's been nearly twenty years since we last saw him... and to think, back then, we worried when he was gone for only a few months,\" Wang Bingbing remarked.","“What can we do? As our cultivation increases, so will the time we need to progress. Although it's been nearly two decades, it oddly doesn't feel that long.\" Wang Ming said. “In the future, we might see each other once every few hundred, if not a few thousand years.\" Xi Meili said.","“This is just the nature of the cultivation world.\" Kelan, who was also there, remarked. \"However, you'll quickly get used to it.\"","“That said... to think he'd go train at White Hell. He's truly the most reckless person I know.\"","“What's that place like?\" Xi Murong asked.","“It's one of the coldest and most perilous regions in the Nine Heavens,\" Kelan replied. “There exist four domains that cultivators universally avoid, known as the Forbidden Zones. White Hell stands as the third most dangerous of them all. Unless you have a powerful physique or a Sun Stone from the Sun God's Temple, you can forget about visiting that place.”","\"Have you ever been there?\" Wang Ming asked him.","“I've been there several times for training. It's not a pleasant place, especially since I hate the cold.\" Kelan shuddered just from recalling his experience within White Hell. Sometime later, Hong Xiuquan asked, \"Senior Kelan, what should we do next in our training?\"","\"Honestly, there's only one thing you can do if you wish to continue improving, and that is to train at other sects—ones better suited to your specific needs,” Kelan replied. \"As much as I would like to continue guiding you guys, I have already given you all I can in the basics as a cultivator. From here on, you must refine your own specializations.”","He continued, \"For example, Wang Xiuying—since your focus is Alchemy, I'll recommend you to one of the top sects for Alchemists. And Wang Ming, with your swordsmanship, I'l send you to a sword sect. It doesn't have to be a sect, either. I can find you personal teachers if you wish. Of course, if you wish to stay here, I won't stop you.\"","After a moment of silence, Kelan spoke, “I'll give you all some time to think over it. Once you have decided, I will speak with—\"","“I am willing to go!\" Wu Zao immediately gave a response. \"I am already noticing a drastic decline in my progress, after all.\"","Before Kelan could say anything else, the others also responded.","“I will also go,\" said Wang Ming.","\"Me too,\" said Shi Lang.","In the end, everyone but Li Jinxi gave a response, agreeing to train at other places. \"Alright, I'll speak with Senior Bai later. Not only does he have more connections, but he has much more experience in this field than I do,\" Kelan nodded.","“What about you, Li Jinxi?\" he turned to ask her a moment later.","Li Jinxi pondered for a moment before responding, *I think I will continue training by myself.\"","\"Are you sure? With your talents, you could easily get into the top sects with ease, even without our help,\" Kelan said, worried that she might be wasting her potential.","“I am,\" she confidently confirmed.","“If you say so...\" Despite saying that, Kelan wasn't going to give up easily.","“Let's see if Senior Bai can convince her...\" he thought to himself. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2144,"title":"Chapter 2144: The Demon Sealing Faction’s Return(2)","paragraphs":["\"What about us?\" Xi Meili suddenly asked, referring to herself and Liya, as they were both dragons.","Kelan gave her a stiff smile. “To be honest, I'm not sure. I do have a few non-human friends I could reach out to, but I can't promise anything. Do you know of any place where you could train?\"","Xi Meili fell silent to ponder, and after a minute of silence, she said, \"I do have a place in mind... but I'm not sure they'll be okay with it.\"","Kelan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Where is this place?\"","“The Holy Dragon Clan. I trained with them for some time when I went there with Yuan, and I really enjoyed it. If it weren't for the Celestial Emperor, I would've stayed there to train a little longer.\"","In truth, Xi Meili wanted to stay behind with the Holy Dragon Clan at the Dragon Spiral Mountain, but after what happened to them, she felt that it would be inappropriate for her to linger, so she ultimately decided to leave with Yuan.","“The Holy Dragon Clan, huh? In that case, I think it would be for the best if you personally reached out to them.\"","\"Aren't they the ones at the Dragon Spiral Mountain?\" Liya asked after recalling their name.","Xi Meili nodded, \"That's right. You saw them right after arriving in the Nine Heavens.\" Liya recalled the mountain of corpses she saw and asked, \"Do you think I can come with you?\"","\"Of course. It was already my intention to bring you along.\"","Kelan spoke a moment later, \"I'l contact the others immediately, but it might take some time for a response. You can do whatever in the meantime.”","Once their meeting concluded, the members of the Demon Sealing Faction returned to their living quarters to rest. Many of them decided to log out of Cultivation Online to train their real bodies on Earth.","After logging out, Meixiu left her room to visit Yu Rou and the Eternal Lotuses, who had risen to become the second-strongest faction on Earth.","“It's been a while, Senior Sister Meixiu.\"","As she passed through, the members of the Eternal Lotuses bowed their heads, greeting her with utmost respect.","Although Meixiu wasn't officially part of their faction, she often visited to train them. The other members of the Demon Sealing Faction would also stop by from time to time, but with everyone following their own schedules, it had become rare for them all to gather together.","\"Are you here to train us today, or are you here for Senior Sister Yu Rou?\"","The members approached her and asked.","“I'm here for Yu Rou today. I'l train with you all next week,\" she said.","\"Okay!\"","Melxiu arrived at their courtyard a few minutes later, where at the center stood a tall, beautiful woman instructing a group of younger girls.","The woman had long, silky black hair and warm brown eyes. Her very presence radiated a natural grace that drew people to her.","“Your posture is wrong. Move your hip a little to the right and straighten your back some more!\"","“Yes, Senior Sister Yu!\"","The woman was none other than Yu Rou.","Meixiu didn't disturb their training and waited for them to be done.","An hour later—\"Okay, we will end our training here today. We'll continue next week at the same time. You are all dismissed.\"","As the group of females dispersed, Yu Rou approached Meixiu with a calm smile, \"It's been two years, Meixiu. How have you been?\"","“I just finished my journey and have returned to Kelan's sect for now. What about you?\" “The same as usual. Training the newbies. Is it just your group that's returned?\"","“The others have returned as well. Everyone is safe and sound.\"","“That's good to hear.\"","Knowing that Yu Rou will ask about Yuan, Meixiu mentioned him first, \"Unfortunately, Yuan is still away,\" she said.","“Is that s0? Can't say I'm surprised,” Yu Rou replied with a bittersweet smile.","“You shouldn't be too hard on him.\"","“I would have been a little sad or lonely. I know he has a lot on his plate, but it's been nearly twenty years since I last saw his face. If you consider the other times he's been absent and how long we've been alive, it's about half of our lifetime.\"","“I know how it feels, but trust me, it will get better.\"","“I know. Anyway, what are you going to do now that you've returned?\"","“I'm going to rest a little before I continue my training at another place.\" Meixiu proceeded to tell Yu Rou about Kelan's plans for the Demon Sealing Faction.","\"So you guys will be doing your own things separately, huh? It makes sense, considering you all have your own talents and path.”","Sometime later, another presence approached them.","\"Hello, Sister Lianhua.\"","\"Hey, Meixiu.\" Bai Lianhua returned the greeting. \"Mind if I join?\"","\"No, go ahead.\"","Bai Lianhua sat down beside them, and the three of them started chatting. After Meixiu recalled the end of her training journey, Bai Lianhua spoke about the Eternal Lotuses and Earth's overall situation.","Ever since Yuan opened the gateway between Earth and the Nine Heavens, flooding the world with spiritual energy, cultivators on Earth had advanced at a pace unlike anything before. Yet, no matter how far their cultivation rose, they soon discovered they could only wield the strength of a Spirit Grandmaster.","This meant that even Spirit King cultivators on Earth were no stronger than a Spirit Grandmaster. Since Yuan secretly created the formation that limited everyone's cultivation, nobody but the Demon Sealing Faction knew the cause of this phenomenon. Thus, much like the phenomenon of Cultivation Online, no one questioned it, choosing instead to continue their lives as usual.","However, Meixiu knew that things would not remain this way forever and that they needed another solution sooner or later. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2145,"title":"Chapter 2145: Yu Family’s Return","paragraphs":["After spending half a day with Yu Rou and Bai Lianhua, Meixiu returned home.","\"You're back.\"","When Meixiu walked through the entrance, she was greeted by a familiar face sweeping the ground.","\"Mother.\"","It was Meifeng. Although the members of Demon Sealing Faction spend most of their time inside Cultivation Online these days, Meifeng continued to clean the mansion daily. \"How have you been lately?\" Meixiu asked.","“The same as usual,\" Meifeng calmly replied as she continued sweeping the floor. “You've entered Spirit Lord. Congratulations.”","Meixiu said after noticing Meifeng's cultivation had reached the second level of Spirit Lord.","“It's nothing compared to your Spirit Sovereign cultivation.”","“Your cultivation would be a lot higher if you didn't spend hours cleaning the house every day.\" Meixiu shook her head. \"Honestly, it's a waste of time.\"","Meifeng halted her movements and replied, \"I have been doing this long before you were even born. Even if the entire world changes, it doesn't mean I have to change. I enjoy doing this, so I will continue doing it, even if it's not necessary.\"","\"Also, I have nothing else to do nowadays. Although the Demon Sealing Faction used to be at the center of attention and constantly flooded with requests and emails, we're pretty much forgotten nowadays since we haven't made any appearances since Yuan left","“Why don't you explore Cultivation Online more? You can even meet Yuan there,\" Meixiu suggested.","“I tried. It was fun at first, but after several years, I got bored.\"","“But you don't find housework boring? I can't understand you.\" Meixiu sighed.","“Why are you so worried about what I do? It's not like I am going to die.\"","“The world is constantly evolving. If you cannot keep up with it, you'll eventually be consumed by it.\"","Meifeng smiled and said, \"Fortunately, I have a capable daughter and son-in-law to protect me when that happens.\"","Meixiu opened her mouth, but no words came out, as she was left speechless by her mother's words.","“What? You're not going to protect me?\" Meifeng asked, raising her eyebrows.","“I never said that,\" Meixiu replied. \"I just didn't expect to hear those words from you, since you've always taught me that we can only rely on ourselves and nobody else.” “That was our life working for the Yu Family, after all. However, things are different now.\" Meixiu fell silent for a moment before asking, \"Have you learned anything about the Yu Family? You mentioned you'd been trying to find them, and that was over ten years ago.\" After a brief look of hesitation on her face, Meifeng responded, \"Yes, I have. In fact, I found them.\"","\"Really?!\" Meixiu's eyes widened at this news.","“Where are they? And what have they been doing since they disappeared?”","“What are you going to do with that information?\" Meifeng asked.","“What am I.\" Meixiu raised her eyebrows. \"You're making it sound like I am going to do something to them once I learn their whereabouts. I'm just curious.”","“I'll tell you after I finish cleaning, or are you too busy to wait?\"","\"No, I can wait. I won't be doing anything for a while since I just finished my training in Cultivation Online.\"","Meifeng nodded and returned to her cleaning.","Sometime later, Meixiu went to look for Meifeng in her room.","“Come inside.\"","Meixiu opened the door and stepped inside Meifeng's room.","Once they were seated, Meifeng began, \"When their reputation was shattered, the Yu Family went into hiding, and I wasn't able to get any information on them. However, a few years ago, they returned.”","\"Returned?\" Meixiu asked with raised eyebrows.","\"As in they stopped hiding. It's most likely because Yuan had completely disappeared from both Earth and Cultivation Online for the last few decades, and they probably believe he's dead or something.\"","Since Yuan was no longer a Player, his achievements were no longer announced by the system, and because this wasn't the first time he had disappeared for long stretches, no one thought much of it at first. But as years passed without a single announcement bearing his name, and with nobody having seen him on Earth, people gradually began to speculate that he had died.","People have tried searching for Yuan in Cultivation Online, but since the Players were only able to ascend up to the Fifth Heaven these days, they were nowhere near close to reaching him.","\"So, where are they right now? And what are they doing now that they have returned?\" Meixiu asked.","“They're currently running a business for the Xiong Family.\"","“The Xiong Family? Aren't they the number one family in the Legacy Ranking? Do they know the Yu Family's background?\"","Meifeng nodded, \"Yes. In fact, they agreed to work with the Yu Family because they are aware of their connection with Yuan. As for the Yu Family's business... they run a talent- recruitment business.”","“Is that 50?\" Meixiu muttered.","\"Are you going to tell Yu Rou?\" Meifeng suddenly asked.","“What's the point? I doubt she even cares about them at this point.\"","“If you say so.\"","After learning about the Yu Family's current situation, Meixiu and Meifeng continued chatting about other things, such as their future plans.","“You may not look like it, but you're already twice the age I was when I gave birth to you. When can I expect a grandchild?\" Meifeng asked.","“You're asking me that when Yuan isn't even on Earth anymore? Are you asking me to find a new partner?\"","\"Of course not. Yuan may not be here right now, but it's not like he'll never return.\" Meixiu fell silent for a moment before speaking, \"Yu Rou plans on leaving Earth to follow Yuan in the Nine Heavens in the future. I also plan to do the same. What about you?\" “It's not like I have any special attachments to this place. If both my daughter and son- in-law are at another place, I will naturally go there with you,\" she said. \"The question is whether I'll still be alive by the time that happens.”","“You can live for hundreds of years as a Spirit Lord. But if you're worried and you don't want to die before seeing your grandchild, then you should put more effort into your cultivation,” said Meixiu.","“If you put it like that, I guess I have no choice but to work harder on my cultivation,\" Meifeng said with a bittersweet smile. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2146,"title":"Chapter 2146: Arrangements","paragraphs":["Several days after the Demon Sealing Sect made their return, Wang Ming and the members who had come from the Jaded Garden opted to descend from the mountain to reunite with their families.","“We'll be back in a few months,” Wang Ming assured.","“Enjoy your time,” Meifeng replied warmly.","“I'm going to visit my grandfather for a few weeks as well,” Wang Xiuying announced and departed from Dragon Spiral Mountain two days later, leaving only Chu Liuxiang, Meixiu, and Meifeng at their residence.","Though they kept in frequent contact with their relatives through calls and video conferences, this marked their first homecoming in many years.","With little else to occupy them, Meixiu and Chu Liuxiang devoted much of their days to Yu Rou and the Eternal Lotuses. Beyond the Eternal Lotuses, they also made visits to the Lord, who was primarily focused on reclaiming his lost cultivation.","Meanwhile, at the Jaded Garden, the Six Spiritual Houses hosted a magnificent weeklong banquet in honor of their prodigies’ homecoming.","“Do any of you regret leaving your homes to follow Yuan?\" an elder inquired during the celebration.","“Not at all,” Wang Ming responded without hesitation. “Meeting someone like Yuan is the greatest stroke of luck I've ever known—and dedicating myself to his path is an even greater privilege.”","“Exactly. Without him, none of us could have achieved this level—even over a lifetime,” Shi Lang added, garnering unanimous nods.","“How has Yuan been lately? I haven't heard a word for years. Some say he might be dead. Is he truly alright?” someone asked.","Wu Zao chuckled, “You don't understand Yuan like we do. That man is extraordinary. Nothing in this world can threaten him, so there's no need to worry. He's definitely alive and well.”","“By the way, is Yuan open to partnerships these days? I'd like to introduce my daughter to him.\"","“You might as well give up. He's beyond our reach,” Xi Murong dismissed.","“But didn't Jinxi manage to win his heart?” Wang Ming interjected.","“What?!”","Those outside the Demon Sealing Sect turned sharply toward Li Jini, stunned to hear of any connection between her and Yuan for the first time.","“W-When? When did this happen?” Li Jinxi's father exclaimed, standing abruptly, face pale with disbelief.","still, Li Jinxi remained silent.","“It was just before Yuan left, if I recall correctly,” said Shi Lang.","“That long ago? And none of you told us?\"","“We were busy,” came the simple reply.","“And what about you, Bingbing? Have you made any progress with him?” the Wang family probed.","“We're just friends!” Wang Bingbing claimed nervously, a blush ising to her cheeks. “You really need to put in more effort,” her mother sighed.","“Shut up!” Bingbing snapped.","After a moment, Li Jinx finally spoke, “There's something I need to share.”","The room quieted as all eyes turned toward her.","“As you know, Yuan departed Earth for the Nine Heavens. I wasn't able to follow him then, but when the opportunity arises again, I intend to leave Earth too,” she said. “It's still far off, but I want to tell you now so you won't be confused if I suddenly disappear.” Upon hearing this, Wang Ming added, “I, too, plan to leave Earth someday. After experiencing the Nine Heavens, this small world no longer satisfies me.\"","Others soon voiced similar intentions—they all hoped to one day depart Earth.","Despite the unexpected revelation, nobody seemed particularly shocked.","After a brief pause, one of them spoke, “We expected this back when Yuan left Earth. Frankly, we were surprised none of you had followed him already.”","“Well... it's not like we didn't want to. We simply couldn't,” Hong Xiuguan replied.","“Will you be unable to return once you leave?” someone asked.","“We should be able to, as long as no one tampers with the portal like last time.”","“In that case, I see no problem with your leaving. This world has indeed become too confining for you.”","“Do you know when you'll go?\"","No","Their families continued questioning them until satisfied, ultimately offering not only their acceptance but encouragement.","Time slipped by swiftly, and before they knew it, a full year had gone.","The Demon Sealing Sect returned once more to Dragon Spiral Mountain and logged back into Cultivation Online for the first time in a while.","Shortly after, Kelan summoned them.","“The preparations are underway,” he informed them. “But nothing is finalized yet. In a few days, your prospective masters will arrive to interview you. If they find you suitable and agree to take you on, the choice will then be yours. We will not force anyone to join a sect that doesn't feel right.”","“Li Jinxi, you are to meet with Senior Bai at the Myriad of Techniques tomorrow. He wishes to have a discussion with you.”","Li Jinxi nodded silently.","“Any questions?”","“Could you provide more details so we know what to expect?” Shi Lang asked.","Kelan obliged, outlining the potential sects they might join.","Once content, they were excused.","The next day, Li Jinx visited the Myriad of Techniques.","“Senior Bai,\" she greeted respectfully upon entering his domain.","“Li Jinx, correct? This will be our first private meeting. Please, have a seat.” Senior Bai indicated the prepared table with two cups of tea.","Pouring her a cup, he continued, “You're probably wondering why I summoned you, so Ill be direct. Kelan tells me you're not only the most gifted among your group but also the most diligent. Yet, you wish to cultivate alone while your peers agree to train at various sects. May I ask the reason behind your decision?”"]},{"number":2147,"title":"Chapter 2147: Heaven’s Sect","paragraphs":["Hearing Senior Bai's question, Li Jinxi responded calmly, without a trace of hesitation. “It's quite simple. I just don't believe there's anything these sects can teach me.\"","After all, she was a reincarnator who carried the memories of her past life. Unlike the others, she was already far ahead in terms of experience.","Cultivation sects were typically stepping stones for the inexperienced or havens for those wishing to settle in one place. But Li Jinxi was neither, and she would gain far more by wandering the world on her own. In fact, most cultivators who graduate from their sects more often than not set out on their own adventures, hoping to encounter good fortune along the way.","However, Li Jinxi couldn't reveal such information to Senior Bai even though she trusted him.","\"So, you deem the sects unworthy of your time?\" Senior Bai murmured, closing his eyes in contemplation.","Ordinarily, such words would come only from cultivators blinded by arrogance. Yet in Li Jinxi's voice, he detected no such conceit. Even though this was his first true conversation with her, he could already discern that she was different from the rest. There was something oddly familiar about Li Jinxi—a feeling he would sometimes get when speaking with Yuan, but he couldn't pinpoint it.","Li Jinxi spoke a moment later, “It's not that I am looking down on these sects. I have more experience than it appears, and I have already graduated from several sects.\"","\"No, I understand where you're coming from. However, you cannot compare the sects in the lower heavens to the sects here,\" said Senior Bai, misunderstanding her.","He knew Li Jinxi was a Player who started her journey in the lower heavens, so in his eyes, all of her experience came from the lower heavens, which is incomparable to the upper heavens.","Realizing Senior Bai's misunderstanding, she said, “I think it would be easier to explain with my abilities.\"","“I see... that is a good idea. It'd definitely be quicker if you showed me your current abilities. That way, I can better gauge whether you would benefit from being in a sect or not.\" Senior Bai nodded.","He turned around and flew to an open area before beckoning her, \"Come at me. No need to hold back.\"","Li Jinxi nodded and retrieved her treasure, the Golden Empress.","“A fine sword.\" Senior Bai remarked with a smile on his face.","\"Here I come.\"","In the next moment, Li Jinxi unleashed her full cultivation without hesitation, striking at Senior Bai with the clear intent to defeat him.","In their very first exchange, Senior Bai was forced back.","His eyes widened as he said, \"My apologies. I underestimated you.\"","Li Jinxi gave a silent nod, allowing Senior Bai a moment to ready himself before launching her second strike—one even stronger than the first. She had known he would underestimate her, which was why she hadn't gone all out at the start.","However, Senior Bai was prepared this time and managed to block her strike. Yet, he was still astonished by her overwhelming prowess.","“She's only a Bronze Immortal, but she exudes the power of a Golden Immortal! Kelan was right—her talent is overwhelming! It's like I am fighting Yuan!\" he cried inwardly.","Li Jinxi's overwhelming prowess and talent reminded Senior Bai of his first exchange with Yuan.","Senior Bai quickly understood why Li Jinxi had no confidence in sects and would rather train herself.","After a while, Senior Bai said, \"That's enough. Let's stop here.\"","Li Jinx halted right away. Even after giving it her all, she hadn't managed to land a clean strike, which frustrated her.","“You're undeniably talented—far more than Kelan gave you credit for,\" Senior Bai remarked. \"Your movement and technique are good enough to become an instructor at an elite sect, and you clearly have a lot of combat experience. However, you also still have a lot of room for improvement, and I firmly believe that you would benefit a lot from joining a sect. While there are only a handful of sects that would qualify to train someone of your caliber, and all of them only accept the best of the best, you should have no issue being accepted by them.\"","Li Jinxi remained silent for a good moment before speaking, \"If you were to recommend me a sect, which one would it be?\"","Senior Bai closed his eyes to ponder.","“Either the Divine Essence Monastery or Heaven's Sect. The Divine Essence Monastery is a top sect in the Ninth Heaven that only accepts female disciples, and Heaven's Sect is operated by the Tian Family, which is the second strongest family in the Nine Heavens. Do you remember Tian Yuexing from the Sword Emperor's Qualification?\" “The so-called “number one genius’ who challenged Yuan and got utterly defeated? I remember.”","\"He's from that sect. Not just him. Many experts who currently stand at the peak of the cultivation world came from Heaven's Sect. In fact, I also used to be a disciple there,\" said Senior Bai.","He continued, \"With your talents, you won't have any problems getting in. If you want, you can decide after taking a look at them first.\"","“I will need some time to consider,\" Li Jinxi responded a moment later.","“Take all the time you need. Once you decide, let Kelan know so he can contact me.\" “Alright.”","Li Jinxi left shortly after.","Once she left, Senior Bai sat down and sighed, \"What a terrifying young lad. The newer generation is truly full of monsters. I'm afraid that it won't be long before the older generation becomes irrelevant.”","After leaving Myriad of Techniques, Li Jinxi returned to her room, where she lay on the bed and quietly stared at the ceiling.","\"Heaven's Sect... that's where I died in my past life...\" she muttered.","Though she had yet to recover all her memories—or the details of her death—she remembered her final moments taking place within Heaven's Sect.","And for the next several days, Li Jinxi remained inside her room to ponder her choices. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2148,"title":"Chapter 2148: Keling","paragraphs":["On the fourth day of the Demon Sealing Faction's return to Cultivation Online, Kelan summoned Wang Ming when his recruiter arrived at the sect.","\"This junior greets Senior.\" Wang Ming bowed to the handsome middle-aged man standing beside Kelan.","The man nodded and introduced himself, \"My name is Liu An, and I am the Sect Master of the Origin Sword Sect. We're a top-five sword sect within the Nine Heavens and number two in the Eighth Heaven.\"","The man proceeded to give a brief history lesson on the Origin Sword Sect to Wang Ming, as well as some of their biggest achievements.","At the end, Kelan spoke, \"After watching over you for the last few decades, I believe your sword style is compatible with the Origin Sword Sect. However, don't just take my word for it.\"","Liu An then spoke, \"I am going to give you a quick test to determine whether you are qualified for the Origin Sword Sect, as well as show you what my sword style is capable of.\"","Wang Ming nodded and followed them to Kelan's private training ground.","Inside, Wang Ming and Liu An faced each other with a sword.","\"Come at me with the intention to kill,\" said Liu An before the fight began.","During the fight, Wang Ming used every card in his hand to try to defeat Liu An. However, the results were quite obvious, and Wang Ming was unable to touch Liu An even after six hours of continuous fighting.","\"Let's stop here.\" Liu An said after placing his sword against Wang Ming's neck.","After the fight, Wang Ming felt a little dispirited. He had anticipated a difficult battle, but he never imagined the gap would be so vast-that he wouldn't even be able to land a single hit on Liu An.","Noticing Wang Ming's face, Liu An spoke, \"I heard from Sect Leader Kelan that you're not even a hundred years old. Is that true?\"","Wang Ming silently nodded.","\"Then you have immense potential and plenty of room to grow. In fact, I can see you quickly becoming a top disciple in my sect if you work hard enough.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Liu An then asked, \"So, what do you think of my sword style? Do you feel any desire to learn it?\"","\"I-I do!\" Wang Ming quickly responded.","Liu An smiled and said, \"Why don't you come to my sect and take a look around before you make a final decision?\"","\"I will do that, then.\"","Liu An turned to look at Kelan and smiled, \"Thank you for giving our sect the opportunity to recruit such a young talent. We owe you a great debt.\"","Kelan shook his head.","\"You don't owe me anything. I am just doing what's best for the kid.\"","\"When can you leave?\" Liu An asked Wang Ming.","\"Immediately!\" he quickly responded.","\"You don't need to say goodbye to your friends?\" Kelan asked.","Wang Ming smiled and said, \"I already said my goodbyes to them.\"","\"Very well. Let's go then.\"","The next moment, Liu An retrieved a flying treasure and boarded it with Wang Ming before disappearing from the sect.","A few hours after Wang Ming left the sect, another expert arrived at the sect, and Shi Lang was summoned.","\"I am Zhong Man, also known as the Demon Spear. I am the Sect Leader of the Heaven-Piercing Spear Sect, and we are the number one spear sect in the entire Nine Heavens. Though you were recommended by Sect Leader Kelan and Sect Leader Bai, I still need to evaluate you to see if you qualify to join.\"","Shi Lang nodded, \"Exactly how I want it.\"","\"The evaluation will take place at our sect, so you can take a look around while you're at it. When can you leave?\"","\"I can leave right now.\"","\"Very well.\"","Wasting no time, Zhong Man left with Shi Lang a minute later.<azab9c> This text is hosted at novel·fire.net</azab9c>","Over the next few days, more and more experts arrived, each coming to take members of the Demon Sealing Faction away.","\"I am an elder at the Celestial Cauldron Sect. We're the number one sect for Alchemists in the Nine Heavens, and most of the top Pill Masters in this world have studied under us. If that's not enough, our Sect Leader is the current God of Alchemy. If your talent permits it, you could even become her disciple.\"","\"God of Alchemy...\" Wang Xiuying swallowed nervously at this title.","\"If you wish to join us, you will need to pass several exams. However, I have to be honest. Considering your lack of experience, I don't think you have what it takes to pass the exams,\" said the elder.","Unlike cultivation sects, which place talent above all else, alchemy sects require both innate talent and accumulated experience. As Wang Xiuying had yet to live a full century, her experience was still lacking.","Even with the Celestial Overlords' influence, Kelan was only able to give Wang Xiuying the opportunity to take the exam. If she wanted to enter the sect, she needed to do so with her own abilities.","\"Even if there's a 99.99 chance that I'd fail, I would still like to take the exam,\" Wang Xiuying said with a determined expression.","Sometime later, Wang Xiuying left with the elder, leaving just Meixiu, Chu Liuxiang, and Li Jinxi at the sect.","Two days later, Kelan called for Meixiu.","When she arrived, Meixiu could see a tall and muscular woman who rivaled Kelan's physique standing next to him.","\"Hello...\" Meixiu had to tilt her head to look at the woman's face.","Despite her rough appearance, the woman smiled and said, \"Hello, little one. I'm Keling.\"","\"Keling...?\" Meixiu turned to look at Kelan, who smiled back.","\"This is Keling, my elder sister.\"","\"I didn't know you had siblings,\" Meixiu remarked.","Kelan sighed aloud. \"I usually avoid anything related to my family-we don't exactly have the best relationship.\"","\"That's an understatement,\" Keling cut in. \"You despise us. So imagine my surprise when you suddenly reached out to me.\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2149,"title":"Chapter 2149: Keling (2)","paragraphs":["\"That's not right.\" Kelan shook his head and elaborated, \"I despise our parents. I harbor no hard feelings toward any of my siblings. After all, it was our parents' decision to feed me giant's blood.\"","\"Even though you gained immense strength from it? All of our siblings envy you, you know?\" Keling said.<az7a60> ᴛʜɪs ᴄʜᴀᴘᴛᴇʀ ɪs ᴜᴘᴅᴀᴛᴇ ʙʏ novel✶fire.net</az7a60>","\"That strength didn't come for free,\" Kelan replied, his fists clenched tightly. \"I endured decades of indescribable pain just to absorb it. Even now, my body still aches at times, as if remembering what I went through back then.\"","\"...\" Keling fell silent.","Although she had also consumed a giant's blood, it wasn't anywhere close to the amount Kelan had to consume, not to mention that he'd consumed high-tier giant blood, so she couldn't even pretend to understand the torment Kelan had to endure.","\"Anyway, let's get back on topic,\" Kelan said a moment later.","Keling nodded and continued, \"Let me start over. I'm Keling, Kelan's elder sister. I specialize in archery, and I'm known as the Star-Piercing Huntress. I came because Kelan begged me to guide you. But to be honest, I've never taken on a disciple before, and my experience as a teacher is minimal. I may not be the most suitable person to teach you. Hell, I don't even know why Kelan came to me for help.","Kelan then said, \"You're the best archer I know, and I only want the best for her.\"","Keling raised her brows and asked suspiciously, \"Is she your girl or something? You don't even treat your own disciples this well.\"","Flustered, Kelan quickly replied, \"She's not! She already has someone-and her partner is a person I owe a great deal to!\"","\"Is that so? Well, that won't change the fact that I might not be a suitable teacher, even if I am the best archer in the Nine Heavens,\" she said.","\"I don't mind.\" Meixiu suddenly said. \"If it doesn't work out, I can always find a different teacher.\"","\"Are you sure? My training methods might not be suitable for a fragile-looking lady like you. Honestly, it's quite barbaric.\"","\"You shouldn't judge her by her appearance,\" Kelan said. \"Despite how she looks, she's very hardworking and surprisingly tough. After all, she endured all of my training without uttering a single complaint. The only other person in their group who didn't complain the slightest was Li Jinxi, and she's in a league of her own.\"","Because of Meifeng's upbringing, Meixiu's mental fortitude far surpassed that of the others—and that was without even considering the experience from her past life.","Keling stared at Meixiu in silence for a good moment before sighing, \"Alright. I'll train you. I've been thinking about starting my own sect recently, so this will be a good experience.\"","\"Then it's settled,\" said Kelan.","\"I'll come back for you in a month, so use this time to prepare yourself,\" Keling said, as she also needed some time to prepare.","Meixiu nodded.","The following day, Chu Liuxiang was summoned by Kelan.","\"Hm? Where's my teacher?\" Chu Liuxiang asked when she saw Kelan by himself.","\"He's running a little late, but he'll be here soon.\"","\"Okay.\"","A few minutes later, a familiar figure appeared before them.","\"Senior Bai? Don't tell me you're going to be my teacher?\" Chu Liuxiang asked with a surprised face.","Senior Bai smiled and said, \"Not quite. You specialize in spiritual techniques-specifically the Yin Element -and you've also been studying Array Symbols, correct?\"","Chu Liuxiang nodded and elaborated, \"I am studying Array Symbols, but it's more of a side project- something I do when I want a breath of fresh air. My focus is still cultivation.\"","\"I understand,\" said Senior Bai. \"Originally, Kelan intended to send you to a sect specializing in the Yin Element, such as the Frozen Cloud Ethereal Sect. But I have a different proposal-why not join my Gates of Heaven instead? We specialize in traditional cultivation methods and spiritual techniques, and we also have many experts in the Yin Element. And should you wish to pursue Array Symbols, I can personally guide you, as I am a Level 7 Array Master.\"","\"Really? That's great because I'd rather train in a place with familiar people,\" Chu Liuxiang said.","Senior Bai nodded and said, \"I have another proposal. As you know, there is a Gates of Heaven in the Fifth Heaven, Seventh Heaven, and another in the Ninth Heaven. If you want the best resources and most experienced lecturers, you should join the Gates of Heaven in the Ninth Heaven.\"","Chu Liuxiang's eyes widened at his proposal, and she said, \"I am already humbled that you would let me join the Gates of Heaven, but to bring me to the Ninth Heaven... are you sure? I'm afraid that I am not talented enough.\"","Senior Bai spoke in a serious tone. \"I'll be honest with you. If not for our connection, you wouldn't have qualified to enter the Gates of Heaven in the Seventh Heaven, let alone the Ninth. But talent alone doesn't determine everything in the cultivation world-luck and connections matter just as much. That said, if you choose to join the sect in the Ninth Heaven, you will likely face ridicule from those around you. I can shield you to a certain degree, but I cannot afford to show excessive favoritism. Take some time to think it over.\"","It wasn't only Chu Liuxiang. The other Demon Sealing Faction members would also face ridicule for their young age, especially if people discovered they had joined through connections.","Yet, despite such a possibility, Chu Liuxiang did not hesitate to reply, \"I don't need to think about it. It's true that I don't qualify to step foot in such a place, let alone train with others who joined through their own efforts. I won't give up such an opportunity just because someone might ridicule me.\"","Senior Bai smiled and said, \"Don't make it sound like you didn't put any effort into it. I only made this proposal because of how hard you trained with Kelan, and I believe you will thrive despite the difference.\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2150,"title":"Chapter 2150: Returning to the Holy Dragon Clan","paragraphs":["\"Since it's decided, I will take you to the Ninth Heaven so you can train in the Gates of Heaven. However, it'll take some time to get approval, so you can continue staying here until then,\" Senior Bai said.","Chu Liuxiang nodded, \"Take your time.\"","\"It shouldn't take too long--three months at most.\"","\"I understand.\"","Senior Bai left shortly after.","\"Don't worry too much about it,\" Kelan said afterward. \"There may be a few bad apples, but most disciples of the Gates of Heaven have good character--a reflection of their leader, Senior Bai. However, if things do get out of hand, don't hesitate to ask Senior Bai for help.\"","\"I'm not worried at all,\" Chu Liuxiang said with a confident smile.","Sometime later, Chu Liuxiang went to speak with Meixiu and Li Jinxi about her arrangements.","\"So, I'll be studying in the Ninth Heaven at the Gates of Heaven,\" she announced.","\"Senior Bai's sect, huh? I'll be training with Kelan's elder sister,\" Meixiu said.","\"Huh? Kelan has a sister?\" Chu Liuxiang's eyes widened with surprise at this news.","Meixiu nodded. \"He has several other siblings, too.\"","\"What about you, Sister Jinxi? Where will you be going?\"","The two looked at her.","\"I haven't decided yet. I was going to train alone in the wilderness, but Senior Bai gave me other options. I can train at the Divine Essence Monastery or Heaven's Sect. Both of them exist within the Ninth Heaven.\"","\"I think you would still benefit from training at a sect even with your experience,\" said Meixiu.","\"I think so, too.\" Chu Liuxiang agreed.","Meanwhile, Xi Meili and Liya just arrived at the Dragon Spiral Mountain.","\"Halt! Identify yourself!\" A guard stopped them once they got close enough.","\"Hello, my name is Xi Meili-\"","\"I remember you! You're Dragon Goddess Yeyou's Envoy's friend!\" The guard interrupted.","\"Yes... I came here with Yuan some time ago.\"","\"Why did you return? Did something happen?\"","\"No. This may sound weird, but I was wondering if I could train here with my friend.\"","\"Training, huh? Let me speak with my superior. Follow me.\"","Xi Meili and Liya followed the guard to the Dragon Spiral Mountain.","Upon returning to the Dragon Spiral Mountain, Xi Meili and Liya were brought to a guest house before the guard left to contact the elders.","\"Xi Meili? That young dragon from last time has returned, and she wants to train here?\" The elders raised an eyebrow at this news.","\"Should I send them away?\" The guard asked after seeing the elder's reaction.","\"What? Are you insane? They're the Immortal-Dragon Goddess' Envoy's companion! They can train here for as long as they'd like!\" The elder said.","Besides the elders and highest-ranking members, the rest of the Holy Dragon Clan were unaware of Yuan's true identity as the Immortal Monarch.","\"I-I understand!\"","Thus, Xi Meili and Liya began living at Dragon Spiral Mountain with the Holy Dragon Clan. The children were overjoyed to see Xi Meili again, while the adults grew curious about Liya's identity.","Alt ough she was also a dragon, Liya had grown up on Earth, and her scent and aura carried a difference that stirred their curiosity.","A month later, Keling returned to take Meixiu away.","\"Good luck, Meixiu,\" Chu Liuxiang and Li Jinxi said in farewell.","\"See you later.\"","Another month passed, and Senior Bai personally escorted Chu Liuxiang to the Ninth Heaven, where she would begin her training at the Gates of Heaven.","Now, it was just Li Jinxi who remained at Kelan's sect.","Kelan didn't rush her and patiently waited for her to decide.","A few days later, Li Jinxi made up her mind.","\"I will go train at Heaven's Sect,\" she said to Kelan.","\"Really? That's wonderful!\" Kelan's face lit up with joy. This meant she would finally receive proper training and be able to unleash her true potential.","\"However, I want to ascend to the Ninth Heaven with my own powers,\" she quickly added.","\"If that's what you want.\" Kelan didn't object to her request.","A few days later, Li Jinxi departed from the sect to begin her journey to the Ninth Heaven. Without delay, she headed straight for the Stairway to Heaven to test whether she could ascend to the Eighth Heaven at her current level.","After spending nearly twenty years in the seventh region of White Hell, Yuan finally emerged from his cultivation. However, he had yet to achieve the next realm of Cold Harmony.","\"How long have I been in cultivation?\" Yuan asked.","\"Almost twenty years,\" Yu Ning responded.","\"That's quite long. Although I am close to reaching the next level of Cold Harmony, I don't think I will be able to achieve it in a reasonable amount of time in this environment. I must head to the eighth region, if not the ninth region.\"","Before leaving the cave, Yuan sent a message through his communication jade slip to Meixiu, Chu Liuxiang, and Li Jinxi about his situation. Normally, they would have quickly responded, but they were currently busy with training and hadn't noticed that Yuan had contacted them.","Without waiting for their response, Yuan left the cave and began making his way toward the eighth region.","However, shortly after leaving the cave, he sensed a faint presence nearby-so weak that it was clear its owner was on the brink of death.","Unable to ignore it, Yuan made a detour and followed the presence.","As he got closer, he sensed several more presences, and they all appeared to be chasing after the weakened presence.","Realizing the situation, Yuan quickened his pace and soared through the harsh environment with his body cloaked in True Primordial Fire.","Sometime later, he caught up to the source of the weakened presence and saw a familiar-looking woman struggling through the seventh region. The Sun Stone she clutched was strained to its limits, unable to","protect her fully.","\"Are you unharmed?\" Yuan asked, calling out gently without drawing too near.","Yet, his words startled her deeply, and without so much as a glance at him, the woman unleashed a fierce martial technique against him. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2151,"title":"Chapter 2151: White Hell Frost Lotus","paragraphs":["\"Whoa!\" Yuan wasn't expecting to be attacked so suddenly, but he still managed to dodge her attack.","\"Calm down! I am not your enemy!\"","Hearing his familiar voice, the woman halted her movements and turned to look at his face. \"You're... the","one from the cave...\" the woman muttered in a weak voice.","\"Hm? No wonder I find your face familiar. So you were that woman who came into my cave during my","cultivation in the sixth region,\" Yuan said after seeing her face clearly. \"You look like you're on the verge","of death. Need some help?\"","\"It doesn't concern you... If you don't want to die, leave me alone,\" she said before turning around and","flying away.","Yuan didn't chase after her. However, he didn't leave either, almost as if he was waiting for something or","someone.","Sometime later, Yuan could sense several silhouettes appearing in the distance and prepared to confront","them. Within moments, these silhouettes arrived before Yuan. When they stopped, they immediately","surrounded and questioned him, \"Who are you? And where's the woman?\"","\"Woman? What are you talking about?\" Yuan asked, pretending to be ignorant of the situation.","\"Don't play dumb. We know you met and spoke with that woman,\" said one of them.","Just as Yuan had sensed their presence from afar, those cultivators also detected his-and naturally, they","could tell he was with the woman. Though they had only been together briefly, it still marked them as","connected in some way.","\"If you're talking about the injured woman I encountered just now, I don't know her or where she went.","Why are you guys chasing after her, anyway?\" Yuan said a moment later.","There were four of them in a group, three men and one woman, and they were all between the second","and third level of God Ascension. In other words, they were all powerhouses. As for the woman, she was","only at the first level of God Ascension.","\"If you don't know her, then why do you care about our business with her?\"","\"Not only was she greatly injured, but she was clearly running away from your group. If you have a good","reason for going after her, I won't interfere. I am just a concerned bystander, after all.\"","\"Interface? What can you, a mere Golden Immortal, even do to stop us? We can kill you with a sneeze.\"","One of the male cultivators sneered in disdain.","\"What can I do? You don't want to find out,\" Yuan responded with a calm smile. \"If you're not doing","anything wrong, you won't have to, either.\"","\"Enough!\" The female cultivator suddenly barked. \"Why the hell are we wasting our time on this meddler?","That bitch is getting away with our White Hell Frost Lotus!\"","\"White Hell Frost Lotus?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at the unfamiliar name. Still, he quickly pieced the","situation together-it was clear this group was chasing the woman for that treasure.","\"You're right. Let's just kill him and get this over with! Gu Ruyan, you can take care of this bastard. We'll","go on ahead.\"","\"Leave him to me. It will only take a few moments to erase his existence from this world,\" said the man","named Gu Ruyan.","Without another word, the other three left the scene to chase after the woman. Yuan didn't stop them and","focused on the man surnamed Gu before him.<azbe1a> Latest content published on novel-fire.ɴet</azbe1a>","\"Your surname is Gu? Do you happen to be from Seven Legacy Families?\" Yuan asked, realizing that it'd","been a long time since he last spoke of their name.","Gu Ruyan's eyes widened slightly with surprise. \"You know me? And you still decided to stand in my","way?\"","Yuan chuckled and said, \"No, I have no clue who you are. In fact, this is my first time hearing your name.","That said, I have had several encounters with the Gu Family before, so I am very familiar with your family.\"","Gu Ruyan narrowed his eyes at Yuan, uncertain whether he was a friend or foe of the Gu Family. If Yuan","turned out to be an ally, the situation would become far more complicated-and killing him would not be","so easy. \"What's your relationship with my Gu Family?\" Gu Ruyan asked.","\"We're good friends,\" Yuan lied, a bright smile on his face.","\"R-Really?\" Gu Ruyan was speechless.","\"No, I am joking.\"","\"You!\" Gu Ruyan's expression immediately darkened, his gaze full of anger and killing intent. \"How dare","you mock me!\"","\"Relax, that was a joke as well. I really am friends with the Gu Family-but the one I know is from the","lower heavens,\" Yuan said calmly.","\"The lower heavens? Why would you be familiar with-\" Gu Ruyan suddenly halted his words, and his","expression grew grim. \"There was an incident in the lower heavens where many members of the Gu","Family, including their patriarch, were slaughtered. No, it wasn't just the Gu Family. The other Legacy","Families, as well as the Ji Family, were also involved. You wouldn't happen to know anything about that,","would you?\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan responded, \"You just brought back some unpleasant memories, but to","answer your question... Yes, I happen to know a thing or two about it. After all, I was also there when it","happened.\"","Gu Ruyan's expression darkened further as he asked in a cold voice, \"I never asked for your name... but if","I had to guess, it wouldn't happen to be Yuan, would it?\"","\"Wow, that's amazing. How did you guess? Are you a fortune teller, by any chance?\"","\"I'LL KILL YOU, YOU BASTARD!\"","Without another word, Gu Ruyan drew his sword and lunged at Yuan, his entire cultivation base surging","forth.","Yuan drew Number One Under Heaven to block the incoming strike. The moment their swords collided, a","powerful ripple spread through the area-yet it barely disturbed the raging snowstorm.","\"According to the information we received, you're one of those outsiders who entered the Nine Heavens","with the Celestial Emperor's help! It hasn't even been a century since then! How in the world did you","reach the Eighth Heaven so quickly?!\" Gu Ruyan demanded, unable to believe a Player could advance to","their realm in such a short time. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2152,"title":"Chapter 2152: Gu Ruyan","paragraphs":["\"So you know that I am a Player, huh? Is it really that surprising for me to be here?\" Yuan responded with a calm smile as he blocked Gu Ruyan's next strike with ease.","\"We have been keeping track of their progress, and most of them are still in the Fifth Heaven! So how in Heaven's name are you in the Eighth Heaven? In the seventh region of White Hell, no less!\" Although those in the upper heavens were forbidden from approaching Players until they reached the Seventh Heaven, many influential clans and powerful sects still kept close watch on their progress. This way, they could not only recruit them once they qualified, but also prepare themselves to deal with them if necessary.","\"And how the hell are you still alive? I thought the others had already taken care of you, hence why we stopped looking for you!\" Gu Ruyan couldn't believe that Yuan had been alive this entire time. The events in the lower heavens sent shockwaves throughout not only that realm but even the upper heavens, for never before had anyone dared to provoke the Ji Family, much less slaughter Lord Ji.","\"Why wouldn't I be alive? You guys didn't even attack me. In fact, that ambush you laid at the Stairway to Heaven had only managed to kill innocent Players.\" When Yuan first heard about the incident, he couldn't help but laugh and feel sorry for the players at the same time.","\"Hmph! Regardless, your luck ends here. I'll finish today what the others failed to accomplish!\" Gu Ruyan declared, retrieving a familiar-looking treasure.","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the rod in his hand. \"The Rod of Destruction, huh? You must be desperate to kill me if you're bringing that out so soon.\"","\"What?!\" Gu Ruyan's movements suddenly halted, and he stared at Yuan with wide eyes. \"Y-You... How do you know about the Rod of Destruction?! This item is extremely scarce and only available to a few people!\"","Without any explanation, Yuan retrieved the Rod of Destruction he obtained from Zeng Guoquan at the Absyssal Underground and showed it to Gu Ruyan.","\"You! Why the fuck do you have that?! How did you obtain it?!\"","\"I picked it up.\"","\"Bullshit!\"","\"So, what are you going to do now? Want to use it at the same time and see who comes out alive?\" Yuan said with a calm smile on his face.","Hearing Yuan's words, Gu Ruyan sneered, \"You probably don't know this, but there are three tiers of rarity for the Rod of Destruction, and the higher the tier, the more powerful it is! While your Rod of Destruction is only tier 3, mine is tier 2! I'll completely obliterate you!\"","\"In that case, why don't you show me just how powerful your tier 2 Rod of Destruction really is? If not, I'll use mine,\" Yuan said, spreading his arms in a provoking gesture.","Without hesitation, Gu Ruyan began pouring his spiritual energy into the Rod of Destruction. Although using such a powerful treasure may seem excessive at face value, Gu Ruyan considered Yuan to be threatening enough to use it. Although Yuan was only a Golden Immortal while he himself was a God Ascension cultivator, Gu Ruyan realized from their brief exchanges that Yuan actually surpassed him in sheer prowess. Moreover, with Yuan's status as a Player blessed by the Celestial Emperor, Gu Ruyan knew he could not afford to treat him lightly. \"This bastard was strong enough to kill Lord Ji and the others in the lower heavens. He cannot be underestimated!\" Gu Ruyan thought to himself as he pointed the Rod of Destruction at Yuan. \"Pulverize this bastard!\"","The Rod of Destruction released a surge of black aura, and from its tip burst a crimson beam that struck toward Yuan in an instant. At the same time, Gu Ruyan used a treasure that instantly teleported him tens of thousands of miles away from his original location.","The instant the crimson beam touched Yuan, it erupted, creating a massive mushroom cloud that swept away the raging snowstorm of the seventh region and obliterated every mountain within a five-thousand- mile radius. The destruction was so powerful that even a God Ascension cultivator would instantly perish beneath its prowess.","\"What the fuck?!\" The other three from Gu Ruyan's group were shocked when they saw the commotion behind them. \"Did that bastard really use the Rod of Destruction to take care of a mere Golden Immortal?! What is that idiot doing?!\"","\"The two of you go ahead! I'll go back and see the situation!\" one of the men said. The other two nodded their head and continued their pursuit. Meanwhile, the one who stayed behind began traveling back to Gu Ruyan.","\"Holy shit...\" Gu Ruyan muttered, his eyes wide and his mouth agape as he stared at the devastation. It was his first time witnessing the Rod of Destruction in action-and its power far exceeded anything he had imagined. \"No wonder the others were going crazy for this thing. The range might not be that wide, but the raw power is insane... anyone caught in the blast would be wiped out without a trace.\"","Sure enough, the power was so overwhelming that not even Yuan's physique could withstand it. His body was completely obliterated, but his soul endured, suffering only minor injuries that quickly healed on their own.","\"Alright, that was a little scary,\" Yuan muttered as his body rapidly regenerated from nothing but his soul. When his form reconstituted, he found himself far from the blast site, having been hurled away by its sheer force.","\"By the heavens... never have I witnessed a treasure so fearsome,\" Yu Ning murmured, her voice dazed. Feng Yuxiang nodded her head in agreement. \"Though the world holds many powerful treasures, few-if any can rival its sheer destructive might.\"","\"And this isn't even the strongest Rod of Destruction. If this is only the second strongest, how terrifying must the first-tier one be?\" Yuan sighed. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2153,"title":"Chapter 2153: Gu Ruyan (2)","paragraphs":["\"What are you going to do next, Young Master?\" Yu Ning asked Yuan shortly later. Yuan initially planned to return to Gu Ruyan, but he changed his mind when he sensed that one of Gu Ruyan's friends had returned. \"He definitely thinks I died to the Rod of Destruction, so I'll deal with Gu Ruyan later. Right now, I should save that woman before his friends catch up to her and kill her.\" Yuan had activated Shadow Veil the moment he restored his body, so Gu Ruyan was unaware that he had survived the attack. Thus, Yuan chased after the other two while Gu Ruyan reunited with his friend who had just returned.","\"Gu Ruyan! What the fuck do you think you are doing, using the Rod of Destruction in this place?! Don't tell me you used it just to take care of that Golden Immortal!\" The friend immediately began lecturing Gu Ruyan the moment they reunited.","\"I-I had no choice! He also had a Rod of Destruction with him! If I hadn't used it, he would've used it on me!\" Gu Ruyan exclaimed his reasoning.","\"What? That Golden Immortal had a Rod of Destruction, too? Unless he's part of the faction, that's impossible. And if he really had one, why did you kill him? What if he was an ally?!\"","\"No, he wasn't an ally. He got the Rod of Destruction from someone else. I heard that Zeng Guoquan had recently perished at the Abyssal Underground. It's likely that he took it from her.\"","\"Didn't Zeng Guoquan die from a natural phenomenon there?\"","\"That's what we were told, but nobody truly knows since no one actually witnessed her death. If not for that, I can't imagine how that bastard got his hands on a Rod of Destruction. Another reason I know he's no ally is because that man was Yuan-the one who slaughtered Lord Ji and many of the Seven Legacy Families' leaders back in Spirit Heaven,\" Gu Ruyan revealed.","\"W-Wait a second. He was that Yuan?! I thought he'd died in the ambush at the Stairway to Heaven!\" His friend exclaimed with disbelief.","\"He said that the ambush had only killed innocent people. I don't know how he managed to slip away back then, but he's definitely dead now. There's no chance he could've survived the Rod of Destruction.\" He was certain the Rod of Destruction had struck Yuan because once its laser locked onto a target, it would cling to them. Even if Yuan had tried to escape with a movement technique or a treasure, it would still have followed him.","\"Regardless, let's get out of here before someone comes and questions us. We cannot let the world know of the Rod of Destruction's existence right now. It's still too early.\" Gu Ruyan nodded, and the two quickly departed to resume their pursuit. However, they chose not to rejoin their companions right away, wary that someone might have witnessed everything.","Meanwhile, the male and female cultivators who had never abandoned the chase finally caught up to the woman they had been pursuing all along. \"We've finally caught you, you little rat who stole our White Hell Frost Lotus!\"","\"That's funny, because I don't recall ever stealing it from you. In fact, I was the one who harvested the White Hell Frost Lotus-you bastards were the ones trying to steal it from me!\" the injured woman snapped.","\"That's nonsense! We had been camping the White Hell Frost Lotus long before you ever showed up! You just got lucky and harvested it while we were distracted!\" one of them retorted.","\"Hah! Empty words! Anyone can claim that without proof! I watched over the White Hell Frost Lotus for an entire year, and not once did I see any of you there!\" she shot back.","The female pursuer shook her head and said, \"Why bother arguing with someone who will soon be a corpse? If you obediently hand over the White Hell Frost Lotus, we'll let you die a peaceful death. Otherwise, we'll make it as painful and shameful as possible.\" The injured woman gritted her teeth in frustration, her eyes clouded with despair as the realization struck-that there was no one to help her, and she was truly going to die here. Tears welled in the woman's eyes, but the extreme cold of White Hell froze them the instant they appeared.","\"This is why you should've accepted my help when I offered it.\" A familiar voice suddenly echoed through the air.","\"Who's there?!\" The two pursuers tensed in alarm, but no matter how they searched, they couldn't sense a single presence nearby, as if they were hearing the voice of a ghost. The next moment, a figure appeared before the injured woman like a ghost.","\"Y-You! You're that Golden Immortal from before! Why the hell are you here?! What happened to Gu Ruyan and Lin Canye?!\" The two instantly recognized Yuan's handsome face and exclaimed in a startled voice. \"Don't tell me you killed them!\" said the male pursuer.","\"That's impossible! There's no way a Golden Immortal like him could kill two God Ascension cultivators!\" the woman expressed her doubt.","Pulver, Yuan complete Browsered Rankings Updatesatte Randomthe Adved woman before him.","offer still stands. Do you need my help?\" Yuan asked her.","\"Why would you risk your life to help me...?\" she asked skeptically. \"We don't even know each other.\"","Yuan smiled warmly. \"So what if we don't? Since when do we need to know someone in order to help them? I saw someone in need, so I offered my hand. That said, you look like someone I know.\" The injured woman was left speechless. Benevolent cultivators like Yuan were rare in the cultivation world, especially at their level. After all, the best way to survive was to mind one's own business, and meddling in matters that didn't concern them was the quickest way to court death.","\"W-What is your name?\" she suddenly asked.","\"My name is Yuan.\"","\"Yuan?\" The other two frowned, their brows lifting at the familiar name, though they didn't immediately recognize it.","\"Please... help me, Yuan,\" the injured woman pleaded. Yuan gave a silent nod in acknowledgment, his gaze steady. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)","ធ","A"]},{"number":2154,"title":"Chapter 2154: Familiar-Looking Sword","paragraphs":["\"Hah!\" The other woman suddenly sneered out loud. \"I don't know how you managed to escape Gu Ruyan and Lin Canye, but you're in no position to help others.\"","Yuan turned to face the woman and asked, \"And who are you? Are you also surnamed Gu? Or do you belong to one of the other Legacy Families?\"","\"You know who we are?\" The woman expressed surprise at Yuan's words.","\"Not really, but now I know you're with the Seven Legacy Families.\"","\"You know our background, yet you still want to defy us? You're dumber than I thought,\" said the man beside her.","Yuan shifted his gaze toward him and sneered. \"Let's not pretend the Seven Legacy Families are some grand power in the upper heavens. You may have been all-powerful in the lower realms, but up here, your influence is nothing special.\"","\"How dare you! Our families may not appear as imposing in the upper heavens, but that's only because we choose not to stand out! In truth, our influence is anything but small!\" the man barked.","\"Shut up! Why the hell are you telling him everything?!\" the woman suddenly snapped at him.","\"S-Sorry... but does it really matter? He's going to die soon, anyway.\"","\"If your friend couldn't kill me even with the Rod of Destruction, what can the two of you little sheep do to me?\" Yuan said.","\"?!?!\" Their eyes went wide, astonishment all over their faces, as Yuan's words were nothing short of unbelievable. Gu Ruyan had a tier 2 Rod of Destruction, which could instantly kill anyone below the third level of God Ascension. Yet, the man standing before them was only a Golden Immortal. Unless Gu Ruyan missed the attack, there was simply no chance that Yuan could've survived it.","\"What should we do, Sister Chen? If what he says is true-\"","\"Zhuang Maojiang, are you an idiot?! Of course he's bluffing! Now hurry up and kill him! I will take care of that thieving bitch!\" she shouted.","Zhuang Maojiang gave a hurried nod before drawing forth his battleaxe, then charged toward Yuan in the next instant. Expecting Zhuang Maojiang to finish Yuan quickly, the woman surnamed Chen circled around the fight and rushed toward the injured woman.","However, in their very first exchange, Yuan completely overpowered Zhuang Maojiang, sending him flying back before turning to confront the woman.","\"What the hell are you doing, Zhuang Maojiang?! Stop playing around and kill him already!\"","\"What the ?!\" Zhuang Maojiang's face twisted in shock as he realized he had just lost to Yuan's sword. His cultivation was higher, and his battleaxe should have held the advantage in direct clashes-yet he still lost, and so decisively at that.","However, the woman's voice jolted him back to his senses, and he forcefully shook off his shock before flying at Yuan once more. This time, he didn't just use raw strength.","\"Heavy Dragon's Descent!\" Zhuang Maojiang raised his battleaxe high, activating a martial technique that caused the weapon to swell in size. Once it had grown several times larger, he brought it down in a vertical slash aimed at Yuan.","\"Hmph.\" Yuan sneered and casually swung his sword upward, meeting Zhuang Maojiang's axe head-on once again. When their weapons collided, the mountains behind Yuan and the ground beneath them split apart. Yet Yuan stood perfectly fine-his grip steady, his stance unshaken, barely moving from the clash. After refining the Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence, Yuan's raw power had skyrocketed, surpassing not only the limits of humans but even those of dragons. At this moment, there was no one who could rival him in sheer strength, and this doesn't even take into account his True Dragon Awakening, which would only further boost his strength.","\"Scram!\" Yuan swung his sword the next moment, sending Zhuang Maojiang and his axe flying into the distance.","\"Impossible!\" The woman surnamed Chen exclaimed after witnessing their exchange. \"Who the hell are you?!\"","\"I already gave you my name,\" he calmly responded.","\"That's not what I meant!\" she cried out loud.","However, her brows suddenly twitched, and her eyes slowly widened as though she had just realized something. \"Wait a second... Yuan? That's the name of the madman who slaughtered the Lord of Spirit Heaven, along with the leaders of the Seven Legacy Families that ruled there! How are you still alive?! I was told you had been taken care of!\"","\"Sorry to disappoint you, but as you can see, I am very much alive.\"","The woman gritted her teeth and drew her weapon-a purple sword that radiated an ominous aura that distorted the very air around it.","Yuan raised his eyebrows when he saw her familiar-looking sword, but before he could even say anything, the sword in his grasp trembled, and Zi Xuan's voice boomed inside his head, \"That's my sword!\" The sword in the woman's grasp was none other than Violet Dream, one of the Exalted Blacksmith's earliest creations. It was also something he had given to Zi Xuan in the past. And Zi Xuan, who had been asleep this entire time, was jolted awake by its familiar aura.","\"You should've stayed hidden after barely escaping with your life last time. Now that you've shown yourself, I'll make sure to finish the job,\" the woman said as she leveled Violet Dream at Yuan's face.","\"This bitch...\" Zi Xuan growled, her trembling voice on the verge of erupting. \"Not only is she tainting my treasure with her filthy hands, but she dares to point it at you?! I'll tear her apart, limb by limb!\"","\"Calm down. There's no need to waste your energy on a weakling like her,\" Yuan said quickly, trying to soothe her anger.","\"But my Violet Dream!\"","\"Don't worry, I'll get it back for you.\"","\"Alright... but you better hurry, or I might accidentally do it myself.\"","Meanwhile, the woman surnamed Chen suddenly felt a chill run down her spine, and an unexplainable urge to flee seized her. Even though Zi Xuan had not emerged from the sword, her killing intent was so overwhelming that it alerted Chen's survival instincts. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2155,"title":"Chapter 2155: Creator’s Mark","paragraphs":["\"So, what are you going to do with that Violet Dream? Put me into an eternal slumber?\" Yuan asked the woman, snapping her out of her daze.","\"You recognize this sword?\" she muttered in a surprised tone, before quickly adding, \"No, I shouldn't be surprised. This is a very famous sword, created by the legendary blacksmith, the Exalted Blacksmith, after all!\"","\"Where'd you get it?\" Yuan then asked.","\"That's none of your business. Instead of wasting your last few words on such questions, why don't you beg for your life instead?\"","\"Beg for my life? I don't think I have done so in all my lives,\" Yuan responded with a smile.","\"Lives?\" The woman raised an eyebrow at his strange choice of words but dismissed it as a slip of the tongue.","\"Sister Chen, let's fight him together! He's far more powerful than he appears!\" Zhuang Maojiang shouted as he finally returned after being sent flying into the distance. He could still feel his arms trembling from his clash with Yuan.","Lady Chen then spoke, \"Get him!\" At her command, Zhuang Maojiang lunged at Yuan from behind as Lady Chen pressed in from the front. However, it didn't take long for them to realize that defeating Yuan wouldn't be easy, even when attacking together. They could not fathom how they were being held at bay by one bound to the Golden Immortal realm.","Sometime later, as they were beginning to lose hope, Gu Ruyan and Lin Canye finally returned to their side. \"What the fuck?! That bastard is still alive! Gu Ruyan, you imbecile! You recklessly used the Rod of Destruction and didn't even kill your target?!\" Lin Canye shouted after seeing Yuan.","\"That's impossible\"! Gu Ruyan exclaimed in a startled voice, sounding like he'd just witnessed a ghost. \"I am certain that the Rod of Destruction had attached to him! His presence even completely vanished after the explosion!\"","\"Then are you trying to say that we're looking at a ghost right now?! One's that's fighting Sister Chen and Zhuang Maojiang?!\" Lin Canye pointed at Yuan's figure in the distance.","Gu Ruyan gritted his teeth and said, \"I don't know how he managed to survive, but we can figure that out later. We need to help them first! That bastard is much stronger than his cultivation suggests!\" Without any hesitation, the two of them joined the fight the very next moment.","\"Welcome back,\" Yuan said to them.","\"What took you two idiots so long to come back?!\" Lady Chen reprimanded.","\"We had to make sure nobody saw the Rod of Destruction going off, so we took a slight detour,\" Lin Canye explained.","\"Whatever. Let's hurry up and kill this bastard. The White Hell Frost Lotus is waiting for us!\" And so, Yuan was forced to contend with all four God Ascension cultivators simultaneously. The injured woman, witnessing this, could only stare in stunned silence, her lips parted and her face awash with disbelief.","\"What's taking you so long to take care of a few pipsqueaks? Hurry up and kill them!\" Zi Xuan urged, her patience running thin.","\"Then why don't you remove some of the restrictions you have placed on the sword? I should be strong enough to handle more now,\" said Yuan, referring to the Number One Under Heaven having its power limited by her due to his lack of cultivation.","\"I guess it's fine to loosen a few restrictions right now, but you are still far away from handling me at my full potential.\" The next moment-<Sword Spirit 'Zi Xuan' has removed a restriction placed upon Number One Under Heaven><Number One Under Heaven has been updated>[Unique Ability (5): When wielding Number One Under Heaven, the wielder's Sword Aura efficiency and power are increased by 100,000%] Sometime later, when they still hadn't managed to defeat Yuan, Lady Chen shouted in frustration, \"Restrict his movements for me!\" To unleash Violet Dream's ability, she needed to land a direct hit, but so far, she hadn't even touched Yuan. At her command, the other three immediately charged at Yuan, intent on pinning him down so Lady Chen could strike.","\"Even if you manage to land a hit, Violet Dream won't affect me.\"","\"You're bluffing!\" Lady Chen snapped.","\"You think so? Then go ahead.\" Yuan suddenly ceased moving, spreading his arms wide in a defenseless stance as he beckoned her forward.","Without hesitation, Lady Chen lunged forward and stabbed the Violet Dream directly in his chest, purposefully avoiding his heart so he wouldn't die immediately. After landing her strike, Lady Chen immediately tried to activate Violet Dream's ability. But her expression darkened when she realized it wasn't responding. Since Number One Under Heaven was out, it'd sealed Violet Dream's ability, turning it into an ordinary sword. However, even without Number One Under Heaven, Violet Dream still wouldn't have any effect on Yuan.","\"W-Why?! Why isn't it working?!\" Lady Chen cried, violently shaking the sword as though she could force it awake.","\"It's useless.\" Yuan suddenly said as he moved his arm and pointed at the Violet Dream before uttering, \"Reveal yourself.\" In the next instant, a glowing symbol surfaced on the sword's blade, radiating a divine","aura.","\"This... this is...\" Lady Chen's eyes widened in a daze as she stared at the golden symbol, unable to believe what she was seeing.","\"Isn't that the Creator's Mark?!\" Gu Ruyan remarked, shock flashing across his face.","\"What? But isn't that something only its creator can reveal?\" Lin Canye cried. A Creator's Mark is something blacksmiths embed within their creations as proof of authorship, serving both as a signature and a means of verifying the weapon's legitimacy. Although anyone could see the Creator's Mark on a treasure, only its creator could activate it.","\"Wait... if the mark has manifested at this moment... does that mean he's the creator?\" Zhuang Maojiang questioned, his voice laced with confusion. Nobody answered his question, as they didn't want to believe the implications. After a long silence, Lady Chen slowly lifted her gaze from the sword to Yuan, who hovered before them with a cold smile.","\"Impossible...\" she muttered. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2156,"title":"Chapter 2156: Barbarians","paragraphs":["\"That's impossible! You can't possibly be the Exalted Blacksmith!\" Lady Chen shouted, her voice sharp","enough to cut through the air. \"I know! This sword must be a fake—it can't be the real Violet Dream!\" Desperately, she created an excuse, however absurd it may be. To her, it was still more reasonable than accepting the notion that Yuan could be the Exalted Blacksmith.","\"You can believe whatever you want, but it won't change the fact that you're holding onto something that belongs to me,\" Yuan said as he beckoned for the weapon. \"Hand me the sword, and I will grant you a painless death. Refuse, and I will take it myself—along with your fingers, perhaps even your limbs,\" Yuan said as his aura surged violently.","Seeing this, the four of them tensed instantly, and Lady Chen quickly drew her Rod of Destruction. Yuan glanced at the rod in her grasp and smiled. \"Have you already forgotten? Your companion tried that on me once before, but here I am, still alive.\"","\"If one isn't enough, how about two?!\" Lin Canye barked, drawing his own Rod of Destruction. \"I have one as well!\" Zhuang Maojiang shouted, quickly brandishing his rod after the others. Seeing this, Gu Ruyan could only watch with clenched fists.","\"I'm flattered, but it doesn't matter how many of those you bring out-you won't kill me,\" Yuan said with a calm smile.","\"Then prove it with your life!\" Lady Chen snapped, spiritual energy surging as she poured it into the Rod of Destruction. When the other two noticed Lady Chen truly preparing to unleash the Rod of Destruction, they quickly funneled their spiritual energy into their own treasures.","The smile on Yuan's face suddenly stiffened, his expression darkening.","\"Hah! So it was all a bluff! You're actually trembling in fear, aren't you?!\" Lady Chen laughed mockingly. In truth, Yuan had no concern for their Rods of Destruction, as such weapons were beneath his notice. His frown was born from something far more troubling.","In the very next instant, several powerful presences emerged, surrounding them. Before the others could even react, many silhouettes materialized, encircling them completely.","\"What the ? Who the hell are you?!\" Gu Ruyan shouted.","Lady Chen opened her mouth to speak, but the words died in her throat as she realized that their encirclement was made entirely of God Ascension powerhouses. While the other four panicked, Yuan remained calm, his gaze sweeping over their encirclement. There were exactly twenty-two figures, each clad in crude garments of thick animal fur, their rugged features giving them the appearance of barbarians. As for these barbarians, their attention was focused on the Rods of Destruction in their hands. \"W-What do you want from us?\" Zhuang Maojiang stammered.","One of the barbarians finally spoke, though his words weren't directed at him. \"Is that the weapon you saw?\"","A calm, gentle voice echoed the next moment. \"Yes. That is the weapon responsible for the explosion- the one that devastated much of our land.\"","The barbarian who had first spoken stepped forward, his voice carrying authority. \"The six of you will come with us. Refuse, and you will die where you stand.\"","\"Who the hell are you to tell us what to do? Do you even realize who we are? We are \" Lin Canye scoffed, his voice dripping with challenge.","However, he never even got to finish his sentence, as the barbarian leader's arm blurred through the air, and in the next instant, Lin Canye's head was sent flying, severed cleanly from his body. Of course, as a God Ascension cultivator, losing his body did not mean losing his life. But the one who struck did not pause, and after severing Lin Canye's head, he extended his hand in a grasping motion toward the lingering soul. An immense pressure coiled around Lin Canye's soul, then crushed it without mercy. This was all done in an instant, faster than anyone could even blink, leaving the other three wide-eyed, trembling in shock and fear. Lin Canye's corpse began falling from the sky, but one of the barbarians went to retrieve it.","\"Anyone else have any objections?\" The barbarian leader asked.","\"...\" Lady Chen and the others hastily shook their head in silence, too afraid to even speak.","And so, Yuan and the others had no choice but to follow the barbarians deeper into White Hell. Of course, this included the injured woman.","\"W-What's happening...?\" she stuck close to Yuan and asked him.","\"We'll know in a bit,\" he responded in a calm voice.","He then glanced at her and asked, \"How's your condition? Can you endure the cold?\"","The woman looked at the Sun Stone in her grasp for a moment before responding, \"I'm fine for now, but I don't think my Sun Stone will last much longer.\"","Yuan then said, \"Don't worry, nothing will happen to you. I promised to help you, so I will get you out of here safely.\"","\"Alright... By the way, I don't think I have introduced myself yet. My name is Yaoqin.\"","\"Nice to meet you, Yaoqin.\" Yuan smiled.","Gu Ruyan and the other two were in utter disbelief. While they trembled at the thought of being kidnapped by these unknown barbarians, Yuan appeared completely at ease, almost as if their current predicament didn't exist at all, and he was just with a group of old pals. The barbarians, too, noticed his calm demeanor and grew curious. Within their ranks, one individual fixed their eyes on Yuan, watching him with far greater intensity than the others.","Yuan noticed the intent gaze and boldly turned to confront it. Positioned at the very back of the formation was a figure wrapped in a great fur robe that concealed most of their features. Yet what could not be hidden were their eyes-clear, piercing blue, and as immaculate as untouched ice beneath a winter sky. Though he didn't recognize the individual, a strange sense of familiarity stirred within him. Suddenly, the image of a silhouette riding a massive mammoth, which he had glimpsed upon first entering the seventh region, surfaced in his mind. 'So you were that silhouette, huh?' Yuan thought inwardly. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2157,"title":"Chapter 2157: Barbarians (2)","paragraphs":["After several days of travel, the barbarians halted at the border of the Eighth Region, where a small settlement unexpectedly stood. Lady Chen and the others were stunned-none of them had believed it was possible for anyone to survive White Hell's extreme environment long enough to build a home there. Shortly after arriving, the barbarians gathered them together and stood around them in silence. After several long minutes of silence, Gu Ruyan finally gathered the courage to ask, \"What are you going to do to us?\" The barbarians turned their gazes on him, and the sheer weight of their eyes made him tremble with fear.","\"What do you think we're going to do?\" a calm voice suddenly replied. Gu Ruyan and the others turned toward the sound, where a tall figure stepped out from one of the nearby buildings. She was a tall, muscular woman, her frame radiating dominance. From her surged an overwhelming aura-the unmistakable might of an expert at the Seventh Level of God Ascension. Following closely behind her was the barbarian who killed Lin Canye, as well as the individual riding the giant mammoth.","\"H-How should I know? You're the ones who kidnapped us without a word of explanation,\" Gu Ruyan finally replied.","\"Without explanation, you say?\" The muscular woman lifted her arm, revealing the Rod of Destruction taken from Lin Canye's corpse. \"Because of this little toy, you not only destroyed a large part of our territory, but also killed one of our people,\" she said coldly.","\"No way...\" Gu Ruyan muttered in a daze. \"I-I didn't know there were people living inside White Hell, much less in the seventh region, hence why I decided to use it!\" he said.","\"I don't care for your reasoning. It doesn't change the fact that one of our people is dead because of you.\"","\"Wait just a second!\" Lady Chen suddenly cut in. \"He's the one who triggered that weapon and killed your people! Why drag all of us into this? You've already killed one of ours, so why not call it even?\"","\"Call it even?\" the barbarian snarled, her glare burning into Lady Chen. \"Do you truly believe your lives are worth the same as ours? Even if we slaughtered every last one of you, it still wouldn't repay the loss of a single one of our people!\"","\"That's unreasonable!\" Zhuang Maojiang cried.","\"Unreasonable?\" the barbarian retorted coldly. \"I heard you were ready to unleash this weapon again before my people intervened. If not for them, even more of our land would have been reduced to ruin!\"","Yuan then spoke, \"I understand why you'd want their lives, but what about me and her?\" He gestured to Yaoqin, who was standing so close to him that she was essentially clinging to his arm. \"We're also their victims,\" he continued.","The barbarian sneered, \"Victims or not, it doesn't change the fact that you are involved. If you hadn't started a fight with them, they wouldn't have needed to use the weapon in the first place.\"","Yuan sighed at her response. \"Since you've clearly made up your mind, there's no point in arguing. So tell me, what do you intend to do with us for our crimes?\"","The barbarian's eyes narrowed. \"Simply executing you would be far too easy. And besides, it would be a waste, as few ever venture this deep into White Hell.\" A vicious smile curved across her lips as she continued, \"Here's how it will be your men will serve as training dummies for our warriors and your women will entertain them in other ways.\"","Lady Chen and Yaoqin's expressions turned grim at the barbarian's words.","\"I'd sooner die than become a toy for you savages!\" Lady Chen shouted, drawing her Rod of Destruction. \"You were fools not to strip us of our treasures!\"","The barbarian laughed. \"We didn't take your treasures because we're not the least bit worried. I can kill you long before you even think of activating that weapon.\"","Lady Chen gritted her teeth, feeling powerless before these brutes. \"I-If you kill us, our families will avenge us-they'll wipe out your insignificant clan!\" Lady Chen shouted desperately.","The barbarian sneered. \"Do you know how long we've lived here? We know White Hell like the back of our hands. Your families would die long before they even reach us, and even if a few survived, they'd never be able to pursue us through this place.\"","\"T-That's-!\" Lady Chen faltered, unable to find her words, and fell silent. The others, too, sank into despair as the weight of their situation settled over them. Yuan alone remained calm, unshaken amidst the tension.","At that moment, the cloaked figure who had been watching Yuan all along could no longer restrain their curiosity and slowly approached him. Standing before Yuan, the figure finally spoke. \"Why aren't you afraid?\" The voice was that of a young woman, clear and unassuming.","\"Should I be afraid?\" Yuan replied with a calm smile.","The figure glanced at the others, trembling in fear, before turning back to him. \"Is it because of your body?\" she asked.","\"My body? What are you talking about?\" Yuan asked with his eyebrows slightly raised.","\"I noticed it the first time I saw you twenty years ago. Your body is different from the others,\" she said. At her words, the surrounding barbarians narrowed their eyes at Yuan. They, too, could sense something unusual about him, though none could discern exactly what it was.","\"Now that you mention it...\" The other female barbarian stepped forward, studying Yuan intently. \"His body isn't being affected by White Hell's environment at all. If anything, it looks as though it grows stronger with each passing moment. It's a bit similar to our own physique.\" After a brief silence, she continued, \"You know what? Rather than letting the others kill you, we'll study your body instead.\"","Yuan let out a faint sigh. \"I couldn't care less what you do with those three idiots, but if you harm me or my friend, I'll be left with no choice but to slaughter everyone here in self-defense.\" His sharp words rang in the barbarians' ears, instantly igniting their auras and filling the air with killing intent. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2158,"title":"Chapter 2158: Absolute Dragon Awakening","paragraphs":["After a long, tense silence, the barbarian suddenly burst into laughter, her voice so powerful it rattled the air itself. \"You'll slaughter us all? With what-your pitiful cultivation base?\" she mocked.","\"I wouldn't recommend it, but you're more than welcome to find out,\" Yuan responded with a calm smile on his handsome face.","The barbarian's grin vanished, replaced by a chilling frown. \"I dislike you. Arrogant, weak, and oblivious- you don't even know when to hold your tongue.\" Without giving Yuan a chance to respond, she lifted her arm high and struck. In the blink of an eye, his head was reduced to nothing.","\"Yuan!\" Yaoqin cried, her eyes going wide with horror. How could it be? He had fallen so easily, when only moments ago his calm and confidence had seemed unshakable.","Seeing this, Lady Chen muttered, \"I knew he was bluffing this entire time... I should've killed him when I had the chance!\" Strangely, even after his head had been annihilated, Yuan's body showed no sign of collapse. It stood tall and unwavering, exuding the eerie impression that he was still very much alive.","\"How unpleasant.\" The barbarian clicked her tongue and reached for Yuan's body. Though she had destroyed his head, she had deliberately left the rest intact since she still intended to study his physique.","What followed left the barbarian-and everyone else-frozen in shock. The headless corpse moved. Against all logic, it raised an arm and caught the barbarian's hand in an unyielding grip. Then, everyone watched as Yuan's destroyed head regenerated completely.","\"Heavens! It's a monster!\" The barbarians cried out loud.","Once Yuan's regeneration was finished, he calmly stared at the barbarian before him and said, \"You'll need to do more than just destroy my head to kill me.\"","\"What the hell are you...?\" The barbarian muttered in a low voice.","\"Is that how he survived the Rod of Destruction?\" Gu Ruyan stared at Yuan in a daze.","The barbarian yanked and twisted, trying to break away from Yuan's grip. But to her utter disbelief, she could not budge an inch. His grasp was immovable, heavy as if a mountain itself were shackled to her arm. 'What is happening?! His raw strength... It's beyond comprehension!' the barbarian cried inwardly, panic flashing in her eyes.","While she was still caught in disbelief, Yuan pulled his other arm back and unleashed a devastating punch toward her face. Despite being lost in thought, the barbarian still managed to intercept Yuan's punch. But his strength was monstrous and beyond her comprehension. The instant their clash resounded, her body was wrenched from the ground, and before she even understood what had happened, she was sent crashing backward.","\"Chief Mu?!\" The other barbarians exclaimed in shock after seeing her being pushed back by a mere Golden Immortal.","The female barbarian, Chief Mu, quickly steadied herself in midair, though the shock on her face lingered and refused to fade. After staring at Yuan in silence, excitement suddenly lit up Chief Mu's face. Her cultivation burst forth in the next instant, flooding the area with tyrannical pressure. \"I don't care who or what you are. Survive ten of my attacks, and I'll let you and your friend live,\" she declared.","Yuan's lips curved into a smile. \"You'd better not go back on your word... or I'll kill you.\" As Yuan stepped forward, he activated Absolute Dragon Awakening the evolved form of True Dragon Awakening after consuming the Dragon Ancestor's Blood Essence. His aura soared skyward, surging to unimaginable heights. Compared to his former True Dragon Awakening, this new power was at least a hundred times stronger. More astonishing still, his cultivation, which had stagnated at Golden Immortal, suddenly shattered its bottleneck, propelling him into True Immortal. Yet this advancement was not a true breakthrough but merely a temporary boost brought on by Absolute Dragon Awakening. For that reason, it could not be counted toward his quest.","\"?!?!\" Chief Mu could scarcely believe what she was seeing-her features frozen in bewildered awe. And yet, instead of fear, a spark of exhilaration flared ever brighter in her eyes.","Since his opponent was a seventh-level God Ascension powerhouse, Yuan couldn't afford to go easy. Not only did he use Absolute Dragon Awakening, but he also retrieved Number One Under Heaven to fight Chief Mu. Though she stood at the Seventh Level of God Ascension-an expert nearing the peak of the cultivation world-Chief Mu didn't dare underestimate Yuan, despite him being merely an Immortal. She summoned her weapon: a pair of axes gleaming with a chilling light, as though carved from pure ice. Gripping them firmly, she advanced to confront Yuan.","With Number One Under Heaven in hand, Yuan cloaked it in his Supreme Sword Aura. Enhanced by its fifth unique ability, the aura sharpened to an unimaginable degree-so keen that even the slightest movement seemed to rend the fabric of space, leaving a visible scar in the air. In response, Chief Mu coated her axes with Supreme Axe Aura. Yet compared to Yuan's enhanced Supreme Sword Aura, hers was clearly inferior. To bridge the gap, she infused her weapons with Celestial Qi.","When they clashed a split second later, their weapon auras erupted outward, tearing countless slits through the surrounding space and exposing the ominous void beyond. Yet, in the next breath, the wounds in reality swiftly mended themselves.","\"That's one,\" Yuan said.","\"I can see why you're so damn arrogant, but you still have to survive nine more strikes!\" Chief Mu exclaimed as she prepared her second strike.","Meanwhile, Gu Ruyan and the others could only watch in stunned disbelief. \"We've been fighting a monster like that this whole time...?\" Lady Chen murmured in a daze.","\"Impossible... How can an outsider wield such power...?\" Gu Ruyan collapsed to his knees in despair.","Yaoqin remained silent, yet the astonishment in her eyes spoke louder than words. The barbarian wrapped in fur robes narrowed her eyes on Yuan, seemingly in deep thought. Moments later, Chief Mu unleashed her second strike, and Yuan confronted it with a smile. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2159,"title":"Chapter 2159: Ten Strikes From Chief Mu","paragraphs":["Chief Mu's second strike carried even greater force than her first. When it collided with Yuan's, the clash of their weapon auras unleashed a ripple that cleaved every mountain within a thousand miles cleanly in half. After using her second strike and seeing Yuan emerge completely unscathed, Chief Mu understood that ordinary attacks would not be able to defeat a monster like him.","On her third strike, Chief Mu gathered her spiritual energy and prepared to launch a martial technique. \"Glacial Roar!\" Chief Mu smashed her axes together, sending millions of tiny ice shards in Yuan's direction. Despite their small size, each of these shards was powerful enough to kill Immortals. Yet, Yuan didn't even bother blocking them, merely using his physique to endure them. <Your Cold Resistance has improved greatly>","\"Heavens! He used nothing but his body to block Chief Mu's Glacial Roar! I've never seen anything like that before!\" The barbarians stared in astonishment. Realizing that spiritual energy had no effect on Yuan, Chief Mu immediately shifted to using Immortal Qi. Though she was capable of wielding Celestial Qi with ease, she held back, as she was enjoying their battle too much to end it quickly.","For her fourth strike, Chief Mu raised her axes high. In the next instant, they swelled to the size of mountains before crashing down toward Yuan's figure, tiny and ant-like in comparison. In response, Yuan activated Number One Under Heaven's third ability, increasing the size of his sword to match Chief Mu's axes. Whoosh! Their clash unleashed a ripple of force so immense that every trace of snow in the surrounding land was erased in an instant. At the point of collision, space itself fractured once more, dark cracks spreading wide-and unlike before, the damage lingered, struggling to mend. Once again, Yuan endured her attack without any injuries.","'Just how many tricks does this monster have up his sleeves?!' Chief Mu cried inwardly as she prepared her fifth strike. For her fifth, sixth, and seventh strikes, Chief Mu continued to wield Immortal Qi, each time pouring in drastically more than before, and every single clash resulted in the space around them breaking.","After their seventh clash, the skies above White Hell darkened over Yuan's battlefield, as though the heavens were warning them to cease or suffer its wrath. \"Look at the sky! It suddenly turned dark!\" one of the barbarians exclaimed. \"You're right! But why? It's not even close to nightfall-and it feels unnatural.\" \"Heaven's Wrath...\" Gu Ruyan muttered in a daze. \"If they continue, they will have to face Heaven's Judgement!\" Their clash had reached such terrifying heights that even the heavens stirred, fearing the disastrous destruction that would follow if it were allowed to continue.","Chief Mu glanced at the dark clouds for a brief moment before disregarding them. As for Yuan, he didn't even spare it a glance, his gaze and focus remaining on Chief Mu like a predator locked onto its prey. Chief Mu sneered after seeing Yuan's calm demeanor and said, \"Alright, enough playing around. I'll get serious now.\" After saying that, Celestial Qi surged within her body.","\"Thank god. I was beginning to think that was all you had as a Seventh-Level God Ascension powerhouse,\" Yuan said sarcastically. \"I suppose it's only fair I get serious, too.\" As his words fell, Yuan's aura erupted violently, so fierce it momentarily split apart the dark clouds above.","\"He wasn't going all out this entire time?!\" Zhuang Maojiang exclaimed in a terrified voice. \"What an ominous aura he has! Is he even human?!\" The barbarians subconsciously stepped back after sensing Yuan's Chaotic Essence. However, Yuan wasn't done yet. The very next moment, Celestial Qi began gathering around his body, boosting his aura even more.","\"You can use Celestial Qi?!\" Chief Mu couldn't contain her surprise and cried out loud.","\"It's only Celestial Qi. What are you so surprised about?\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"There's no way he's using Celestial Qi as a Golden Immortal! He must be hiding his true cultivation! It's no wonder he could match Chief Mu! Everything makes sense now!\" The barbarians said, convinced that Yuan was just suppressing his cultivation.","\"No, that's his real cultivation.\" The barbarian wrapped in fur robes remarked.","\"What? How is that possible?\" The barbarians looked at her with puzzled faces. \"If he's really just an Immortal... How is his body able to endure it?\"","\"I...\" she opened her mouth only to instantly close it back up before silently shaking her head, as she was just as puzzled as the rest of them.","Suddenly, another voice rang out, \"Heaven Refining Physique. That's how he's doing it.\" At those words, everyone turned in shock. An old woman had appeared among them without a sound, as if she were a ghost.","\"G-Gramny Mu!\" The barbarians stared at her with wide eyes.","\"Grandmother, what are you doing here? Weren't you in seclusion?\" the fur-robed barbarian asked. Gramny Mu glanced at Yuan and Chief Mu before replying, \"With this kind of commotion, who could possibly concentrate? If I forced myself to continue, I'd only end up injured.\"","Lady Chen and the others swallowed nervously at the old woman's presence. Though no aura radiated from her, they could tell she was anything but ordinary-perhaps even stronger than Chief Mu herself.","\"By the way, what was that you just mentioned? Heaven Refining Physique?\" The fur-robed barbarian continued to ask.","Granny Mu stared at Yuan's figure for a moment before responding, \"It's a one-of-a-kind physique, so only one of them can exist at any given time. The last person to possess it stood uncontested at the peak of the cultivation world. To be honest, even I do not know its full capabilities, but I can say this much- back then, its wielder was unrivaled.\"","\"In that case, shouldn't we stop my mother before she kills him? It'd be such a waste to kill someone with such a rare and powerful physique.\"","Granny Mu burst out laughing at her words and quickly said, \"If he's who I think he is, your mother won't be able to kill him.\" The barbarians stared at her with their eyes filled with disbelief, wondering if she knew Yuan. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2160,"title":"Chapter 2160: Granny Mu","paragraphs":["Hearing such words, the fur-robed barbarian asked what was on everyone's mind, \"Grandmother... you know him?\"","\"Hard to say,\" she calmly responded. \"He looks exactly like someone once knew, but his cultivation is much lower, and there's something different about him. That said, the one I knew disappeared millions of years ago, but with his cultivation, I wouldn't be surprised if he is still alive.\"","\"Is this person the same one you would constantly reminisce about to Mother and me?\" the fur-robed barbarian asked.","Granny Mu responded with a silent nod of her head.","In the next instant, Chief Mu delivered her eighth blow, merging her martial technique with Celestial Qi to unleash a strike of devastating force. Yuan, however, met it head-on, unflinching. An exhilarated smile spread across his face. It had been ages since he'd been able to fight with his full strength, and the thrill of it set his blood ablaze.","Right before the clash, Granny Mu released her Celestial Qi, enveloping the barbarian settlement to shield it from the impending blast. Just as Granny Mu raised the barrier, a violent ripple tore through the land. Everything within ten thousand miles was erased, save for what her protection covered. Their clash not only reshaped White Hell's landscape but also left behind a massive crater.","However, moments after the cataclysm, the broken terrain began to mend on its own. This was no miracle, but a natural occurrence in places where spiritual energy condensed so heavily that even the land restored itself, some faster than others, depending on the area.","After the clash, Yuan slowly wiped his face with his hand, only to see a faint smear of blood. It was the first time he had been injured-but the wound was nothing more than a shallow cut, so insignificant it barely counted as an injury at all.","He turned to Chief Mu, who looked unscathed. Though her body bore no wounds, the shock of Yuan's unfathomable existence had damaged her mind.","Meanwhile, the dark clouds above swelled outward, their shade deepening into an even heavier darkness.","\"Maybe we should've taken this fight somewhere else—a place where we cannot be disturbed,\" Chief Mu spoke as she looked at the dark clouds with a slight frown on her face.","Yuan smiled and said, \"What are you scared of? It's just some dark clouds. It'll go away sooner or later.\"","Chief Mu narrowed her eyes. \"Just some dark clouds? Don't tell me you've never faced a Heavenly Tribulation before.\"","\"On the contrary,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"I've experienced them several times.\"","Chief Mu wasn't surprised to hear that Yuan had already experienced several Heavenly Tribulations because of how heaven-defying his existence was.","\"Anyway, enough yapping and give me your ninth strike,\" Yuan said a moment later. \"I don't have too much time to waste here.\"","Chief Mu's eyebrows twitched, and she spoke in an annoyed tone, \"You're so certain that you will endure all ten of my strikes, huh? Unfortunately for you, that won't happen!\" Suddenly, Chief Mu released a chilling aura that made Yuan's skin crawl. This cold was unlike the frigid air of White Hell-it was something else, something otherworldly. <Your Cold Resistance has drastically increased!>","Yuan blinked in surprise at the notification. Chief Mu's chilling aura was so intense that merely standing near her gave him the same result as enduring the seventh region of White Hell. 'Is this the secret to how they can live within White Hell?\" he wondered inwardly, his curiosity piqued.","Chief Mu then spoke with a confident smile on her face, \"Forget about the tenth strike. If you survive this ninth attack, I'll consider it your win.\"","Yuan nodded, \"If you say so.\"","This time, Chief Mu took her time preparing for the next strike. Her cold aura steadily intensified, soon surpassing even the seventh region's frost. It grew so dense and concentrated that it condensed into a semi-transparent armor around her body.","Yuan briefly considered taking the attack head-on to temper his body, but quickly dismissed the thought. The cold radiating from her felt potent enough to freeze even his soul.","Realizing what Chief Mu was trying to do, Granny Mu hastily said to the others, \"Get as far away as you can from here.\" Without hesitation, all of the barbarians turned to flee in the opposite direction from the battlefield.","\"W-Wait! What about us?!\" Lady Chen exclaimed.","\"And who the hell are you?\" Granny Mu looked at them with raised eyebrows.","The fur-robed barbarian proceeded to explain their situation to her.","\"I see. Then you will remain where you stand. If you can survive the aftermath, I may consider letting you go,\" Granny Mu said, a cold smile curling her lips.","\"No way...\" Lady Chen and the others collapsed to their knees, their eyes fixed on Yuan and Chief Mu. As Chief Mu's aura swelled in preparation for her ninth strike, Yuan braced himself. His Chaotic Essence surged to its fullest, and he summoned forth the True Primordial Fire. Flames of primordial origin erupted around him, engulfing his figure until he stood encased in an infernal armor, radiating heat that defied the very cold closing in on him.","On top of that, Yuan brought out all of his treasures, such as the Robes of Destruction and the Soul Emperor's Crown-treasures he had decided to wear only when he was fighting in earnest. After all, Yuan was already overwhelmingly strong without relying on treasures. If he wore them all the time, he would feel no excitement in battle, and worse, it would only hinder his training.","Gu Ruyan and the others stared in disbelief, mouths agape, as Yuan covered himself in treasures of immense power. Until this moment, they had been certain he was already fighting with the aid of treasures to overcome their differences in cultivation, but seeing him summon them now proved how wrong they had been.","As though the treasures weren't enough, Yuan also activated God of War's Astral Arts, wrapping himself in yet another layer of protection.","Chief Mu also completed her preparations at the same time. She looked at Yuan and muttered, \"Though it was brief, I had fun. Unfortunately, it's time for you to die now.\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2161,"title":"Chapter 2161: White Hell Barbarian Tribe","paragraphs":["\"It's time for me to die?\" Yuan spoke with a smile on his face. \"Who are you to decide when I die?\"","\"Chief of the White Hell Barbarian Tribe, a seventh-level God Ascension cultivator, that's who I am,\" Chief Mu calmly responded, her aura continuously increasing with every passing moment.","\"Then allow me to apologize in advance, since I will be disappointing you.\"","\"Arrogant even in the last few moments of your life, huh?\" Chief Mu sneered.","\"And you continue to underestimate me even after all this time? That will be your downfall.\"","\"Enough talking. You can die now.\"","Chief Mu's aura abruptly stilled for a heartbeat before erupting outward like a nuke. In the same instant, she shot forward like a meteor, her voice ringing out, \"Shiva's Glacial Sunder!\"","Yuan's smile vanished, replaced by a grave expression as his aura shifted, becoming something entirely otherworldly.","\"Ahhh... It's truly him...\" Granny Mu fell to her knees after sensing this otherworldly aura coming from Yuan.","A portion of Yuan's aura suddenly turned golden before wrapping itself around Number One Under Heaven. The golden aura radiated such unfathomable might that Chief Mu's heart trembled, a primal sense of danger gnawing at her soul to escape. But the moment had already passed, and there was no turning back now.","Wreathed in a golden aura, Yuan swung Number One Under Heaven, releasing a single golden sword arc forged from Supreme Sword Aura and something otherworldly. Not only was his Supreme Sword Aura enhanced by Number One Under Heaven's ability, but the golden aura strengthened it even further, and it flew toward Chief Mu with unstoppable force.","Chief Mu gritted her teeth and swung her axe, unleashing all the energy she had gathered. It erupted like a massive fireball-yet it was white, and so cold that it froze the very space around it, leaving a trail of ice in its wake.","Chief Mu braced for their energies to explode on impact, but to her shock, Yuan's Supreme Sword Aura cleaved straight through her attack and passed on, severing both of her arms in a single stroke.","Once cleaved apart, the condensed energy of Chief Mu's attack lost all control and erupted, unleashing a catastrophic explosion that instantly consumed and froze half of White Hell, the frost spreading as far as the fourth region.","Right before the explosion occurred, Granny Mu shielded the fur-robed barbarian behind her, as well as Yaoqin. As for Gu Ruyan and the other two, they hastily retrieved all of the life-saving treasures from their spatial ring and activated them without hesitation.","For several minutes, White Hell-the coldest place in the Nine Heavens-froze in its entirety for the first time. Not only the mountains and land, but even the air and space themselves turned to ice. From the outside, White Hell appeared as nothing more than a colossal block of frozen crystal. Of course, this frozen state didn't last for long, and within minutes, it began to melt.","<Your Cold Resistance has improved drastically>","<Your skill 'Ice Harmony' has developed into 'True Ice Harmony'> Yuan, who was the closest to the explosion, had managed to upgrade his Ice Harmony to the next level within those few minutes, a testament to how powerful Chief Mu's attack was.","When the ice finally melted and White Hell returned to normal, Chief Mu stared at Yuan in utter disbelief, unable to comprehend what had just transpired. \"He cut through... my most powerful attack? And he is still alive after eating that much energy? There's no way...\" she muttered in a daze.","Though Yuan had survived Chief Mu's martial technique, the effort drained him so greatly that he lost control of his body and plummeted from the sky. Though consciousness never left him, and his exhausted body regenerated almost instantly, Yuan could not move a muscle. His paralysis stemmed not from the exhaustion but from the crushing burden of the golden aura he had dared to wield. Indeed, Yuan had managed to invoke Heaven's Supremacy without fully completing his quest, though he could only summon enough of its power to enhance his Supreme Sword Aura once.","'Looks like I managed to use Heavenly Supremacy, even if only a little,' Yuan thought with an inward smile, satisfied with the result. More importantly, he realized something-that he didn't need to complete the quest to wield it. After all, would he truly be worthy of Heaven's Supremacy if he relied on the system to wield it?","Just as Yuan was about to crash into the ground, a gentle energy wrapped around him, slowing his descent and placing his paralyzed body softly upon the earth. Of course, even without the aid, a simple fall would not have harmed him, as his physique was strong enough to withstand even powerful treasures.","Granny Mu walked up to the motionless Yuan, looked down at him, and said, \"You're still as crazy as ever, aren't you?\"","Though he was unable to move his body, Yuan was able to make facial expressions and move his lips. He raised an eyebrow and asked as he stared at Granny Mu's unfamiliar face, \"Who are you?\"","\"Hm? You don't remember me?\" Granny Mu said. She continued, \"I guess my appearance has changed a lot since we last met. Mu Hanyan, does that name ring any bells for you?\"","\"Sorry, it doesn't...\"","Granny Mu narrowed her eyes slightly, and she began doubting whether Yuan was truly the one she knew. \"That feeling his golden aura emitted... there's no mistaking it, but what if someone else besides him could use it?\"","After a moment of silence, Granny Mu asked, \"What is your name?\"","\"Yuan.\"","\"Are you sure it's not Tian Yingzhe?\" she asked with a skeptical gaze.","Yuan's eyes widened slightly upon hearing this familiar name. Granny Mu could tell that Yuan recognized the name but didn't say anything and patiently waited for his response.","However, before he could do so, Chief Mu descended from the sky and landed right before him. \"What the hell was that golden aura?!\" She shouted as she wrapped her spiritual energy around him and pulled him off the ground. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2162,"title":"Chapter 2162: Let Them Go","paragraphs":["\"Does it really matter what it was? I survived your ninth strike, so I win our little game,\" Yuan responded with a calm smile on his face.","\"I'm gonna kill you, you damn freak!\" Chief Mu angrily shouted, but she was not emitting any killing intent.","\"That's enough.\" Granny Mu suddenly said. \"Put him down.\"","\"H-Huh? Mother? How long have you been there?\" Chief Mu was startled to see Granny Mu. She had been so focused on Yuan that she didn't even realize Granny Mu's presence.","\"Long enough to watch the entire thing. You've lost spectacularly, my foolish daughter.\"","\"T-That's-!\" Chief Mu cut herself off, grinding her teeth in frustration. Never had she imagined being unable to kill a mere Immortal even after exerting her full might. Though the Nine Heavens greatly restricted her power, the gap in their cultivation should've allowed her to win with ease, and this humiliation would surely linger and haunt her forever.","After a moment of silence, Chief Mu released Yuan. She intended to drop him onto the ground like trash, but Granny Mu prevented his fall a second time with her spiritual energy.","\"Why are you being so gentle with him? He won't die even if you crush him with a mountain,\" Chief Mu couldn't help but ask, a slight frown on her face.","Granny Mu ignored her and asked Yuan again, \"Are you sure your name isn't Tian Yingzhe?\"","\"It's a bit complicated,\" Yuan responded.","\"So you are Tian Yingzhe,\" she said in a confident tone. \"Since you don't remember me, you must have amnesia...\"","\"Something like that.\"","Granny Mu sighed, \"To think that after millions of years, our reunion would be in such a fashion.\"","\"Wait... you know him?\" Chief Mu asked, her eyes widening.","\"I do. But you've no time to worry about my affairs,\" Granny Mu replied, tilting her gaze toward the heavens. The dark clouds their clash had scattered had already gathered once more this time, heavier and angrier than before.","\"Oh... I completely forgot about that...\" Chief Mu sighed.","As a seventh-level God Ascension cultivator, Chief Mu normally wouldn't worry about this level of Heaven's Judgment. However, she had exhausted most of her energy trying to kill Yuan, and she'd even lost both of her arms.","\"I'll deal with it,\" Yuan suddenly said.","\"What? How the hell are you going to do that when you can't even move?\" Chief Mu said while glaring at him.","Yuan looked at Granny Mu and said, \"You can put me down now. I have recovered enough to move my body.\"","After Granny Mu set him down, Yuan soared into the sky, heading straight for the rumbling black clouds. \"We both know you can't harm me,\" he said, his mocking smile fixed on the heavens. \"So stop delaying and get this over with.\"","The heavens roared in fury. In the very next instant, judgment descended-not a single bolt, but two. One bore down on Yuan as his rightful punishment. The other, meant for Chief Mu, veered unnaturally, drawn into Yuan's body as though he had seized her punishment for himself.","Naturally, Heaven's Judgment had no effect on Yuan. If anything, it only tempered his body further. What's more, since one of the strikes had been meant for Chief Mu-a Seventh-Level God Ascension cultivator-it carried far greater power than his own judgment.","\"Hahaha! That's it! Keep up the good work!\" Yuan laughed out loud.","\"That's insane... He not only possesses Ice Harmony, but also a Heavenly Physique that can withstand Heaven's Judgment?\" Chief Mu muttered, swallowing nervously. Even at her peak, uninjured and with her full energy, she would not be able to face Heaven's Judgment as effortlessly as Yuan.","A few minutes later, the judgment ceased, and the dark clouds scattered almost instantly as the lightning subsided.","Once Heaven's Judgment ended and Yuan returned to the ground, he looked at Chief Mu and spoke, \"So, as promised, you'll let me and my friend live, right?\"","Chief Mu sneered, \"Whatever.\" Although she didn't want to admit it, she realized that she wouldn't be able to kill Yuan even if she wanted to.","\"What about them?\" Yuan suddenly turned to look at Gu Ruyan and the others. Yaoqin was completely unhindered thanks to Granny Mu, but the other three had also somehow managed to survive barely with the help of their life-saving treasures.","Before Chief Mu could respond, Granny Mu said, \"I said that I would consider letting them go if they could survive the aftermath.\"","\"What?! But they killed one of our people! You can't let them go!\" Chief Mu exclaimed.","Granny Mu turned to look at Yuan and asked him, \"What do you think? Should I let them go or...?\"","\"P-Please! Let us go!\" Lady Chen cried. \"I swear I'll never trouble you again!\"","\"Me too!\" The other two also shouted.","Yuan's lips curved into a gentle smile as he said, \"Let them go.\"","\"What? You can't be serious!\" Chief Mu stared at him in disbelief.","\"If you say so,\" Granny Mu replied with a calm nod.","But before Gu Ruyan and the others could breathe a sigh of relief, Yuan continued, his smile turning colder, \"After all, I want to kill them with my own hands.\"","\"What?!\" Without another word, Yuan charged at them.","Gu Ruyan and the other two hastily readied themselves to face Yuan. But Yuan no longer toyed with them, and he fought as though he was still battling Chief Mu. The three resisted with all they had, yet before Yuan's overwhelming power, they were utterly helpless.","In just a few moments, Yuan had destroyed all three of their physical bodies and seized their souls.","\"Please! Spare us!\" Gu Ruyan cried.","\"Have mercy!\" Zhuang Maojiang shouted.","\"I-I will do anything you want! I will be your slave or whatever! Just let me live!\" Lady Chen pleaded. However, Yuan ignored them and struck their souls with his Supreme Sword Aura, instantly cutting their souls in half and killing them for good.","\"As ruthless as ever:\" Granny Mu said with a smile. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2163,"title":"Chapter 2163: Mu Hanyan","paragraphs":["While Yuan dealt with Gu Ruyan and the others, Chief Mu consumed a recovery pill that restored her severed arms and exhausted energy. Unfortunately, there was no pill that could erase the humiliation she felt from losing to Yuan, nor was there anything she could do about it since she had already given him her word that she wouldn't touch him if he won, not to mention her mother seemed to know him. Chief Mu may be the leader of the White Hell Barbarian Tribe, but her mother, Granny Mu, the leader before her, held more power and authority.","\"Mother, who is that man?\" Chief Mu asked.","A bittersweet smile appeared on her face as she responded, \"Your father...\"","\"WHAT?!\" Chief Mu exclaimed.","\"At least that was my dream at one point in my life,\" Granny Mu continued.","\"D-Don't ever do that again, mother... It's really bad for the heart... and soul.\"","Once Yuan was finished with the members of the Legacy Families, he returned to Yaoqin's side and asked her, \"Are you okay?\"","She nodded in a daze, \"Yes... thank you...\"","After pondering for a moment, she retrieved a glowing blue flower from her spatial ring and extended her arms, offering it to Yuan. \"This is the White Hell Frost Lotus. I'll let you have it for saving my life,\" she said. Yuan glanced at the lotus and reached for it. However, instead of taking the treasure, he pushed it back toward her and said, \"You risked your life for it, so keep it. While it's a decent treasure, it won't benefit me right now.\" Had she given it to him before he acquired True Cold Harmony, it would've definitely helped a lot.","Yaoqin stared at him with a flushed face, and she silently nodded her head before stowing the treasure back inside her spatial ring.","\"Why don't we have a private chat now that everything's calmed down?\" Granny Mu said as she approached them.","Yuan nodded, \"Sure.\"","Before turning around and walking away, Granny Mu glanced at Yaoqin before throwing a necklace in her direction and said, \"Wear it. It'll keep you warm in White Hell up to the eighth region.\"","\"T-Thank you, Senior!\" Yaoqin hastily bowed to her. The moment she wore the necklace, all of the coldness magically disappeared, something even the Sun Stone could not achieve.","Sometime later, Yuan followed Granny Mu into one of the buildings at the settlement.","Once seated, Granny Mu asked, \"So, what brought you to White Hell?\"","\"Before that, can you tell me what your relationship with Tian Yingzhe was?\" Yuan asked.","\"You're speaking as if you're not Tian Yingzhe.\"","\"I will explain it once you answer my question.\"","Granny Mu sighed. Suddenly, she retrieved an appearance-altering pill and consumed it, transforming from her elderly appearance to that of a beautiful teenager with white hair and ice-blue eyes. Seeing Yuan's lack of response, she sighed again.","\"So, you truly don't remember anything. Then let me start from the beginning,\" said Mu Hanyan. \"Since ancient times, women have led the White Hell Barbarian Tribe. To preserve this tradition, each leader leaves White Hell to seek out a partner, receiving his talents before returning home and raising the child alone. Since I was the last Chief's daughter, I was destined to be the next leader, so I left White Hell to find a suitable partner when I was of age, and that's where I met you-Tian Yingzhe. He was outstanding and the most talented individual I have ever seen, so I decided to bring his talents to White Hell. Unfortunately, Tian Yingzhe did not seem to like the idea of me going after him merely for his genes, so he refused. However, even though he already refused my request, I still decided to follow him, and I was even prepared to never return to White Hell for him. As you can see, that did not happen... mostly because Tian Yingzhe vanished like a ghost.\"","Yuan had many questions after hearing her story, but he couldn't help but ask this one, \"What if the Chief's child turns out to be male?\"","\"That's not possible. We can only give birth to females.\"","\"Huh? But what about the other barbarians? There were many men in the tribe.\"","\"We may be from the same tribe, but the leaders have a different bloodline, and our bloodline only gives birth to females,\" she calmly explained.","After a moment of silence, Mu Hanyan spoke, \"Now that I have explained my relationship with Tian Yingzhe, shouldn't it be your turn to explain? If you are not Tian Yingzhe, who the hell are you?\" From her tone and the look in her eyes, Yuan could tell Mu Hanyan wasn't lying-that she truly cared about Tian Yingzhe.","\"I am Tian Yingzhe and not at the same time,\" Yuan said. \"I died and reincarnated.\" He gave a simple yet clear explanation.","The room fell silent again.","\"How'd you die?\" Mu Hanyan asked.","\"I don't remember. I have yet to recall all of my memories, hence why I don't have memories of you, either.\"","\"Makes sense.\" Mu Hanyan sighed.","\"Well, now that you're back, why don't you fulfill my old request and give me your seeds?\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows, but before he could respond, she continued, \"I'm just joking. We are only allowed to have one child.\"","\"Anyway, what are you doing in White Hell?\" she then asked.","\"I'm here to train my cold immunity. I have achieved True Cold Harmony thanks to your daughter, but it seems like it can still be improved on.\"","Mu Hanyan stared at him with wide eyes, and she asked him after a moment of stunned silence, \"How long has it been since your reincarnation?\"","\"I stopped paying attention long ago, but it hasn't been a hundred years yet,\" he calmly answered. \"Not even a hundred years ago?! And you've already achieved True Cold Harmony?! You're as ridiculous -if not even more ridiculous than before!\" she exclaimed. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2164,"title":"Chapter 2164: Shiva’s Hell","paragraphs":["\"You know, I've only just achieved True Cold Harmony after cultivating for tens of millions of years...\" Mu Hanyan sighed. \"Unfortunately, I might not be able to achieve the next realm so quickly.\"","Hearing his words, Mu Hanyan fell silent for a moment before speaking, \"If you want fast progress, I may know a place where you can further improve your Cold Harmony.\"","\"Really?\" Yuan's eyes lit up with excitement. \"Where is it?\"","\"It's where I was training before I was disturbed by your appearance,\" she said. \"That said, it's not a place accessible by strangers. In fact, it's only accessible by the Chiefs of our tribe. Despite our relationship, I cannot let you enter it so easily.\"","Yuan smiled and replied, \"Since you brought it up, then there's a way for me to train there, right? Otherwise, why even bother telling me about it?\"","\"You're right. There is a way.\" Mu Hanyan leaned forward and continued with a mysterious smile, \"If you agree to fulfill one of my requests, I'll let you train in there. Considering that you've achieved True Cold Harmony in such a short time, I'm willing to wager that you'll achieve the next realm in another fifty years.\"","\"What's the request?\" Yuan asked.","\"I'll tell you later, but you must make a decision now. Don't worry, it won't be anything unreasonable,\" she said, reassuring him.","\"You're not going to tell me to impregnate your granddaughter, are you?\" Yuan looked at her with a skeptical look. \"If so, I'll have to decline.\"","Mu Hanyan stared at him with wide eyes and a dumbfounded expression. \"Hahaha!\" she suddenly burst out laughing. \"So you caught on, huh? Fine, I won't ask you to impregnate anyone.\"","\"...\" Yuan was speechless.","\"But you still won't tell me your request now?\"","\"Nope.\"","Yuan sighed, falling silent as he pondered her offer. He had no idea what kind of place Mu Hanyan referred to, but one thing was clear-if he wished to evolve his physique, he first needed to advance his True Cold Harmony. And if he pursued it through normal means, it would take him at least a hundred years. Moreover, even though Mu Hanyan predicted that he could achieve it within 50 years, he had a feeling that he would be able to do so even faster than her prediction.","After a long moment of silence, Yuan nodded his head in a defeated manner, \"Alright, you win. I'll accept your request as long as it doesn't involve me impregnating anyone.\"","\"Then it's a deal.\"","Sometime later, Yuan and Mu Hanyan left the building.","When she saw Yuan leaving, Yaoqin, who had been waiting outside, approached him and asked, \"If you don't mind me asking, how much longer do you intend to stay in White Hell? If possible, I'd like to stay with you until you leave.\"","\"I can't give you an exact time, but I plan to train here for several more years,\" Yuan said. \"I don't mind if you wait, but you won't be able to follow me to where I'll be going.\"","\"I see...\" Yaoqin fell quiet for a moment before nodding. \"Then I'll keep training here-if they don't mind, and if I finish before you return, I'll leave on my own. I plan to consume the White Hell Frost Lotus, so it'll take several years.\"","Yuan looked at Mu Hanyan and asked, \"You wouldn't mind letting her train here for a bit, do you?\"","\"Who is she to you, anyway?\" she asked, staring at Yaoqin with slightly narrowed eyes.","\"She was in trouble, chased by three I killed, and I helped her.\"","\"So you're her savior, huh? Why am I not surprised? You've always gone out of your way to help those in need. Whatever. As long as she doesn't cause any trouble, I don't mind,\" Mu Hanyan said.","\"Thank you.\"","Yaoqin bowed to her, \"Thank you, Senior. I promise I won't cause any trouble. I will also return the necklace when I am done.\"","Mu Hanyan pointed at a certain building and said, \"You can use that place to train.\"","Yaoqin didn't linger and immediately went inside the building to begin her cultivation. \"When do you want to start your training?\" Mu Hanyan asked Yuan shortly later. \"Right now.\"","She nodded and said, \"Follow me.\"","Chief Mu noticed where Mu Hanyan was bringing Yuan and blocked them, \"W-Wait a second! Mother, don't tell me you're going to let a stranger enter that place, which is only meant for us?! That's against our tradition!\"","\"Nothing is eternal. It's for a good cause,\" she calmly replied.","\"That doesn't make any sense!\"","Mu Hanyan narrowed her eyes at Chief Mu and asked in a cold voice, \"Are you questioning my decision? You must think you're above me now after taking my position a mere thousand years ago, huh?\"","\"That's...\" Chief Mu clenched her fists in frustration, but she held her tongue. Even as the tribe's chief, her fear of her mother was still deeply rooted in her heart.","\"Also, he's not the only one I am going to break tradition for,\" Mu Hanyan suddenly continued.","\"What do you mean?\" Chief Mu questioned with a puzzled face.","Mu Hanyan turned to look at the fur-robed figure in the distance and beckoned her. \"Come over here, Xuelian.\"","\"You don't mean...\" Chief Mu swallowed nervously.","\"What is it, grandmother?\"","\"You're on the verge of reaching Cold Harmony, correct? Even though you're not the Chief yet, I'll make an exception and allow you special permission to enter Shiva's Hell.\"","\"Really?!\" the fur-robed woman cried out, her tone overflowing with joy and disbelief.","Mu Hanyan nodded and turned to face Yuan. \"If I am going to make exceptions, I might as well do it for two people. Also, it's a pain in the ass to open the training area, so you'll be training with my granddaughter, Mu Xuelian.\"","\"I don't mind.\" Yuan calmly nodded.","\"Follow me.\" Mu Hanyan began flying toward the eighth region with Yuan and Mu Xuelian following behind. Although Chief Mu no longer stopped them, she still decided to follow them. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2165,"title":"Chapter 2165: Shiva (1)","paragraphs":["After leaving the White Hell Barbarian Tribe's settlement, Mu Hanyan brought Yuan and Mu Xuelian into the eighth region. Of course, Chief Mu followed behind.","\"How are you feeling? Can you handle the cold here?\" Mu Hanyan asked, her head turned toward Yuan.","\"It's a bit chilly, but it feels good,\" he calmly nodded. After achieving True Cold Harmony, the seventh region's chill no longer fazed him. To Yuan, the once-lethal cold now felt like nothing more than a refreshing breeze against his skin. As for the eighth region, it felt no more than a morning chill at the end of summer.","\"Good. Because we'll be heading to the core of White Hell-Shiva's Heart,\" said Mu Hanyan.","Hearing the name Shiva twice now, Yuan couldn't help but ask, \"What's with this Shiva? This is the second time you've mentioned this name now.\"","\"It's the name of our guardian spirit, or something along that line. They've been protecting our tribe ever since we moved into White Hell. No, you can even say that it's because of Shiva that we can live within White Hell,\" she explained.","\"A guardian spirit? So it's a beast?\" Yuan asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"I don't know. That's just what our ancestors called them—though no one has ever actually seen them,\" Mu Hanyan admitted with a shake of her head.","\"What? You've never even seen them? Then how do you communicate with them-or even know they exist?\" Yuan pressed.","\"Oh, we communicate,\" she said firmly. \"Though we've never seen them, they speak with us through voice transmissions.\"","A doubtful look appeared on Yuan's face as he said, \"Sorry if this offends you, but... are you sure it's not a scam?\"","\"H-How dare you insult our guardian spirit!\" Chief Mu angrily shouted. \"I'll rip your tongue out!\"","Mu Hanyan burst into laughter. \"I knew you'd say that. But they've been with us since ancient times, and in all that time, they've never asked for anything. On the contrary, they've granted us powerful cultivation techniques and unique physiques. Why would a deceiver give so much, and for so long?\"","\"I guess it doesn't make sense...\" Yuan mumbled.","Some time later, they reached the end of the eighth region and stood before the entrance to the ninth. \"What... is this place?\" Yuan muttered, swallowing nervously. This was nothing like the snowy wasteland he expected of White Hell. Before him stretched not ice or snow, but a field of white and blue flowers, and the ninth region was so small that Yuan could see its far edge clearly with his divine sense.","\"Are we still in White Hell?\" Yuan had to ask.","Mu Hanyan smiled and said, \"Don't let the peaceful and warm appearance fool you. If you don't have a special physique-my physique, not even a Cultivation God could linger in this place without being frozen.\"","\"Don't tell me this is the training area?\" Yuan remarked.","\"No, this isn't the training ground. Do you see that glacial tree in the center?\" Mu Hanyan asked, her gaze fixed on the massive, crystal-like tree that stood there, resembling a towering structure of pure ice.","Yuan nodded. \"I do. It's impossible to miss.\"","\"Your destination, Shiva's Hell, is there.\"","Yuan used his divine sense to look around the crystal tree, and sure enough, there was a sealed gate on the ground right before it that seemed to lead underground.","Yuan's eyes narrowed slightly upon seeing this gate, almost as if he recognized it.","\"So, how am I supposed to get there when even a Cultivation God isn't safe in there?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","\"That's why I brought my granddaughter here with you,\" said Mu Hanyan as she turned to look at Mu Xuelian, who was calmly standing beside her. \"There's a reason why only the leader of the White Hell Barbarian Tribe is allowed entry-because only we have the physique capable of entering.\"","\"That doesn't explain anything about my predicament,\" Yuan said.","\"It's quite simple. You just need to enter while holding hands with my granddaughter.\"","Yuan became speechless. After a moment of silence, he spoke, \"You serious?\"","Mu Hanyan stared at his face for another moment before responding in a serious tone, \"No, I am just joking.\" Before Yuan could even respond, she retrieved a necklace that was similar to the one she gave Yaoqin and said, \"You can enter as long as you're wearing this.\"","\"...\" Yuan accepted the necklace in silence, but he couldn't help but wonder if she always had such a character.","\"Alright, let's go.\" The next moment, Mu Hanyan led the way and entered the ninth region. Mu Xuelian and Chief Mu followed her without hesitation.","The moment Yuan stepped into the ninth region, a chilling sensation coursed through him, making his entire body tremble. 'What is this feeling...' He couldn't describe it. It was cold and hot at once, and the chill itself felt different-unnatural, otherworldly. On top of that, his instincts screamed danger, warning him not to take another step forward. However, Yuan gritted his teeth and endured the sensation as he forced himself to proceed.","When they reached the sealed gate, Mu Hanyan suddenly produced a dagger whose blade looked as though it had been forged from the same crystal as the tree. Without hesitation, she drove it into her palm, the blade piercing clean through her hand. She then scattered her blood across the sealed entrance. Moments later, the barrier shifted and parted, revealing a staircase descending into the abyss below.","\"Go ahead. We won't follow you inside,\" Mu Hanyan said.","Mu Xuelian immediately began descending the staircase, and Yuan followed behind. Once their figures disappeared into the darkness, the entrance sealed itself again.","\"Mother... can you tell me the real reason you allowed him to enter Shiva's Hell?\" Chief Mu suddenly asked as she stared at Mu Hanyan. \"Don't even bother lying to me. I know you better than anyone else in this world.\"","After a moment of silence, Mu Hanyan responded in a calm voice, \"You're right. It wasn't our relationship that made me break our tradition. It was Shiva's instruction to bring him here.\"","\"W-What did you say?!\" Chief Mu exclaimed, her eyes wide with shock. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2166,"title":"Chapter 2166: The Heart of Shiva","paragraphs":["\"Say that again!\" Chief Mu demanded, not daring to believe her ears just now.","Mu Hanyan turned to look at her and calmly repeated, \"I brought him here because Shiva instructed me to.\"","\"N-No way...\" Chief Mu's jaw dropped. \"When did that happen? When did Shiva contact you?\"","\"It happened right after your clash with him ended,\" she replied. \"Bring me the man with the golden aura -that was Shiva's exact instruction, word for word.\"","\"Seriously...\" Chief Mu sighed out loud. \"Why didn't you tell me something this important beforehand?\" \"What's the point? If Shiva wanted you to know, they would've contacted you.\"","\"Wait... then what about my daughter? Did Shiva also ask for her?\"","Mu Hanyan nodded.","\"Did Shiva tell you why they wanted to see them?\"","\"No.\"","Chief Mu clenched her fists and muttered, \"I don't care what happens to that man, but if anything happens to my little girl...\"","\"Relax a bit. I doubt Shiva would harm them, especially Xuelian.\"","\"I know Shiva's never harmed us before, but I cannot help but have a bad feeling about this event. It's too sudden.\"","\"Shiva is an existence beyond our comprehension. There's no point trying to understand them or predict their goals.\"","Mu Hanyan turned to stare at the crystal tree with a profound gaze. \"The last time Shiva contacted us, it was to instruct me to leave White Hell and find a partner... And now, after millions of years, just as I reunite with Tian Yingzhe, they reach out again. This... this cannot be a coincidence...\" she thought inwardly. 'Oh, Tian Yingzhe... what in heaven's name are you, truly?'","Meanwhile, after many minutes of descending, Yuan and Mu Xuelian still haven't reached the end.","\"What's your relationship with my grandmother?\" Mu Xuelian suddenly started a conversation.","\"We used to travel together, I guess.\"","\"You guess? What's that supposed to mean?\"","\"Well, I don't have all of my memories, and it was your grandmother who said that we used to travel together.\"","\"Amnesia, huh? If you've traveled with my grandmother, you must be quite old.\"","\"Yes and no. It's complicated. Anyway, why don't you tell me a little about yourself, too?\"","\"There's nothing interesting about me. I have never left White Hell, and if I am not spending my time cultivating my physique, I am training with my mother and grandmother.\"","\"What kind of physique do you have that allows you to live within a place like White Hell?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Sorry, but I cannot tell you,\" she swiftly and firmly rejected.","\"Is that so?\"","The conversation ended there, and the two of them would not utter another word to each other for a few more hours until they finally reached the bottom of the staircase, where a small, narrow tunnel awaited them.","\"This is your first time here, correct?\" Yuan asked as they began walking through the tunnel.","\"That's right. Only those who have inherited the position of Chief may enter, and I am nowhere near inheriting my mother's position.\" In order to take over her mother's position, Mu Xuelian would need to leave White Hell and find herself a talented partner to receive their seeds.","Minutes later, they emerged from the tunnel into a dazzling light. A cavern of surreal beauty unfolded before them, its towering ceiling veined with massive roots of crystal, each faintly aglow as though pulsing with hidden life. At the center, the roots coiled tightly around a colossal block of ice, suspended in midair like a hanging lantern. Beneath the roots, at the cavern's center, lay a small glowing pond-barely large enough for two people. Its surface shimmered and flickered, as though countless stars dwelled within its depths.","\"So, how does training here work?\" Yuan asked as Mu Xuelian slowly approached the pond.","She gazed at it for a long moment, as though lost in its beauty, before answering. \"According to Mother, we simply need to submerge our bodies in this liquid.\"","\"Is that all? Are there any special preparations or rules that I need to know before doing so?\"","\"Not as far as I know,\" she shook her head.","Mu Xuelian then circled the pond and continued forward until she came upon a long, thick block of ice carved in the shape of a bed. Standing before it, she showed no hesitation as her hands moved to her fur robes, calmly removing them. She first pulled down her hood, unveiling her long, beautiful white hair. Then she slipped off her robes, letting them fall onto the ice bed.","Yuan's eyes widened as her flawless, jade-like skin and naked buttocks came into view. To his surprise, Mu Xuelian had worn nothing beneath her fur robes.","\"Um...\" Yuan parted his lips to speak, but before a word escaped, Mu Xuelian slowly turned around. The cavern's glow fell across her bare figure, every delicate curve revealed without concealment, her beauty laid bare before his eyes.","Yuan expected Feng Yuxiang's voice to resound at any moment, yet to his surprise, there was only silence. He instinctively reached out to their connection, only for his brows to twitch as he realized it had been severed. 'Feng Feng? Yu Ning? Yingying? Can you hear me?' When nobody responded, a ripple of panic ran through Yuan as he turned his focus inward, peering into his Dantian. Sensing that their presence was still there, he sighed in relief. But for some reason, he could no longer communicate with them.","\"Are you done staring?\" Mu Xuelian suddenly spoke, snapping him out of his daze.","Yuan quickly realized that he had been unconsciously staring at her and apologized, \"Sorry, I didn't mean to stare.\"","\"You can continue staring if you want, but I will go ahead and begin my cultivation.\"","Mu Xuelian moved to the pond and paused at its edge. With cautious grace, she lowered her foot, letting her toe touch the shimmering surface. When she confirmed the pond would not harm her, Mu Xuelian slid her foot deeper before stepping fully into the water. She made her way to the edge, saving some space for Yuan, and sat down, her body gradually sinking until she was immersed in the luminous liquid, as though surrendering herself to its embrace. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2167,"title":"Chapter 2167: Shiva (3)","paragraphs":["Watching Mu Xuelian enter the pond so calmly, Yuan thought it looked comfortable-an odd sight for him. \"This place is supposed to temper my Cold Harmony... How could training possibly feel comfortable?\" he wondered. After all, the path that had brought Yuan to where he stood today had been paved with hardship. Unless he was consuming a treasure, every method of training he had known was grueling and agonizing, offering not a single breath of peace or comfort. 'I should start my training, too.'","Yuan snapped out of his thoughts and also began to undress, placing his neatly folded robes on the ice bed. He approached the pond and silently stared at it. Though Mu Xuelian had saved him some space, there was barely enough room for him, and it seemed impossible to train in it together without touching her. \"There's not enough space for both of us, so my back will be touching yours, if you don't mind,\" he said. Of course, they could take turns cultivating inside the pond, but it would take too much time, something Yuan didn't have.","\"I don't mind,\" Mu Xuelian calmly responded.","\"Then if you'll excuse me...\" Yuan entered the pond, the glowing liquid rising to embrace his body as he submerged himself. As expected, the space was just enough for the two of them, their backs pressing lightly against each other. The touch of Mu Xuelian's skin was astonishingly soft and smooth as the finest tofu. Yet Yuan immediately banished the thought, clearing his mind to focus on cultivation. Almost the moment he entered the pond, a bone-chilling cold surged through him, seeping into his core until it felt as though his very organs were encased in ice. 'I knew it wasn't as comfortable as it looked!' Yuan cried inwardly. Yet, it wasn't anything unbearable. In fact, the pain didn't compare to his other experiences.","<Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has activated>","<Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has begun refining Shiva's Essence>","<Your Cold Resistance has improved tremendously>","'Shiva's Essence... is that the identity of this liquid?'","A year passed in the blink of an eye. Throughout that time, Yuan and Mu Xuelian remained motionless within the pond, the cavern unchanged save for one thing-a single drop of Shiva's Essence that fell from the ice above, rippling into the water below. The second drop appeared almost two years later. A single drop of Shiva's Essence would enter the pond every year, slowly refilling it, but with Yuan and Mu Xuelian absorbing it, the liquid was being exhausted much faster than it could be replenished.","After another year of cultivation, Yuan could already feel his True Cold Harmony reaching the next level, which was incredibly shocking, considering it took him nearly 20 years to achieve True Cold Harmony. However, just as Yuan was about to have a breakthrough, a chilling pressure suddenly filled the room, and he could feel Mu Xuelian's body trembling nonstop. In the next moment, before Yuan could even ask if she was okay, Mu Xuelian suddenly leaped from the pond, landing directly on the ice bed.","Yuan opened his eyes to see Mu Xuelian seated cross-legged on the bed, completely exposing her little sister. Without warning, luminous blue symbols began to surface on her skin, etching themselves across her body like living tattoos. Not daring to disturb her, Yuan watched in silence as the symbols shifted across her body, eventually converging into a single, massive mark upon her chest. As the symbol glowed brighter, the presence in the cavern grew heavier, clearer-almost as if something otherworldly was descending upon them. \"This pressure... It's the same as back in Han Zexian's Cavern!\" Yuan clenched his fists and prepared to face whatever was about to happen.","In an instant, the glowing symbol on Mu Xuelian's chest faded from sight. A breath later, her eyes opened, shimmering with a profound blue light that seemed deeper than before. And if one looked closely, they would see that the vanished symbol was now etched within her pupils.","\"Who are you?\" Yuan spoke first, breaking the silence.","Mu Xuelian didn't respond and merely stared at him with curiosity. A moment of silence later, she opened her mouth and spoke, but it was in a foreign language. Yet, for some reason, Yuan could understand it. \"I am Shiva,\" she said, her voice echoing with power. \"The one who reigns over all that is cold.\"","\"Shiva...? So you're the guardian spirit Mu Hanyan mentioned. What have you done with Mu Xuelian?\"","\"I am merely possessing her body.\"","\"Why?\"","\"So that I can speak with you, human who wields the power of gods.\"","\"Power of gods? What are you talking about?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","In response, she extended her arm, raising a finger toward him. At its tip shimmered a faint golden aura. A chill moved down Yuan's spine, and his eyes widened at the familiar golden aura. \"Heaven's Supremacy?!\" he exclaimed, so shocked that he couldn't remain seated and stood up. Although Shiva's golden aura couldn't be compared to Yuan's, it was definitely Heaven's Supremacy.","\"How... how are you using that power?\" Yuan asked, as he always thought it was a power unique to him. Shiva gently blew on her finger, snuffing out the golden aura as though it were a candle. \"What a foolish question. You are asking why a god can wield godly power,\" she calmly replied.","\"I don't understand. I thought it was some kind of technique,\" he admitted.","\"A technique?\" Shiva's laughter rang out, sharp and sudden, only to cease just as quickly. Her expression hardened, her tone dropping into icy disdain. \"Don't you dare compare our power to your mortal tricks.\"","Yuan clenched his fists tightly before asking another question, \"When you say god... are you referring to the Outer Gods? Are you an Outer God?\"","\"An Outer God, huh? That's merely how the beings of this world address us, not our true title. That said, it is true that we are gods-true rulers of this universe.\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2168,"title":"Chapter 2168: Outer Gods’ True Identity","paragraphs":["\"If Outer God isn't your title, then what is your true one? How should I address your kind from now on?\" Yuan asked.","\"Your kind...?\" Shiva's eyes narrowed dangerously. \"Bold words for a mere human. Were I not powerless in this moment, I would kill you for such disrespect.\"","Yuan's lips curled into a smile. \"Oh, I'm terrified,\" he mocked.","Shiva said nothing. Her silence was heavy, her displeasure evident in the narrowing of her eyes. Yet for some reason, she held her fury in check, as though restrained by something unseen. \"We call ourselves Eternals, as our existence is everlasting.\"","\"Eternals, huh? So, what does an Eternal like you want from me? You possessed Mu Xuelian's body just to speak to me, so surely, you want something from me.\"","\"Indeed, I want something from you.\" Shiva spoke as she slowly lifted her head to look at the crystal above him and continued, \"Do you see that block of ice above you?\"","\"What about it?\"","\"My very essence is sealed within that ice, and I would like you to break that seal and set me free,\" she said with a solemn expression.","\"You're sealed?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow, and he immediately recalled the cavern he found at the Heavenly White Tiger Clan's territory, where another Eternal was being sealed. \"Aren't you an almighty god? How and who has the power to seal you in this place?\"","Shiva fell silent again. \"I'll tell you once you release me,\" she eventually said.","\"No way.\" Yuan immediately declined. \"Since you don't want to tell me anything, allow me to tell you what I think about Eternals and my relationship with them. In my past life, I have fought and defeated Eternals—\"","\"Hahaha!\" Shiva suddenly laughed, interrupting him. \"A human defeating Eternals? That's not possible. Not even your strongest cultivators—a Cultivation God-would be able to touch us, let alone defeat us!\"","Yuan shrugged and said, \"Whether you believe me or not is up to you. Anyway, while I don't remember everything, I know that I have been fighting Eternals since the beginning, so if you think I will release you, who could be a potential threat to me and this world, you can keep dreaming.\"","Shiva's eyes narrowed, her voice low and edged with disdain. \"Did you imagine all Eternals to be on the same side? Hardly. We are no strangers to discord. Just as the beings in this world have factions that collide, so do we. Moreover, if you're worried that I might destroy your world or something after being released, that is needless worry. We, Eternals, cannot directly intervene here. In other words, we cannot touch this realm.\"","\"What?\" Yuan's eyes widened with shock after learning this new information. \"Eternals cannot touch the Nine Heavens? Why?\"","\"Because this world is protected by an absolute power that even we Eternals cannot touch. It is also why I was sealed in this world.\"","\"Absolute power? Can you elaborate?\" Yuan asked.","\"No, because you wouldn't understand it.\"","\"Then tell me who sealed you in this world and why they did it.\"","Shiva sighed, \"Very well. If it's the only way to convince you to unseal me.\" After a deep breath, she explained, \"I was sealed in this world because of the absolute power that protects this place. Since I am sealed here, it means the other Eternals cannot help me, as the seal can only be removed with god's power. As for who sealed me here... It was another Eternal. I lost our fight, and as punishment, I was sealed here.\"","\"How long have you been sealed here?\" Yuan asked.","\"Too long.\"","Yuan fell silent to digest this information. 'So she was sealed in this world because Eternals cannot interfere with this place, and since she can only be unsealed with Heavens' Supremacy, she's essentially trapped in here forever...or until someone who can wield Heavens' Supremacy-someone like me comes to her rescue.'","Sometime later, Yuan asked, \"What are you going to do once I unseal you? Return to the void beyond our world?\"","\"If only it were that simple,\" she shook her head. \"As Eternals, our bodies cannot be destroyed even by another Eternal. In order to seal me in this world, they had to separate my 'Essence' from my body. In my current state, I do not have the power to return to the void, much less regain my body.\"","\"Your essence... so something like your soul? Can't you just make another body like cultivators who reached God Ascension can do?\"","\"Make another body? Don't compare ours to your fragile shells,\" she sneered. \"They cannot simply be recreated. Even if it were possible, it would take trillions of years.\"","\"Then what are your plans?\"","\"Leave this world and regain my body,\" she said.","Yuan raised an eyebrow. \"Isn't that basically what I said?\"","\"Yes. I didn't say you were wrong.\"","\"How are you going to achieve that without a body? Don't tell me you're going to use Mu Xuelian...\" Yuan frowned.","\"That is exactly what I am going to do. I protected and cultivated their tribe for countless years for a reason,\" Shiva said in a firm tone. \"Nothing is free in this world.\"","\"What if I placed your Essence in another place and helped you regain your body? Like a Soul Weapon, which can hold souls?\" Yuan asked.","\"That's impossible,\" she said flatly. \"I won't repeat myself—do not apply the logic of this world to my existence. No Soul Weapon can contain my Essence. The only reason I can inhabit this girl is because of her unique physique, which I have cultivated for countless years. Even if you unseal me, I will not be able to go anywhere without this girl.\"","Unsure of how to respond, Yuan remained silent.","\"Now that I've told you everything, what is your answer?\" Shiva spoke a moment later. \"Of course, I am not asking your help for free. If you free me, I will not only help you evolve your physique, but I will even show you the full potential of your physique.\"","\"What do you even know about my physique?\"","\"You mean the Heaven Refining Physique?\" Shiva said with a profound smile. \"Or should I call it the Eternal Constitution?\"","\"The what...?\" Yuan stared at her, his eyes wide with disbelief. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2169,"title":"Chapter 2169: Eternal Constitution","paragraphs":["\"Eternal Constitution, you say...?\" Yuan swallowed nervously.","A cold smile tugged at Shiva's lips as she spoke, \"You don't even know about the Eternal Constitution, and you dare claim that I don't know anything about your physique? I don't know how you came to possess the Heaven Refining Physique, but it is basically an inferior version of the Eternal Constitution—a physique that only belongs to Eternals. It is also because of your physique that you're able to use Heaven's Supremacy. Otherwise, your body wouldn't have been able to handle it.\"","\"...\" Yuan fell silent. He'd acquired the Heaven Refining Physique due to a fateful encounter with a treasure in the Primordial Era. However, he didn't know anything about its origin until now. 'So it turned out to be related to the Outer Gods, huh?' he sighed inwardly.","\"Free me from my seal and I shall teach you how to use the Heaven Refining Physique to its true potential,\" Shiva repeated her offer.","After pondering for a moment, Yuan spoke, \"Before I give you an answer, I'd like to ask you another question.\"","\"If you want any more information from me, you'll have to accept my offer. Otherwise, I won't say another word,\" she responded in a firm tone.","However, Yuan ignored her words and continued asking his question, \"Do you know an Eternal by the name of Shura?\"","Shiva's eyes widened abruptly, surprise flashing across her face. \"Shura, you said...?\" she muttered.","Seeing her reaction, Yuan continued, \"I'll assume you know him, judging by your reaction. Now my real question is... are you friends or foes with Shura?\"","After a moment of silence, Shiva opened her mouth and spoke, \"Why does my relationship with another Eternal matter to you, a human?\"","\"It's very important, but I cannot tell you until you give me an answer.\"","Just in case Shiva planned on lying, Yuan retrieved the Grail of Truth.","Shiva narrowed her eyes at the treasure and sneered inwardly, 'Does he really think such a toy would work on me? I don't like how he's constantly underestimating me, but I need his help to free me from this place...'","\"Shura, huh? It has been a long time since I last heard that name.\" A flicker of nostalgia crossed Shiva's face as she spoke. \"He's my twin.\"","\"What?\" Yuan's eyes widened upon hearing this shocking revelation. \"Twin as in siblings? Eternals can be siblings? Does that mean you also have a parent?\"","Shiva shook her head and explained, \"We are twins because we were born at the same time and in the same area. Eternals are being born from the universe itself, and if we are all born from the same source, we are technically all siblings. Of course, not every Eternal sees it this way. Anyway, since we were born in the same place, we naturally grew up together. That said, we're neither allies nor foes with each other. He's something akin to a neighbor.\"","\"Sounds complicated...\" Yuan muttered.","\"Does my answer satisfy your question?\" Shiva then asked.","\"Yes, it does.\"","\"Then what is your answer? My patience is limited. If you continue to test me, I will kill you even if you are the key to my freedom. I simply need to wait longer-until the other Eternals destroy this world.\"","Yuan fell silent after hearing her last words.","\"You heard that right. There are Eternals who want to destroy this world. However, that's all I am going to say.\"","Yuan didn't become silent because he was shocked to learn that Eternals were trying to destroy the Nine Heavens, as he'd known this since the Primordial Era.","Sometime later, Yuan sighed, \"Alright, I'll free you.\"","Shiva's expression immediately brightened. \"You won't regret your decision.\"","\"So, what am I supposed to do?\" he asked.","Shiva pointed at the ice above him again and said, \"It's quite simple. All you need to do is destroy that block of ice with Eternal Essence-or what you call Heaven's Supremacy.\"","Yuan's eyes lingered on the block of ice, his expression calm yet resolute. In the next breath, he drew Number One Under Heaven, its blade shrouded in the golden radiance of Heaven's Supremacy, and unleashed a strike against the frozen monolith. Yet the ice not only repelled his sword, it even dispersed the golden aura surrounding it.","Shiva sighed at the results and remarked, \"As I figured, your Eternal Essence is too weak to break the seal. Is that all you got?\"","Yuan gave no reply to her remarks. Instead, he steadied himself for another attempt, carefully gathering the power of Heaven's Supremacy. When the time came, he invoked Absolute Dragon Awakening, his aura erupting as he delivered his most powerful strike. But even so, the block of ice remained untouched, and not even the faintest scratch marred its surface.","\"It doesn't matter how much you increase your mortal strength with techniques or what martial techniques you use. The only thing that can damage the seal is Eternal Essence, so even if you increase your cultivation by a million times, nothing will change until you strengthen your Eternal Essence.\"","\"In other words, I have to evolve my physique, reach True Immortal, and fully regain my ability to use Heaven's Supremacy before I can break your seal. Then you'll have to wait a little longer. I was just on the verge of a breakthrough before your interference.\"","\"And how long will that take?\" Shiva asked.","\"Who knows? But it shouldn't be too long.\"","Without another word, Yuan resubmerged his body in the pond and closed his eyes, continuing his cultivation.","A moment later, he opened his eyes and asked, \"Are you going to possess Mu Xuelian's body until I free you?\"","Shiva didn't immediately respond. She looked at her own palm and mumbled after a moment of silence, \"This girl's body is reaching its limits, so I will have to leave for now. I'll see you again soon.\" Mu Xuelian's eyes suddenly returned to normal, and her body collapsed the next instant. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2170,"title":"Chapter 2170: True Immortal","paragraphs":["\"Hey, are you okay?\" Yuan hurried out of the pond and rushed to Mu Xuelian's side, finding her drenched in sweat and gasping for breath.","After catching her breath, Mu Xuelian lifted her head to glare at him. \"Who... who are you...?\" she muttered.","\"I'm Yuan,\" he instantly replied.","\"You know that's not what I meant... You know what? Forget it...\" Though Shiva had possessed her, Mu Xuelian had remained conscious the entire time, seeing and hearing everything that transpired throughout their conversation.","Mu Xuelian quietly climbed back onto the ice bed and began cultivating.","Seeing that she was fine, Yuan returned to the pond and continued his cultivation.","In the blink of an eye, another year had passed.","<Your 'True Cold Harmony' has developed into 'Flawless Cold Harmony'>","<Progress: 100% >","<Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique (Completed) has fulfilled all requirements for a breakthrough>","<Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique(Completed) has evolved into 'Eternal Constitution (Incomplete)'>","The instant Yuan's physique evolved, he could feel his bottleneck instantly being broken, and his cultivation surged all the way to the peak of True Immortal.","<You have absorbed enough Immortal Qi for a breakthrough!>","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough!>","<You have reached True Immortal!>","<You have completed the Unique Quest: ???>","<You have discovered the existence of Eternal Essence>","<Your understanding of Eternal Essence has increased drastically>","<You have learned Eternal Essence>","[Eternal Essence]","[Rank: ???]","[Mastery Level: ???]","[Description: An otherworldly power wielded only by ???]","Yuan opened his eyes after reaching True Immortal and learning Eternal Essence. Within his gaze flickered a profound radiance, vast and unfathomable, like the reflection of a secret that belonged solely to the universe.","Mu Xuelian, who had been cultivating on the ice bed for the entire time, also opened her eyes upon noticing Yuan's movements. Yuan stood from the pond and tilted his head to gaze at the ice. He retrieved Number One Under Heaven and prepared for his third attempt. This time, instead of using Absolute Dragon Awakening or other martial techniques, Yuan focused solely on his Eternal Essence.","Silence lingered for only a moment before a golden brilliance surged from Yuan's form, flooding the cavern with light. With a swift motion, he raised his sword and swung it at the ice in a strike so powerful it shook the cavern to its core.","Mu Hanyan and Chief Mu, who had been waiting for them outside, sensed the tremble and were immediately startled by it. \"Heavens! What was that?!\" Chief Mu exclaimed.","Mu Hanyan looked at the ground and muttered, \"It came from below...\"","\"What the hell are they doing down there?\" Chief Mu swallowed nervously.","As curious and worried as she was, there was nothing either of them could do but wait.","Meanwhile, underground, Yuan stared at the ice with a frustrated expression. Despite reaching True Immortal and regaining his ability to use Eternal Essence, he was only able to put a faint scratch on the ice.","\"Don't tell me I waited an entire year just for this pitiful progress,\" Mu Xuelian's voice suddenly echoed in the","cavern.","Yuan turned to look at Mu Xuelian, who was staring at him. However, when he saw that her eyes appeared normal, he asked, \"Did Shiva ask you to say that?\"","Mu Xuelian quietly nodded.","Yuan sighed. \"At least I can damage the ice now. If I keep at it, it should eventually break.\"","\"Hah! At this rate, it'll take you thousands of years to break the seal-she said,\" Mu Xuelian relayed.","\"Then do you have any suggestions? Maybe you can teach me how to improve my Eternal Essence.\"","\"Eternal Essence isn't something that can be taught. However, I do have a way to improve its strength, and that is to \" Mu Xuelian suddenly halted her sentence, her eyes wide with disbelief.","\"What did Shiva say?\" Yuan asked.","\"...\" After a moment of awkward silence, Mu Xuelian finally spoke, \"If you want to strengthen your Eternal Essence, cultivate with this girl and refine her essence... is what Lord Shiva said.\"","\"What kind of nonsense are you spewing?\" Yuan asked with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"I-It's not nonsense. Your Heaven Refining Physique isn't limited to treasures and energies. You can also refine other things. For example, this girl's essence.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at Shiva's words. \"Isn't that just dual cultivation?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"It's not the same thing. You'll be doing more than just absorbing her energy and improving your cultivation. You'll be refining her essence into Eternal Essence.\"","\"What even is this 'essence' that you're talking about? It's not her soul, right?\"","\"Everything in this universe is made of essence-from humans to treasures-and for us Eternals, it's Eternal Essence. So when you wield that power, you're essentially turning your own existence into your power. Don't mistake it for spiritual energy because it's not the same thing. The stronger one's influence in the universe is, the denser their essence.\"","\"Turning my own existence into my power? That's confusing as hell,\" Yuan remarked. \"Does that mean if I use too much Eternal Essence, I could erase my existence?\"","\"Yes, it's possible.\"","\"Fuck! You should've told me something that important earlier!\" Yuan exclaimed.","\"What are you worried about? You have the Heaven Refining Physique, so you can always replenish your essence.\"","\"That's not the issue here...\" Yuan sighed.","He continued after realizing something, \"Hold on. If you're asking me to refine Mu Xuelian's essence, aren't you basically asking me to refine her existence? I'm not going to do that.\"","\"While you can definitely erase her existence if you refine too much of her essence, she'll be fine as long as you don't do that. You are also underestimating how much essence a human being carries.\"","\"What about injuring her? Would it affect her talent or health?\"","\"It will affect her talents, and depending on how much you refine, it could also affect her health.\"","\"And why does it require us to dual cultivate? Isn't this something meant for Eternals?\"","\"As Eternals, we can refine essence with nothing but will alone,\" Shiva explained. \"But you are human, and for humans, it is easier—and far safer—to refine another human's essence through dual cultivation, since your bodies are directly connected.\"","\"You can't be serious...\" Yuan sighed as he rubbed his eyes in a stressful manner. \"What's with this weird development?\" (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2171,"title":"Chapter 2171: Refining Essence","paragraphs":["\"What are you hesitating for? I thought humans loved the act of dual cultivation, especially men,\" Mu Xuelian said, relaying Shiva's words. More chapters in t.me/+9n1w1vacSaZhYzAy","\"This isn't ordinary dual cultivation-and I already have partners,\" Yuan said with a slight frown. \"I won't cultivate with someone I just met, let alone against her will.\"","\"I don't understand.\"","\"In case you forgot, that body doesn't belong to you but to Mu Xuelian.\"","\"It... It is not against my will,\" Mu Xuelian suddenly said.","\"What?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Lord Shiva's will is my will. If Lord Shiva commands me to cultivate with you, then I shall,\" Mu Xuelian said.","Yuan frowned. \"Is that what Shiva told you to say?\"","She shook her head. \"No, these are my own words. The White Hell Barbarian Tribe exists only because of Lord Shiva. Her will is our will.\"","Yuan's gaze hardened. \"Then you don't understand what it means to have a will of your own. If it isn't something you truly desire without external influence, you can't call it your will. What you're describing is simply obedience. You're no different from a servant following orders. Anyway, I am not going to cultivate with you just to strengthen my Eternal Essence.\"","Mu Xuelian's eyes suddenly shifted, a familiar symbol emerging within them and shining with profound radiance. \"Then how else are you going to strengthen your Eternal Essence? Are you going to tell me to wait for you to chip away the seal slowly?\" Shiva asked.","Yuan smiled and said, \"You said that 'essence' exists in everything, correct?\"","\"That is correct. From the very air you breathe to the dirt beneath your feet-everything contains essence.\"","\"Then I can simply refine those essences. Why does it have to be dual cultivation?\"","Shiva fell silent for a moment before she suddenly burst out laughing. \"If you are thinking about refining nature's essence, you can forget about it. Your Heaven Refining Physique is merely a fake-a replica of our Eternal Constitution. You may be able to refine essence, but that is limited to only the essence of other living beings. Only those with a true Eternal Constitution can refine nature's essence! In other words, only an Eternal such as myself can do it!\"","\"My physique is a fake? And what makes you so certain of that?\" Yuan questioned.","Shiva's lips curled into a sneer. \"Because it's impossible. How could a mere human carry such a physique? Even if you had somehow obtained a genuine Eternal Constitution, your soul remains human. And a human soul will never have the capacity to refine the essence of nature itself.\"","\"We won't know until we try.\" Yuan sat down and closed his eyes.","\"How are you going to try when you don't even know how to sense essence?\" Shiva remarked.","Yuan ignored her. A few moments later, he smiled and said, \"I can sense 'essence'.\"","\"What?\" Shiva's eyebrows twitched upon hearing his words; her gaze filled with disbelief. \"He can sense essence in such a short time when he'd only just learned of its existence? I guess he didn't obtain the Heaven Refining Physique for no reason...\"","<Eternal Constitution (Incomplete) activated>","<Eternal Constitution (Incomplete) has begun refining 'Qi'>","As a cultivator, he was most familiar with spiritual energy, so he decided to absorb it first. Yet unlike before, where he would refine the spiritual energy and store it inside his Dantian, Yuan did not stop there. He continued breaking it down, refining it past all limits, until the spiritual energy itself was erased from existence.","<You have successfully refined 'essence' from 'Qi'>","At the moment of his success, the cavern's spiritual energy dropped by nearly half. Yet the essence he managed to refine was so minuscule it was practically nonexistent.","'He managed to refine nature's essence?!' Shiva's eyes widened at the unbelievable sight before her. 'Does this mean he actually possesses a true Eternal Constitution?! That's impossible!'","After his initial success, Yuan turned his attention to the pebble in front of him. Although refining spiritual energy into essence was simple since he knew how to absorb spiritual energy, he wasn't sure how to 'absorb' the pebble before him. After pondering for a moment, Yuan had this thought-'If I cannot absorb it because of its solid form, I just need to break it down to the point where I can absorb it!'","Yuan reached for the pebble before him, channeling Eternal Essence through his hand. With a light squeeze, the stone crumbled-shattering further and further until it dissolved into particles so fine they vanished, as though it had evaporated from existence. He then attempted to absorb the 'essence' that was left behind.","<Eternal Constitution (Incomplete) activated>","\"It worked!\" Yuan exclaimed, a bright smile spreading across his face.","He looked at Shiva with a boastful smile and said, \"So, what were you saying just now?\"","\"...\" Shiva remained silent as she stared at him, a deep frown etched across her face. Her gaze on him carried a dangerous edge-like killing intent that was there, yet not.","\"What? Too speechless to even speak?\" Yuan chuckled.","She finally responded, \"What is your relationship with Shura?\"","\"Why are you asking me this now?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"You've just proven that you possess a true Eternal Constitution. But that should be impossible... unless an Eternal willingly bestowed their own upon you!\" Shiva explained. She continued, \"Since you mentioned Shura, I can only assume he gave you his Eternal Constitution. But that would also mean he gave up his body for you.\"","\"...\" After a moment of silence, Yuan responded, \"I don't know.\"","\"You don't know? What the hell is that supposed to mean?\" Shiva frowned.","\"Exactly what it sounds. I don't know because I don't remember. I recently reincarnated, so my memories are still in shambles. I remember meeting Shura and him bestowing me a 'gift' in a past life, but I do not recall anything else,\" he admitted.","'He doesn't seem to be lying...' Shiva thought inwardly.","Yuan then asked, \"If Shura gave me his physique, does that mean he's somewhere out there with just his 'essence' like you currently are?\"","She silently nodded. (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2172,"title":"Chapter 2172: Refining Shiva’s Essence","paragraphs":["\"For Shura to have given you his Eternal Constitution... It's unimaginable for an Eternal to do such a thing,\" Shiva murmured, disbelief still lacing her voice. \"Your connection with him must be unfathomable...\" She continued, \"But merely possessing a true Eternal Constitution wouldn't let you refine nature's essence—not with a human soul. Since you mentioned reincarnation, your soul must have already surpassed human limits. In other words, you are no longer truly human, but something between that of a human and an Eternal.\" More chapters in t.me/+9n1w1vacSaZhYzAy","\"So I'm a half-god?\" Yuan remarked with a smile.","\"Don't flatter yourself. You may have surpassed human limits, but you are nowhere near a god-not even one percent,\" Shiva sneered.","\"Maybe not right now, but eventually.\"","Shiva didn't respond. She couldn't. As much as she wanted to dismiss his seemingly foolish words, she knew that if Yuan continued to grow and refine his Eternal Constitution, he would one day reach true godhood.","\"I will concede this-you are remarkable for a human,\" Shiva said, her tone grudging. She shook her head lightly before continuing, \"But even with your ability to refine nature's essence, this place holds far too little of it to truly advance your Eternal Essence. If you want to see any drastic improvements to your Eternal Essence, you need to refine this girl's essence through dual cultivation.\"","Yuan's gaze shifted to the liquid and asked, \"What about this liquid? I can sense an immense amount of essence coming from it.\"","Shiva sneered, \"Are you out of your mind? That liquid was created from my essence. It's not something your body or mind can handle. Stop being stubborn and cultivate with this girl already. Or is there another reason you keep refusing? Do you like men?\"","Yuan frowned and said, \"Keep your delusions to yourself. I already told you that I have partners. I won't betray them by cultivating with a stranger.\"","\"Then you can just make this girl your partner,\" Shiva said.","\"That's not how it works.\"","\"I fail to understand,\" Shiva said with a weary sigh. \"You say you already have multiple partners, so clearly the notion of having more than one does not trouble you. Why, then, is this girl any different? Why will you not accept her? Are you worried about her talents? I can guarantee she's exceptionally talented-and this is coming from a god. Even her body and appearance are far beyond that of ordinary humans.\"","Yuan sighed. \"I don't expect a god born of the void to understand human emotions or morals. You'll just have to accept it.\"","\"Is that so? Then I will waste no more words on you,\" Shiva said, her voice edged with disdain. \"If you wish to refine the essence, go ahead. But try not to die, or all I've done for you will be for nothing.\" She closed her eyes, and when they opened once more, the profound light within them had vanished.","Mu Xuelian's gaze returned, clear and human, as she regained control of her body.","Shortly after regaining control, Mu Xuelian glared at Yuan and asked, \"Do you dislike me? Have I done anything that has offended you?\"","\"Of course not,\" he calmly replied. \"I understand why Shiva doesn't understand, but aren't you human? Surely, you understand why I refuse to cultivate with you.\"","Mu Xuelian narrowed her eyes slightly and responded, \"While it may have been Lord Shiva's will, I still have my own feelings, and I did not reject the idea of cultivating with you. You're clearly an extraordinary individual. If I had encountered you during my travel to the outside world to seek a partner, you would've definitely been my first choice. In fact, now that I am aware of your existence, I probably won't settle for anyone else.\"","Mu Xuelian rose from the ice bed, her figure gliding with grace as she suddenly advanced toward him.","\"What are you doing?\" Yuan asked, his voice steady as she stepped close, leaving only inches between them.","Mu Xuelian lowered her head for a moment, her eyes flicking downward to his naked sword before locking with his. \"I want your child. These are my words, spoken from my own will,\" she said the next moment, her voice firm and full of determination.","A fragment of Tian Yingzhe's memories suddenly surfaced in Yuan's mind. In it, a woman resembling Mu Xuelian stood before him, naked as she was now, speaking nearly the same words.","\"Sorry,\" Yuan said, his tone calm but firm. \"I won't impregnate someone simply because they ask, especially if that person is someone I barely know.\" The words left his lips unconsciously, the same words Tian Yingzhe had once spoken to Mu Hanyan.","\"In that case, I'll ask you again once we get to know each other better,\" Mu Xuelian said softly, unaware that she was repeating the exact same words her grandmother, Mu Hanyan, said in response to Tian Yingzhe's rejection.","Before Yuan could even respond, Mu Xuelian turned around and returned to the ice bed to cultivate in silence.","\"...\" Yuan rubbed his eyes and sighed before clearing his mind to focus on the liquid in the pond. 'Since it's liquid, I can't reduce it to dust like the pebble... should I try to vaporize it instead?'","Acting on the thought, Yuan called forth his True Primordial Fire, its searing flames engulfing the pond's surface. But to his astonishment, the liquid remained utterly unchanged, and not even a single bubble rose. The liquid didn't boil, much less vaporize. 'If even True Primordial Fire cannot vaporize it, then I'll have to find a different method...'","After a moment's contemplation, Yuan sank into the pond, letting the liquid envelop him fully. Then, with the same method he used in body tempering, he began trying to absorb the energy in the liquid before refining it.","<Eternal Constitution (Incomplete) activated>","<Eternal Constitution (Incomplete) has begun refining Shiva's Essence>","'It's working!' Yuan felt a surge of elation at the results. Yet the joy was fleeting, for in the next instant, his body was overwhelmed, assaulted by waves of pain so intense they defied imagination. But despite the pain, he endured it.","Sometime later...","<You have glimpsed a realm that lies beyond Flawless Cold Harmony> (More chapters in Buyers club for TMT)"]},{"number":2173,"title":"Chapter 2173: Releasing Shiva From Her Seal","paragraphs":["’A realm beyond Cold Harmony, huh?’ Yuan wasn’t surprised by this new discovery. In fact, he anticipated something like this existed because of the existence of Eternals.","If Cold Harmony was the limit of humans, then there must be a realm only achievable by gods.","’This human... he’s actually refining my essence!’ Shiva could only stare in shock and disbelief as Yuan refined the liquid from the sealed ice above. Despite its name, Shiva’s Essence was not truly her existence, but something born from it.","’Even though it’s not truly my essence... It’s not something that can be refined by someone who’s not even a god!’","Shiva’s intrigue toward Yuan deepened.","’He may have surpassed my expectations, but even then, he’ll need many years to refine enough of my essence to break the seal.’","Yet, not even a week later, Shiva noticed that the liquid in the pond had drastically decreased by half.","’He absorbed half of the essence already?!’","Shiva began to wonder if she had fallen into an illusion, for everything unfolding before her eyes defied logic. Yet she knew that only another Eternal could possibly affect her, and since Eternals could not touch the Nine Heavens, she was forced to accept that the impossible before her was, in truth, reality.","Yuan’s progress did not slow down after refining half of Shiva’s Essence. If anything, it increased, and after another three days, Yuan completely absorbed every last drop of liquid in the pond.","<Your ’Flawless Cold Harmony’ has transcended past its limits and evolved into ’Absolute Cold Harmony’>","<Through Shiva’s Essence refinement, you have learned the Skill ’Shiva’s Eternal Frost’>","[Shiva’s Eternal Frost]","[Rank: Eternal]","[Mastery Level: ???]","[Description: The pinnacle of coldness—powerful enough to freeze even gods]","<You have discovered ’Eternal’ rank techniques>","[Warning: Eternal-rank techniques cannot be used within the Nine Heavens due to ???]","’I cannot use Eternal-rank techniques in the Nine Heavens, huh? This must be due to the ’absolute power’ that Shiva mentioned...’ Yuan thought to himself.","<Your understanding of Eternal Essence has improved drastically>","After absorbing all of Shiva’s Essence, Yuan retrieved Number One Under Heaven and began gathering his Eternal Essence.","’It’s gotten so much more powerful than before!’ Mu Xuelian swallowed nervously.","Even though she could not comprehend it, she understood that his golden aura had strengthened tremendously compared to just days ago.","’With that much Eternal Essence, it might be possible!’ Shiva trembled in anticipation as she watched Yuan prepare to strike the ice.","The next moment, Yuan swung his sword at the ice.","Sha!","Like a hot knife going through tofu, Yuan completely sliced the block of ice in half, revealing a glowing blue orb within.","’I’M FREE!’","After being freed from the seal, Shiva instantly shot toward Mu Xuelian, who was sitting on the ice bed.","\"What are you doing?!\" Yuan cried out.","But his body, drained and paralyzed from pushing Eternal Essence to its very limit, refused to move. Helpless, he could only watch as Shiva slipped into Mu Xuelian’s body.","Mu Xuelian’s body stiffened for a brief moment before her eyes began to glow.","\"Relax, I am not going to hurt this girl,\" Shiva said.","\"Then what are you doing?\"","\"It’s not like I can wander around without a body,\" she explained. \"Until I regain my body, I will have to use this girl’s body as my own. That being said, it’s not like I will take complete control. I will only take control when necessary, as my essence puts too much of a burden on her body.\"","\"What are you going to do now that you’re free from the seal? Leave the Nine Heavens to find your body? Something else entirely?\" Yuan asked her a moment later.","\"As much as I want to start looking for my body immediately, I don’t know where to begin. The Eternals who sealed me have definitely hidden my body somewhere, and I doubt I will ever find it by wandering.\"","\"My original plan was to find another Eternal who could help me, but I have changed my mind.\"","Shiva jumped from the ice bed and landed right in front of Yuan.","\"I’m very intrigued with your existence, and I’m confident that if I follow you, I’ll eventually encounter Shura or another Eternal, so that’s what I am going to do.\"","\"You’re going to follow me...?\" Yuan felt a headache forming the instant he heard those words. He wanted to refuse, yet deep down he knew that Shiva wasn’t asking.","\"Why do you seem dissatisfied? You’re going to have a god by your side. You should feel honored,\" Shiva sneered.","\"...\"","Although he didn’t want to admit it, it would definitely benefit him to have an Eternal by his side. After all, he still had a lot of questions about their existence. Moreover, he could keep an eye on her.","’If she’s by my side, I won’t have to constantly worry about an Eternal roaming the Nine Heavens...’ he sighed inwardly.","Furthermore, Mu Xuelian was a cultivator at the 3rd level of God Ascension. Her power could come in handy.","\"So, what do you say?\" Shiva asked.","\"It’s not like I have a choice,\" Yuan replied.","Shiva narrowed her eyes and spoke, \"You may be an inferior being—one that’s not even worthy of being in my gaze—but I have made you a promise, and I intend to keep it.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Have you forgotten already? I said that I’d help you realize your physique’s true potential and even evolve it.\"","\"Oh?\" Yuan was pleasantly surprised; he had expected her to say she’d already helped him enough with the information she provided him.","Shiva suddenly placed a hand on his chest and closed her eyes.","\"Now that I am free, I can inspect your body properly,\" she said a moment later. \"You indeed have the Eternal Constitution, but it’s not complete. I don’t want to owe a human any debt, so I will help you complete it.\""]},{"number":2174,"title":"Chapter 2174: The Method to Completing the Eternal Constitution","paragraphs":["\"Are you going to directly evolve my physique with your god-like power or something?\" Yuan asked.","Shiva looked at him with an odd gaze.","\"I may be a god, but I am not omnipotent. Furthermore, I do not have my body, and my powers are sealed within the Nine Heavens.\"","\"Then how will you help me?\"","\"By telling you the steps to complete it. I am going to explain it now, so listen carefully.\"","Shiva proceeded to explain the process, \"In order to complete your Eternal Constitution, you will need to attain the three supreme physiques. You already possess one of them, so you need the other two.\"","\"Supreme physiques...?\" Yuan recalled Xiao Hua mentioning it in the past, calling them the pinnacle of physiques.","\"I currently possess the Golden Immortal Physique, and I am aware of the Harmonic Spirit Constitution, but what is the third one?\" he asked.","\"The Myriad Impervious Physique, which is obtainable by attaining the highest level of immunity for fire, cold, poison, and lightning—something you have already achieved. All that remains is for you to merge them and forge the physique.\"","\"Hm? But I have only just attained the highest level of Cold Immunity—Absolute Cold Harmony. I still need the other three,\" said Yuan.","Shiva shook her head and sighed, \"Let me rephrase it—the Myriad Impervious Physique, which is obtainable by attaining the highest level of immunity attainable by humans. Your Cold Immunity has surpassed human limits. Hell, you’re probably the only human to have ever reached such a realm.\"","\"Is that so... then how do I combine them?\"","\"Since you already have the immunities, you just need to consume the Iridescent Harmony Fruit.\"","\"The Iridescent Harmony Fruit, huh? What about the Harmonic Spirit Constitution?\"","\"You will need three treasures and an Untainted Body. A Seven-Colored Herb, Boundless Spirit Dew, and a Primordial Crystal. Ah, you also need something that contains an immense amount of spiritual energy—something like a large and high-quality Spirit Jade—so you technically need four treasures.\"","\"...\"","Yuan stared at Shiva with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"What is it? I know they’re extremely rare—perhaps even extinct by now, but without them, you won’t be able to complete the Eternal Constitution.\"","Without a word, Yuan drew three items from his spatial ring.","\"What in the...\" Shiva’s eyes widened at the sight.","A rainbow-colored flower, a black pearl, and a palm-sized Ancient-grade Spirit Jade lay before her.","To her surprise, Yuan had already collected three of the four treasures required for the Harmonic Spirit Constitution.","The Seven-Colored Herb, the Ancient Spirit Jade, and the Primordial Crystals—Yuan had carried these treasures for as long as he could remember. The Ancient Spirit Jade and the Seven-Colored Herb, in particular, had followed him since his days in the lower heavens.","\"I also have an Untainted Body, so I am just missing the Boundless Spirit Dew,\" Yuan said.","Shiva couldn’t help but laugh, \"You sure came prepared. It’s almost like you knew this would happen.\"","Yuan shook his head with a smile and said, \"No way. It’s just a coincidence... or fate.\"","\"In any case, once you attain all three supreme physiques, I’ll tell you the next step.\"","\"There are more steps?\"","\"Of course. Did you think it would be that easy to obtain a complete Eternal Constitution?\" Shiva sneered.","\"Easy...? I don’t think anyone has ever attained all three supreme physiques before...\" he remarked.","Though he doesn’t have all of his memories, Yuan knew that none of his past lives had ever attained all three supreme physiques in one lifetime, so this would truly be an unprecedented achievement if he managed to do it.","Sometime later, Yuan and Mu Xuelian left the cavern and returned to the surface, where Mu Hanyan and Chief Mu were waiting.","\"They’re done with training already?\" Mu Hanyan remarked when the door suddenly opened.","Yuan emerged from the hole the very next moment.","\"Hey! What happened down there?!\" Chief Mu immediately questioned him. \"And what happened to my daughter?! I swear, if anything—\"","Chief Mu cut off mid-sentence as Mu Xuelian stepped out of the hole a moment later. However, there was something different about Mu Xuelian. There was an aura around her that made both Chief Mu and Mu Hanyan freeze with apprehension.","\"I’m done here,\" Yuan said, snapping them out of their daze.","\"Already...? It’s barely been three years! Are you telling me that your True Cold Harmony reached the next realm in this short time?!\" Mu Hanyan exclaimed, not daring to believe her ears.","\"Something like that,\" Yuan responded with a mysterious smile, keeping the truth to himself.","No one could predict how she might react if Yuan revealed the truth—that he had not only attained Flawless Cold Harmony, but had ascended beyond it, stepping into a realm that transcended the very limits of humanity.","\"D-Did anything else happen down there?\" Chief Mu asked.","\"Are you referring to Shiva? Yes, I spoke with her.\" Yuan calmly admitted.","\"What did she say?! Why did she summon you?!\"","Yuan looked at Mu Xuelian with a raised eyebrow.","\"I see. So it wasn’t because Mu Hanyan was trying to help out an old friend but because of your command that she led me here,\" he said, sounding a little disappointed.","\"How else would we have met—is what Lord Shiva said,\" Mu Xuelian relayed.","\"What are you talking about...?\" Chief Mu muttered with a dumbfounded look on her face.","Mu Xuelian closed her eyes for a brief moment, and when they opened again, a profound symbol shimmered within their depths.","\"T-That symbol and presence!\"","Mu Hanyan instantly fell to her knees and kissed the ground with her forehead.","\"This lowly servant greets Lord Shiva!\"","\"What?!\" Chief Mu’s eyes nearly fell out of their socket after hearing Mu Hanyan’s words. However, she didn’t have the time to ponder and quickly followed her mother’s action, kowtowing on the ground.","\"This lowly servant greets Lord Shiva!\"","Shiva then spoke, \"I have been released from my prison and taken residence within this girl’s body.\"","\"?!?!?!\"","Her words left Mu Hanyan and Chief Mu speechless."]},{"number":2175,"title":"Chapter 2175: Leaving White Hell","paragraphs":["Chapter 2175: Leaving White Hell","“C-Congratulations on regaining your freedom, Lord Shiva!”","After a brief moment of silence, Mu Hanyan snapped out of her daze and spoke loudly.","Shiva nodded and said, “The White Hell Barbarian Tribe has fulfilled their duties well. I shall bestow upon your tribe a fitting reward before my departure.”","Meanwhile, inside Yuan’s head—","“Young Master! You’re okay!” Feng Yuxiang’s worried voice resounded.","“Feng Feng? What happened to you?” Yuan asked.","“That’s what I wanted to ask! Our connection with you severed the moment you entered that cavern! However, we were obviously still within your Dantian.”","After Yuan entered Shiva’s Hell, their connection severed, so they’d spent the last three years in the dark.","“Did you try leaving?” Yuan then asked.","“I did, but there was a mysterious force that kept us from leaving your Dantian, almost like we were sealed inside a prison.”","“Is that so... Anyway, I’m fine. I’ll explain everything to you later,” said Yuan.","Sometime later, Yuan and the others returned to the White Hell Barbarian Tribe’s settlement.","Mu Hanyan gathered every member of the tribe to greet Shiva.","“We greet Lord Shiva!”","Shiva, who was in control of Mu Xuelian’s body, proceeded to bless every member of the tribe with her powers, instantly improving their physiques and even increasing their cultivation by an entire level directly.","Once everything was done, Yuan approached one of the members and asked, “Do you know what happened to Yaoqin?”","“Ah, you mean the woman who was cultivating here? She left a month ago, but she also left behind something for you.”","The tribe member went inside the building where Yaoqin had cultivated and grabbed the items left behind by Yaoqin before handing them to Yuan.","“Thank you.”","Yaoqin had left behind a note and a medallion with her name on it.","[Unfortunately, I was unable to see you again before I left. However, if you are ever near the Divine Essence Monastery, please visit me so that I can properly repay the debt I owe you for saving my life. Signed Yaoqin.]","“The Divine Essence Monastery, huh? That’s in the Ninth Heaven. I was going to visit that place one day, anyway.” Yuan stored the note and Yaoqin’s medallion inside his spatial ring.","“Yingzhe, Lord Shiva has called for you,” Mu Hanyan suddenly approached him and said.","“Call me Yuan. I am no longer Tian Yingzhe,” he said.","“Alright...”","Yuan followed Mu Hanyan to another building, where Chief Mu and Mu Xuelian were present.","“You’re leaving soon, right? Lord Shiva asked what your plans are afterward,” Mu Xuelian said.","“The Primordial Realm,” he calmly responded.","“What?” Mu Hanyan and Chief Mu stared at him with wide eyes. Although they have spent most of their lives within White Hell, even they were aware of the notoriety behind the Primordial Realm.","“That place where countless dangerous criminals are imprisoned? Why are you going there?” Mu Hanyan couldn’t help but ask.","“I have some business there, that’s all.”","Yuan looked at Mu Xuelian and said, “I know you want to follow me, but if you don’t want to go there, you can wait here until I return from the Primordial Realm.”","However, Mu Xuelian shook her head and said, “No, I will follow you.”","Yuan looked at Chief Mu and asked, “Did your daughter tell you about her plans to follow me?”","Chief Mu silently nodded.","“Nothing to say?”","“What is there to say? She may be my daughter, but she’s also Lord Shiva’s vessel right now. I do not have the authority to question her decision.”","Mu Hanyan then said, “Honestly, I was already planning on letting Xuelian leave White Hell. Do you remember our agreement? I was going to ask you to let her follow you.”","“I had a feeling it would be something like that, but it’s pretty shameless of you to demand anything when you tricked me,” Yuan said, his eyes slightly narrowed.","Mu Hanyan faced him and apologetically bowed her head, “I’m sorry. If you wish to punish me, I will accept any punishment you may have for me.”","“Forget it. Considering our past, I’ll forgive you.”","“Thank you...”","“When are you going to leave?” Mu Xuelian asked.","“Right now, but I can wait for you if you need some time to prepare,” he said.","“Then give me a few hours to say goodbye to my tribe.”","Yuan nodded.","Sometime later, Mu Xuelian left to say her goodbye to the rest of the tribe.","“Have you reunited with that mischievous little girl yet?” Mu Hanyan suddenly asked Yuan.","“Who?” Yuan asked with a puzzled face.","“You know... that little girl you brought everywhere as Yingzhe. The one who was constantly getting into trouble and required our saving. I think her surname was Xu...”","“Xu Jiaqi? Yes, I have already met her. Why do you ask?”","“How is she doing these days? I haven’t left White Hell since your disappearance.”","“She’s currently a leading figure of Celestial Overlords,” said Yuan.","“I see... Give her my regards the next time you see her again.”","“I will.”","A nostalgic smile tugged at Mu Hanyan’s lips as she reminisced about their past.","“That little girl was constantly getting in my way. I find it cute now, but it was pretty annoying back then. Treat my granddaughter well.”","“Are you not worried about Shiva possessing her body?” Yuan suddenly asked.","“No, Lord Shiva is our guardian spirit. She wouldn’t do anything to harm her.”","Yuan then asked, “How much do you know about Outer Gods—or Eternals?”","“Besides the very basics? Not much... if anything.”","“Alright.”","A few hours later, Mu Xuelian returned and was prepared to leave White Hell.","Yuan didn’t linger and left with her shortly after.","As they traveled, Yuan asked, “Hey, Shiva, do you know anything about an Eternal sealed within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory?”","“Heavenly White Tiger Clan? I know of a few other Eternals sealed within the Nine Heavens before me, but none from that area, so they were most likely sealed after me.”","“There are more sealed Eternals in the Nine Heavens...?”","Her words left Yuan speechless."]},{"number":2176,"title":"Chapter 2176: The Final Moments of the Immortal Monarch’s Life","paragraphs":["\"There are more sealed Eternals in the Nine Heavens...?\" Yuan muttered in a daze.","\"Of course. Since we cannot kill each other, the Nine Heavens is the perfect place to seal each other,\" said Mu Xuelian, relaying Shiva’s words.","\"Eternals cannot kill each other? That’s the first I’ve heard of it,\" Yuan remarked.","\"It isn’t a law that binds us,\" Shiva explained. \"It’s simply that none of us possesses the capability to kill another Eternal.\"","\"The most we can manage is to cast one another into a deep slumber... or seal each other away,\" she continued.","A sudden flicker of realization crossed Yuan’s face, and he murmured softly, \"I remember...\"","\"What?\"","\"I remembered the end of the Immortal Monarch’s life...\" Yuan sighed, his gaze distant as he recalled the final moments of the Immortal Monarch’s life.","The Immortal Monarch, with the Nine Divine Supremes by his side, fought against several Eternals. Despite their seemingly overwhelming prowess, they were only able to put the Eternals to sleep, and it came at a heavy cost.","The devastation of their battle had shattered the Divine Heavens, dividing them into the Nine Heavens and giving birth to Earth, which drifted unfathomably far away. Moreover, the Immortal Monarch and several of his companions perished as a result.","’It’s been a long time since their slumber... those Eternals should be waking up soon, and when that happens, the Nine Heavens will become chaotic again...’","\"Shiva, I must ask... Why are the Eternals so interested in the Nine Heavens? Aren’t you guys the most powerful beings in the universe? Why pay attention to a small world like ours? I doubt we have anything worth your attention.\"","Shiva smiled faintly and said, \"You’re right. The Nine Heavens has nothing that could capture our interest. That is why Eternals pay no heed to the world itself... but rather to what lies hidden within it.\"","\"What is hidden within the Nine Heavens...? A treasure? Do we have a treasure that’s powerful enough to capture even Eternals’ attention?\"","Yuan turned to Shiva for an answer. However, Mu Xuelian merely shook her head and said, \"Lord Shiva said she’s not going to tell you.\"","\"What? Why not? You already revealed so much.\"","\"She said she doesn’t want more competition.\"","\"Competition...? So you’re after this treasure as well.\"","Yuan’s eyes narrowed.","His voice hardened as he continued, \"Then let me warn you clearly—if you do anything that might harm the Nine Heavens, I will stop you myself, just as I did with the Eternals I cast into slumber.\"","Mu Xuelian’s eyes flickered as Shiva took control.","\"You’ve put Eternals to sleep before? I’m very intrigued. Tell me more,\" she said with a chilling smile on her face.","\"I’ll tell you if you tell me what you’re looking for,\" he said.","Shiva sighed and returned control to Mu Xuelian without uttering a word, a clear refusal to his demands.","\"Don’t tell me then. I’ll figure it out eventually, anyway.\"","’A human putting Eternals to sleep? How ridiculous...’ Shiva sneered inwardly.","Sometime later, they finally left White Hell’s territory.","\"So this is the world beyond White Hell...\" Mu Xuelian gazed at the endless greenery stretching toward the horizon, her face brimming with wonder and astonishment—resembling Xi Meili when she had first stepped out of the Ancient Dragon City.","\"Is this your first time outside?\" Yuan asked.","She nodded, \"Besides the tribe chief, we can only leave White Hell when we look for partners.\"","\"Is there a particular reason such a rule exists?\" Yuan asked.","Mu Xuelian answered calmly, \"My mother said it’s tied to our physiques. While we possess a body that can endure—and even flourish—in extreme cold, the moment we leave such conditions, our strength begins to wane. If we remain outside for too long, our bodies will deteriorate... and eventually, we would cripple ourselves and die a painful death.\"","Yuan looked at her with raised eyebrows and said, \"Doesn’t that mean you won’t be able to follow me for too long?\"","After a moment of silence, Mu Xuelian continued in a dazed voice, \"According to Lord Shiva, that is no longer the case, as she’d just fixed the physique’s weakness as a reward for our loyalty, so we can leave without worry now. Also, as the chief’s daughter, my physique is different, so that weakness was never a problem for me.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Sometime later, Yuan said, \"Let’s stop by a city first so I can think about our next steps.\"","\"Didn’t you already decide to visit the Primordial Realm?\" Mu Xuelian asked.","\"Yes, but the Primordial Realm isn’t a place you can just visit as you please. It’s a heavily protected place. Also, I don’t know where it’s located, so I will need to acquire the directions first.\"","\"Okay.\"","After reaching a city, Yuan found a restaurant and settled in a private room to eat his fill while quietly pondering his next steps.","Naturally, he ordered the entire menu.","\"I ordered every dish on the menu, so you can pick whatever you want to eat,\" Yuan said to Mu Xuelian, who silently nodded with a dazed look on her face.","When the dishes were brought out, Mu Xuelian’s eyes widened and her mouth fell open in astonishment at the colorful array before her. In White Hell, they could only eat the meat of magical beasts they hunted themselves, prepared in the simplest of ways—a far cry from the vibrant feast laid out before her now.","Without hesitation, she began trying every single dish on the table.","Seeing how much Mu Xuelian was enjoying the food, Yuan ordered the entire menu for a second time.","Of course, it wasn’t just the two of them. Yingzi, Feng Yuxiang, and Lan Yingying also came out to eat shortly later.","Mu Xuelian stared at the three who appeared like ghosts with a dumbfounded look on her face. \"Who are they...? And where did they come from?\"","\"Oh, right. I hadn’t introduced you to my companions yet.\"","Thus, Yuan began their introduction the very next moment."]},{"number":2177,"title":"Chapter 2177: Dusk Intelligence","paragraphs":["\"My name is Feng Yuxiang. As you can probably guess from my aura, I am a phoenix, and I am the Young Master’s most loyal and number one servant,\" Feng Yuxiang introduced herself first.","Lan Yingying went next.","\"I’m Lan Yingying. I am also a beast—a Divine Serpent.\"","\"Yingzi.\"","\"They’re all your servants?\" Mu Xuelian asked Yuan.","He shook his head and said, \"Although Feng Yuxiang and Lan Yingying are bound to me through a contract, I don’t see them as servants. They’re my precious friends and companions. As for Yingzi, she’s just following me around as a traveling companion.\"","\"Is that so... I’m Mu Xuelian. Nice to meet you all.\"","While they dined, Feng Yuxiang asked, \"Young Master, if you don’t know where the Primordial Realm is, why don’t you just ask those guys from the Celestial Overlords?\"","Yuan shook his head and sighed, \"No, I cannot get them involved. They will also try to persuade me not to go, anyway. I’ll probably have to find an information broker—\"","\"Oh, right. There’s the Dusk Intelligence. Although we’re in the Eighth Heaven, they should also have a branch here.\"","Feng Yuxiang sighed softly. \"I don’t want to sound grim, but Xiao Hua’s condition is worsening. Lately, she’s been moving about more and more in her sleep, as though trapped in pain... or lost in a nightmare she cannot wake from. I’m worried.\"","Yuan nodded with a solemn face, \"That’s why we cannot delay our trip to the Primordial Realm any longer.\"","Once they finished eating and paid the bill, Yuan began asking around about the Dusk Intelligence. Sure enough, they also existed in the Eighth Heaven.","Several teleportation formations later, Yuan found himself on the other side of the Eighth Heaven.","Rather than being nestled within a bustling city, the Dusk Intelligence Yuan sought was currently hidden away in a remote city, isolated in the middle of nowhere. The atmosphere in this place was much more gloomy and suspicious, almost like Yuan had found himself in a dark alley.","\"What is your purpose in this city?\" The guard of this city questioned Yuan when he got close to the gate.","\"I’m here for the Dusk Intelligence,\" he said.","\"The Dusk Intelligence, huh?\" The guard sighed.","\"Is something wrong?\" Yuan asked.","\"You see, the Dusk Intelligence in our city has temporarily closed its doors, so nobody can enter. It has been like that for the last four years.\"","\"Did they say their reason for closing?\"","\"No, they just suddenly closed their doors.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before nodding, \"Thanks for letting me know, but I will take a look for myself anyway.\"","\"Well, I can’t stop you. However, the fee for entering this city is—\"","\"Is a spirit stone enough?\" Yuan showed the guard a single spirit stone.","\"Y-Yes...\" The guard nodded in a daze as he accepted the spirit stone.","Yuan and Mu Xuelian entered the city shortly after and made their way to Dusk Intelligence’s operating building.","Sure enough, when they arrived, the doors to the building were closed. Yet, someone was sweeping the ground outside.","Yuan calmly approached the young man cleaning and asked, \"I have some business with the Dusk Intelligence.\"","The young man gave him a brief glance before he returned to focusing on the ground.","\"Can’t you see that the doors are closed? The Dusk Intelligence hasn’t opened for four years.\"","\"If it’s closed, why are you cleaning it?\"","\"Because I am getting paid to do it.\"","\"...\"","Yuan suddenly retrieved a black medallion from his spatial ring and showed it to the young man.","\"Is the Dusk Intelligence still closed?\"","\"Look here—\"","The young man’s throat stiffened at the sight of the black medallion in Yuan’s grasp.","\"T-Th-That’s the—!!!\"","\"Since you recognize this medallion, you must also be part of Dusk Intelligence.\"","The young man immediately dropped his broom and bowed to Yuan, \"Please forgive me for my rudeness. I wasn’t aware of your identity.\"","\"Forget it. Is the Dusk Intelligence really closed?\" Yuan asked.","\"Please, follow me.\"","Without offering an explanation, the young man began walking away.","Yuan silently followed him to the back of the building, where another door was located.","The young man knocked on the door.","\"What is it?\" A cold voice resounded.","\"The God of War has arrived.\"","\"What?!\"","The door instantly swung open, and a middle-aged man walked out to confirm Yuan’s identity.","\"Welcome, God of War! Please, we have been anticipating your arrival!\" The middle-aged man said.","\"You’ve been anticipating my arrival?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at his wording.","The middle-aged man nodded and said, \"You’ll understand in a few minutes. Please, come inside.\"","Yuan quietly nodded and entered the building.","Once they were inside, the middle-aged man brought Yuan to the top floor, where a teleportation formation existed. Not only that, it was already activated.","\"What’s this?\" Yuan questioned.","\"The gateway to our—the Shadow Army’s hideout,\" answered the middle-aged man without an ounce of hesitation in his voice.","\"The Commander is waiting for you.\"","\"The Commander... Dong Ye?\"","\"That is correct.\"","\"Alright.\"","Without hesitation, Yuan stepped onto the teleport formation and disappeared from the building.","When Mu Xuelian tried to follow, the middle-aged man hastily stopped her, \"W-Wait a second. Who are you, and what is your relationship with the God of War? We weren’t expecting extra company...\"","\"I’m someone who will be carrying his child in the future,\" Mu Xuelian calmly responded.","\"Y-You must be his wife! I apologize!\" The middle-aged man hastily stepped aside, allowing Mu Xuelian access to the teleport formation.","Without another word, Mu Xuelian stepped into the teleportation formation and vanished from the building. When she emerged moments later, she found herself standing in an entirely different city.","Yuan was standing right in front of her, and he appeared to be in a daze as he looked at their surroundings.","\"This place is... the City of Xian...\" he mumbled, a sense of nostalgia washing over him.","A minute later, before they could go anywhere, a figure appeared before them like a ghost.","\"Welcome to the Shadow Army’s hideout, my liege.\"","Dong Ye greeted him with a bow."]},{"number":2178,"title":"Chapter 2178: Primordial Realm’s Location","paragraphs":["\"Dong Ye. It’s been a while,\" Yuan returned the greeting with a warm smile.","\"Indeed, it has.\" Dong Ye nodded.","\"I heard that you’ve anticipated my arrival.\"","Dong Ye smiled and said, \"I knew you’d come here sooner or later. Let’s talk somewhere more private, shall we?\"","Yuan nodded.","As they walked through the empty streets of the city, Yuan asked, \"Did you create this place?\"","\"No, I did not. As much as I loved the city I grew up in, I wouldn’t do something as disrespectful as recreating it without your approval.\"","\"Then...\"","\"It was created by my liege,\" Dong Ye revealed, confirming what was in Yuan’s mind.","\"I see... Unfortunately, I still don’t have all of my memories as the God of War.\"","\"It’s fine. You’ll eventually recall everything. By the way, my liege, who is your new companion?\"","\"I’m someone who will be carrying his child in the future,\" Mu Xuelian calmly responded, repeating what she said earlier.","\"What?\" Dong Ye turned to look at Yuan with raised eyebrows.","Yuan rubbed his eyes and sighed out loud, \"It’s nothing like that. She’s from the White Hell Barbarian Tribe.\"","\"The White Hell Barbarian Tribe? No wonder she looks so familiar,\" Dong Ye remarked.","\"You know them?\"","\"How could I not? Someone from her tribe used to follow you around. I believe her name was Mu Hanyan...\"","\"That’s my grandmother,\" Mu Xuelian said.","\"Unbelievable... To think her granddaughter would be following you after so many years... Is she still alive?\" Dong Ye asked.","\"She’s still alive,\" Mu Xuelian said.","Sometime later, as they drew closer to the towering pagoda in the distance, Yuan remarked, \"This place is quiet. It’s like a ghost town.\"","\"Ah, that’s because most of them are in training. One doesn’t become part of our Shadow Army without extensive training, after all.\"","\"How do you find these people?\" Yuan asked.","\"From the streets. Most of them are either homeless or orphans.\"","\"I see... and how do you train them?\"","\"Believe it or not, this place is where those who have reached the very end of their training curriculum come to train. Naturally, we cannot allow anyone we do not trust to enter,\" said Dong Ye.","\"That’s why we begin by cultivating their loyalty. Since most of them come from the streets, it isn’t difficult to earn their trust. Still, we test them thoroughly for many years. Only when we are certain of their loyalty do we gradually reveal the truth—introducing them to the existence of the God of War and dispelling the false history woven by the previous Celestial Emperors.\"","\"Once we are certain they will be able to handle it, we invest our full resources into them—raising their cultivation and instructing them in the Shadow Army’s techniques.\"","Yuan then asked, \"What happens to those who fail?\"","\"What do you think we do with them?\" Dong Ye asked with a mysterious smile on his face.","\"I doubt you would do something as stupid as disposing of the failures... right?\" Yuan narrowed his gaze at Dong Ye.","He immediately chuckled and said, \"Of course not. I wouldn’t have lived this long if I had done such audacious acts behind your back. Anyway, to answer your question, we simply set them free.\"","\"I have the ability to eat memories, so I take away the memories of those who do not qualify to stay with us. However, it’s not like we abandon them afterward, either. We continue to support those who deserve it from the shadows, and those who do not... we simply let them go.\"","\"How does it work?\" Yuan asked, his curiosity piqued.","\"For example, we have a young boy who failed his training quite early on. After taking away the necessary memories, we sent him to a sect we manage, where he can continue his life as a cultivator. Of course, it’s not like we forced him on this path, either. We confirm what they want to do in their life before we take their memories.\"","\"As for the troublemakers who don’t deserve our support... we just toss them back into the street, where they belong.\"","\"I see... It’s not a perfect system, but nothing in this world is perfect. Most importantly, it helps people in need,\" Yuan mumbled with a satisfied smile on his face.","Sometime later, they arrived at the pagoda.","\"Invincible Heaven,\" Yuan read the grand name of the pagoda hanging by the entrance.","Once inside, they were moved to the highest floor, where a throne stood—untouched for millions of years, yet without a single speck of dust upon it.","\"Please, my liege.\" Dong Ye gestured toward the throne.","Yuan stepped forward and seated himself upon it, his gaze sweeping through the open windows that offered an unobstructed view of every corner of the city.","\"...\"","Mu Xuelian gazed silently at Yuan. The instant he sat upon the throne, a profound and innate aura of dominance surged from him, stirring within her an almost irresistible urge to bow in reverence.","Tears streamed down Dong Ye’s face, and in that moment, he looked like a child who had finally been reunited with his parents after being lost for countless years.","\"Dong Ye, do you know why I visited the Dusk Intelligence?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","Dong Ye’s expression immediately turned serious as he nodded, \"Does it have something to do with the Primordial Realm?\"","Yuan nodded, \"I want to know where it’s located.\"","Dong Ye then said, \"Do you know of a place called the Primordial Chaos?\"","Yuan’s eyes narrowed slightly at this familiar name.","\"Of course. Just like White Hell and the Vanishing Valley, it’s one of the Forbidden Zones. Don’t tell me the Primordial Realm is in such a dangerous place?\"","\"The Primordial Chaos is not only a Forbidden Zone, it’s the most dangerous Forbidden Zone, so it’s essentially the most dangerous place in the Nine Heavens. Unfortunately, the Primordial Realm is inside that place. Fortunately, it’s only at the outskirts,\" Dong Ye revealed.","\"How troublesome,\" Yuan sighed at this information."]},{"number":2179,"title":"Chapter 2179: Primordial Chaos(End of Immortal Monarch’s Return Arc)","paragraphs":["The Primordial Chaos was among the most perilous places in the Nine Heavens, its unique environment cutting cultivators off from spiritual energy. Once their reserves were spent within its depths, they could not recover their strength until they escaped its boundaries.","Though the Primordial Chaos was technically part of the Nine Heavens, only its outermost edges lay within those boundaries. To venture any deeper was to step beyond the Nine Heavens’ protection and into the unknown. Moreover, the creatures that roamed within its depths were all at least of the God Ascension realm.","\"Although the Primordial Chaos is a dangerous place, it’s not the location that’s the most worrying, but the Celestial Emperor’s dogs that are protecting that place,\" Dong Ye sighed.","\"It’s constantly guarded around the clock by at least ten God Ascension realm cultivators. Five of them are at the 5th level God Ascension, and two are at the 7th level.\"","\"Ten God Ascension experts, huh? That is indeed troublesome...\" Yuan sighed, wondering how he would get past ten experts.","Seeing his reaction, Dong Ye confidently patted his chest and declared, \"Don’t worry, my liege. I have spent the last few decades preparing for this exact purpose. The Shadow Army will distract the guards while you enter the Primordial Realm.\"","\"Won’t that alarm the Celestial Emperor, though? Even if I manage to get inside, getting out is my biggest issue, especially if you cause a scene right outside.\"","Dong Ye smiled and said, \"My liege, you’re underestimating how much we’ve prepared for this moment. I know I said decades, but in reality, we’ve been preparing for this moment since the Primordial Era.\"","\"What do you think the members of the Shadow Army do when they complete their training? They infiltrate the Celestial Emperor’s side as spies. Currently, three of the ten experts guarding the Primordial Realm are our people, so even if we get rid of the other seven, we won’t immediately alert the Celestial Emperor.\"","\"I see... and how long do you think I have inside the Primordial Realm?\"","Dong Ye pondered for a moment before speaking, \"The guards at the Primordial Realm are replaced once every one thousand years, and it has already been eight hundred years since the last replacement, so you have about two hundred years before the Celestial Emperor is alerted.\"","\"Two hundred years? That’s more than enough time,\" Yuan nodded.","\"When would you like to depart for the Primordial Realm?\" Dong Ye then asked.","\"As soon as possible.\"","Dong Ye nodded and said, \"In that case, please give me a few days to prepare for your escort.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Then I’ll go prepare now. If you’ll excuse me—\"","\"Dong Ye.\" Yuan suddenly stopped him.","\"My liege?\" Dong Ye turned around with a puzzled face.","A warm smile spread across Yuan’s face as he said, \"Thank you for your efforts and sacrifices through all these years. When our battle is over, I swear upon my soul—I will repay you.\"","Dong Ye’s eyes widened before he immediately dropped to his knees.","\"My liege, this worthless life of mine has been yours ever since you saved me from the streets and bestowed upon me a purpose. From that day onward, all I have ever sought is to repay you, so there’s no need for you to say such words.\"","\"Even if you say that...\" Yuan didn’t know how to respond as tears flowed from Dong Ye’s eyes.","Dong Ye’s past mirrored Tian Xian’s—growing up without a family, he spent much of his childhood living as a bandit. If it weren’t for Tian Xian, Dong Ye would’ve been executed long ago.","After Dong Ye departed, Yuan rose from the throne and walked to the window. As he drifted into thought, he suddenly became aware of a powerful gaze fixed upon him.","\"Who are you?\" Yuan asked out loud.","\"...\"","There was no response, and a moment later, the mysterious individual withdrew their gaze.","Yuan narrowed his eyes toward the distant mountain, where a lone silhouette stood upon the peak—gazing unmistakably in his direction.","However, this silhouette vanished like smoke before Yuan could do anything, disappearing like a ghost.","Yuan felt no concern that the figure posed any danger, as he doubted Dong Ye would allow such a threat into this place. Yet curiosity stirred within him, for the individual’s presence seemed even more formidable than Dong Ye’s.","When Dong Ye returned to his side a few days later, Yuan questioned him about the silhouette.","\"A-A silhouette, you say...?\" Dong Ye swallowed nervously.","Yuan looked at him with raised eyebrows.","\"What’s with that reaction? Don’t tell me that was an intruder?\"","\"No, that’s not possible.\" Dong Ye immediately dismissed that notion.","He continued, \"I have an idea who you’re talking about, but I cannot disclose any information on that individual.\"","Yuan became even more intrigued after hearing this.","\"You can’t tell me? So that person is even more important than me, huh?\" Yuan remarked with a smile.","Dong Ye’s eyes widened at his statement, and he hastily responded, \"Not a chance! There’s nobody more important in my eyes than my liege! However, that person’s circumstances are unique...\"","After a moment of silence, Dong Ye sighed and said, \"I can tell you this, though. My liege, you are very familiar with that person.\"","\"I am? Then why are they keeping their distance?\"","Dong Ye shook his head.","\"I am not sure myself, but I’m sure they’ll approach you once they’re ready.\"","\"If you say so. In any case, have you finished with the preparations?\"","\"Yes, we can leave for the Primordial Realm at your command.\"","\"Let’s leave now, then.\"","\"Please, follow me.\"","Yuan nodded and followed Dong Ye away.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the Shadow Army’s hideout, the silhouette mumbled in a longing tone, \"Tian Yang...\"","Some time later, Dong Ye led Yuan to their destination, where a carriage awaited them. Yuan’s brows rose—not at the carriage itself, but at the flag it bore.","\"Isn’t that the Celestial Family’s flag?\" he remarked."]},{"number":2180,"title":"Chapter 2180: Entering the Primordial Realm","paragraphs":["\"It is the Celestial Family’s flag,\" Dong Ye confirmed with a calm smile on his face.","\"This way, we’ll be able to approach the Primordial Realm without being stopped.\"","\"Impersonating the Celestial Family, huh? Most people wouldn’t even dream of doing something like this,\" Yuan chuckled.","Not even madmen would dare impersonate the Celestial Family—the most powerful clan in the Nine Heavens. For those bold enough to try, death would be the least of their concerns.","However, offending the Celestial Emperor was the Shadow Army’s specialty.","\"Greetings to the God of War.\"","Aside from the carriage, there was a group of God Ascension experts there.","\"They will not only escort you to the Primordial Realm but will also act as a distraction,\" Dong Ye said.","\"It is an honor to finally be of assistance to the God of War,\" they all said, bowing to him.","Yuan acknowledged with a nod, \"I’ll be relying on you guys.\"","After Yuan and Mu Xuelian stepped into the carriage, Dong Ye swallowed an appearance-altering pill before taking his place at the front as the rider.","Moments later, they left the hideout and appeared in a location that was entirely different from the building Yuan had entered from.","Then, without hesitation, they soared toward the sky, entering the Starry Sky hours later.","\"My liege, it’ll take two years just to get there, even at our speed, so make yourself comfortable,\" Dong Ye said.","\"Alright.\"","Yuan retrieved the Mystic Sword Tablet to study it.","As for Mu Xuelian, she spent most of her time staring out the window with a constant look of wonder, as this was her first time entering the Starry Sky.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, almost two years have passed.","\"My liege, I should’ve probably asked you this sooner, but you have the Four Ancient Seals, correct?\"","\"I do.\"","\"We’re almost at our destination, so if you could, assemble the Ancient Seals now so you don’t have to do it later.\"","\"I have to assemble the seals?\"","The next moment, Yuan retrieved the Four Ancient Seals and examined them closely. At first glance, each appeared whole on its own, yet when placed side by side, it became clear—they were fragments meant to fit together into a greater whole.","<You have assembled the Four Ancient Seals, creating an Ancient Key>","Despite its name, the Ancient Key did not resemble a key at all. If anything, it looked like a large seal stamp.","A month later, Dong Ye’s voice resounded, \"My liege, we’re almost at the Primordial Chaos. Please prepare yourself.\"","A few minutes later, Yuan realized that the spiritual energy in the air had suddenly vanis hed.","<You have discovered Primordial Chaos>","<You have entered Primordial Chaos>","For cultivators, a world devoid of spiritual energy was no different from fish stranded without water. Without spiritual energy, once a cultivator’s reserves were depleted, their dantian would gradually wither—and given enough time, the cultivator themselves would perish.","\"I cannot sense any spiritual energy...\" Mu Xuelian was not used to such an environment and instinctively began to panic.","As for Yuan...","<Chaotic Dragon Core has activated>","<You have begun refining Chaotic Essence>","Though the Primordial Chaos was devoid of spiritual energy, it was anything but empty, and it brimmed with Chaotic Essence in overwhelming abundance.","Yingzi emerged from his shadow after sensing the familiar energy.","\"This is Chaotic Essence,\" she remarked after quickly recognizing it.","She looked at Yuan and questioned, \"Have we returned to the Primal Expanse?\"","He shook his head and explained, \"No, we’re still in the Nine Heavens.\"","Yingzi walked to the window and stared outside.","\"But this feeling... It’s the same as the Primal Expanse,\" she muttered.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the outer reaches of the Primordial Chaos, ten God Ascension realm experts sat in silent cultivation, encircling a massive black metal door that loomed alone in the desolate expanse.","However, since there was no spiritual energy for them to absorb, these God Ascension cultivators were merely doing mental cultivation and not actually cultivating.","Suddenly, the expert at the seventh level of God Ascension opened his eyes and spoke out loud, \"We have company.\"","The other nine opened their eyes at his words.","\"That flag... the Celestial Family. Was there an inspection scheduled for today?\"","The experts showed no alarm at the sight, for the Celestial Family frequently came to inspect the Primordial Realm.","\"It might be a surprise inspection.\"","\"I’ll go speak with them,\" said one of the fifth-level God Ascension experts as he rose to his feet and approached the carriage.","Sometime later, the cultivator returned and said, \"It’s a surprise inspection. Prepare to greet the Celestial Family.\"","\"What a pain in the ass.\" One of them complained in a low voice.","Soon, all ten of them left their post and approached the carriage.","\"We greet the Celestial Family.\"","However, in response, the experts guarding the carriage suddenly encircled them.","\"What is the meaning of this?\" one of them questioned with a deep frown.","Still concealed by his disguise, Dong Ye suddenly drew out a treasure and activated it without warning. In the next instant, a massive barrier materialized, enclosing everyone within its confines.","\"T-This is—! It’s an ambush!\"","After confirming the guards were trapped, Dong Ye turned to the carriage and said, \"My liege, you’re good to go. We’ll take care of things from here.\"","Yuan and Mu Xuelian emerged from the carriage the next moment and immediately flew toward the metal black door in the distance.","\"They’re here for the Primordial Realm!\"","Even upon realizing this, the guards did not panic. Instead, mocking laughter erupted from them.","\"Haha! What a futile effort! Without the Ancient Key, not even a Cultivation God can open the Primordial Realm!\"","But the moment they saw Yuan draw forth the Ancient Key, their laughter died instantly, their faces twisting into shock and horror.","\"Why does he have the Ancient Key?!\"","\"Impossible!\"","\"W-We must stop him from opening the Primordial Realm!\"","The guards erupted with power at once, unleashing the full extent of their cultivation without hesitation.","\"Kill them,\" Dong Ye’s commanding voice resounded the next moment."]},{"number":2181,"title":"Chapter 2181: Inside the Primordial Realm","paragraphs":["Upon hearing Dong Ye’s command, the Shadow Army began its fight with the guards of the Primordial Realm.","\"We cannot let that crazy bastard open the Primordial Realm and let the criminals inside loose!\" The guards fought with desperate ferocity, as though not only their own lives, but the lives of their families, hung in the balance.","The Primordial Realm housed countless dangerous and heinous criminals, and none of them dared even to imagine what would happen if these criminals were set free in the Nine Heavens.","Meanwhile, upon reaching the entrance of the Primordial Realm, Yuan poured his spiritual energy into the Ancient Key, activating it. Then, without the slightest hesitation, he drove it into the waiting keyhole.","The sealed doors opened, causing the entire ground to tremble.","\"Let’s go.\"","Yuan entered the Primordial Realm with Mu Xuelian following behind.","Once Yuan and Mu Xuelian’s figures disappeared into the Primordial Realm, the doors closed again.","\"What? They didn’t fully open the Primordial Realm and instead went inside?\" The guards were left dumbfounded by the unexpected development, as they thought Yuan was there to release the criminals.","\"Who the hell are you bastards and what is your goal here?! Do you have any idea what you’ve done?!\" The seventh-level God Ascension expert roared at Dong Ye, his opponent.","\"We are the Shadow Army, and we are here to piss off the Celestial Emperor,\" Dong Ye laughed out loud.","\"The Evil God’s Shadow Army?!\" The guards instantly recognized their infamous name.","\"Hah! Kill us then! Let’s see what will happen afterward!\"","Dong Ye shook his head and said, \"Although I told them to kill you guys, we’re not really going to kill you. Do you think we aren’t aware that the Celestial Emperor is tracking your lives with a Life Tablet and that if we kill you, it would immediately alert him?\"","\"We won’t kill you for now, but we will destroy your physical body in case you try anything.\"","In the middle of their fight, three of the guards, who were Shadow Army spies, suddenly betrayed the other seven.","\"What the fuck are you three doing?!\"","\"They must be spies!\"","\"Do you think you’ll get away with this?!\"","With the betrayal and the Shadow Army’s overwhelming might, the fight ended in the blink of an eye.","The Shadow Army destroyed the guards’ physical bodies but left their souls alone so that the Life Tablet tracking their lives wouldn’t activate.","\"Great job, everyone. However, we’re far from done,\" said Dong Ye.","He proceeded to use his memory-stealing abilities on the guards, stealing their identities.","\"The Celestial Family does random inspections, and we must be ready for them when that happens,\" he said afterward.","\"Yes, commander!\"","Meanwhile, Yuan and Mu Xuelian appeared inside the Primordial Realm.","\"What is this place...?\" Mu Xuelian murmured, her eyes wide with curiosity and disbelief as she studied their surroundings. Above them stretched a pitch-black sky, where streaks of crimson lightning slithered like serpents through the void.","The land was even more dreadful—a desolate plain of scorched earth, fractured with countless cracks, as though it bore the aftermath of an ancient apocalypse.","Yet, despite the dark skies, the red lightning appeared frequently enough to constantly illuminate the world.","*Cough* *Cough*","Mu Xuelian suddenly started coughing.","\"The air outside was already awful, but in here it’s even worse! The atmosphere feels suffocating!\" she exclaimed, raising her hands to cover her mouth.","Yuan faced her and shrugged, \"I suggested you not follow me in here earlier, but you wanted to be stubborn.\"","He looked at the sky and sighed, \"But this place is definitely very... tragic. Not only does this place lack spiritual energy, but the Chaotic Essence is at least ten times denser than outside.\"","\"There’s no way any cultivator can survive in this environment. Why did you want to come here?\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"No, there are definitely people living in here. I can sense someone not too far away from us.\"","\"You’re using divine sense? Aren’t you worried that you’ll exhaust your spiritual energy? You can’t replenish it in this place, after all,\" Mu Xuelian asked.","\"I don’t have any issues replenishing my spiritual energy since I can refine the Chaotic Essence in this place. Ah, Chaotic Essence is what you’re sensing right now, and it cannot be refined by humans.\"","\"As Lord Shiva said... you’re not human...\" Mu Xuelian stared at him with a dumbfounded face.","\"So, what’s next?\" she asked a moment later.","\"Ask for directions,\" he answered, his gaze shifting toward the presence he had already sensed.","Just as Yuan began to take flight, Mu Xuelian suddenly shouted, \"Wait!\"","\"Hm?\" Yuan turned around to see Mu Xuelian glaring at him from the ground.","\"Oh, right. You cannot replenish your spiritual energy, so it’d be wise to save it for when you truly need it.\"","Yuan made a gesture toward her figure, and the next moment, Mu Xuelian’s body lifted off the ground and flew beside him.","\"Thank you,\" she said.","Yuan silently nodded before flying away with Mu Xuelian.","They flew for hours without encountering so much as a single tree—or any sign of life at all.","Some time later, Yuan halted before a half-destroyed mountain, its upper half completely gone, while the remaining portion was riddled with cracks, as though it might collapse into ruin at any moment.","\"Wait here,\" Yuan instructed Mu Xuelian before striding toward the lone cave in the distance. When he was halfway there, a silhouette emerged from its depths.","When the figure finally stepped out of the cave, it was revealed to be a gaunt, middle-aged man. His limbs were so frail and thin they seemed as though they might snap under the mere weight of his own stance.","Yet, his eyes were filled with life and killing intent.","Seeing Yuan’s healthy appearance, the man frowned and said, \"There’s nothing for you to take here.\"","Yuan responded with a calm smile, \"I’m just here for directions.\""]},{"number":2182,"title":"Chapter 2182: Inside the Primordial Realm(2)","paragraphs":["\"You’re here to ask for directions...?\" The skinny man wore a dumbfounded look on his face after hearing Yuan’s words.","He focused on Yuan’s appearance again. In the Primordial Realm, due to its chaotic environment, having a healthy appearance was a privilege accessible only to the most powerful individuals and families.","But what truly set Yuan apart from the ordinary dwellers of the Primordial Realm was the vast reservoir of spiritual energy within him. Though he tried to conceal it, those who had long been starved of such energy could instinctively sense its presence.","Yet a privileged background did not mean one was above resorting to robbery. In the Primordial Realm, where resources were scarce and the law of the jungle reigned supreme, even the lofty could be driven to desperate means. In fact, it was usually the most powerful individuals who took advantage of their privilege.","\"Who... Who are you looking for?\"","\"The Asura Clan,\" Yuan calmly answered.","\"The—?!\"","The man’s eyes widened in shock and disbelief at the mention of the Asura Clan, as though he had just laid eyes on a ghost.","\"You’re seeking the Asura Clan?! Get lost! How dare you toy with me!\" the man roared, slashing the air with his arm.","Yuan tilted his head, his expression puzzled. \"What makes you think I’m joking? I’m being serious.\"","\"Nonsense! Nobody in this world would willingly seek out the Asura Clan—not even the insane!\"","\"I’m not insane, but I am seriously looking for the Asura Clan,\" Yuan shrugged.","\"N-No... I don’t know why you’re looking for the Asura Clan, but I want no involvement.\"","Without another word, the skinny man turned around and walked back inside the cave, his figure disappearing into the darkness.","\"...\"","\"It seems finding the Asura Clan will take more effort than I expected...\" Yuan sighed.","He turned to leave, heading back toward Mu Xuelian. But after only a few steps, he halted, a strange sensation prickling across his back, forcing him to turn around.","When Yuan turned, he found the skinny man—who had vanished into the cave—now standing behind him, a dagger pressed firmly against his back.","\"What is the meaning of this?\" Yuan asked, his voice calm and steady.","\"I–Impossible...!\" the man muttered, disbelief etched across his face. Ignoring Yuan’s words, he lashed out again, this time with even greater force.","However, Yuan had no intention of simply standing still, even if the strike posed no threat to him. In a swift motion, he twisted his body, extended his arm, and clamped his hand firmly around the man’s neck, lifting him into the air.","\"How?! You’re just a mere True Immortal!\" The skinny man shouted.","Despite his frail appearance, he was a cultivator at the first level of God Ascension. In his mind, it was impossible for an Immortal to withstand his strike.","\"I don’t think I have done anything deserving of this backstab,\" Yuan said.","After snapping out of his daze, the skinny man laughed out loud, \"You speak like someone from the outside. This is the Primordial Realm! Do I need any reason to attack someone so defenseless?!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes and said, \"I’ll give you a chance to live. Tell me where I can find the Asura Clan, and I’ll spare your life for your offense.\"","The man opened his mouth—not to speak, but to spit.","\"Hak-too!\" he snarled, hurling the glob straight at Yuan’s face.","Yuan calmly blocked the spit with spiritual energy.","\"Hahaha! What a waste of spiritual energy!\"","Without a word, Yuan clenched his fist, crushing the man’s neck. However, the man wasn’t dead yet. As a God Ascension cultivator, unless Yuan destroyed his soul, he would remain alive.","Even so, in the Primordial Realm—where cultivation resources were almost nonexistent—reconstructing a body was impossible for the weak.","Yuan nonchalantly tossed the body on the ground and returned to Mu Xuelian’s side.","\"Quite ruthless,\" she remarked.","\"He struck first,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Besides, most who dwell in this realm are criminals deserving of death.\"","\"So, what now?\"","\"Look for someone else who can help us.\"","Yuan looked around and continued a moment later, \"Unfortunately, I don’t sense anyone else nearby, so we can only wander around until we encounter someone.\"","After picking up Mu Xuelian, Yuan flew away and continued their search.","’Although that man was weak for a God Ascension cultivator, he still had some power in him. The Primordial Realm hasn’t opened since the Primordial Era, so how did that man cultivate, much less reach God Ascension?’ Yuan pondered as they traveled.","He couldn’t fathom how cultivators survive in this environment. Also, there was the existence of Exiles, people who are allowed outside for a chance of freedom through the Supreme Heaven’s Legacy.","Sometime later, Yuan stopped moving when he noticed a drastic change in the atmosphere.","\"Do you sense that too?\" Mu Xuelian asked with her brows slightly raised.","He nodded.","\"Something is about to happen,\" Yuan murmured, tilting his head toward the blackened sky, where the lightning serpents were converging upon a single point.","Moments later, he could sense several presences appearing from a distance, all of them rushing in their direction.","\"People are coming.\"","A few minutes later, four cultivators appeared before Yuan and Mu Xuelian. Unlike the skinny man they previously encountered, these four cultivators appeared a little healthier. Two of them were True Immortals, while the other two were at the first and second levels of God Ascension.","\"Scram if you don’t want to die,\" said the second-level God Ascension cultivator.","\"...\"","\"Why don’t you scram?\" said the other God Ascension cultivator.","The two True Immortals didn’t say anything, but it was clear they also had no intention of leaving.","\"I will not warn you again,\" said the second-level God Ascension cultivator.","\"Let’s not be too greedy. There are only a few of us here, so we can share it. Even if you fight and defeat us all, you might lose more than you gain,\" said one of the True Immortals.","The second-level God Ascension cultivator frowned and fell silent to ponder."]},{"number":2183,"title":"Chapter 2183: Inside the Primordial Realm(3)","paragraphs":["As the second-level God Ascension cultivator pondered, his gaze fell upon Yuan and Mu Xuelian. Although Yuan was only a True Immortal, his appearance and abundant spiritual energy implied that he came from a powerful family. However, what truly surprised him was Mu Xuelian’s existence.","There were many God Ascension realm cultivators within the Primordial Realm, but those who had as much spiritual energy as Mu Xuelian were incredibly rare, including those with a much higher cultivation than hers.","’Besides that white-haired woman, I can defeat the others, but it’ll exhaust too much energy. Since there are only a few of us, there’s no need to risk it.’","The second-level God Ascension cultivator didn’t acknowledge it openly, but he decided not to chase the others away.","Minutes later, the massed lightning within the clouds erupted, unleashing a single devastating bolt that descended like a heavenly judgment.","The bolt was so intense it ripped through the very fabric of space, leaving behind a rift that seethed with turbulent spiritual energy.","Seeing this, the cultivators immediately began absorbing the spiritual energy, replenishing what little reserve they had left.","Yuan and Mu Xuelian watched with intrigue, as they’d never seen anything like this before.","’So this is why that cultivator wanted everyone else to leave...’ Yuan thought to himself, finally understanding the situation.","However, he still had questions, such as where the spiritual energy was coming from.","’Why aren’t those two cultivating and just watching? Are they mocking us?’ The cultivators wondered when they realized Yuan and Mu Xuelian were idling not far away.","’They might attack us while we’re cultivating...’","Worried that Yuan and Mu Xuelian might attack out of nowhere, the cultivators remained vigilant.","A few minutes later, Yuan suddenly spoke, startling the others.","\"Hey, I have a question. Do you know where I can find the Asura Clan?\"","\"?!?!\"","The cultivators snapped their heads toward Yuan, their faces frozen in disbelief. Yet after a brief silence, they quickly averted their gazes, acting as though they had never heard his words at all.","Seeing this, Yuan started to absorb the spiritual energy from the rift at a terrifying rate, shocking the cultivators.","’What the hell is that insane absorption rate?! At this rate, he’ll absorb all of the spiritual energy in minutes!’ they cried inwardly.","\"If nobody answers, I will continue to absorb the spiritual energy,\" Yuan said.","\"I will answer—!\" one of the True Immortals hastily said.","However, before he could answer Yuan’s question, a powerful presence emerged nearby, swiftly closing in on their location. Even before the figure came into view, an aggressive voice thundered through the air, \"If anyone still dares to absorb that spiritual energy after this warning, I’ll skin you alive when I get there in a minute.\"","\"This presence... It’s a fifth-level God Ascension cultivator!\"","Everyone there subconsciously halted absorbing the spiritual energy, and the True Immortals even prepared to flee, as this fifth-level God Ascension cultivator seemed to have plenty of spiritual energy just by how he was willing to use voice transmission.","\"Before you leave, can you answer my question?\" Yuan said, snapping them out of their daze.","\"S-Screw you! If I cannot acquire any more spiritual energy, what’s the point of answering you and offending the Asura Clan?!\"","Then, the True Immortal turned around and flew away. The other True Immortal also left silently.","As for the God Ascension cultivators, they exchanged glances before turning to look at Mu Xuelian and said, \"If the three of us worked together, we might be able to deal with this bastard.\"","Mu Xuelian raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Why should I work with you? This is your problem, not mine.\"","The second-level God Ascension cultivator frowned and responded, \"Why the hell are you here if not for the spiritual energy?\"","\"We were just passing by when this phenomenon happened. I don’t need the spiritual energy, anyway,\" she calmly responded.","\"You don’t need the spiritual energy...?\" Not just the second-level God Ascension cultivator, but even the other guy trembled in anger after hearing her words.","In the Primordial Realm, nearly every cultivator was starved for spiritual energy. For someone to claim they had no need of it was like boasting of never needing food because they are always full and have never starved before, while standing before the homeless, gaunt with hunger.","The God Ascension cultivators wanted to tear Mu Xuelian apart after hearing her words, but they controlled themselves, as they would gain nothing from it, not to mention the incoming threat.","\"Hmph! If you want the spiritual energy, you can fight for it!\"","Without hesitation, the second-level God Ascension cultivator began absorbing the spiritual energy again.","Seeing this, the other cultivator also followed.","\"Courting death!\"","The fifth-level God Ascension cultivator arrived at the scene a few minutes later. Upon his arrival, he immediately unleashed a powerful martial technique at the two who ignored his warning.","\"This crazy bastard!\"","The two cultivators hastily stopped their cultivation to block the incoming attack.","\"Fuck! My spiritual energy!\"","While they were able to block the attack properly, it had consumed more spiritual energy than what they had absorbed from the rift.","\"Hahaha! This is what you fools get for defying my warning! Now, die for your sins!\" The fifth-level God Ascension cultivator laughed madly as he continued his assault on the other two.","\"Damn it! I’m not going to waste my spiritual energy on a madman! It’s not worth it!\"","The second-level God Ascension cultivator did not hesitate to run away.","Seeing this, the first-level God Ascension cultivator also fled.","\"...\"","The fifth-level God Ascension cultivator didn’t chase after them. He turned to look at Yuan and Mu Xuelian for a brief moment before ignoring them to absorb the spiritual energy from the rift.","However, Yuan also started absorbing the spiritual energy the very next moment.","\"What the fuck do you think you’re doing, you little brat?!\"","Yuan responded with a calm smile, \"If you tell me where I can find the Asura Clan, I’ll let you have all of the spiritual energy here. If not, I don’t mind fighting to the death.\""]},{"number":2184,"title":"Chapter 2184: Asura Clan’s Location","paragraphs":["The man’s expression darkened after hearing the name Asura Clan.","\"What did you just say?! The Asura Clan?! Are you insane? How dare you utter their name before me! You must be trying to get me killed!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and responded, \"What are you so afraid of? You’re not the first person I’ve asked about the Asura Clan, but you all have the same terrified reaction, almost as if you’ll die just for talking about them.\"","\"What nonsense are you spouting? Anyone living in this forsaken world would tremble at their name! Unless... you’re not from the Primordial Realm? No... that can’t be.\"","For a brief moment, the man considered the possibility that Yuan had come from the outside, but he quickly dismissed the thought as impossible. After all, the Primordial Realm has been closed since the Primordial Realm.","\"So what if I am from the outside world?\" Yuan suddenly said.","The man’s eyes widened with shock and disbelief.","\"You... are you serious?\" The man swallowed nervously, as he couldn’t imagine what sort of heinous crime Yuan had committed to force the Celestial Emperor to throw him in an abandoned prison like the Primordial Realm.","Yuan silently nodded in acknowledgement.","’No wonder his appearance is so clean... but he’s only a True Immortal. What could he have done to—No, I shouldn’t involve myself in his business. He’s too dangerous.’","\"Why are you looking for the Asura Clan?\" the man then asked.","\"I just have some business with them. Why does it matter to you?\"","The man frowned and said, \"I want no involvement in your search for the Asura Clan if you’re trying to fight them. If they kill you and discover I was the one who pointed you their way, I’ll be as good as dead myself.\"","’Is that why everyone was afraid to tell me the directions? Because they’re afraid that I might fight them?’ Yuan wondered to himself.","He then smiled and said, \"Don’t worry, I’m not going to fight them.\"","The man pondered for a moment before pointing toward the south and saying, \"You can find the Asura Clan at the border of the Spirit Tree.\"","\"Spirit Tree, right? Thanks for the information.\"","Yuan stopped absorbing the spiritual energy.","\"Before I leave, I have one more question. Where is the nearest city?\"","The man then pointed west and said, \"There’s one a week away in that direction.\"","Yuan didn’t linger and left with Mu Xuelian shortly after.","Once Yuan left, the man sighed in relief.","\"For the first time since the Primordial Era, someone new has been tossed inside the Primordial Realm... I can only hope this is just a one-time event.\"","The man worried over the implications. If the current Celestial Emperor were to make use of the Primordial Realm again, it could plunge the realm into chaos—disrupting the fragile society and norms its residents had managed to build through many eras.","\"Let’s not overthink it and hurry up and consume the spiritual energy before someone else comes...\"","Meanwhile, Yuan and Mu Xuelian sped toward the nearest city, arriving at their destination in under a day of travel.","Although the man said it would take a week, he was talking about walking distance since cultivators in the Primordial Realm only fly when it’s an emergency, as it would be a waste.","Once they arrived in the city, Yuan used his divine sense to scan the city. He wanted to look for a teleport formation, but he didn’t find one even after searching the entire city.","\"Looks like we will have to go to another city,\" Yuan said to Mu Xuelian.","Yuan shifted his attention to a nearby pedestrian, who was a young man and a pure mortal.","\"Hey, can I ask you a question?\"","The young man turned to face Yuan, and the instant he saw his appearance, shock overtook his face.","\"How may this lowly one serve you?!\" he cried, dropping to his knees and kowtowing before Yuan.","Yuan raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner at the young man’s unexpected reaction and questioned, \"Do you recognize me?\"","The young man, not daring to raise his head, responded, \"No, I do not!\"","\"Then why are you reacting like that?\"","\"Because you are a cultivator!\"","\"...\"","\"He’s probably like that because cultivators are rare in the Primordial Realm. In a world where spiritual energy rarely exists, I highly doubt many would even attempt to become one,\" Yu Ning remarked.","\"That makes sense...\" Yuan mumbled, finding Yu Ning’s words very logical.","\"Anyway, I would like to ask you... Do you know which city has a teleport formation?\" he then asked the young man.","\"A... what?\" The young man responded in a confused tone, almost as if he’d never heard of this term.","\"I don’t think teleport formations exist in this world,\" Yu Ning suddenly said.","\"If you think about it, teleport formations can only be activated with spiritual energy. Even if they somehow manage to activate it, they’ll still need spiritual energy to teleport.\"","\"...\"","Yuan became speechless when he realized that he’d overlooked this fact.","\"Senior Immortal?\"","The young man spoke when Yuan didn’t say anything for some time.","Yuan snapped out of his daze and asked, \"Then do you know how far away the Spirit Tree is?\"","\"The legendary Spirit Tree, where only the most powerful cultivators go?! I’m sorry. While I have heard of its name, I don’t know where it’s located. I reckon that only powerful cultivators will know since it’s not something us ordinary mortals even dream of.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before speaking again, \"Hey, I have another favor. Can you tell me more about this world? I’ll treat you to a meal for your assistance.\"","\"Really?!\"","Yuan nodded, \"I’ll even let you choose the restaurant. Let’s talk while we eat.\"","\"Okay!\"","\"...\"","After a moment of awkward silence, the young man asked, \"Is it okay for me to stand up now?\"","\"Of course. You don’t need to be so formal, either. Just treat me like a friendly neighbor or something,\" Yuan said."]},{"number":2185,"title":"Chapter 2185: Primordial Realm’s Three Region","paragraphs":["\"I have never met a cultivator as kind as you, Senior Brother,\" said the young man as he led Yuan to a nearby restaurant.","\"Are you sure you want to eat at this place?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow after seeing the rundown building the young man had brought him to.","\"Don’t let its crummy appearance fool you, Senior Brother. This shop has some of the best noodles in this city—and the cities nearby.\"","\"Alright. I’ll trust you.\"","Yuan scanned the restaurant with his divine sense just in case the young man was luring him into a trap. Of course, he wasn’t worried about being ambushed in the slightest. Fortunately, the restaurant was clear, and he found nothing suspicious.","Once they were seated inside, the young man ordered for them.","\"Boss, let me get three large bowls of noodles with meat dumplings.\"","\"Three large bowls of noodles with meat dumplings on the way,\" said the old man working behind the counter.","\"Now, what did you want to know about this world? I may look young, but I am quite knowledgeable, if I may say so myself. I even know some things that only cultivators would know,\" said the young man in a boastful tone.","\"You see, I live in a secluded part of this world and only recently began to expand my views, so I don’t know much about the situation of the rest of the world.\"","\"In that case, should I tell you what I know about our world?\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Very well,\" the young man began. \"As you likely already know, we now live in the Primordial Realm—a place once used to imprison criminals during the Primordial Era. At first, the criminals fought endlessly among themselves, but after tens of thousands of years of bloodshed, they came to realize they might never leave. So, they ceased their battles and instead turned their efforts toward building a society of their own.\"","\"Now, the Primordial Realm is controlled by four powerful backgrounds. The Zhao Family, Chaotic Sect, the Inferno Alchemists, and the Asura Clan. Not only do they each rule over the majority of the Primordial Realm, but they are absolute powers that even cultivators cannot defy—especially the Asura Clan. Despite having the smallest population amongst the powerhouses, the Asura Clan is undoubtedly the strongest in the Primordial Realm.\"","\"With that said, the Primordial Realm is split into three regions. The Realm of Chaos, ruled by the Chaotic Sect. Zhao Province, ruled by the Zhao Family. The final region is the Land of Inferno, ruled by the Inferno Alchemists. Although the Asura Clan is a powerhouse, they only rule a small area of the Primordial Realm. However, the place they rule is arguably the most important area in this entire world.\"","\"The Spirit Tree?\" Yuan said.","The young man nodded and elaborated, \"The Spirit Tree is the only place in this world that lets cultivators... well, cultivate. Of course, there are the Spiritual Rifts, but those are rare and random, so cultivators cannot rely on them.\"","\"Spiritual Rifts? Is that when lightning strikes and tears through space, releasing spiritual energy?\" Yuan asked.","\"Yes, that’s what I heard. Unfortunately, I have never personally witnessed it, even with my 20 years of experience.\"","Yuan then asked, \"How spacious is the Primordial Realm? Let’s say I want to get to the other side of the world. How long would that take?\"","The young man pondered for a moment before responding, \"I don’t think the Primordial Realm is that big. From what I’ve heard through traveling merchants, it could take up to 10 years to travel around the world on foot, so it’s probably not that big for cultivators who can fly.\"","\"Only ten years on foot? The Primordial Realm is quite small, then. By the way, which region are we currently in?\"","\"The Realm of Chaos.\"","\"I see.\"","The owner of the restaurant approached the table with their noodles shortly after.","\"What do you think?\" the young man asked.","\"It’s actually delicious. What is this meat? I have never tasted anything like this before,\" Yuan remarked as he gazed at the meat dumplings.","Before the young man could respond, Yingzi suddenly emerged from Yuan’s shadow.","\"Whoa!\" The young man was startled by Yingzi’s sudden appearance and stared at her beautiful face with a dazed look.","\"What’s up?\" Yuan looked at her.","Yingzi pointed at the meat dumpling and said, \"I want to taste it.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Yuan handed her a dumpling.","After tasting the meat, she responded, \"As I thought, I have tasted this meat before. It’s from a common beast in the Primal Expanse.\"","\"What? Really?\" Yuan’s eyes widened at this information.","Yingzi nodded, \"I am certain. I have feasted on them a few times before.\"","\"...\"","Yuan fell silent to ponder the implications.","’Beings from the Primal Expanse can be found in the Primordial Realm? Just what is this place, anyway?’ he wondered inwardly.","\"Anyway, let’s order some more. I won’t be satisfied with just one.\"","Yuan gestured at the owner and said, \"I want 20 more of this.\"","\"T-Twenty?!\" The old man’s eyes widened.","\"Um... I’ll need you to pay upfront if you’re going to order that much food...\"","Yuan nodded, \"How much?\"","\"Including the three bowls I’ve already served, 23 small chaos coins.\"","\"Uhh...\"","The old man frowned at Yuan’s reaction and said, \"You don’t have the money?\"","\"Wait just a minute...\"","Yuan turned to the young man and asked, \"Do you have any money on you?\"","\"What?! Don’t tell me you actually don’t have any money?! Then why did you say you’ll treat me?!\" The young man exclaimed.","\"I do have money. I just don’t think they’ll work here since I have never heard of ’chaos coins’.\"","\"Each region has their own currency, but it can be used in other regions,\" said the young man.","Yuan retrieved some gold coins and showed them to the young man, \"What about this? It’s gold coins.\"","\"Gold coins?! That’s ancient currency!\" the young man exclaimed, his eyes wide with disbelief."]},{"number":2186,"title":"Chapter 2186: A Single Gold Coin","paragraphs":["\"I-Is that real?\" the young man stammered after hearing it was a gold coin. Most of the earliest people cast into the Primordial Realm had arrived empty-handed, but in the chaos, a few managed to smuggle in their treasures and valuables. As a result, items like gold coins, spirit stones, and other treasures did exist in the Primordial Realm—but they were exceedingly rare and priceless.","This was especially true given that many eras had passed since the Primordial Era, and most of such valuables had long since been claimed by the powerful or lost to the ravages of time.","\"Of course, it’s real.\" Yuan nodded. \"Anyway, can I pay with this?\"","\"Pay with the gold coin?! I apologize for my language, but are you insane?! A single one of those coins can turn a poor family into a rich one! If you’re going to use that gold coin to buy noodles, I’d rather you give me the gold coin and I pay for the noodles for you! Hell, I’ll even go into debt to pay for your noodles!\" said the young man, making his voice as low as possible even though they were the only customers inside the restaurant.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Let’s do that then.\"","He placed the gold coin on the table and calmly slid it in front of the young man.","\"...\"","The young man didn’t immediately accept the coin and could only stare at it with a dazed face. He couldn’t comprehend how Yuan could casually give away such a precious item.","’Am I being scammed right now?’ he wondered inwardly.","However, the possibility of a cultivator scamming a mortal for some noodles was just as inconceivable.","’Whatever. Even if I might go broke, I’m willing to take the risk!’","After a moment of hesitation, the young man grabbed the gold coin and immediately put it inside his pocket.","\"Sorry for the delay, owner. I’ll pay for the noodles right now.\"","The young man got up from the table and went to pay the old man.","\"Is that your friend?\" the old man asked as he accepted the money, a slight frown on his face.","\"Something like that.\"","The old man shook his head and sighed, \"He’s sketchy. Don’t get involved with people like him. I’m warning you because you’re a regular at my restaurant.\"","\"Thank you for the advice...\" The young man didn’t argue and returned to the table to wait for the food.","\"Do you have any more coins? I’d like to take a look at one.\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"Here... It’s my last coin...\"","The young man handed Yuan a small black coin with a hint of purple mixed within, its surface gleaming with a crystal-like sheen. Yuan studied it closely, though the material and design were unfamiliar to him.","Yingzi moved her head closer to the coin and said, \"This is made of shadow crystals...\"","\"What? You also recognize this material?\" Yuan looked at her with surprise.","She nodded and said, \"Shadow Crystals are rare resources found only in places untouched by light. My homeland had them in abundance. They are similar to spirit stones but contain Chaotic Essence instead.\"","\"And they’re using such rare materials to make coins to use as currency? Well, I guess it doesn’t really hold any value to cultivators since they cannot cultivate Chaotic Essence.\"","\"Thanks.\" Yuan handed the coin back to the young man before asking, \"Is there a place where I can sell some gold coins? It’s not convenient to travel without money.\"","The young man pondered for a moment before responding, \"Our city is quite small and poor, so you won’t find anyone able to buy them here. How many are you trying to sell?\"","\"A handful?\"","\"A hand—?! You have that many?! But you don’t have a single chaos coin?! That doesn’t make any sense!\"","If the young man knew Yuan actually had tens of millions of gold coins in his possession, not even the heavens would be able to predict his reaction.","\"I came from a very, very seclusive place...\" Yuan gave a random but somewhat believable excuse.","\"In fact, I am currently traveling the world and gaining experience for a trial, and my family didn’t give me any money when I left.\"","\"A trial...? Cultivators are truly something else... If only I could become one, too. Unfortunately, I was born into an ordinary family, and I am not desperate enough to risk my life for glory.\"","Yuan smiled faintly and said, \"To become a cultivator in an environment like this... I can hardly imagine how one could even begin the path without the fortune of a privileged birth.\"","\"Truly.\" The young man sighed. \"Forget spiritual energy—even if someone were granted an endless supply, most couldn’t so much as obtain a cultivation technique.\"","Sometime later, Yuan asked, \"Since you don’t know where the Spirit Tree is located, do you know someone who does?\"","\"You can try the First City. Their city is the most prosperous in the Realm of Chaos, and it’s where most cultivators gather. Oh, you can probably sell your gold coins there, as well.\"","\"First City? What is the name of this city?\" Yuan then asked.","\"The Seventh City.\"","\"What an odd naming choice. How many cities are in this region?\" he asked further.","\"Seven,\" the young man swiftly replied. \"Each city is ranked according to its value, and that rank becomes its name. As such, the names can change.\"","\"So this is the worst city, huh?\"","\"Only by a small margin. Besides the top three cities, the disparity between each city isn’t as much as you imagine.\"","The noodles began arriving shortly later, quickly filling the table.","\"You’re not going to eat?\" Yuan asked when the young man didn’t touch the noodles.","\"A single bowl is enough to keep me going for an entire day.\"","\"One bowl for an entire day? No wonder you’re so skinny.\"","\"What can I do when that’s all I can afford? I’m used to it by now, anyway,\" he said with a bittersweet smile.","\"Well, today is a special day, so eat until you’re full,\" said Yuan.","\"If you say so.\" The young man nodded and reached for a bowl."]},{"number":2187,"title":"Chapter 2187: A Single Gold Coin(2)","paragraphs":["Although there were 20 bowls of noodles, the group finished them in less than half an hour.","\"Wow, I have never been this full before,\" said the young man as he patted his stomach, which was noticeably rounder.","\"Will you be heading to the First City immediately?\" he then asked.","Yuan nodded, \"Yes, that’s my intention.\"","The young man fell silent, almost as if pondering something.","Seeing his expression, Yuan asked, \"What’s on your mind?\"","\"Well... I was just wondering if I could follow you to the First City. After all, I won’t be able to sell the gold coin you gave me in this city, and it’s too dangerous to travel alone. Of course, I understand if you refuse.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"I don’t mind. In fact, we can sell the gold coins together. After all, I am not familiar with the First City.\"","\"I have never been to the First City, either, so I don’t think I’ll be of much help there. However, I’ll still try my best.\"","\"Sure.\"","\"Before we depart, I need to return home and let my family know I’ll be gone for a long time,\" the young man said.","\"You won’t be gone for too long. It’ll take a few days at most.\"","The young man wore a puzzled look on his face and said, \"What? But the First City isn’t close to our city. It’ll take at least a few months just to get there.\"","Yuan chuckled and replied, \"That may be the case if we walked there. I intend to fly there. Of course, I’ll take you with me.\"","\"Fly?! You can actually fly?!\" The young man stared at him with awe.","\"I sure can.\"","\"That’s amazing! I’ll go home right now to let my family know!\"","Since he had nothing else to do, Yuan followed the young man to his home.","\"Mother, father, I’m going to leave this city for a few days—a few weeks at most—to seize an opportunity.\"","\"Where are you going?\" asked the mother.","\"The First City.\"","\"What? Are you sure? That’s at least two months away—not including the time it’ll take you to come back!\" the father exclaimed.","\"Oh, I won’t be walking there. I made a new friend, and he’s a cultivator who can fly.\"","His parents looked at him with worried expressions on their tired faces.","\"Wu Qi... are you sure you’re not being tricked by this person? Why would a cultivator want anything to do with you, much less take you to the first city?\"","\"Don’t say that! He may be standing outside, but he can definitely hear you!\"","\"Where and how did you meet this cultivator?\"","The young man, named Wu Qi, summarized the situation to them.","\"A gold coin for twenty-three bowls of noodles...? Aiya... I knew I raised a gullible son, but to think you were this stupid...\" The mother sighed while shaking her head.","\"Son... listen to your mother and wake up. I doubt this guy is a cultivator, much less generous enough to give you a gold coin for some noodles.\"","Wu Qi gritted his teeth in frustration and shouted, \"Fine! Don’t believe me if you don’t want to! You can even call me stupid, but I am going to trust my guts and head to the First City!\"","Without another word, he turned around and stomped away.","\"Wu Qi!\"","\"Stop right there!\"","Seeing this, his parents immediately went to block his path.","\"Let me go!\" Wu Qi shouted.","\"No! You’ll have to step over our dead bodies if you want to throw away your life!\"","\"Do you have any idea how much effort we’ve put into raising you?!\"","\"...\"","Wu Qi fell silent after hearing such words.","At that moment, Yuan entered their home and said, \"I apologize for the intrusion. I wasn’t going to intervene, but seeing how things have progressed, I think it would be for the best if I stepped in.\"","\"You! Are you that so-called cultivator?! We know you’re trying to scam our son, so get lost!\" The mother approached Yuan in an aggressive manner.","\"Mother! Don’t!\"","Yuan silently shook his head before hovering his body off the ground.","\"As you can see, I am a real cultivator.\"","Everyone in the room froze, their eyes staring at Yuan in disbelief.","To further convince them, Yuan used his spiritual energy to grab a nearby chair, placing it behind him and sitting on it.","After a moment of silence, the mother who was standing right before Yuan snapped out of her daze and immediately fell to her knees.","\"Please excuse this lowly mortal for her foolishness. I am willing to accept any punishment—\"","\"Forget it,\" Yuan interrupted.","\"I know you’re worried for your son, but rest assured that I will bring him back safely.\"","\"If Senior Immortal says so, we will believe it.\"","Of course, despite saying that, the mother was still worried. Unfortunately, as mortals, they were powerless before a cultivator, so all they could do was nod their heads and agree.","\"Don’t worry, mother. I trust Senior Brother,\" said Wu Qi as he patted her back.","Once things were settled with Wu Qi’s family, they left his home.","\"Do you know the direction to the First City?\" Yuan asked.","Wu Qi scratched his head for a moment before responding, \"Not exactly, but I know it’s somewhere in that direction.\"","He pointed toward the north.","\"Alright.\"","Without another word, Yuan wrapped his spiritual energy around Wu Qi and Mu Xuelian before flying into the sky and soaring toward the north.","\"Whoa! I am flying! I am really flying!\" Wu Qi exclaimed, his face full of excitement.","\"Oh, by the way, my name is Wu Qi. May I ask for your name, Senior Brother?\" Wu Qi said after realizing they hadn’t had any introductions.","\"My name’s Yuan. She’s Mu Xuelian.\"","\"Can I call you Senior Yuan?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","A few hours later, they arrived at another city.","\"This is the Fourth City, so we’re definitely heading in the right direction,\" said Wu Qi.","\"Alright. Let’s keep going this way, then.\""]},{"number":2188,"title":"Chapter 2188: Chaos’ Auction House","paragraphs":["After arriving at the Fourth City, Yuan continued flying in the same direction without stopping for another full day.","That night, Wu Qi slept while still in the air, as he was a mortal who needed sleep. Though they were flying at great speed, the world felt strangely still when he closed his eyes, granting him a surprisingly peaceful rest.","When Wu Qi opened his eyes again, it was already morning, and he could see another city in the distance.","\"That tall black building in the city... It’s the First City. We’re almost there,\" he said after noticing the pagoda in the distance.","\"Alright.\"","Hearing this, Yuan sped up some more.","A few minutes later, they arrived at the city entrance.","When the guards at the entrance saw Yuan, who was fast approaching in the air, they instantly lowered their heads—both in respect and in an effort to avoid drawing his attention.","\"Is this the First City?\" Yuan asked as he descended before the guards.","\"Correct, Senior Immortal. This humble city is indeed the First City,\" responded one of the guards in a respectful manner.","Although they have seen many cultivators come and go, they rarely see any of them fly to travel, as that was a luxury only the most powerful and influential cultivators could enjoy.","\"I got a few questions, if you don’t mind.\"","\"We’ll do our best to answer Senior Immortal’s questions.\"","\"I’m trying to sell some valuables. Do you know of a place that deals with such things?\"","Without raising their heads, the guards responded, \"For valuable treasures, there are two options.\"","\"If Senior Immortal is in a hurry to sell his treasures, there is the Inferno Marketplace.\"","\"If Senior Immortal isn’t short on time, he can try the Chaos’ Auction House for a higher chance of obtaining more money. The auction house opens once every two weeks, and they plan to open in two days.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before speaking, \"Can one of you show me the way to the auction house?\"","\"It’d be my pleasure.\" One of the guards stepped forward and bowed respectfully.","Their reverence left Yuan feeling uneasy. In the Nine Heavens, where nearly everyone was a cultivator, such displays of deference were rare.","Sometime later, the guard led Yuan to the auction house, which was only fifteen minutes away from the entrance.","\"This is the Chaos’ Auction House. If Senior Immortal has any more questions, this humble servant will be more than willing to answer them.\"","\"No, that’s all. Thank you.\"","\"Then, if you’ll excuse me.\"","The guard gave him one last bow before turning around and walking back the way they came.","\"Let’s go,\" Yuan said as he entered the auction house.","\"Welcome to Chaos’ Auction House, the most reliable and best auction house in the entire region! Are you here to buy or sell?\" A young woman approached Yuan almost immediately after he entered the building.","\"I’m here to sell.\"","\"In that case, please follow me to the seller’s room.\"","Once they were seated inside a medium-sized room, the young woman gestured toward the table and said, \"I will get the treasure examiner right now. In the meantime, you can place everything you plan on selling at our auction house on the table.\"","After saying that, she gave them a slight bow before leaving the room.","Yuan reached inside his spatial ring and grabbed a handful of gold coins without even looking and casually placed them on the table.","Wu Qi, who was sitting next to him, stared at the pile of gold coins with wide eyes and his mouth agape.","Yuan noticed his reaction and asked, \"Is this too much?\"","Wu Qi silently nodded his head.","\"I see.\"","Without another word, Yuan reduced the pile of gold coins by half.","\"What about you?\" Yuan then asked.","He shook his head and said, \"Well... you’re already selling gold coins—many of them, at that. I doubt my single gold coin will catch anyone’s attention. Instead, I’ll sell it at the Inferno Market.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"We can just ask the auction house to sell your gold coin before mine. That way, you’ll definitely be able to sell it for much more. Or, you can sell it together with mine.\"","\"I don’t think the auction house will let us manipulate them like this...\" Wu Qi swallowed nervously.","However, before Yuan could respond, the door opened, and a well-dressed middle-aged man walked inside the room.","\"Sorry for the wait. I am your examiner, Chen Cheng. Let’s see what you have—\"","Chen Cheng’s movements froze when he saw the small pile of gold coins on the table.","\"Are my eyes deceiving me, or are those gold coins?!\" he exclaimed after a moment of silence.","Yuan nodded and confirmed, \"They are indeed gold coins.\"","Hearing this, Chen Cheng swiftly approached the table, nearly tripping on himself in the process.","When he reached the table, he dropped to his knees, his eyes fixed on the gleaming gold coins laid out before him.","\"There are so many! And in such pristine condition?!\" Chen Cheng’s jaw fell open at the sight. In his fifty years as an examiner at the auction house, he had only ever encountered two gold coins—and both had been badly worn and damaged beyond recognition.","Since every gold coin in the Primordial Realm dated back to the Primordial Era, it was only natural that most had long since become worn or damaged.","\"I’ve only ever seen gold coins in such condition within books! To think I would behold so many at once today! I could die this very moment without regret!\" Chen Cheng exclaimed.","However, he suddenly snapped out of it and cleared his throat.","\"Ahem... my apologies for failing to contain my excitement. If you don’t mind, I’ll need to examine these coins and verify their authenticity before we proceed to the next steps,\" he said.","Yuan nodded.","\"Take your time.\"","\"Oh, you missed one.\" Yuan gestured at Wu Qi, who was holding a single gold coin in his grasp."]},{"number":2189,"title":"Chapter 2189: Chaos’ Auction House(2)","paragraphs":["\"You also have one?!\" Chen Cheng exclaimed as he stared at the gold coin in Wu Qi’s grasp.","\"Uh... yes?\" Wu Qi quickly placed the gold coin onto the table.","\"Alright, give me a few minutes to verify them.\"","Chen Cheng retrieved a pair of white gloves and a monocle-like item and carefully inspected each coin once he was prepared, treating each of them as though they were priceless treasures.","Some time later, after setting down the final gold coin, he drew in a deep breath.","\"I have examined them all... and I can confirm each one is genuine,\" he said, his voice still tinged with daze and disbelief.","\"Since you’ve confirmed their authenticity, will the auction house accept them?\" Yuan asked.","Chen Cheng nodded.","\"Yes, we can sell them for you. When would you like to put them up for auction?\"","\"As soon as possible. You open up in two days, right? Can you sell them in two days?\"","\"That’s...\" Chen Cheng’s expression immediately shifted to one of concern upon hearing Yuan’s response.","\"Is there a problem?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","Chen Cheng hesitated for a moment before responding, \"To be honest with you, there are too many gold coins. I highly doubt we’ll be able to sell them at a satisfactory price on such short notice.\"","\"If you want the most profit, I suggest spreading their auctions and selling a single gold coin every few years. If you wish to sell all of them at once... Well, there are very few people in this world who would be able to afford them, so you’ll be losing out on the majority of their value.\"","Yuan shook his head and said in a firm voice, \"I cannot wait a few years. Just sell them all in two days to the highest bidder. You can spread them out, such as selling them in small batches, but I want it all to be sold as soon as possible.\"","He couldn’t care less about losing the majority of the profit; to him, it was only a handful of gold coins—worthless in his eyes.","Of course, to Wu Qi and Chen Cheng, Yuan’s actions seemed outrageously wasteful.","\"Please, Esteemed Guest... It isn’t that I object to selling it your way, but this auction house is under the management of the Chaotic Sect. If they discover how much money I squandered, losing my position would be the least of my worries...\" Chen Cheng said with a weary sigh.","\"In that case...\"","Yuan fell silent to ponder.","After a moment of silence, he said, \"Alright, I won’t sell the gold coins.\"","\"What?! But that’s—!\"","\"Let me finish.\" Yuan interrupted him and retrieved something from his spatial ring.","\"I’ll give you one week to sell this,\" he said as he placed a pebble-sized stone on the table.","\"What is that?\" Chen Cheng asked with a puzzled face.","Wu Qi was also curious about the item Yuan had just taken out.","Before they could ask him how this pebble could replace the gold coins, Yuan revealed the item’s name to them.","\"It’s a Spirit Stone.\"","\"A what?!\" Chen Cheng exclaimed, stumbling back in shock.","Wu Qi only looked more puzzled, as he’d never heard of a Spirit Stone before.","Once Chen Cheng recovered from his shock, he approached the spirit stone on the table and inspected it from afar, not daring to get too close.","\"If this is really a Spirit Stone... It’ll definitely sell more than the gold coins, as it’ll attract not just collectors but cultivators as well!\" he exclaimed.","\"What is this Spirit Stone?\" Wu Qi asked out of curiosity.","\"It contains spiritual energy and is what cultivators require to cultivate,\" Chen Cheng gave a brief explanation.","\"So it’s something like the Spirit Tree? I heard that place also has spiritual energy,\" Wu Qi remarked.","\"No, the Spirit Tree is different.\" Chen Cheng shook his head. \"Anyway, although one week is not a lot of time... I think it’s enough to spread the word far enough.\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"By the way, do you know where the Spirit Tree is located?\"","\"The Spirit Tree...? No, I do not. It’s a heavily guarded secret by the rulers of this world, so only the most powerful and influential cultivators are privy to that information.\"","\"I see. Then, do you think the Spirit Stone will attract someone from the ruling backgrounds?\"","\"Oh, surely. I have no doubt that someone from the Chaotic Sect will show up for it since I will be contacting them later about it. The others are also likely to appear, but I cannot guarantee it.\"","\"Alright. As for the gold coin... can you still sell one of them?\"","\"Of course. Do you still want to sell the gold coin in two days, or would you like to sell it alongside the Spirit Stone?\" Chen Cheng asked.","\"Two days,\" he said.","\"I understand. Then would you like the auction house to hold the Spirit Stone for you?\"","\"Go ahead.\" Yuan nodded.","\"Thank you for your trust. We will not disappoint you. I’ll take the Spirit Stone to our vault now. Be right back.\"","Chen Cheng left the room shortly after with the Spirit Stone and a single gold coin.","\"Why didn’t you wait a little longer to sell the gold coin?\" Wu Qi suddenly asked.","\"I want to bring you back to your home before the auction,\" Yuan said.","\"Eh? I don’t mind staying here a little longer,\" he said.","However, Yuan shook his head and said, \"It’s for your safety. I have a feeling that things might get chaotic at the auction for the Spirit Stone.\"","\"If you say so...\" Wu Qi nodded.","Chen Cheng returned to the room a few minutes later and said, \"I have secured your treasures. You can come back on the day of the auction if you have nothing else for me now.\"","\"Then we’ll be back in two days,\" Yuan said.","\"Here is a token.\"","Chen Cheng continued after handing them three metal tokens, \"Show this to our workers when you show up. It means you are our esteemed guests.\"","Yuan accepted the token before handing one to Wu Qi and Mu Xuelian.","\"See you in two days.\""]},{"number":2190,"title":"Chapter 2190: Auction for a Single Gold Coin","paragraphs":["\"See you in two days.\"","However, just as Yuan and his group approached the exit, Yuan came to a sudden halt.","\"Did you forget something?\" Chen Cheng asked.","\"Actually, I have an odd request,\" Yuan faced him and continued, \"Can I borrow some money?\"","\"Excuse me?\" Chen Cheng’s eyes widened with disbelief, not daring to believe his ears.","How could someone with so many gold coins and even a spirit stone ask for money? It made zero sense.","Seeing Chen Cheng’s confused expression, Yuan explained, \"You see, we don’t have any currencies. That’s why we’re trying to sell the gold coin and spirit stone as soon as possible. Don’t worry, I’ll return twice the amount you lend me.\"","\"H-How much do you want?\" Chen Cheng asked in a dazed voice.","\"Just enough to rent a few rooms and eat some food for the next two days.\"","Chen Cheng reached into his pocket and retrieved a large leather bag and said, \"Here’s ten large chaos coins and a hundred small chaos coins. You can live luxuriously for an entire month, much less two days.\"","\"Thanks.\" Yuan accepted the money and left the auction house shortly after.","Once they were outside, Yuan asked Wu Qi, \"How much did he give us? I’m not familiar with its value.\"","Wu Qi then explained, \"Ordinary people like my parents earn about two hundred small coins a month. As for your large coin... a single one is worth ten thousand small coins, so you essentially have 100,000 small coins.\"","\"I see.\"","\"In that case, let’s go eat.\"","Wu Qi nodded, \"I’m glad you said that because I am starving.\"","They proceeded to wander the city until they found a restaurant that seemed appealing enough to enter.","Sometime later, after they finished their meal, Yuan’s group went to rent three rooms in a hotel.","\"Senior, what are you going to do for the next two days?\" Wu Qi asked him.","\"I’m going to cultivate,\" he said.","\"In that case, I’ll take a look around the city. I doubt I will ever come back here, after all.\"","\"Here, take this.\"","Yuan handed him a single large coin.","\"This is...?\" Wu Qu stared at it with a dumbfounded face.","\"You don’t have any money, right?\"","\"I can’t take this...\"","\"Just take it. Or I’ll just throw it away.\"","Yuan flicked the coin into the air, forcing Wu Qi to catch it.","\"Thank you...\" Wu Qi muttered as he stared at the coin in his grasp.","\"Then I’ll leave now. Have fun.\" Yuan said before entering his room to cultivate.","Since the Primordial Realm was full of Chaotic Essence, he could improve his Chaotic Dragon Core again.","Meanwhile, Wu Qi wandered through the city. Though the Primordial Realm was a land steeped in danger and lawlessness, its cities remained remarkably safe due to an iron rule.","Compared to the Nine Heavens—no, even compared to Earth—the population of the Primordial Realm was laughably small. Since most of its dwellers were mortals, strict laws forbade cultivators from fighting in or near the cities, lest humanity itself edge toward extinction.","Those who violate this law would be branded as criminals and hunted by all four ruling backgrounds.","However, the moment one stepped beyond the safe zone, everything became fair game—whether mortal or Immortal. Though some might call this contradictory, such was simply the way their society functioned.","Two days passed in a flash, and in that time, word of a gold coin being sold at the Chaos Auction House spread to every corner of the city, stirring the interest of many collectors. Unfortunately, the news went no further; with spiritual energy scarce in the Primordial Realm, communication jade slips were exceedingly rare and reserved only for true emergencies.","However, while the gold coin had stirred the interest of mortal collectors, the announcement of a spirit stone to be auctioned in a week spread like wildfire, reaching even the ears of cultivators in distant regions.","\"What? A spirit stone in the Primordial Realm? How is that possible?\" A cultivator questioned the legitimacy of this news.","\"The Chaos’ Auction House announced it, so it must be true. I doubt they’d do something as foolish as lying about this.\"","\"Even if it’s a spirit stone, I don’t get the hype. It doesn’t last forever, and I doubt it’ll have much effect on cultivators beyond a certain level.\"","\"You really don’t get it, huh? How do you think mortals become cultivators in a world that lacks spiritual energy?\"","\"You don’t mean...\"","\"That’s right. The only way for a mortal to become a cultivator is either to go to the Spirit Tree or a Spiritual Rift, as these are the only ways for us to acquire spiritual energy. However, neither of these options is viable for most people. Although a single spirit stone may not benefit cultivators like us, it’s a godly treasure for ordinary mortals. I bet a lot of powerhouses will fight for it to help their children become cultivators.\"","To embark on the path of cultivation, one must first absorb spiritual energy. Yet in the Primordial Realm, there were only two sources: the Spirit Tree, guarded within the Asura Clan’s territory, and the rare Spiritual Rifts—unpredictable anomalies that could never be relied upon.","Because of this, spirit stones became treasures of immense value. In fact, every spirit stone brought to the Primordial Realm in the past had been used in precisely this way. Unfortunately, spirit stones have long since become extinct, so the number of people becoming cultivators has drastically decreased.","On the day of the auction for the gold coin, Yuan made his way to the auction house with Wu Qi and Mu Xuelian.","\"Wow, there are so many people here,\" Wu Qi remarked as they arrived at the auction house. The street was so crowded it became a sea of bodies, making it impossible to move any closer.","\"Are they all here for the gold coin? Or are they waiting for the spirit stone? Either way... I like this!\" he chuckled."]},{"number":2191,"title":"Chapter 2191: Auction for a Single Gold Coin(2)","paragraphs":["It took a couple of hours, but Yuan’s group eventually made it to the entrance of the auction house.","\"I’m sorry, but the seats are already fully occupied. If you’re here to bid for the gold coin, you’ll have to do so out here,\" said the worker at the entrance.","Yuan didn’t say anything and retrieved the token he got from Chen Cheng, showing it to him.","The worker’s eyes widened at the sight of the token, and he quickly said, \"Please excuse me for not recognizing you, esteemed guests! We have reserved seats for you all in room three!\"","He then stepped aside to let Yuan’s group into the building.","\"Hey! How come they get to go inside but we’re not?!\"","Those who weren’t allowed inside began complaining outside. However, Yuan’s group simply ignored them and quickly disappeared inside.","A few minutes later, they arrived at their room and went inside. Their room was located above the ground floor, allowing them not only a perfect view of the stage but also of other guests.","Yuan and the others took a seat by the window and began waiting for the auction to begin.","\"Most of these guests are mortals with a few cultivators sprinkled within,\" Yuan remarked as he gazed at the crowd.","\"I’m not surprised. Only collectors would be interested in something like a gold coin since it doesn’t have any practical use,\" said Wu Qi.","Minutes later, they heard a knock on the door.","\"Esteemed guests, it’s me, Chen Cheng. May I bother you for a moment?\"","\"You can enter.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Chen Cheng opened the door and bowed to them, \"I came here immediately after hearing of your arrival. I hope this room is to your liking. If not, we can change it.\"","\"Our room is just fine. Do you need something from us?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s not me. The Chaotic Sect wants to have an audience with you,\" said Chen Cheng. \"After I spread news of the spirit stone and notified the Chaotic Sect, I was contacted by them and was told they wanted to speak with you.\"","\"Did they say what they wanted to speak to me about?\"","Chen Cheng shook his head.","\"No, I was not told the details.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"Tell them I’ll speak with them after the auction—for the spirit stone.\"","\"Is it not possible to speak to them before? They sounded a bit impatient...\"","\"So what? It’s just five days. They can wait,\" Yuan calmly replied, leaving Chen Cheng speechless.","\"I understand. I’ll let them know. If you need any service or have any questions, there will be a servant available right outside your room. Now, if you’ll excuse me.\" Chen Cheng bowed to him before leaving the room.","\"Why are you making the Chaotic Sect wait? They’re one of the most powerful and influential backgrounds in this world...\" Wu Qi stared at him with a dazed and confused face.","\"They probably want to see if they can buy the spirit stone directly from me. Even if that’s not the case, I’m just trying to send a message.\"","\"A message?\" Wu Qi became even more puzzled.","Yuan smiled but did not elaborate.","Seeing how Yuan didn’t want to explain, Wu Qi didn’t press further and returned to looking at the platform below.","About an hour later, Chen Cheng walked onto the platform and stood before the crowd with a satisfied smile on his face. The Chaos’ Auction House had a thousand seats, but there were usually no more than a hundred or so guests. However, not a single seat was empty today.","\"Welcome to the Chaos’ Auction House, fellow guests and esteemed guests. I am Chen Cheng, an appraiser for the auction house. Normally, the auction is done by someone else, but due to circumstances, I will be hosting it today. Therefore, allow me to apologize in advance for my lack of experience and any mistakes I may make during the auction.\"","\"Before we begin, allow me to explain some of our rules...\"","Chen Cheng proceeded to reveal the typical auction rules.","\"You are not allowed to threaten other guests with your background. Once you call out a bid, you are not able to take it back—\"","A few minutes later.","\"Now, let us begin the auction! For our first treasure, we have an excellent sword crafted by the renowned blacksmith Xi Yang from the...\"","Yuan watched the auction with interest at first, but his interest disappeared after several items when he realized that everything being auctioned was meant for mortals.","’What was I expecting from the Primordial Realm, a world where there is no natural spiritual energy?’ Yuan shook his head inwardly.","A world without natural spiritual energy didn’t just make cultivation difficult. It also made crafting treasures almost impossible, so most of the weapons in this world were ordinary weapons without any special capabilities.","After a dozen items were sold, it was finally time for the gold coin to be auctioned.","\"Before we begin selling the last item for the day, I would like to thank everyone here for their participation and appearance,\" said Chen Cheng as another worker pushed a cart onto the stage.","Atop the cart rested a single gold coin, displayed upon a luxurious cloth and treated as though it were a priceless treasure.","\"And now, the main item of today’s auction—a gold coin untouched by time! Not only is it perfectly pristine, but it bears not a single mark of damage!\" Chen Cheng proclaimed as he gestured at the cart.","\"Oooh! It really is a pristine gold coin!\" many guests exclaimed, leaning forward in their seats to catch a clearer glimpse.","Naturally, the auction house had cleaned up the gold coin before the auction, but even if they hadn’t done such a thing, the coin was like new.","After a brief pause, Chen Cheng’s voice rang out once more, \"We will now begin the auction for this gold coin! The starting bid—five hundred thousand small Chaos Coins!\""]},{"number":2192,"title":"Chapter 2192: Auction for a Single Gold Coin(3)","paragraphs":["\"Five hundred thousand? For a single coin?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at the absurd starting price. Now he understood why Chen Cheng gave him so much money without hesitation.","\"550,000!\"","Someone immediately increased the bid.","\"560,000!\"","\"590,000!\"","\"690,000!\"","The guests continued bidding one after another, and in the blink of an eye, raised the bid to over a million small Chaos Coins.","\"A million...?\" Wu Qi’s eyes widened, his jaw falling open as he stared at the chaotic scene. For someone from an ordinary family like him, such a sum was nothing short of astronomical. It was something he could only dream of.","However, the auction was just getting started.","\"1,200,000!\"","\"1,500,000!\"","\"3,000,000!\"","In the blink of an eye, someone doubled the highest bid, causing heads to turn.","\"Isn’t that the Golden King, who is a hardcore collector for anything gold?\"","\"I knew he’d show up for the gold coin.\"","\"I heard that almost everything in his house is gold—including the house itself.\"","The other guests started chatting with each other. Although a thousand guests were present, most of them had no plans to bid for the gold coin, as it was obviously beyond their capabilities.","However, the bidders inside the auction house were not the only ones competing. Many guests who had been unable to enter due to limited space were placing their bids from outside.","The bidding for the gold coin continued fiercely for several more minutes before it slowed down, and the number of bidders drastically decreased.","Sometime later, Chen Cheng announced the winner.","\"S-Sold to the Golden King for 70 million small Chaos Coins!\"","Sure enough, the Golden King won the bid.","\"Holy shit... 70 million?! I knew gold coins were expensive, but I didn’t think it would be worth this much!\"","In the past, most gold coins had sold for only a few million at best, with the highest ever recorded at seven million. But those had all been damaged coins. A flawless coin like the one Yuan offered had never been seen before.","\"This marks the end of today’s auction. Once again, I would like to thank everyone who has come today for your participation.\" Chen Cheng bowed to the crowd.","\"If you have purchased an item, please head to the collection room to complete the transaction.\"","\"One last announcement before I take my leave... If you haven’t heard already, the Chaos Auction House will be offering a Spirit Stone for sale in five days. However, due to its immense value and high profile, strict requirements will be enforced for participation. I ask for your understanding,\" he said before turning around and disappearing from the stage.","\"Let’s collect our money, shall we?\" Yuan turned to face Wu Qi with a smile.","\"Okay...\" Wu Qi nodded in a dazed manner.","After leaving the room, they were led to the collection room by the servant who had been waiting outside.","There were two collection rooms in the auction house. One was for the buyers and the other for sellers.","\"You can collect your money here once the buyer completes the transaction,\" said the servant.","Sometime later, Chen Cheng showed up in their room with a large chest.","\"After deducting our auction house’s fifteen percent fee, your profit from the sale of the gold coin amounts to 59,500,000 small Chaos Coins. We’ve already converted them into large Chaos Coins for your convenience—there are 5,950 in total,\" Chen Cheng explained as he opened the box and revealed a mountain of coins in it.","\"Do you have any questions for me?\"","Yuan retrieved thirty large Chaos Coins from the box and handed them to him.","\"This is more than I lend you...\" Chen Cheng said with a surprised face.","\"Consider it a bonus,\" Yuan said with a smile.","\"Thank you!\" Chen Cheng bowed deeply.","Yuan turned to Wu Qi and asked, \"You ready to return home?\"","\"Yes!\" he nodded.","\"I’ll carry the money for you,\" Yuan said as he stored the box inside his spatial ring.","\"?!?!\"","Both Wu Qi and Chen Cheng stared at him with a bewildered look on their faces, as they had never seen a spatial ring before.","\"W-Where did it go?!\" Wu Qi asked.","Yuan showed him the ring and said, \"In here.\"","\"I have never seen anything like that before!\" he remarked.","\"That function... don’t tell me it’s a Spatial Ring...?\" Chen Cheng asked after swallowing nervously.","Yuan calmly nodded.","\"Heavens...\" Chen Cheng was speechless.","Spatial Rings were unimaginably rare—so rare that fewer than ten existed in the entire Primordial Realm, each belonging only to the realm’s most powerful figures.","’Not only does he have many pristine gold coins and a spirit stone, but he also has a Spatial Ring?! Just who in the world is this guy?!’ Chen Cheng cried inwardly.","\"If there’s nothing else, we’ll be taking our leave now,\" said Yuan.","\"O-Oh, okay. I’ll see you in five days for the spirit stone’s auction.\" Chen Cheng nodded.","Yuan and his group started walking toward the door, but before they could reach it, it swung open, and two figures stepped into the room.","When Chen Cheng saw these two figures, his face immediately twisted with surprise.","\"This humble servant greets the Chaos Elders!\"","\"Chaos Elders?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow as he looked at the man and woman, both dressed in black, standing by the entrance.","They also stared back, and after a moment of silence, the man opened his mouth to speak, \"Are you the one with the Spirit Stone?\"","\"Who’s asking?\" Yuan responded.","\"We’re from the Chaotic Sect,\" replied the woman.","\"I see. And what do you want?\"","\"We’re here to talk.\"","\"Talk? I’m pretty sure I already said to wait until after the auction for the spirit stone,\" Yuan said.","The woman frowned and said, \"How impudent. The Chaotic Sect went out of its way to approach you, and you’re telling us to wait? Do you really think you’re above us because you have a spirit stone?\""]},{"number":2193,"title":"Chapter 2193: Wu Qi’s Gift","paragraphs":["The atmosphere in the room instantly became heavy with the woman’s words.","However, Yuan remained unaffected and calmly responded, \"Is the Chaotic Sect so great that waiting five days is considered offensive?\"","The woman’s face flushed red as she spoke, \"Are you mocking our Chaotic Sect?!\"","Yuan casually shrugged, \"If you find everything that comes out of my mouth offensive, then let’s just stop here. I have other things to do.\"","Without waiting for a response, Yuan walked around them and toward the exit.","\"Where the hell do you think you’re going?! We’re still talking!\"","\"We can talk in five days, or we can not talk at all. The choice is up to you,\" Yuan replied without stopping his legs.","\"If you dare take a step through that door, you will regret it for the rest of your life,\" said the woman in a grim tone.","Yuan halted his steps and turned his head to look at her with slightly narrowed eyes.","\"Are you threatening me? In that case, you can forget it. I won’t talk to the Chaotic Sect anymore.\"","\"You impudent bastard! Have you forgotten where you are?! Not only are you in the Chaotic Sect’s territory, but you are also selling your Spirit Stone at our auction house!\"","\"So what you’re saying is, I should sell the Spirit Stone elsewhere? Am I hearing that correctly?\"","\"I’m going to kill you!\" The woman shouted as her body surged with killing intent.","\"Stop.\" The man finally stepped in and spoke, \"Let’s all calm down a bit.\"","However, Yuan said, \"Sorry, but you’ve stepped in a little too late. I have already made up my mind that I won’t speak with the Chaotic Sect. If you continue to pester me, I’ll even take back the spirit stone that will be auctioned in five days.\"","\"That... would not be possible,\" said the man. \"While I can look past the issue of not talking, I cannot let you take back the spirit stone, especially after all the advertisements we’ve done for it. If you take back the spirit stone and halt the auction, it’d cause tremendous damage to the Chaotic Sect’s reputation, and we’d have to stop you at all costs.\"","\"If you don’t want such a thing to happen, then let’s end our conversation here.\"","The very next moment, Yuan left the room without any hesitation.","\"Are we really going to let him go after all that?\" The woman asked the man.","After a moment of silence, he spoke, \"There are too many people here now. Let’s lay low until the auction is finished. We’ll take care of him afterward.\"","\"Alright.\"","The man turned to look at Chen Cheng and said, \"Unless you have a death wish, you will act like you heard and saw nothing today.\"","Chen Cheng was so terrified that he didn’t even dare to speak and silently nodded his head.","Meanwhile, after leaving the auction house, Yuan immediately left the city to bring Wu Qi back to his family.","\"Senior... I don’t mean to be nosy, but why did you offend the Chaotic Sect? Nothing good will come out of it.\"","\"Why? I didn’t like their attitude.\"","\"That’s it?\" Wu Qi was dumbfounded.","\"Yes, that’s it.\"","\"Aren’t you afraid that they might hunt you later?\"","\"It’ll be fine. Although this means that I won’t be able to get information on the Spirit Tree from the Chaotic Sect, there are other places I can go, such as the Zhao Family and the Inferno Alchemists.\"","\"I just hope that they won’t hunt me down for being with you...\" Wu Qi sighed.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Don’t worry, they didn’t even look at you, as all of their attention was on me.\"","Sometime later, they returned to the Seventh City.","Yuan brought Wu Qi straight to his home, where his parents were anxiously waiting.","\"Mother! Father! I am back!\" Wu Qi said as he entered the building.","\"Oh! You’re really back!\" His mother cried after seeing him.","\"Is there really a need to cry? I told you that I would be back.\"","Once they calmed down, Yuan retrieved the box of money from his spatial ring and placed it on the floor.","\"Here’s your money,\" he said.","Wu Qi then asked, \"We’re not going to split it?\"","\"No, it’s all yours. After all, it came from selling your gold coin.\"","\"But you gave it to me...\" Wu Qi said in a dumbfounded voice.","Even if Yuan said he wanted 90 percent of the money, he wouldn’t have refused. Hell, even one percent of the wealth from selling the gold coin would allow his family to live comfortably for the rest of their lives.","Yuan smiled and said, \"If I really need money, I can just pawn off a few gold coins. Moreover, I will have plenty from selling the spirit stone in a few days.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Wu Qi sighed, \"I don’t even know how to begin to thank you for changing my—our lives.\"","\"You don’t have to thank me.\"","\"Even if you say that... Oh! I know! Please wait here for a minute!\"","Wu Qi suddenly turned around and ran away, quickly disappearing from their view.","He returned moments later with something in his grasp.","\"I bought this a few years ago from a wandering merchant. Unfortunately, I don’t know if it has any uses or if it’s even valuable at all since I got it because it looked neat.\"","Resting on Wu Qi’s palm was a crystal the size of a finger. At first glance, it looked pitch-black, but upon closer inspection, faint black liquid seemed to swirl within.","Yuan accepted it casually, but the moment he examined it more closely, his eyes widened in surprise.","’There’s an immense amount of Chaotic Essence within this crystal!’","He wasn’t sure what it was, but he was certain that if he absorbed it, his second cultivation would skyrocket several realms without any issues.","Yingzi emerged from his shadow to take a look since it also piqued her curiosity.","\"You know what this is?\" he asked.","She shook her head and said, \"No... but merely looking at it sends chills down my spine.\""]},{"number":2194,"title":"Chapter 2194: Auction for the Spirit Stone","paragraphs":["\"Thanks, Wu Qi, for this gift,\" Yuan said to him after stowing away the crystal.","\"Do you think we can meet again in the future?\" Wu Qi asked.","\"Honestly, I don’t know, since I won’t be staying in the Primordial Realm for long.\"","\"What?\" Wu Qi raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","Yuan smiled and said, \"I am actually not from this world, but from the Nine Heavens, which exists beyond this world.\"","Wu Qi’s jaw dropped, too speechless to even utter a sound. However, everything about Yuan made sense after learning of this revelation.","’No wonder he has so many gold coins and treasures that are insanely rare in this world! To think he had come from the outside world!’","After a moment of silence, Wu Qi asked, \"Can I ask why you decided to come to our world?\"","\"I have some business with the Asura Clan, that’s all.\"","Wu Qi swallowed nervously. Though he still had many questions, he decided not to ask them.","\"In that case, good luck...\"","Yuan nodded, \"Goodbye.\"","Yuan left the city shortly after and immediately made his way back to the First City.","As he traveled, he pondered whether he should consume the black crystal he got from Wu Qi.","’The amount of Chaotic Essence it contains is unlike anything I have ever seen. If I consumed it, I could probably create at least two more Chaotic Hearts...’","However, he also understood that it was unwise to consume something so mysteriously powerful. Though he may have a god-like body, it was not omnipotent.","Moreover, the vast amount of Chaotic Essence within the crystal could take him several years just to absorb, so he also needed a place and time to do it properly.","A day later, Yuan returned to the First City.","He’d only been gone for a little over two days, but the number of visitors had grown several times since then, and most of them were cultivators.","Among the cultivators, nearly half wore matching attire, divided into three distinct groups. One faction was clad in black robes, another in red and gold, and the last in green. Obviously, these three groups belonged to the Chaotic Sect, Inferno Alchemists, and the Zhao Family—the three ruling factions in the Primordial Realm.","However, the Asura Clan was nowhere to be seen.","As Yuan and Mu Xuelian made their way through the crowded streets, nearly every gaze was drawn to them. Mu Xuelian, a peerless beauty with cultivation at the peak of the God Ascension realm, commanded admiration, while Yuan radiated an unfathomable aura—even as he suppressed it.","\"Who’s that beauty? With her cultivation and appearance, there’s no way I haven’t heard of her.\"","\"Judging by her appearance, she doesn’t seem to be with any of the top three factions. Maybe she’s from a hidden family?\"","\"Look at that handsome man next to her. Although his cultivation isn’t too impressive, I can feel something unfathomably profound coming from his very presence.\"","\"He’s suppressing it, but he clearly has a lot of spiritual energy in his body!\"","Despite their interest, nobody tried to approach them. In the Primordial Realm, cultivators preferred to mind their own business, as those who stand out tend to become targeted.","Of course, that didn’t apply to everyone, and eventually, someone approached Yuan and Mu Xuelian.","\"Excuse me, may I have a moment of your time?\" A well-dressed middle-aged man approached them and said.","\"How can I help you?\" Yuan responded as he glanced at the man’s green robes.","\"I am a recruiter from the Zhao Family. I was wondering if I could treat you two to some tea.\"","\"Maybe another time. We’re busy now,\" Yuan calmly replied.","\"I understand. If you ever have the time, please visit the Zhao Family in the Zhao Province.\" The man nodded and then offered him a token.","Yuan accepted the token and continued walking.","’At least they’re not as arrogant as those two from the Chaotic Sect,’ Yuan smiled inwardly as he made his way to the auction house.","They arrived at their destination shortly after, and unsurprisingly, it was filled to the brim with people, far more than before. Of course, most of the people there belonged to one of the three top factions.","When Yuan eventually reached the entrance, he was immediately greeted by the same worker he had met the previous week.","\"Welcome back, esteemed guests. Allow me to escort you to your room.\"","Yuan followed the worker to the same room from last time.","\"Please, make yourself comfortable while I let Appraiser Cheng know of your arrival.\"","The worker left, and several minutes later, Chen Cheng knocked on the door.","\"Esteemed guest, it’s me, Chen Cheng.\"","\"Enter.\"","Chen Cheng entered the room at his command.","\"Welcome back, esteemed guest. I hope—\"","\"Did those two idiots make things difficult for you after I left?\" Yuan suddenly asked, catching him off guard.","\"I-Idiots...?\" Chen Cheng swallowed nervously as he quickly closed the door behind him.","\"Sorry about how things went, but I didn’t appreciate their attitude.\"","\"No... there’s no need for you to apologize...\" Chen Cheng recalled the Chaos Elders’ plans for Yuan after the auction and couldn’t help but feel bad for him.","\"I guess something did happen after I left,\" Yuan suddenly said, startling Chen Cheng.","\"W-What do you mean? Nothing happened after you left! Although the Elders were upset, they left without saying anything!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at Chen Cheng and sighed, \"You’re not very good at lying.\"","\"T-That’s—!\" Chen Cheng was speechless.","\"So, what did they say? Are they going to kill me after the auction or something along those lines?\"","\"!!!\"","Seeing Chen Cheng tremble, Yuan calmly chuckled, \"I see. So that’s their plan.\"","\"How...\" Chen Cheng suddenly spoke. \"How can you be so calm? You’re going to be hunted by the Chaotic Sect, you know! Unless you have connections with the Asura Clan, you will never be safe in this world ever again! If you had agreed to talk with them, none of this would’ve happened!\""]},{"number":2195,"title":"Chapter 2195: Auction for the Spirit Stone(2)","paragraphs":["Yuan smiled at Chen Cheng’s words and said, \"I appreciate your concern, but the Chaotic Sect is nothing in my eyes.\"","\"Nothing... in your eyes?\" Chen Cheng swallowed nervously. In his mind, only someone from the Asura Clan would dare speak with such arrogance.","’Is he actually from the Asura Clan? But then why would he need information on the Spirit Tree? No, let’s stop thinking about this. It’s beyond me.’","After a moment of hesitation, Chen Cheng said, \"The Chaos Elders intend to take care of you after the auction. Please be careful.\"","He gave a swift bow to Yuan before walking toward the exit.","\"Thanks for the information,\" Yuan said as Chen Cheng left the room.","Sometime later, Chen Cheng appeared on the stage to begin the auction.","\"Welcome or welcome back, esteemed guests, to the Chaos’ Auction House. I am Chen Cheng, an appraiser, and just like last week’s auction, I was tasked with today’s auction.\"","He proceeded to give the same speech as last week, going through the rules and whatnot.","\"Now, without further ado, let us begin this week’s auction.\"","\"For the first item, we have a rare Divine-grade sword. Its name is Bloody Enlightenment, and it was once wielded by the Mad Bloodhound.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow when he saw the item being auctioned.","\"They’re selling a Divine-grade sword for the first time? I guess they decided to bring out all of the good stuff for the guests today,\" he remarked.","Since most of the guests at the auction were cultivators, there was no sense in offering items meant for mortals. Besides, with the Spirit Stone so highly anticipated, everyone present was guaranteed to have deep pockets.","\"A hundred million!\"","\"A hundred fifty million!\"","In the blink of an eye, the item was sold for 210 million small Chaos Coins. Though spiritual treasures required spiritual energy to unleash their full potential, they remained incomparably more durable than ordinary weapons, granting their wielder a tremendous advantage over those without one. For this reason, they were still highly sought after and expensive.","Of course, they also served as symbols of status and power.","The next several items were also spiritual treasures, and each was better than the last.","Sometime later, it was finally time for the spirit stone to be auctioned.","\"And now, the moment you’ve all been waiting for—\"","With a flourish, Chen Cheng pulled away the cloth covering the display case, revealing the spirit stone within. Though it appeared far less impressive than the treasures auctioned before it, the instant it was unveiled, every guest’s eyes lit up with awe and excitement.","\"It’s really a spirit stone! We haven’t seen one of those since they were all used up long ago!\"","\"If I had that spirit stone, my son would be able to cultivate! I must get my hands on it even if I have to go into debt!\"","Chen Cheng went on, \"Before we begin the bidding, allow me to introduce today’s item. As you all surely know, a spirit stone is a cultivation resource brimming with spiritual energy. While such stones are plentiful in the outside world, within the Primordial Realm, one has not been seen for millions of years since they’ve all been used.\"","\"A spirit stone never decays nor loses its potency, so there is no need to rush in using it.\"","\"Now then, the auction will begin at two hundred million—\"","\"One billion!\"","Someone swiftly bid for the spirit stone before Chen Cheng could even finish, which started a chain reaction.","\"One billion and a hundred million!\"","\"One billion and two hundred million!\"","In the blink of an eye, the bidding for the spirit stone soared to an astounding one billion, five hundred million.","\"Heavens... I knew it was going to be a fierce competition, but to think it’d reach a billion at the very start...\"","\"The Chaotic Sect is especially fierce today.\"","\"Who do you think will win in the end?\"","\"Surely, it must be the Inferno Alchemists, right? They’re the wealthiest faction in the world.\"","\"But they have the most access to the Spirit Tree, so they’re not really starved for spiritual energy.\"","\"So it’s a fight between the Chaotic Sect and the Zhao Family, huh?\"","\"The Zhao Family will likely win the auction since they have more money than the Chaotic Sect.\"","Most had expected the Zhao Family to claim victory, yet by the end, all were left speechless when the Chaotic Sect secured the spirit stone with a bid of eleven billion.","\"Eleven billion? That’s insane! Do they even have that much money?\"","Unbeknownst to the crowd, the Chaotic Sect would not have hesitated to pay even more—for they knew they would soon reclaim their wealth regardless.","\"And with that, today’s auction comes to an end. We look forward to seeing you all at the next—\" Chen Cheng began.","\"Wait! Who is the owner of the spirit stone? I would like to speak with them!\" Someone from the crowd suddenly interrupted.","\"Me too! I would also like to speak to the seller!\"","The place quickly filled with people wanting to meet Yuan.","\"I-I’m sorry, but the seller wishes their identity to remain a secret—\"","But before he could finish, the doors to the auction hall burst open, and a figure strode inside, declaring, \"I am the owner of that spirit stone.\"","\"What?\"","Everyone in the room turned their heads to look at Yuan, who’d just entered the room.","\"Who is that?\"","\"I don’t recognize him, either.\"","Chen Cheng stared at Yuan with wide eyes.","\"Who are you? And can you prove that you are the seller?\" someone suddenly asked.","Yuan calmly nodded.","\"Of course.\"","He proceeded to reach inside his pocket and retrieved another spirit stone.","\"Heavens! He has another spirit stone!\"","While the crowd erupted with excitement at the appearance of a second spirit stone, the auction’s winners wore twisted expressions—ugly, as though they had just swallowed a live fly.","They turned to glare at Chen Cheng, who noticed it and quickly shook his head, as if trying to say he didn’t know anything about a second spirit stone."]},{"number":2196,"title":"Chapter 2196: Auction for the Spirit Stone(3)","paragraphs":["\"A second spirit stone! He actually has a second spirit stone!\"","\"Do you intend on selling that spirit stone as well?!\"","Yuan responded to the inquiry, \"Yes, I do intend on selling the spirit stone, but I don’t want money for it.\"","\"What do you want?\" someone asked.","\"I’ll give this spirit stone to whoever can provide me with the location of the Spirit Tree.\"","\"What...?\"","The room fell into instant silence, the guests glancing at one another with uncertain, wary looks.","Although the spirit stone was an attractive offer, it wasn’t something worth offending the Asura Clan for.","Seeing the deafening silence, Yuan reached into his pocket and retrieved a third spirit stone, causing everyone to widen their eyes again.","\"He’s pulled out another spirit stone!\"","\"Heavens! How many of those does he actually have?!\"","While some started considering telling Yuan about the Spirit Tree, others wondered if he would pull out more spirit stones if they waited a little longer.","\"If you don’t mind me asking, why are you searching for the Spirit Tree?\" Someone suddenly asked.","Yuan turned to look at the individual, a middle-aged man wearing green robes, who was the same person bidding against the Chaotic Sect for the spirit stone at the very end.","The man continued, \"Even if you know its location, you cannot enter it without the Asura Clan’s permission.\"","\"I want to go there exactly because I have some business with the Asura Clan.\"","\"...\"","The room fell silent again.","When no one responded, Yuan spoke up. \"Perhaps some of you prefer not to speak in public, so I’ll end it here. My offer will remain in effect until I am informed of the information I need to know. You can find me in room 302 at the Black Inn, four blocks from here.\"","Having said that, Yuan turned around and disappeared, leaving everyone speechless.","The other guests began leaving shortly after.","Meanwhile, Yuan went to collect his earnings for the spirit stone.","\"Your earnings for the spirit stone are nine billion, three hundred and fifty million small Chaos Coins after deduction from our auction house’s 15 percent fee. However, due to the massive amount, we regret to inform you that it’ll take some time for the money to be transferred,\" said Chen Cheng.","\"And how long will that take?\" Yuan asked.","\"We should have the money ready by next week,\" he said.","Yuan smiled and asked, \"You sure the Chaotic Sect isn’t trying to screw me over?\"","\"I... have no comments...\" Chen Cheng shook his head.","\"Very well. Since I have some time to spare, I’ll wait. However, if I don’t have my money by then, I’ll personally visit the Chaotic Sect, and there won’t be any conversations, if you know what I mean.\"","\"T-That’s...\" Chen Cheng opened his mouth but didn’t know how to respond.","Yuan continued, \"Don’t worry, I wasn’t talking to you, but the sneaky rat in this room.\"","\"?!?!\"","Chen Cheng’s eyes widened at his words.","In the next moment, the hidden presence unveiled itself, revealing none other than the male Chaos Elder from the other day.","\"That’s quite the bold threat, even though it’s nothing but an empty one.\"","\"If you think it’s an empty threat, you can go ahead and test me. Then, I’ll be back in a week.\"","Yuan turned and left. After departing the auction house, he returned to his hotel room to wait for someone to accept his offer—and it didn’t take long.","At the sound of a knock, Yuan opened the door to find a figure cloaked in grey, their appearance concealed from head to toe.","\"Is the offer still available?\" asked the man in a rough tone.","\"Sure is. Want to talk inside?\"","However, the man shook his head and said, \"There are too many people here. Let’s talk somewhere more private.\"","\"Sure. Lead the way.\"","\"Want me to come with you?\" Mu Xuelian asked him from the other room through voice transmission.","\"No, you can stay here.\"","And so, Yuan followed the man out of the hotel. Before long, they had left the city behind entirely, traveling until even the distant outline of its walls was lost from sight.","\"Surely, this is far enough,\" Yuan said.","The man halted his movements and turned toward Yuan, who wore a calm expression despite the sketchy situation.","\"You’re a little too calm. Are you not worried that I might rob you?\" asked the man.","\"Would I have followed you all the way out here if I were worried?\" Yuan responded.","\"Fair enough.\"","The cloaked figure pulled back his hood, revealing himself as the very man who had questioned Yuan at the auction house about his interest in the Spirit Tree’s location.","\"I don’t mind telling you the location of the Spirit Tree, but I must ask, what business do you have with the Asura Clan?\"","\"Just some personal business.\"","The man narrowed his eyes and fell silent to ponder.","\"Are you... planning to fight the Asura Clan?\" he finally asked.","Yuan raised an eyebrow. \"And what makes you think that?\"","\"You’re wealthy enough to possess three spirit stones, so you’re clearly from a powerful background. If I had to guess, you belong to one of the factions long denied access to the Spirit Tree... and now you seek revenge against the Asura Clan.\"","Yuan was amazed at the misunderstanding, but he didn’t deny it and played along to see where they would go.","\"Are you now going to say that you won’t tell me the Spirit Tree’s location because you don’t want any involvement?\"","However, to Yuan’s surprise, the man shook his head and said, \"No, that’s not it. In fact, I—we would like to help you.\"","\"We?\"","\"The Asura Clan has monopolized the Spirit Tree since ancient times, and there are many people who are sick of it. That’s why many of us are going to put an end to it. Why don’t you join us? We’ll get you to the Spirit Tree and back you in your revenge,\" the man urged."]},{"number":2197,"title":"Chapter 2197: Location of the Spirit Tree","paragraphs":["Hearing the man’s offer, Yuan couldn’t help but smile.","\"I see. So you’re going to attack the Asura Clan. How many people do you already have with you?\" he asked.","The man then said, \"We have the majority of the top factions on our side. The Asura Clan might be powerful—undoubtedly the most powerful in the Primordial Realm—but if we all work together, not even they will be able to stop us.\"","\"You sound very confident. Have you fought the Asura Clan before?\"","\"Nobody has seriously fought the Asura Clan in ages. However, they are not omnipotent. Moreover, they have fewer than ten people in their faction, while we have over ten thousand experts. There’s no way we will lose to them.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"When do you plan to attack the Asura Clan?\"","\"We’re already fully prepared, so we can attack whenever. Right now, we’re just waiting for an opportunity to launch our attack.\"","\"In other words, it might happen a week or a hundred years from now,\" Yuan shook his head. \"Unfortunately, I am short on time.\"","\"Why are you in such a hurry?\"","Yuan pondered for a brief moment before responding, \"Because I am hunted by the Chaotic Sect, and the longer I am away from my family, the more dangerous things get for me.\"","\"What? Why is the Chaotic Sect hunting you?\" The man frowned at this news.","Yuan gave a brief explanation of his situation with the Chaotic Sect.","\"Those arrogant bastards are always trying to take advantage of others! It’s because of this behavior that we decided not to include them in our plan, as people like them are likely to backstab us.\"","\"But you don’t need to worry. As long as you join us, not even the Chaotic Sect will be able to touch you.\"","\"If you say that, it’ll be hard for me to refuse,\" Yuan said with a smile.","After a moment of silence, he continued, \"Alright, I’ll join your cause. However, can you still tell me the location of the Spirit Tree? I won’t approach the Asura Clan alone. I just want to have peace of mind knowing where I can find them.\"","\"Even if you know the location, you won’t be able to enter it without the Asura Clan or the Inferno Alchemist’s assistance.\"","\"What’s the Inferno Alchemist have to do with this?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Well, the Spirit Tree exists in its own dimension, and it can only be accessed by the Asura Clan or the head of the Inferno Alchemists.\"","\"What’s their relationship with the Asura Clan?\"","The man stared at Yuan with a baffled expression. \"You... you truly know nothing of this world? Just how isolated has your life been until now?\"","Yuan silently shrugged.","\"Anyway, the Inferno Alchemists are basically the only alchemists in the Primordial Realm. But without spiritual energy, they can hardly practice their craft. That’s why they struck a deal with the Asura Clan—unlimited pills for them in return for access to the Spirit Tree.\"","\"Our lack of access to the Spirit Tree is also another reason why we cannot attack them whenever we want.\"","\"Are the Inferno Alchemists not on our side?\" Yuan questioned.","The man shook his head and said, \"No, those guys only care about alchemy and money, and since they already have access, they wouldn’t want to jeopardize it.\"","\"Then how do you plan on reaching the Spirit Tree, much less attacking the Asura Clan? Do you intend on forcing the alchemists to lead you to the Spirit Tree or something?\"","\"You’re quite insightful. That’s right. We are going to force them to take us to the Spirit Tree. The Inferno Alchemists barely have a hundred members in their faction, so it won’t be difficult to subdue them.\"","Yuan found it amusing how this man was so quick to reveal their schemes to someone who was no more than a stranger.","’Does he have ulterior motives, or is he really just this... loose-lipped?’ he wondered inwardly.","\"So, where’s the Spirit Tree located?\" Yuan asked as he retrieved two spirit stones and showed them to the man.","\"The entrance to the Spirit Tree is located at the Burning Tree in the Land of Inferno, but like I said, you won’t be able to enter it without the Asura Clan or the Inferno Alchemists.\"","\"I know. Here are your spirit stones.\" Yuan casually handed him the spirit stones.","\"Take this.\"","In exchange, the man handed him a token and continued, \"This will not only serve as an identification but also a communication device. If it activates, you must immediately head to the Spirit Tree, as that is when we will launch our attack.\"","\"Alright.\" Yuan accepted the token.","The man left shortly after, while Yuan returned to his room to wait for the auction payout.","A week passed in the blink of an eye, and during this time, several more individuals approached Yuan for his offer.","In case the man lied about the location of the Spirit Tree, Yuan acted like the offer was still available to confirm the location.","And out of the eight people that approached him, three of them mentioned the Burning Tree, while the other five all gave him different locations.","\"The Burning Tree, huh? Just wait a little longer, Xiao Hua. You’re almost home.\"","After a whole week had passed, Yuan returned to the Chaos Auction House for the payout.","\"So, do you have my money, or do I have to make a trip to the Chaotic Sect?\"","Chen Cheng quickly responded, \"Rest assured, esteemed guest, you will receive your payment. Regardless of your situation with the Chaotic Sect, we cannot steal your money or treasures at the auction house, or nobody would dare to trust us again.\"","\"Please, follow me. Your money is stored in another room.\"","Yuan nodded and followed Chen Cheng to a different room, where over a dozen large chests were gathered.","\"The money is all here. You can count them if you’d like.\"","With a sweep of his divine sense, Yuan verified that the chests held all the money. But amidst the coins, something unusual stood out.","A few of them had a subtle and unique aura hidden within them.","\"Thanks.\"","Yuan pretended not to notice it and tossed all of the money into his spatial ring."]},{"number":2198,"title":"Chapter 2198: Second Chaotic Heart","paragraphs":["After storing the money, Yuan turned around and began walking toward the exit.","\"Esteemed guest... It’s not too late...\" Chen Cheng suddenly spoke, halting his movements.","Yuan turned to face him and asked, \"What are you talking about?\"","Chen Cheng sighed before elaborating, \"It’s not too late to apologize to the Chaotic Sect. Just like the gold coins, you should have more spirit stones in your possession, right? You can show your sincerity by offering some of them to the Chaotic Sect, and there’s a good chance they’ll forgive you.\"","Yuan smiled and responded, \"You should really work at a different place. Someone like you does not belong in a place like the Chaotic Sect.\"","Chen Cheng shook his head and said, \"I grew up in the Chaotic Sect. It’s not a place I can leave whenever I feel like.\"","\"Is that so? What a pity. As for apologizing to the Chaotic Sect... I’d rather they hunt me,\" said Yuan before walking out of the room.","Shortly after Yuan left, Chen Cheng went to another room, where the Chaos Elders were waiting.","\"It’s been done. He accepted all of the money without any issue,\" Chen Cheng informed them.","\"Great job. Once we take care of him, I’ll consider giving you a promotion,\" said the man.","Chen Cheng didn’t respond to that statement and silently bowed.","\"Is there anything else I can do for you?\"","\"No, we’ll handle the rest,\" said the woman as she stood up with an excited smile on her face.","\"It’s time to hunt.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan returned to the hotel and retrieved the coins that had a subtle aura hidden within them.","\"Looks like a tracker. They’ll probably attack once we leave this city,\" Yuan calmly remarked.","\"So, what are we going to do?\" Mu Xuelian asked.","\"This doesn’t change anything. We’ll still head to the Spirit Tree. If they attack us, we’ll just take care of them. If you’d rather not get involved, you can wait here.\"","\"No thanks. If I stay behind, I might as well have never entered this place with you,\" she refused without hesitation.","\"In that case, do whatever you want. It’s not like I was going to ask you to help me, anyway. I can deal with them myself.\"","\"Then when are we going to leave?\" Mu Xuelian asked.","\"In a few days, after I absorb all of the Chaotic Essence from the Chaos Coins,\" he calmly replied.","\"Okay.\"","Yuan stowed away the Chaos Coins with the aura and took out the untampered Chaos Coins from his spatial ring, piling them into a little mountain before him in the middle of the room.","’With this much Chaotic Essence, I can easily create another Chaotic Heart.’ Yuan thought to himself as he sat before the mountain of coins.","Without hesitation, he began his cultivation.","Over the next several days, Yuan’s second cultivation, which had been stagnant at Chaotic Master since he left the Primal Expanse, soared towards the heavens.","<You have absorbed Chaotic Essence>","<You have absorbed enough Chaotic Essence for a breakthrough!>","<You have reached Early Chaotic Commander>","<You have absorbed enough Chaotic Essence for a breakthrough!>","<You have reached Intermediate Chaotic King>","<You have absorbed enough Chaotic Essence to start forming your second Chaotic Heart!>","<You have begun forming your second Chaotic Heart!>","<You have absorbed enough Chaotic Essence for a breakthrough!>","<You have reached Perfect Chaotic Emperor>","<You have successfully formed your second Chaotic Heart!>","<Your second Chaotic Heart has merged with your Chaotic Dragon Core, drastically strengthening it!>","<You have reached Early Chaotic Overlord!>","By the time Yuan finished absorbing all of the Chaotic Essence, his cultivation reached Early Chaotic Overlord, which was akin to a cultivator who had just entered Bronze Immortal. However, his prowess was obviously incomparably more powerful than that of a Bronze Immortal.","\"If I had known how much these coins would benefit my cultivation, I would’ve sold a few more spirit stones,\" he sighed, seriously considering selling more spirit stones later.","\"...\"","Mu Xuelian, who had witnessed everything, was left speechless. As an ordinary cultivator, she couldn’t perceive Yuan’s second cultivation, so to her eyes, nothing had changed. Yet she could clearly feel that something about him was profoundly different.","Shiva, who watched through Mu Xuelian, was also quite stunned to witness a human cultivating Chaotic Essence.","’A human possessing Chaotic Hearts, huh? That shouldn’t be possible without a completed Eternal Constitution... How many secrets are contained within that body?’ Shiva thought to herself.","As for the Chaos Coins, once Yuan absorbed all of their Chaotic Essence, they crumbled into nothingness, leaving behind only a mound of gray dust that resembled ashes.","This also meant Yuan had obliterated billions worth of the Chaotic Sect’s currency. If word of it ever spread, it would spark chaos across the region and send shockwaves through the world’s financial balance.","\"Alright, I’m ready to leave the city,\" Yuan said.","Mu Xuelian nodded, and together they departed not long after.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the city, the Chaos Elders had been waiting for Yuan to finally leave the city.","\"Get ready! He’s finally on the move!\" The woman said to the man after noticing Yuan had left the city through the tracker.","The man nodded before turning to face the others in the room.","\"You guys ready?\"","\"I was born ready.\"","\"Finally, we can stretch our arms. I was beginning to die of boredom.\"","Thus, the Chaos Elders, along with several members of the Chaotic Sect, began trailing Yuan through the tracker. Yet, they held back their assault, choosing instead to wait until he had ventured far enough from the city.","After days of aimless wandering, Yuan and Mu Xuelian finally stopped moving when several presences materialized out of thin air, closing in from every direction.","Within moments, five figures surrounded them, each one emanating the oppressive aura of a God Ascension expert.","\"About time you showed up. What took you so long?\" Yuan spoke out loud as he faced the Chaos Elders.","\"So you knew,\" muttered the male Chaos Elder.","Yuan retrieved one of the coins they used to track him and flicked it at him.","\"How could I not when you made it so obvious?\""]},{"number":2199,"title":"Chapter 2199: Confronting the Chaos Elders","paragraphs":["\"So you knew we were tracking you, yet you still decided to leave the city alone? I can’t even imagine what’s going through that mind of yours,\" remarked the female Chaos Elder, her tone full of mockery.","\"It’s nothing complicated. There’s just no reason for me to worry. After all, you’re not a threat to me,\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"Still trying to act tough? Not only are you just an Immortal, but we outnumber you.\"","Yuan chuckled. \"So what? You may be God Ascension cultivators, but you only have slightly more spiritual energy than I do. Right now, you’re no different from mere Immortals.\"","\"This little bastard is very talkative...\" mumbled one of the other cultivators.","\"Elder Pan, can we kill them already?\" said another.","The male Chaos Elder, surnamed Pan, glared coldly at Yuan as he spoke. \"I don’t know what hole a bastard like you crawled out from, nor what background you have—but no one who insults the Chaotic Sect walks away unscathed. Still, being the generous man that I am, I’ll grant you one final chance.\"","\"Be a good boy and hand over everything in your possession, and I will grant you a swift and painless death.\"","Yuan smiled and replied, \"If you want my stuff, you’ll have to work for it. However, the results might not be what you’re expecting.\"","\"What a pointless struggle.\"","\"If you want to die a horrible death, allow me to help you!\"","One of the experts suddenly lunged at Yuan with a Divine-grade spear in his grasp.","Yuan didn’t even bother dodging the attack and stood still as the spear struck his chest.","\"What?!\"","To the wielder’s shock, the spear slammed into Yuan and stopped dead, unable to push forward.","In the midst of the wielder’s shock, Yuan grabbed the spear and casually yanked it from his grasp.","\"This is how you use a spear.\"","Yuan surged with Chaotic Essence as he lunged the spear, the thrust detonating with cataclysmic force—splitting the air in a deafening boom and rending open the very fabric of space as it hurled at the shocked expert.","\"What are you doing?! Dodge it!\"","The spear expert snapped out of his daze at the sound of Elder Pan’s voice, and he hastily summoned his spiritual energy in an attempt to block the incoming strike.","However, due to their environment that forced everyone to be mindful of their spiritual energy usage, the expert subconsciously held back the amount of spiritual energy he used.","Due to this mistake, the spear ripped through his spiritual energy like paper before carving a gaping hole through his body. That being said, even if the expert had used all of his spiritual energy to defend, it wouldn’t have been enough to block the strike.","Before the spear expert could recover, Yuan closed the gap and flicked his arm that was surging with Supreme Sword Aura, striking the man’s head and sending it spinning skyward.","With his physical body destroyed, the man immediately tried to flee with his soul. However, Yuan extended his arm in the direction the man was fleeing and mumbled, \"Shiva’s Eternal Frost.\"","In the next instant, the temperature plummeted as if they’d been thrust into the ninth region of White Hell, and everything within ten thousand miles was sealed in ice.","The other four cultivators did not freeze outright, yet they felt their blood beginning to solidify. The fleeing soul, however, was sealed entirely, entombed in eternal frost.","’That bastard’s using my powers!’ Shiva exclaimed inwardly after witnessing the scene.","Though the power itself was pitifully weak, it was not something mortals could wield, making Yuan’s ability to unleash it a feat in its own right.","Meanwhile, Yuan was surprised by how demanding the technique was. A single strike had emptied his reserves in an instant, and that was only enough to allow him to barely activate it. Fortunately, his energy recovered just as swiftly.","’As expected, a technique that surpasses human limits is quite demanding...’ Yuan smiled inwardly.","Instead of disappointment, excitement stirred within him at the thought of the day he could wield Shiva’s power to its fullest potential.","Yuan’s gaze swept over the remaining four, his eyes like ice as he murmured, \"One down... four to go.\"","Elder Pan and the others trembled—not from Yuan’s overwhelming might, but from the unfathomable aura that still lingered from Shiva’s Eternal Frost.","\"What’s wrong? Don’t tell me you’ve lost all will to fight this quickly?\"","Yuan’s words jolted them from their daze. Elder Pan barked, \"Fool! You may have slain one of us, but that technique must have drained nearly all your energy!\"","Yuan only smiled. \"You’re not wrong. But unlike you, I can simply replenish it whenever I wish.\"","\"You’re really stupid if you think that bluff would!\"","Suddenly, one of the cultivators vanished from sight and reappeared behind Yuan, his saber already cleaving toward Yuan’s neck.","This time, Yuan did not stand idle. He lifted his arm and caught the incoming saber between two fingers, stopping it cold in an instant.","\"You feeling cold? Let me warm you up a bit,\" Yuan murmured, unleashing the Primordial Fire—flames so searing they twisted the very air as they consumed the man.","\"Ahhhh!\"","The man’s screams tore through the sky as he plummeted to the ground, thrashing desperately in a futile attempt to smother the flames. But the Primordial Fire would not relent, and it devoured him piece by piece until only his soul remained.","Once again, the cultivator attempted to flee with his soul.","\"You think you can strike at me and leave as you please?\" Yuan sneered, summoning the Primordial Fire once more.","Flames engulfed the man’s soul, and since it was far more durable than flesh, the fire gnawed at it slowly, wringing screams of unending agony.","Yuan didn’t bother waiting for the Primordial Fire to finish devouring the soul. Instead, he turned his gaze upon the remaining three, their faces ashen, as though they had just seen a ghost.","\"Not looking so confident anymore, huh?\" Yuan remarked with a cold smile."]},{"number":2200,"title":"Chapter 2200: Confronting the Chaos Elders(2)","paragraphs":["\"Damn it! What kind of mess did you drag me into, Elder Pan?! Elder Zi! You offended a monster!\" The third cultivator shouted at the Chaos Elders.","\"It... it wasn’t supposed to be like this...\" Elder Zi murmured, her dazed eyes clouded with disbelief, struggling to accept the reality before her.","\"L-Let’s talk about this!\" Elder Pan suddenly said. \"If you agree to stop here, we’ll overlook the fact that you killed two of our members and act like we don’t even know each other!\"","\"And if I refuse?\" Yuan asked just for the entertainment.","\"Then you’ll be hunted by the entire Chaotic Sect!\"","\"If I kill all of you right here, would the Chaotic Sect even know who I am?\"","\"They will! After all, we wouldn’t be here if we didn’t receive the Chaotic Sect’s approval! In other words, they know who you are and that if we don’t return, you’ll be the first one they suspect!\" Elder Pan said.","\"And what assurance do I have,\" Yuan asked, \"that if I spare you now, you won’t return with more to hunt me later? You can’t blame me for not trusting you, either.\"","\"That’s...\" Elder Pan didn’t know how to respond.","No, it was more like he couldn’t, as there was simply no way he would let Yuan go after this humiliation.","Of course, Yuan already knew this, and he calmly declared, \"I refuse your proposal. Now, die for me!\"","Yuan activated True Dragon Awakening, causing his aura to skyrocket. However, he didn’t stop there and further strengthened himself with his second cultivation.","\"Screw this—I’m out of here!\" the third cultivator exclaimed, turning to flee without hesitation, abandoning the Chaos Elders. But before he could escape, Yuan summoned a wall of Primordial Fire, encasing them in a blazing sphere that sealed every path.","\"W-Why?! We have no enmity, and I never even raised a hand against you!\" the cultivator cried, his voice breaking as Yuan barred his path.","\"You’re right, which is precisely why you’re still alive. Stay there and don’t lift a single finger until I tell you to do so if you want to live. I’ll be with you shortly after I deal with these two,\" said Yuan before turning to look at the Chaos Elders, who were clearly panicking and trembling in fear.","\"Wait... please... calm down! We were wrong, okay? Have mercy!\" Elder Zi, the female Chaos Elder, pleaded with teary eyes.","Yuan coldly sneered, untouched by her tears, \"Would you have spared me if you were in my shoes? Probably not.\"","\"But—\"","As Elder Zi opened her mouth, Yuan drew Number One Under Heaven and unleashed a swift, devastating strike. A flash of golden sword light filled her eyes, and in the next heartbeat, his Supreme Sword Aura cleaved her body and soul clean in two.","Elder Pan stared at Elder Zi’s split corpse with a terrified expression. He couldn’t even begin to fathom how an Immortal could kill a God Ascension cultivator with such ease. Even if they weren’t as powerful as God Ascension cultivators in the Nine Heavens, they’re still beings that cannot be touched by mere Immortals.","\"Was it worth it?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"What...?\" Elder Pan muttered.","\"If you think about it, things ended up like this because you couldn’t wait a few days. Try to be a little more patient in your next life, alright?\"","Elder Pan trembled at Yuan’s words. Then, after a tense silence, his face flushed red as he roared, \"If you think I’ll go down without a fight, you’re—\"","However, Yuan didn’t even give him the chance to finish his sentence and swung his sword that was wreathed in a golden aura .","In an instant, Elder Pan’s entire being was erased from existence.","Yuan turned to look at the remaining cultivator afterward and spoke in a nonchalant voice, \"Do you want to live?\"","The cultivator, too terrified to speak, could only silently nod his head.","\"Bring me to the Burning Tree within the Land of Inferno, and I’ll let you live.\"","\"The Burning Tree...? You might as well just kill me now. There’s no way we’ll get there alive. Even if we do, we won’t make it back,\" he said.","\"If you’re worried about the Asura Clan attacking us, rest assured—they won’t,\" Yuan said calmly.","The cultivator frowned and asked, \"Why are you so certain? Are you tied to the Asura Clan? No... if you were, you wouldn’t need me to lead you there...\"","\"Stop asking so many questions. Don’t forget your place—if you’re no use, say so, and I’ll cut you down immediately.\" Yuan’s voice was flat and cold.","The cultivator gritted his teeth, fists white with tension.","After a moment of silence, he loosened his fists and murmured, \"Fine. I’ll take you to the Burning Tree.\"","\"Good. Then let us be on our way,\" Yuan said.","The cultivator sighed, as though surrendering to fate, and started flying south.","\"So, how are you related to the elders? And how did you end up in this situation?\" Yuan questioned as they traveled.","\"There are twenty-four elders at the Chaotic Sect—well, twenty now since you just killed four of them. We were ordered by the Sect Leader to take care of the ’insolent bastard’ who dared to insult and look down on our sect. In other words, I’m just following orders.\"","\"If that’s true, you’re truly unlucky.\" Yuan shook his head, but he did not feel pity.","He continued, \"Is the Chaotic Sect always like this?\"","\"Pretty much. We do not tolerate anyone who disrespects us.\"","\"I’m surprised you guys survived this long with that kind of mentality.\"","\"It’s because we don’t let people look down on us that we’ve survived this long. As long as we don’t mess with the Asura Clan, we won’t go anywhere.\"","\"If you say so.\"","A few days later—","\"We’ve just entered the Inferno Alchemists’ territory,\" said the cultivator.","\"How long until we reach the Burning Tree?\" Yuan asked.","\"If nothing goes wrong, we should arrive in a week,\" he said.","\"Very well.\" Yuan nodded."]}]);
